>Attributes</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Intelligence: </b>1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Wits: </b>3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Resolve: </b>4</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Strength: </b>3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dexterity: </b>3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Stamina: </b>1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Presence: </b>1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Manipulation: </b>2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Composure: </b>4</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">[5/4/3 distribution, +1 Composure]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Skills</b></u><b> (<i>Profession, </i><u>Rote</u>)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Occult</i>: </b>4+1 (Awakened Magic)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Politics: </b>3 (Chicago Consilium)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Athletics: </b>4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><u>Stealth</u>: </b>3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i><b>Weaponry</b></i>: 4</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Expression: </b>2 (Dance)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><u>Subterfuge</u>: </b>2</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Advantages</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Health: </b>6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Willpower: </b>8</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Defense: </b>7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Initiative: </b>7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Speed: </b>11</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Size: </b>5</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gnosis: </b>1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Wisdom: </b>7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Max Mana/Per Turn</b>: 10/1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Merits</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Artifact: </b>5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Infamous Mentor: </b>3 [Consilium Status 3, Fixer (for Status requisition purposes) 2, Allies (Adamantine Arrow) 3, Contacts (Knights of Alhambra) 1]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Professional Training (Sleepwalker Servant)</b>: 2 [Asset Skills: Occult, Weaponry. Contacts (Consilium Sleepwalkers, non-Awakened Occultists)]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>High Speech: </b>1<br /> <b>Familiar: </b>4 (temporary)<br /> <b>Status (Guardians of the Veil): </b>1*</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Arcana: </b></u>Mind 2, Space 2, Time 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Praxes</b></u><br /> Divination (Time 1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Attainments</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Counterspell (Mind, Space, Time)<br /> Mage Armor (Mind, Space, Time)<br /> Mind's Eye<br /> Sympathetic Range<br /> Temporal Sympathy</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Rotes </b></u>(Not yet active)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Psychic Domination, Mind 2 (Subterfuge 3, Reach 4)<br /> Choose the Thread, Time 2 (Occult 5, Reach 4)<br /> Postcognition, Time 1 (Occult 5, Reach 5)<br /> Perfect Timing, Time 1 (Stealth 4, Reach 5)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Dedicated Tool</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A hand mirror with hairline fractures.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Nimbus</b></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Long-term:</b> Doubts and regrets grow stronger, a sense of being trapped and needing to escape. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Immediate: </b>Moonstone seems to speak backwards, shrinking and growing and warping like a funhouse mirror.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Signature: </b>The object is like the Snow Queen's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Snow_Queen#Story\" target=\"_blank\">devil-mirror</a>, mentally reflecting the worst parts of the observer back at them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tilt: </b>-1 to Dexterity rolls.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Aspirations</b></u><br /> - Investigate La Grange Park. (short-term)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Learn something about the mage who attacked us. (short-term)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Distance myself from Hakim in a significant way. (long-term)<br /> <br /> [completed: Perform for a Crowd, Engage in Social Maneuvering, Join a Cabal, Teach Ragnar something about magic, Acquire a Familiar]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Obsession</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The potential shared Sympathy of the Deathstorm victims.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Equipment</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dao (Damage 2, Initiative -2, Strength 2, Size 2, Availability 2, page 221)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dance wear (+2 to relevant Social rolls, Durability 1, Size 2, Structure 1, Availability 3, page 277)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Occult paraphernalia [incense, candles, sigils, papercraft, etc] (+1 to relevant Occult or Social rolls, Availability 1, grants access to +1 Sacrament yantra)</span></span><br /> A pair of +2 Sacrament yantras, for Space and Time respectively<br /> Valentine's business card, suitable for contacting him sympathetically<br /> iPhone (photos: Stormborne group shot, imitation of Mathias)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cloak of Night (Artifact 5)</b><br /> An archaic hooded traveling cloak, ink-black, with a leaden clasp in the shape of a death's-head moth. Retrieved from a Highstorm by Hakim.<br /> Contains the spells Shadow Flesh (Death 4) and Wards and Signs (Prime 2). Effective Gnosis 3 and Arcana 4. Contains up to 10 Mana. Moros Path tool.<br /> <b>Effect 1:</b> Gain [base Potency 4, more with spell factors] Withstand against all spells targeting me specifically for 1 scene. Activated by closing the clasp around the neck. 7 dice before spell factors. (Wards and Signs, 1 reach spent on instant casting, 1 reach on advanced duration, 1 reach spent on changing primary factor from duration to potency.)<br /> <b>Effect 2:</b> Dissolve into a two-dimensional shadow for [base Duration 5 turns, more with spell factors] as per Shadow Flesh. Activated by pulling the hood over the head. 7 dice before spell factors. (Shadow Flesh, 1 reach spent on instant casting.)<br /> <br /> <b>Moonstone's Fear (Familiar 4)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Moonstone's Fear lurks hazily in Mind Twilight as a human-sized and slightly more humanoid version of Alux. Toothsome, amorphous, light-consuming. Moonstone has nightmares that Alux can fly, and so Fear can fly.<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 5, Resistance 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 15<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Familiar<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Fear 2<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Counterspell, Drain, Hallucination, Reveal Flaws<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must spend 1 Willpower to act against someone who successfully resisted a fear attack.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Physical contact with the real Alux.<br /> <br /> <b>Counterspell: </b>As it specifically represents Moonstone's fear of the Abyss consuming and nullifying his magic, Fear can counter Awakened spells by injecting fear and self-doubt into the caster's Imago. When Moonstone perceives a spell being cast in Active Sight, spend one Essence to activate this Numen, which recreates the Prime 2 &quot;Universal Counterspell&quot; Attainment. Fear rolls Rank+Influence in the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Drain: </b>As written. When used on Moonstone, Fear may choose to take only 1 success on its activation roll, effectively letting him steal its own Willpower- if he's at least minimally strong.<br /> <br /> <b>Hallucination: </b>As written, with an eye towards nightmarish hallucinations drawn from Moonstone's subconscious.<br /> <br /> <b>Reveal Flaws: </b>Fear draws a target's hidden faults to the surface, writing words such as &quot;weak&quot; or &quot;greedy&quot; or &quot;liar&quot; on their skin in Mind Twilight. This Numen costs one Essence, is resisted by Resolve+Composure+Gnosis, and lasts until Fear uses another Numen or Influence. For each net success Fear achieves, the target suffers a -1 penalty on its next contested roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Special - Goetic Struggle: </b>As the embodiment of a specific complex drawn from Moonstone's unconscious, Fear can use its Influence to help him resist fear. When Moonstone would otherwise be affected by a supernatural fear effect such as Awe or Nightmare, it triggers a Clash of Wills. Roll Gnosis+Mind against the goetia's Rank+Influence. If Moonstone succeeds, the supernatural fear effect fails and he gains 1 Willpower. If Fear succeeds, Moonstone is affected by the power as if the attacker rolled an exceptional success.</span></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>History</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/6XS57ej.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <u><b>Look</b></u><br /> 38 year old male. Southeast Asian ethnically, adopted by an American family before his first birthday. Usually presents as masculine, but prefers to look more femme for ritual work and dancing (same thing, really.) Usually fidgeting or playing with his fingers or shifting his weight as a nervous habit, but moves like an acrobat when he's focused.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Background</b></u><br /> Moonstone has spent the past decade or so as the companion and faithful servant of Hakim (aka Lamont Torres-Wilson), a Moros and respected Thunderbolt Guardian of the Chicago Arrow. He maintained his master's (&quot;like a Zen master! it's not weird!&quot;) sanctum, assisted with his rituals, tended his wounds, nurtured a painfully obvious and ambiguously-requited attraction, and sometimes even fought by his side directly. Most recently, he stood by his master and comforted him through a contentious break with his cabal as Hakim became more reclusive, retreating from Consilium politics into more mystical and esoteric research even Moonstone wasn't privy to. And then, during a sudden and unexplained return to downtown Chicago, he was killed. And now Moonstone is alone. It has been a very long time since Moonstone was alone.<br /> <br /> Sometimes he feels like his life before he met Hakim happened to someone else. Short version: he could always see magic, and that was just one of the things that made people think he was crazy. He was an international adoption, and never quite fit his old-money family's expectations for their perfect demure daughter. Dropping out of the UCLA dance program they'd enrolled him in and taking a one-way bus ticket to Chicago in 2001 was the first time he ever felt like he was in control of his life. Meeting Hakim and his cabal after witnessing and remembering a Supernal summoning was like Hagrid telling Cinderella she'd been a wizard all along. For someone who had never quite fit into the assumptions of Sleeping society, it was a homecoming.<br /> <br /> Except he wasn't a wizard. After a few years, even the optimists stop believing that constant exposure to magic is going to help you Awaken. Even the arcane can become routine. You decide in your heart that you're going to accept the gift of living among people who see the world as it truly is, but you're never really going to be one of them. And you become happy with that. There are so many ways you can help them and be useful to them. Do you think magicians cook their own dinner? Who draws the chalk circles and buys the eye of newt? Who catalogues the grimoires? Who guards your sleeping body when you're in the Dreaming Earth? Who speaks in your name at Consilium when you can't be bothered? Who backs you up with a blazing sword when a Gulmoth breaks through the summoning circle? Sleepwalkers, baby. Accept no substitutes.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Awakening</b></u><br /> Moonstone pretty much locked up and shut down once he heard about Hakim's assassination. He was practically catatonic, unable to leave his room in their apartment/sanctum in La Grange (a sadly necessary downgrade from the old Chicago sanctum after the split with his old cabal) for what seemed like weeks. Choking vines grew from the walls, jeering Fae knocked insistently at the door, Time stretched agonizingly out until he'd been confined to a dusty corner for a month and everything else had been claimed by the thorns. It had to end. And it did.<br /> <br /> He stood up and screamed and screamed and tore at the vines until his hands were bloody, climbed like Jack up the beanstalk on a path that didn't exist until he created it, chased a timid fairy with the face of his parents' perfect daughter and a controlling ogre that was Hakim and his father and mother and caseworker all at once, severed the hangman rope of the Norns that tied him down to the path of Destiny, bound the two fairies together with the stolen rope in a wicker man made from thorny Hedge-vines, conjured fire with a word and burned them to death in a great and terrible sacrifice, a ritual of his own for once, and sprouted wings and rose into the heavens on the smoke of the wicker man and their pleas for him to come back to earth with them. But he was in Arcadia, and he couldn't hear them anymore.<br /> <br /> He woke up in his room, bloodied from shattering mirrors by hand, sputtering from smoke inhalation, and his bedsheets and clothes and photos of him and Hakim were burning in a foul smoky pile on the floor. It had been exactly one hour since he heard about Hakim's death. Dutiful as always, he put out the fire and bandaged his wounds and checked himself into a mental hospital. Fate wouldn't keep him there any longer than he had to be.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Connections</span></span></b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Binder:</span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Moonstone is a patron of Marlin's bookstore, and the two of them sometimes play chess at the park.<br /> <b>Phoenix: </b>Hakim was the mage who killed Phoenix's hunter cell.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Resource Stats</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Health: </b>XXX//O<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>3/8<br /> <b>Mana: </b>7/10<br /> (<b>Cloak of Night, Mana</b>: 10/10)<br /> (<b>Moonstone's Fear, Essence: </b>15/15)<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Divergent, Guilty, Triumphant, Informed (Rumors)<br /> [-1 Strength until Monday night]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Divergent [Persistent]</b><br /> Your character has a difficult time relating to other people and himself. If the self is a bowl of clear water, his bowl ripples and boils and freezes and spills more easily than most in response to stimuli. The character has learned to manage the Condition most of the time, but stressful situations can make this more difficult. This Condition has an Active and Passive form.<br /> <b>Passive:</b> The character experiences symptoms, but can set them aside. When they have less than half their Willpower remaining, or when they fail a Resolve+Composure roll in response to a stressor, the Condition switches to Active for the rest of the scene.<br /> <b>Active:</b> The character's symptoms are more pronounced. Apply a -2 to all Social rolls and rolls involving Resolve. The character has 1 less Withstand against Mind spells targeting them. When they regain their full Willpower pool, or at the end of the scene, this Condition switches to Passive unless they still have less than half their Willpower remaining.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The character's illness is cured by mundane or, more likely, supernatural means.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> The character acts in a significantly self-defeating way due to their illness, or fails a Resolve+Composure roll called for by the Storyteller to resist a stressor.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Beats and Experiences</b></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Beats: </b>0/5<br /> <b>Experiences (Unspent/Total): </b>4/4<br /> <b>Arcane Beats: </b>1/5<br /> <b>Experiences (Unspent/Total): </b>4/4</div></div> </div> </div></span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 08-18-2017, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:33:21-07:00","id":922118,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - I like the idea of an author and the skills/personality Michael Korn would have. I also certainly welcome new players, because I want people to be able to join and try out new games! In regards to your submission, if you're saying he <i>willed</i> a ship to appear, that is well within the purview of Fate magic. However, for something like that to happen in the middle of an ocean is at least a Weaving spell (3 dots), but seems more like a Patterning spell (4 dots). A more sensible interpretation or tweaking would be to say that he <i>foretold </i>that a ship was coming (a Knowing / 1st dot Time spell).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=922048#post922048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big question! On a scale of 1 to 10, where 1 is Henry Wu and 10 is Takashi Natsume, how much does the Athenaeum care about the cryptids' wellbeing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh...Can you provide different rating anchors, or clarify what you're looking for here? I haven't provided (or firmly created) a lot of details about the Mysterium in this world, but they will likely be pretty hands-on and practical. Downtown Chicago has a lot of Mysteries rich for the taking...for someone willing to risk the dangers of staying in the city for long. Some Mystagogues will be focused on caution and preserving what's already been found, especially given recent events in Awakened politics (more coming soon). Others will be very much intrigued by what they could find in Chicago. Mystagogues gathering and living in the outlying suburbs will probably be more responsible for protection and safekeeping of collected knowledge. Does that help at all?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Digging the updated character concept and info. I can tell that you have a lot of knowledge about the game, and your character would very likely have a fair bit more exposure to Awakened society than other characters. I'm fine with this, as long as you put an appropriate number of points into related Merits (e.g., Contacts, Status), which we can talk about down the road. I like the added details about Moonstone's personal history pre-Awakening, and I think I would enjoy the chance to RP as NPCs who interact with you post-Awakening (&quot;Wait...Since when can you do <i>that</i>?&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T12:05:53-07:00","id":922141,"title":"","content":"I'm actually running a Mage game myself right now, so all those Important Capitalized Setting Nouns are fresh in my mind, haha. I was planning to mostly represent that knowledge with the Infamous Mentor merit, which is effectively a grab bag of other social merits with the asterisk that they aren't really &quot;yours.&quot; I'll come back and add some info on the Awakening itself and the other questions later today!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T12:07:46-07:00","id":922143,"title":"","content":"I'm loving all the others applying here, hopefully gonna have a lot of fun wit you all.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Would you want anything more on Sara, rwknoll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:08:42-07:00","id":922209,"title":"","content":"I am sorry about the mix up, I changed the Awakening a bit. I will change it again if you don't like it. I tried a combination of time and fate. Read the outmost eddies on the current to get him to trade waters. When he floated on his back and stopped fighting the currents, just by luck the right one got him to the correct trade waters. Like choosing the correct lottery ticket. Compelling Fate. To keep him from giving up, he saw a vision of the ship that would save him like you suggested. If this doesn't sit well with you I can remove fate and just use time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:40:46-07:00","id":922224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=922209#post922209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry about the mix up, I changed the Awakening a bit. I will change it again if you don't like it. I tried a combination of time and fate. Read the outmost eddies on the current to get him to trade waters. When he floated on his back and stopped fighting the currents, just by luck the right one got him to the correct trade waters. Like choosing the correct lottery ticket. Compelling Fate. To keep him from giving up, he saw a vision of the ship that would save him like you suggested. If this doesn't sit well with you I can remove fate and just use time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally cool, and no worries! I only commented on it because I know you said you haven't played before, and I thought the story you presented (while cool) seemed unrealistic for a fledgling Mage. The Awakening can be a more artistic and narrative description; I only commented on yours because that detail seemed out of place. I really like, and appreciate, the changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:43:50-07:00","id":922315,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately one of our applicants is <i>still</i> having problems with account verification <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but he has asked me to post a current draft of his character concept, so everyone can have more details about what he's thinking.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Oscar \u201cLynx\u201d Valewood </b></u><br /> Concept: Animist and College student<br /> <br /> <b>History: </b>Oscar was born in Norway, Europe. His father was a marine biologist, his mother a lawyer. His upbringing was simple enough. His parents were engrossed in their careers, so he was often left to his own devices; as a child, this involved after-school activities, television shows, books and video games; as an adolescent, it involved staunch rebellion. The lack of attention had him run away from home at the age of 17.<br /> <br /> By ran away, of course, we mean he ran to the nearest forest of considerable size and got lost.<br /> <br /> He wandered between trees and up hills, and eventually found himself atop the regional mountain range. At first, he thought nothing of it. Woods and lakes joined with foliage, moss lingered where the shade lay. It was when the mist settled that he felt it \u2013 the jolt of fear. The wild had its aural environment, of course, but in the mist, it grew more prominent. He started seeing shadows skulking about, felt eyes on him where there were none. Yet the fear was not unwanted \u2013 it was an exhilaration. As the tension rose, he saw the greatest shadow yet before him, its eyes set on him like predator hunting prey. In spite of the thrill, Oscar ran away then \u2013 his metaphorical tail between his legs.<br /> <br /> He returned home the next morning. His parents chalked his absence to \u201cjust teenage things.\u201d<br /> <br /> The event had Oscar filled with longing, an ache he couldn't quite put his finger on. It felt like a second world existed, somewhere just out of sight. His parents and peers dismissed his thoughts and ideas whenever he brought this up, and with that, he found only solace in solitude.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening </b>\u2013 Thyrsus<br /> <br /> His Mystery Play had begun in the forest, but it was slow and subtle. The Supernal had trickled into his life, little by little, strengthening his sense to the \u201csecond world\u201d, but as the repeated dismissal of his experiences by those he deemed closest to him, the trickle slowed down to a halt. In the end, he felt empty.<br /> <br /> It was merely the interlude to the events of his 22st year.<br /> <br /> By the time Oscar was 21, his daily life was not particularly productive. Sure, he stayed in shape with frequent trips up the mountains in hopes of recapturing that feeling; he practised a little bit of art and drawing to try to remember what he had seen and felt.. He held a couple of part-time jobs, though he half-arsed his way through those without exceptional results. His academic ambitions weren't anything to brag about either. He tried to maintain some spiritualistic aspect in his life \u2013 but the emptiness had crawled into the entirety of his being. Nothing he did mattered.<br /> <br /> One day, though, he woke up, having had a dream that he couldn't truly explain \u2013 a dream so familiar it stirred a sense of wanderlust. During one of the rare moments his family was all gathered for breakfast, he mentioned he'd like to study abroad. Though surprised, both parents were in favour, offering to pay his tuition and rent \u2013 on the condition that he later produce results. They stated the experience would serve him well. He applied to a variety of schools all around the states, landing a college close to La Grange.<br /> <br /> The dam that kept the Supernal truth at bay burst when he landed on US soil. What would've been a simple bus trip from the airport to his apartment in La Grange became a dangerous trek through the Primal Wild. It was an encore of the fear and longing that had overwhelmed him four years ago, only this time he did not freeze when the mist washed over him, nor did he flee when he came face to face with the large and advancing shadow. When they stood face to face, he saw the shadow for what it was: the great Lynx. Without thinking Oscar embraced it as an old friend that he had known for his entire life. He embraced the Wild. He became the Lynx. The Lynx became him. At last, he was Truth.<br /> <br /> <b>Preferred game style:</b><br /> Exploration of mysteries and finding answers; philosophical quandaries and tough situations. More or less the same as Retias above.<br /> <br /> <b>Other Notes:</b><br /> His relationship to his parents is strained. They focused more on furthering their own careers, rather than family life. They weren't really there for him - sure, they had vacations and the occasional family outing, fancy dinner at restaurant, and he does love them, but there's a definite distance between them. In many ways, Oscar fears he was a mistake in their carefully planned life, and sometimes it seems like they would love nothing more than to tell him that. They do care, though, as they had no hesitation to let him study abroad while paying for his tuition and rent.<br /> <br /> As a character, he is usually calm and prudent in any given situation, but he tends to defer to decisions and judgement calls through instinct and gut feeling. He is reserved, though knowledge of others who have seen \u201cwhat lies beyond\u201d makes him giddy \u2013 nobody's ever \u201cgotten\u201d him before, and that tie makes him ever so curious. He isn't confrontational, but he is quick to judge: he measures people by how they treat their tools, their pets, and the world around them. Order-wise, he'd be a Mystagogue \u2013 he thirsts for knowledge and wants answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T18:08:49-07:00","id":922327,"title":"","content":"<b>For everyone:</b> There may still be a few more people posting character concepts soon. I do not think I will be able to balance and sustain the game I have in mind with more than ~6 players, for the same reasons that most tabletop games don't have parties of 6+ players. I hope people can appreciate that and be understanding.<br /> <br /> If we don't get any more submissions over the next few days, I will likely take everyone who has posted so far, so it will depend on how many people we end up getting characters for. Because of that, I would like people to think about ways they might be acquainted or related to other characters that have been submitted. I think this adds more cohesion to starting Chronicles of Darkness groups; even if they're only loosely related or acquainted, it will make it easier for me to help bring the characters together without feeling like I'm railroading.<br /> <br /> For example, if you wanted to play a homeless character, maybe arrange to have another PC know you because they periodically check up on you and offer you a warm meal. If you're a professor, maybe another character has met you at a conference or taken one of your classes.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> - In reviewing your character background, I still need some more information about how to fit Michael into the setting I've detailed at the start of this thread. Characters will be based out of the Chicago metro area, with a lot of the action taking place in either La Grange or Chicago. How do you want to make that work for Michael? Does he live in La Grange, or maybe is staying in the Chicago area for a while doing some research for a new book? And how might we connect him to some of the other character concepts posted here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T21:32:26-07:00","id":922452,"title":"","content":"Possible connections for Vo are probably...<br /> <br /> MEDICAL: Nerve damage sucks! She has to go in for a checkup on that nonsense once in a while. Perhaps she's met someone in these hospital visits?<br /> <br /> ACADEMIC: Students of hers, students of her colleagues, or generally people involved with U of C.<br /> <br /> NEIGHBORHOOD: Sometimes you just have neighbors... or you're the center of a line of neighborhood gossip because of your recent train-accident of a divorce. Maybe people who live nearby have talked to her, whether to show their support in this trying time or just to pry.<br /> <br /> THERAPEUTIC: It kind of really sucks to be Vo right now, and it's not out of the question that she might be involved in therapy, whether she's meeting someone who goes to a counselor in the same facility or she's involved in group therapy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T00:13:50-07:00","id":922490,"title":"","content":"Vo studies physics and Sara is a talented hacker. Maybe there are links there we can play on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T00:22:42-07:00","id":922491,"title":"","content":"<b>Bardo (Dr. Marvin Bates) Concept: Necromancer in training</b><br /> Born the only son of a traditional bostonian couple that had suffered a couple of abortions, Marvin didn't seem long for this world. Sickly and weak since birth, the child managed to survive the first day of his life against all odds. Then he lived for a week. Then a month. Whether it was little Marvin's determination, the obsesive love of his parents, or something stranger still, the fact is that Marvin succeeded where his stillborn brothers couldn't and managed to grow up to became a child, then a teenager and finally a young adult that was the pride of his parents.<br /> <br /> Although his health was always precarious at best, or maybe as sort of strange compesation of nature, Marvin demonstrated from an early age a vivacious ingenuity and a sharp intellect. Good natured, he decided to use his prodigious faculties to help those like him and so, with the blessing of his parents, he studied to became a doctor. His analitical mind and strong memory served him well and he graduated as the first of his promotion.<br /> <br /> Now Marvin is growing old, his parents died not a couple of years ago and he visits their tomb and that of his stillborn brothers every week. Married to one of his younger colleages and co-workers at the hospital (working in the maternity wing) they still have no child of their own. On one hand the job consumes a lot of time from both of them, and Marvin secretely fears that he may be incapable of siring healthy children as happened to his parents. He doesn't want to visit more small tombs the weekends.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening (Path Moros)</b><br /> The Awakening of Dr. Marvin Bates was at once more and less traumatic than most. He was beside the bed where their parents were dying of old age in his own hospital when, maybe due to the emotional overload, things started to get strange. He could felt how with each breath his parents were less and less alive, while nearby in the maternity ward the life was flourishing. As a certain undefinable spark was obviously getting extinguished in his parents, a new light grew stronger by the second in the newborns. Marvin finally awoke when he left the room where his parents laid dead to look for his wife to give her the news, only to saw the unmistakable gaze of his parents coming from a couple of recently born twins.<br /> <br /> <b>Game Style</b><br /> I want to explore the limits of magic and the life-death divide, including life extension and undeath.<br /> <br /> <b>Ties</b><br /> I might be related to Vo trhrough the hospital. I migth be her doctor even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T03:38:18-07:00","id":922526,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> - What kind of doctor would you like him to be? Surgeon, pathologist, internal medicine? Is there any particular kind that you think would suit him? I can make suggestions, otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T03:54:52-07:00","id":922530,"title":"","content":"Bardo's gonna be in this? <b>NUUUUUUUU!!!</b> He's the 6th character! Dammit, why didn't I look in this section sooner? It would've been real fun to kick back up the adventures of Pops and Son. Oh well, that's how the cookie crumbles, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T04:18:32-07:00","id":922533,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> Yep, It would have been real fun. I'm not yet in though, just applying.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Suggest away. Originally he was a surgeon, but I'm open to change things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 06-28-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T05:13:35-07:00","id":922545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=922530#post922530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bardo's gonna be in this? <b>NUUUUUUUU!!!</b> He's the 6th character! Dammit, why didn't I look in this section sooner? It would've been real fun to kick back up the adventures of Pops and Son. Oh well, that's how the cookie crumbles, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey there! I've posted across multiple forums because I know that there might be a fair number of people interested in playing. The only fair way I felt I could recruit for a game like this would be to leave recruitment open for several days and then select the ~4-6 players whom I think would fit best together and with the game world I'm creating. So, feel free to apply if you like, there's still time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T06:00:26-07:00","id":922563,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> - Surgeon sounds great. Another idea would be a forensic pathologist / medical examiner. That always made a lot of sense to me as a Moros mage, because you get tons of opportunities to practice your craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T06:57:13-07:00","id":922591,"title":"","content":"No problem, I just need to add to the background to bring it up to date. I will have something you can judge today. Please tell me if it is OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T07:56:01-07:00","id":922628,"title":"","content":"Added some info about Awakening and game preferences, because the post wasn't big enough already.<br /> <br /> Character connections: Moonstone isn't a total recluse among Sleepers, even if he doesn't exactly have a day job. Here's a few ideas!<ul><li>He's got a background in dance, and sometimes performs in the local cabaret/burlesque/pole scene to feel pretty and blow off steam (he has a lot of steam). He might be friends with a regular audience member or patron or someone involved in the local arts scene.</li> <li>He's one of those people who regularly plays chess with strangers at the park. Strategy games are fun, and it's a nice way to interact with other people without getting to know them too closely.</li> <li>He's queer, and might know other LGBT people from a meetup group or brief torrid fling.</li> <li>He's had some lifelong mental health issues that were being managed through Mind magic and the solid routine of being with Hakim and his cabal. Now that he's by himself, he's backsliding and he knows it. After his Awakening (which looked from the outside like a self-harming nervous breakdown), he briefly checked himself into the hospital and has been seeing a therapist to see if it gets him anywhere. He may have met someone there, or just be known as &quot;that dude who lost his boyfriend and is taking it really hard.&quot;</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T08:22:57-07:00","id":922641,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Character Sheet</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Player:</b> Epicarp (or crapcarp, whichever you prefer)<br /> <b>Chronicle:</b> The Supernal Suburbia<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Phoenix<br /> <b>Alternate Name:</b> Garrick Royce<br /> <b>Sympathic Name:</b> Timothy Carlyle Kemp<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Order:</b> (Adamantine Arrow)<br /> <b>Cabal:</b><br /> <b>Legacy:</b> (Tamer of Fire)<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Compassionate<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Rigid<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Hero in Darkness<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u></b><br /> <b>Intelligence:</b> 2<br /> <b>Wits:</b> 3<br /> <b>Resolve:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Strength:</b> 3<br /> <b>Dexterity:</b> 3<br /> <b>Stamina:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Presence:</b> 3<br /> <b>Manipulation:</b> 1<br /> <b>Composure:</b> 2<br /> <br /> [4/5/3 w/ extra dot in Resolve]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> <b>Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:</b> 1<br /> <b>Investigation:</b><br /> <b>Medicine:</b> 2<br /> <b>Occult:</b> 1 (Mythology)<br /> <b>Politics:<br /> Science:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Athletics:</b> 2<br /> <b>Brawl:</b> 4 (Striking)<br /> <b>Drive:<br /> Firearms:</b> 1<br /> <b>Larceny:</b> 1<br /> <b>Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy:</b> 2<br /> <b>Expression:</b> 2<br /> <b>Intimidation:</b> 2<br /> <b>Persuasion:<br /> Socialize:<br /> Streetwise:</b> 1 (Hunters)<br /> <b>Subterfuge:</b><br /> <br /> [4/11/7; extra Occult dot hasn't been added]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages</u></b><br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5 (7)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> Size: 5<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 1<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 7<br /> <b>Max Mana/Per Turn:</b> 10/1<br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits</b></u><ul><li>Alternate Identity (Garrick Royce) 1</li> <li>Status (Dojo) 1</li> <li>Defensive Combat (Brawl) 1</li> <li>Safe Place 2</li> <li>Martial Arts 3</li> <li>Danger Sense 2</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Arcana:</b></u> Forces 2, Mind 2, Prime 2<br /> <br /> <u><b>Praxes</b></u><ul><li>Supernal Vision (Prime 1)</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Attainments</u></b><ul><li>Precise Force (Forces 2)</li> <li>Mind's Eye (Mind 2)</li> <li>Universal Counterspell (Prime 2)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><ul><li>[insert Rotes]</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Long-Term</i> - Events play out like a written tale. A college graduate gets the opportunity they needed, a devious businessman gets the comeuppance they deserve, an innocent child is afflicted with tragedy that changes the course of their life forever, the unconnected situations of strangers weave into one another to bring them together.<br /> <br /> <i>Immediate</i> - The skin of the Fallen World cracks as the pure, raw stuff of creation itself pours out. Cracks form wherever the spell was focused. If he cast an Unveiling spell on himself, his eyes would glow and cracks would form from that point on his face. If he cast a Fraying spell on someone, cracks would appear on the wound.<br /> <br /> <i>Signature</i> - The cracks shrink into words of High Speech. The High Speech describes a deed in a classic mythological sense. For the Unveiling spell, the words might read &quot;And illusions were swept aside&quot;. For the Fraying spell, it might read &quot;Tongues of flame had lashed against flesh&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i>Tilt</i> - The elemental force is too much to handle, resulting in a -1 penalty on Composure rolls.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Aspirations</b></u><ul><li>Solve bill problem</li> <li>Join an Order</li> <li>Fail to keep the other Hunter cell away</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Obsessions</b></u><ul><li>[insert Obsession]</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Equipment</b></u><ul><li>[insert equipment]</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Details</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><b>General</b></u><br /> <b>Age/Birthday:</b> 19/February 20<br /> <b>Gender:</b> Male<br /> <b>Height:</b> 6' 5&quot;<br /> <b>Build:</b> Athletic<br /> <b>Occupation:</b> Martial Arts Teacher<br /> <b>Ethnicity:</b> Mixed<br /> <b>Nationality:</b> American<br /> <b>Hair Color:</b> Grey<br /> <b>Eye Color:</b> Brown<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Bisexual<br /> <br /> <b><u>Background</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Sleepwalking</i> - Timothy was born to an Awakened mother and a Sleepwalking father who happened to be a former Thaumaturge. Due to this heritage, Timothy was born with a sensitivity for magic and knew about it ever since he could remember.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, his father resented magic after practicing it for so long to negative result. His parents divorced and was raised by his father alone. He gained his father\u2019s resentment toward magic, which was further cemented after finding out about a sorcerer who gained immortality through regular acts of human sacrifice. Working together with a Hunter cell, they ended the lich. It turned out the cell was based in La Grange, and they offered him a place to stay there among their ranks. He accepted, believing it would be best to be missed than risk getting his friends and family involved (he doesn\u2019t know his father practiced magic, he just knew magic existed).<br /> <br /> So he was a Hunter for a few years, taking on the name Garrick Royce as a code name. He utilized his magic sensitivity to take out those who practiced the forbidden arts. Most of them were gutter mages, and of the few that were Awakened, were usually troublesome rogue mages, Banishers, Scelesti, and the like. Oftentimes, he was used as an unwitting pawn by the Orders to take them out. However...<br /> <br /> <i>Awakening</i> - It all started with a dream. He saw a tall, thin, pitch-black shape jut from the distance. It birthed a light brighter than a thousand suns, frightening his eyes away to hide in his eyelids. He woke up to find the morning sun shining in his eyes. Later that day, he was in a populated cafe when he began to hear voices in his head. Worse, he could sense magic...coming from him. He was reading the thoughts of the ones around him. The message of his dream was clear: Magic had come for him.<br /> <br /> Every day since brought with it another incident. He read invisible words in between the inked ones in his book, he felt the ebb and flow of various energies against him as he walked down the street, his heart broke in the same manner as some stranger who had lost a loved one. Each night came with the same dream. The landscape always varied from windy plains, to thundering storms, to a calm sunset, but the event was always the same. The tower shone its light, blinding him. The only difference was that it got closer and closer every time.<br /> <br /> He refused the tower\u2019s call. Pushing the daily events to the back of his mind, and shouting defiance at the tower even as it blinded him. He would not have magic claim him, he would fight it to his last breath. And he would fight alone, he couldn\u2019t bring the others into this. He fought for as long as he could, but the magic pursued still.<br /> <br /> It all came to a head during the tragic hunt that took his comrades\u2019 lives. The dream collided with the waking world. The tower, now right in front of him, stood over reality along with a dragon who guarded the entrance. He cried rebellion against tower and dragon. The dragon responded by burning him alive. Dead for a time in Fallen reality, his comrades mourned his loss, which was cut short by the ending of their own lives.<br /> <br /> He revived in the middle of the tower itself. His stalwart opposition to magic proved his resolve to the Obrimos Watchtower. He wept at the irony, then the Watchtower poured truth into his soul: Magic is a pure force. It did not corrupt those who wielded it for evil ends, they corrupted themselves. Magic could just as easily inspire and enrich lives. That understanding gave him a pen with which to write his name on sacred pages. Now, he understood. Now, he accepted.<br /> <br /> Now. he Awakened.<br /> <br /> <i>Awakened</i> - Only a week has passed since that fateful day, the loss still fresh on his psyche. So far, he's managed to drown his grief in exercises, training, and teaching, but he knows that will only last for so long...<br /> <br /> <u><b>Personality</b></u><br /> Phoenix is very much a what-you-see-is-what-you-get type of person. He never wore a mask and probably will never fully understand why some people do that. He was also never one to take anyone's bullshit, no matter how much authority they had. If he feels like punching you in the face for making some snark, well, expect to have a fist in your face then. He's not stupid, though. Experience has taught him that punching authority figures results in lots of trouble. That doesn't mean he'll take things lying down, he'll just counter in a way that gives him less trouble.<br /> <br /> A lover of mythology, quite a bit of his free time is spent in the local library with his nose in a book. His Awakened perspective has not only enhanced his appreciation for the classics, but it's also given him some unique insight into the world. The tale is what's real, not the tired laws of science. He is the Hero of his own story, as is everyone else to theirs. While this perspective does give him a rare degree of compassion, seeing everyone as necessary to fill out their own roles in the world, it does tend to make his thinking rigid. He might make assumptions about how one's story is supposed to go, or certain possibilities about what could happen won't enter his mind.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Daily Life</b></u><br /> Phoenix works as a martial arts teacher at the local dojo (many students who have watched a little too much anime have taken to calling him Royce-sensei). This was very practical as a former Hunter, as it helped pay the bills and he spent his down time training and keeping in shape, not to mention it was one of the things he was good at. The leader of his cell owned the house he lives in. With them gone, their next of kin decided to let him have the house, seeing as he was a good friend to the previous owner and had a job. Unfortunately, the bills are a bit too big for his income to handle all alone, so he\u2019s looking for some roommates.</div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Status</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Health:</b> 0000000<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5/5<br /> <b>Mana:</b> 10/10<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 7<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Guilty<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> None<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Experience Log</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Beats:</b> 0/5<br /> <b>Experiences (Unspent/Total):</b> 0/0<br /> <b>Arcane Beats:</b> 0/5<br /> <b>Arcane Experiences (Unspent/Total):</b> 0/0<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dots Purchased - XP Cost</b></u><ul><li>[insert dots purchased]</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 07-03-2016, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T08:31:57-07:00","id":922647,"title":"","content":"Caladriu could Michael know your character through playing chess please. He has been known to play from time to time. Nothing more though he is straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T10:36:05-07:00","id":922717,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that works! Chess buddies it is. I wonder who wins a game when both players have Fate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T10:45:10-07:00","id":922724,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - I find the idea of your character very, very cool. I've always thought it would be really interesting to roleplay a Hunter who went through a transformation to become something like a Kindred, Uratha, or Mage. The character background and description of his Awakening are both very fleshed out and rich. Great details and interesting ideas.<br /> <br /> One reaction I had while reading your submission, similar to Moonstone's, is that your character is not necessarily going to have automatic access as a newly-Awakened mage to <i>accurate</i>, helpful, IC knowledge about magic-related issues. I've been a player in other campaigns with players who argued that they should have bonuses to certain checks or de facto knowledge about certain topics because of how they constructed their back stories. While I can definitely appreciate the ability to pull in plot hooks and use that well-crafted backstory in my story as a ST, I would ask you to have that knowledge represented in experience points through Merits or Skills in some way (e.g., Occult dots/specialties related to Awakened society or magical creatures). It's all too easy for Hunters to <i>think</i> that they know about what it was they're up against, but that information can be inaccurate or completely misguided, too.<br /> <br /> The other thing I want to be transparent about, and this applies to everyone, is that I'm still learning the Mage 2E rules and I'm a relatively less experienced Storyteller. I am really excited about running this game, and I will do everything I can to make it interesting and well-written on my part -- and I absolutely encourage people to let me know as we go how they think I'm doing, for better or worse. But there's a possibility I'll make a bunch of mistakes, and I don't want to let you down because I don't fulfill the hopes you have for a long-term character like that. Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> Please let me know what you think about my comments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T10:48:52-07:00","id":922726,"title":"","content":"This would be my first time playing 2E mage too, so am hoping you're patient with my mistakes too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:17:35-07:00","id":922743,"title":"","content":"Understood! I'm more than happy to gate knowledge behind an Int+Occult or Politics roll where each success yields a rumor about some specific phenomenon we're dealing with, or something along those lines. I'd rather be helpfully spouting the information you want to make available to the party than spoiling surprises and making the strange and exotic seem familiar and boring.<br /> <br /> There's definitely part of me that wants to make use of all those misspent years reading Mage books, but I fully sympathize with wanting to keep your game world under your control as an ST, so to speak. I'll play with the approach that &quot;the world consists of the stuff that the ST describes, don't assume other things exist until they're on-screen.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:55:53-07:00","id":922761,"title":"","content":"I hope this submission is better (it's still kinda short, though):<br /> <br /> <b>1. Concept</b>: Cryptid Hunter.<br /> (May need adjustment depending on where Mystagogues fall between &quot;use all beings as tools&quot; and &quot;it doesn't matter if you're human or youkai&quot;)<br /> Phillip Pittman was always fascinated by the unknown. He certainly was more fascinated by things that go bump in the night than by his job as a dietician. His determination to capture a cryptid (on camera or otherwise) pushed him to comb forests around the supposed sightings alone.<br /> <b>2. Awakening</b>: Thyrsus<br /> On one of his searches, he got lost in the woods. High from deprivation, he went further on the trail. Somewhere along the way, the trees began to grow to gigantic size. Finally, he encountered an impressive creature (details tbd) and stalked it. Even as it eluded his grasp, he Awakened, beholding the majesty of the Primal Wilds. (Could make the hunt successful, with a primitive spear)<br /> <b>3. Prefered style</b>:<br /> The gamestyle should focus mostly on Mysteries and adventure, preferably Bio-Archaeomancy. Player (me) is interested in being the most awesome scolar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:57:26-07:00","id":922762,"title":"","content":"Love the character ideas. Wish there was room for another. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:04:24-07:00","id":922766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href