o\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Death</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Forces</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Life</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><i>Matter</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><b>Mind</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Prime</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><b>Space</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Spirit</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Time</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb\u25cb</td> </tr> </table></div> <b><u>Advantages</u></b></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Gnosis: 1<br /> Wisdom: 7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Ritual Interval: 3 hours<br /> Yantras: 2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Mana: 10 Max, 1/turn<br /> Obsessions: 1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Speed: 9<br /> Initiative: +6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Defense: 3 (+2/3)<br /> Armor: 0</td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><u><b>Merits</b></u><br /> Resources 3<br /> Shadow Name 1<br /> Library (Occult) 1<br /> Library (Academics) 1<br /> Safe Place 1<br /> Sanctum 1<br /> True Friend 3 (Daisy)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><u><b>Praxes</b></u><br /> Read the Depths (Mind 3)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><br /> Enhance Skill (3 Reach, Academics 3)<br /> Scrying (4 Reach, Occult 3)<br /> Exorcist's Eye (5 Reach, Occult 3)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b><u>Attainments</u></b><br /> Counterspell (Space, Mind, Spirit)<br /> Mind's Eye<br /> Sympathetic Range<br /> Mage Armor (Space, Mind)<br /> Targeted Summoning (Mind)</td> </tr> </table></div> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Long-Term</i> - Sudden occult obsessions and dramatic revelation, being lost, places turning in on themselves<br /> <br /> <i>Immediate</i> - A dark fog with red eyes peering out; causes a feeling of dread.<br /> <br /> <i>Signature</i> - A smoky residue and a feeling like melted wax<br /> <br /> <i>Tilt</i> - Composure -1<br /> <br /> <u><b>Aspirations</b></u><ul><li>Be inducted into an order.</li> <li>Encounter a Goetia</li> <li>Long term: Keep magic a secret from his family.</li> <li><b>Obsession: </b>Find a cure for the Sleeping Curse.</li> </ul><u><b>Equipment</b></u><ul><li>Brass Knife (0L, -1 Init, Size 1; Dedicated Tool, -2 Paradox)</li> <li>Smartphone (+2, Dur 2, Size 1, Struct 1, Avail 3)</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Details</b></span></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u><b>General</b></u><br /> <b>Age/Birthday:</b> 34<br /> <b>Gender:</b> Male<br /> <b>Height:</b> ?<br /> <b>Build:</b> Average<br /> <b>Occupation:</b> Bookstore Owner/Inheritor<br /> <b>Ethnicity:</b> White<br /> <b>Nationality:</b> American<br /> <b>Hair Color:</b> Brown<br /> <b>Eye Color:</b> Blue<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Heterosexual<br /> <br /> <b><u>Background</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>1. Character concept/archetype: </b>Small bookstore owner with the perfect suburban life.<br /> <br /> Success is funny. It can build up in a family line, creating conditions that make success more and more likely. Building up a wealth that doesn\u2019t provide excess so much as it allows freedom from financial woes. But that kind of comfort can inhibit success, too. When Marlin followed his brother and sister into college, he didn\u2019t come out a doctor or a lawyer (like they did, respectively), he barely scraped through. Not because he got bad grades, or didn\u2019t take enough classes, but because swapping majors 5 times in 3 years isn\u2019t exactly an optimal path. Marlin was simply interested in everything. Eventually his counselor got him to stick to his half-finished lit degree, just so he would graduate with something.<br /> <br /> Not that a degree really mattered to Marlin. He knew that with careful management, the family trust would put him through life at an acceptable level of comfort. No, what he got out of college was Daisy. They married shortly after graduation, then he got a job as a paper pusher to put her through library school. She got a real job (at the Chicago Public) and he dropped his. He opened a small bookstore for something to do. They moved to the suburbs and had a son.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Awakening:</b><br /> <br /> For the past couple years, Marlin gradually became interested in the occult. At first as a curiosity, then as an affectation. He kept occult books in a back room, locked it up, and told spooky stories to customers. His growing fascination with the culture surrounding magic only grew as he attracted more of that type to the store, though he certainly didn\u2019t believe. He conceived of performing a ritual of sorts, inviting select customers, making an event of it. \u201cIt\u2019s like performance art,\u201d he said to himself. He didn\u2019t tell Daisy; she wasn\u2019t interested in or as comfortable with this stuff.<br /> <br /> Marlin prepared for a trial run. He didn\u2019t want to disappoint anyone when performing the ritual for real. He got the silver candlesticks, the ritual robes, drew a pentagram on the floor of the store\u2019s upstairs room. He read from the book, performed the ritual gestures, and enjoyed himself immensely. Until the demon appeared.<br /> <br /> The room filled with dark fog. Red eyes peered out from the shadows. Marlin dropped the book, staggered back.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou dare disturb me, mortal?\u201d Its voice was hostile and corrosive. \u201cYou meddle with things you do not understand! I should destroy you for your offensive ignorance!\u201d<br /> <br /> Marlin swallowed, reeling with fear and revelation. \u201cI-I-\u201c<br /> <br /> The demon sneered, and Marlin felt clawed hands grasp at his limbs.<br /> <br /> \u201cI-If my ignorance is so offensive, then teach me! Help me to understand!\u201d<br /> <br /> The demon roared with gales of laughter. \u201cWith pleasure!\u201d The fog retreated into the summoning circle, and pulled Marlin with.<br /> <br /> In the Iron Gauntlet, Marlin was forced to confront his flaws. His complacency, his lack of direction, and despite all his knowledge, his lack of understanding. Despite that, when all was done, he mounted the stairs of the Watchtower and signed his name. When he awoke, the candles were out. And the book was gone.<br /> <br /> Since then, Marlin has been struggling to balance the family man with the warlock. He uses Mind magic to stay awake and sneak out at night, and has been leaving the shop closed more days. Despite his efforts, Daisy has noticed him growing distant. He\u2019s terrified that one day he might decide that using magic on the people he\u2019s closest to is acceptable.<br /> <br /> (<b>Notes:</b> The son\u2019s name is Forest, and he\u2019s 7. The store is called Marlin\u2019s Books and the logo is of a swordfish. Marlin\u2019s shadow name is Binder. It\u2019s up to the ST as to whether he actually got his hands on a magic book that let him summon a Wraith or if it was just a figment of his Awakening!)<br /> <br /> <b>Spellcasting template</b><br /> Casting <i>Spell Name</i> (Arcana X)<br /> X Reach free: Spending X on ...<br /> Spending Mana<br /> Containing/Releasing (paradox) vs (wisdom)<br /> <br /> Yantras: (Yantra) X, ...<br /> Factors: Potency X, Duration X, ... (focus on important ones)<br /> Spellcasting roll: (spellcasting)<br /> <br /> <br /> Trait X + Trait X + X (modifier) = (dice) -&gt; (success, link)</div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Status</b></span></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Health:</b> <b>L</b>OOOOOO<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 3/7<br /> <b>Mana:</b> 9/10<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> [Shaken (Arcane)]<br /> <b>Tilts:</b> None<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Experience Log</b></span></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Beats:</b> 1/5<br /> <b>Experiences (Unspent/Total):</b> 0/1<br /> <b>Arcane Beats:</b> 2/5<br /> <b>Arcane Experiences (Unspent/Total):</b> 1/1<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dots Purchased - XP Cost</b></u><ul><li>Sanctum 1 - 1</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 12-30-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:01:41-07:00","id":923254,"title":"","content":"Here are some thoughts I received via PM from the player of Lynx, who is still waiting on forum activation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are just preliminary thoughts. Also, there's definitely going to be a LGBT theme in this campaign, I can feel that...<br /> <br /> LGBT: Oscar is bisexual. He never really thought about his sexuality, but he's a curious fella. Not much for the partying scene, though, maybe bear scene? He isn't reserved. Might end up promiscuous (though let's not get too detailed about that). Considering the potential cast, it's a natural fit. That, and Thyrsus. Primal. Passionate. Yeah... Of course, the LGBT is the easy way.<br /> <br /> RAGNAR: LGBT, as mentioned above. The Literature bit could also work, as Oscar does like books.<br /> <br /> MOONSTONE: Again, LGBT.<br /> <br /> DR. ASPHODEL / Vo: Student / college / university scene, perhaps? I don't know if Oscar attends the University of Chicago, but there's always the LGBT angle...<br /> <br /> LITERATURE: Oscar likes (or liked, rather) to read in his youth \u2013 his passion faded away after the forest incident, but after having Awakened, he spends about an hour every evening catching up on fiction and fantasy (after he's half-arsed his way through studies, of course).<br /> <br /> Michael Korn: Best-selling sci-fi/fantasy author, you say? I think fanboyish glee might be the immediate reaction if Oscar recognises Michael, being a fan of his books. They might also live in the same neighbourhood, which would certainly help.<br /> <br /> PHOENIX: Martial Arts is the easy link. Oscar always wanted to learn martial arts during his time, but his town had a distinct lack of practitioners and teachers. There's also the shared love of literature. Bunch of potential links here. (Also, fun fact, I ran a campaign once where I had an Obrimos named Phoenix who was a Tamer of Fire. That campaign was... special.)<br /> <br /> BARDO: Oscar is a life mage, but he'd still respect a doctor's opinion, so there's a possibility there.<br /> <br /> I think he's conflicted about the whole necromancer aspect. He already knows the dead hold no spirits (though he doesn't really know about ghosts...) so to him, death is a part of nature - on the other hand, one shouldn't really cheat death, you know? He can't really explain it. Depends if he'd be the right doctor for it, really.<br /> <br /> SPIDER / Sara: This one stumps me a bit. I don't think Oscar would dislike her, but I don't know how they'd have met. Maybe through college? Or maybe they've chatted online or frequented the same forums in the last two years?<br /> <br /> Philip Pittman: Mysterium acolytes together, I guess? </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely noticing that in the last few days, more and more players are adding or updating character backgrounds to make themselves part of the LGBT community. I am in full support of the LGBT community and view myself as an ally for people who identify as LGBT. I also want to be clear that you don't need to make your character gay/bisexual, etc. to fit in with the other characters. I want to ask...are people feeling pressured to add this to increase their chances of being picked? Or did recent conversation or other players' ideas pique your interest in exploring this with your character?<br /> <br /> This is a conversation we can discuss more at length once characters are selected.<br /> <br /> Also, to clarify: I would like you to have ties to at least <b>one other</b> PC. You don't have to be related to <i>all</i> of them. My hope is that the process of these mages coming together and forming a cabal will be more natural if the characters have ties, even loose ties, to each other prior to their Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:26:29-07:00","id":923269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923254#post923254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm definitely noticing that in the last few days, more and more players are adding or updating character backgrounds to make themselves part of the LGBT community. I am in full support of the LGBT community and view myself as an ally for people who identify as LGBT. I also want to be clear that you don't need to make your character gay/bisexual, etc. to fit in with the other characters. I want to ask...are people feeling pressured to add this to increase their chances of being picked? Or did recent conversation or other players' ideas pique your interest in exploring this with your character?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that wasn't my intention. I didn't take a look at anybody else's submissions because I didn't want to be influenced by them. I normally give my characters an aspect of myself, because I've found that it helps me get invested in them- I've tried creating characters who shared nothing in common with myself, and I had trouble getting in the mindset of the character. Since I've never previously played a character who shared my sexuality, I figure &quot;why not&quot;. It was only after I submitted Ragnar's concept that I noticed that both Vo and Moonstone were LGBT as well. <br /> <br /> An all-LGBT cabal could make for an interesting Chronicle, but I would welcome straight characters just as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:57:48-07:00","id":923318,"title":"","content":"Effin' finally. Account verified at last. Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Valewood here. Thanks to rwknoll for relaying my character concept and potential character links.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:03:01-07:00","id":923325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923318#post923318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Effin' finally. Account verified at last. Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Valewood here. Thanks to rwknoll for relaying my character concept and potential character links.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesss. Finally! So glad everything worked out.<br /> <br /> When you have the chance, please create your own submission post so I can perma-link it to the thread's OP. That way you can make any changes, etc. and I'll be able to find it more easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:03:46-07:00","id":923326,"title":"","content":"I would say I don't feel pressured or anything, but I also noticed the theme of so many LGBT characters and I do think it had an impact on my decision to make Sara bisexual. I'm equally content for her to be heterosexual or another sexuality, but none of those options bother me at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:10:42-07:00","id":923336,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> Glad to hear your input on this topic. As long as you're happy with it and don't feel pressured, I think it's great. It's about consent for me. I just want to make sure everyone feels they can design and play their character in the way that they prefer, within the rules and guidelines we agree upon as a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:17:46-07:00","id":923340,"title":"","content":"Finally can post! <br /> <br /> Anyway here's my character's Acanthus Awakening, crunch to come soon(TM): <br /> <br /> <i>For the past twenty one years, James' life had been mundane to say the least. Wake up, go to school, come home, sleep. Wake up, go to school, come home, sleep. The same song every single day, with only slight variations in the tune. Once he got a job he thought he would finally get out of this rut but life was not to be so. It then became wake up, go to work, come home, sleep. The lyrics changed but the song remained the same.<br /> <br /> But even rivers eventually are redirected by an impediment and thus change their millennia long course. So too was it for James and his lifelong rut on one fateful day when the boss brought in a new painting for his office. It was an ugly painting all things considered, and he couldn't have spent more than half a grand on it but nevertheless it was the talk of the office for a week. But one by one James' coworkers lost interest and went back to their daily grind. But James couldn't get the painting out of his head, not matter how best he tried. He lay awake at night thinking of its rough contours, its pale hue, and its damnable blue eyes. <br /> <br /> Just by its appearance had James' song been altered, now it was go to work, watch the painting, come home and repeat. Over the coming weeks he became gradually more haggard and only for a few minutes would he allow himself sleep. Even in his dreams had been infected by the painting, as he drifted through short slivers of sleep he was enveloped by the painting. Its silver-painted frame glistened in the void of his slumber and sung to him. It promised him all would be right, if only he would free it from his philistine boss. <br /> <br /> Eventually even his coworkers noticed his quickly slipping sanity, his tirelessness showing in every facet of his life, and began to drift away from him. But he didn't care, no soon he would have the painting. Yes he had come to that conclusion last night amid a short and restless slumber. Tonight, he would be the last to leave and when all others were gone he would free the painting. Time crawled and James could feel everyones eyes on him. They knew, they all knew! If only the clock were to go more quickly, then he could just free the painting and run away from this grey rut. <br /> <br /> Finally the hour had come and James was the last person in the office. He slowly moved towards his boss' office, the clicks of his shoes against the concrete continually echoed through the building filling him with heart-stopping fear. He would be found, of course he would, but it didn't matter now. All that mattered was the painting, he needed it, he must have it in his hands. And so he trudged forward, heedless of the sound of his feet slamming into the concrete floor. <br /> <br /> As he creeped into his boss' office, his heart was filled with joy. There it was, with the moonlight softly falling upon it and illuminating its pale blue eyes. His hands hovered over the painting for a moment, almost worshiping its grotesque form but a moment was all that remained between him and his prize. In an instant he finally held it and swiftly retreated to adorn his meager abode with his prize. That night was pure bliss and such a high unknown to even the most prolific of junkies.<br /> <br /> But like all highs, so too comes the following low. The next day his boss was furious, demanding however stole his painting return it immediately or they would be prosecuted to the full extent of the law. One by one his coworkers were interrogated, and with each name called, James' heart beat a furious drum solo. By some stroke of luck, the day ended before his name could be called. In a frantic flight, James returned to his home. He stared at the painting with hate in his eyes. It was all its fault his life was ruined, it had done this to him. James vision filled with red and when it cleared, he saw the painting in shambles. Its silver limbs splayed across his apartment while its soft hide was ripped into a billion pieces. Yet still its eyes gazed as him, imploring his mind to continue to look upon it in its malefic glory. James broke down and when he woke, the sun had rose and his cheeks stained by tears.<br /> <br /> As he strode to work, he felt as if he were a prisoner on Death Row coming to meet his chair. Today would be the end of him, he knew it. As he reached work, he tried to fall back into his rut but found he could not, his mind still filled with visions of the painting and its army of ugly blue eyes. Eventually his name was called and he felt his blood turn cold. Slowly he began the walk to his doom, his steps mirroring those he made on that fateful night. <br /> <br /> As he passed the boundary into his boss' office though, he found that was not where he was. Instead he found himself in a eerie world, silent and yet deafening in equal measure. Movement moved like quicksilver but also left afterimages of the movement, time struggling to keep up with sight. He found himself of a glass road fenced in by a hedge of thorn made of silver. Seeing a large figure in the distance, he knew his destination and began moving forward along the path. Gradually more colors joined the the silver fence, blue and white joined in equal measure with black began to paint the barrier and as he got closer to his destination he saw wood join the metallic hedge.<br /> <br /> At last he reached his destination, a towering figure whose wicked eyes had haunted him for far too long. He became enraged at its sight and, looking to strike it once again, found a glass dagger with which to stab at it. He carved into the tower his name, announcing he finally rejected the painting. It no longer held sway over him, nor would a rut ever again confine him to such a sorry fate. This he swore with his name, this and more. Upon leaving that strange place, he clothed himself in the name Zosimus, for he found its tune flowed more sweetly and true. </i><br /> <br /> EDIT: Can someone tell me how to insert a custom image for my avatar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","user":"ChaosArchon","date":". 06-29-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:27:09-07:00","id":923346,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I know you said overlap isn't an issue, but since we've got like 4 acanthus and 0 mastigos, I could rework Moonstone as mastigos. That path would really suit him and the trigger for his Awakening just as well, and I was planning to get Mind anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:29:01-07:00","id":923350,"title":"","content":"Given the high volume of submissions I've received, I'm going to call it and say that I will <b>not</b> be accepting any new submissions at this time.<br /> <br /> I will plan to review the list further and post here with an update tomorrow at the latest with my final thoughts and decision about the characters. I really appreciate everyone taking the time to create thoughtful, fleshed-out characters. I hope you enjoyed the process and will forgive me for asking you to do this if I don't end up picking your character. I have some hard decisions to make because of the overall quality of these posts!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12044_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12044\" data-vbnamecard=\"12044\">ChaosArchon</a> - Go to your user profile on a PC, hover your mouse over the user avatar, and click &quot;Edit Avatar.&quot; Not sure how to do it on mobile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:31:32-07:00","id":923352,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><