-serif\"><i>Immediate</i> - Totemic aspects of Lynx's magic manifest on or around him and envelop the area, e.g., his shadow appears a bear, or he looks an appropriate anthropomorphic animal; a person's nature or personality manifests as an appropriate odour, e.g., someone deceitful smells foul, somebody tranquil smells like still water.<br /> <br /> <i>Known totems</i> - Bear for healing. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i>Signature</i> - Remnants of fur and/or his distinct Supernal odour.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i>Tilt</i> \u2013 His empowered primal charisma splashes onto those nearby, resulting in a +1 bonus on Presence rolls. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Aspirations</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Get to know a Thyrsus. (short)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Join an Order. (short)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Get to know a werewolf. (long)</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Obsessions</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Look for the Great Lynx from his Awakening.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Equipment</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">First-Aid Kit (Bonus +1, Durability 1, Size 2, Structure 3, Availability 2)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Personal Computer (Bonus +2, Durability 2, Size 3, Structure 2, Availability 2)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Smartphone (Bonus +1, Durability 2, Size 1, Structure 1, Availability 2)</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Yantras &amp; Tools</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">&lt;Leatherbound Book (Order Tool)&gt;: </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Copper Cup (Path Tool): Healing spells, sharing spells. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Silver Lynx Pendant (Dedicated): Dedicated tool only. Maybe cleansing. </span></span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Details</b></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>General</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Age/Birthday:</b> 21; 05/05/95</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Gender:</b> Male</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Height:</b> 5' 9&quot;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Build:</b> Bear-ish</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Occupation:</b> Student</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Ethnicity:</b> Caucasian</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Nationality:</b> Norwegian</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Hair Colour:</b> Dark, cropped</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Eye Colour:</b> Blue-grey</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Beard:</b> Scruffy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Sexuality:</b> Bisexual</span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://pre12.deviantart.net/504d/th/pre/f/2011/140/c/4/c499566b350ce498c49aef132fc404ea-d3grr1d.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Picture.</a> (He looks something like this, at least. Closest thing I could find.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b><u>Background</u></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i>Childhood &amp; Adolescence</i> - Oscar was born in Norway, Europe. His father was a marine biologist, his mother a lawyer. His upbringing was simple enough. His parents were engrossed in their careers, so he was often left to his own devices; as a child, this involved after-school activities, television shows, books and video games, the earlier years spent with a baby sitter; as an adolescent, it involved staunch rebellion, and the lack of attention had him run away from home at the age of 17.<br /> <br /> By ran away, of course, we mean he ran to the nearest forest of considerable size and got lost.<br /> <br /> He wandered between trees and up hills, and eventually found himself atop the regional mountain range. At first, he thought nothing of it. Woods and lakes joined with foliage, moss lingered where the shade lay. It was when the mist settled that he felt it \u2013 the jolt of fear. The wild had its aural environment, of course, but in the mist, it grew more prominent. He started seeing shadows skulking about, felt eyes on him where there were none. Yet the fear was not unwanted \u2013 it was an exhilaration. As the tension rose, he saw the greatest shadow yet before him, its eyes set on him like predator hunting prey. In spite of the thrill, Oscar ran away then \u2013 his metaphorical tail between his legs.<br /> <br /> He returned home the next morning. His parents chalked his absence to \u201cjust teenage things.\u201d<br /> <br /> The event had Oscar filled with longing, an ache he couldn't quite put his finger on. It felt like a second world existed, somewhere just out of sight. His parents and peers dismissed his thoughts and ideas whenever he brought this up, and with that, he found only solace in solitude. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i>Awakening</i> - His Mystery Play had begun in the forest, but it was slow and subtle. The Supernal had trickled into his life, little by little, strengthening his sense to the \u201csecond world\u201d, but as the repeated dismissal of his experiences by those he deemed closest to him, the trickle slowed down to a halt. At last, he felt empty.<br /> It was merely the interlude to the events of his 22st year.<br /> <br /> By the time Oscar was 21, his daily life was not particularly productive. Sure, he stayed in shape with frequent trips up the mountains in hopes of recapturing that feeling; he practised a little bit of art and drawing to try to remember what he had seen and felt.. He held a couple of part-time jobs, though he half-arsed his way through those without exceptional results. His academic ambitions weren't anything to brag about either. He tried to maintain some spiritualistic aspect in his life \u2013 but the emptiness had crawled into the entirety of his being. Nothing he did mattered.<br /> <br /> One day, though, he woke up, having had a dream that he couldn't truly explain \u2013 a dream so familiar it stirred a sense of wanderlust. During one of the rare moments his family was all gathered for breakfast, he mentioned he'd like to study abroad. Though surprised, both parents were in favour, offering to pay his tuition and rent \u2013 on the condition that he later produce results. They stated the experience would serve him well. He applied to a variety of schools all around the states, landing a college close to La Grange.<br /> <br /> The dam that kept the Supernal truth at bay burst when he landed on US soil. What would've been a simple bus trip from the airport to his apartment in La Grange became a dangerous trek through the Primal Wild. It was an encore of the fear and longing that had overwhelmed him four years ago, only this time he did not freeze when the mist washed over him, nor did he flee when he came face to face with the large and advancing shadow. When they stood face to face, he saw the shadow for what it was: the great Lynx. Without thinking Oscar embraced it as an old friend that he had known for his entire life. He embraced the Wild. He became the Lynx. The Lynx became him. At last, he was Truth. At last, he truly felt </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>alive.</b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i>Awakened</i> - [insert history since Awakening]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Personality and Daily Life</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Though Lynx often puts on the smile \u2013 and usually he means it \u2013 he is ruled by emotion and instinct. He can be calm and (rarely) prudent, but he prefers to let loose whenever possible. He'll exclaim excitement if the situation calls for it, he'll laugh without abandon, and he doesn't care about modesty when it comes to the human body. He doesn't hide himself, and he doesn't like lying either \u2013 whatever his mood, he is easy to read. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">He isn't confrontational by nature, but he is quick to judge \u2013 he measures people by how they treat their tools, their pets, their equals and lessers, and the world around them. Regardless of how he judges others, his opinion is rarely set in stone. Dislike is met with avoidance \u2013 why deal with something if you don't like it? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Lynx struggles to express himself. To him, the truth's with his gut feeling \u2013 and he can rarely justify it further than that. Then again, he was never great at analysis. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Having a lawyer and marine biologist as parents has left Lynx with an understanding of multiple topics. Many of his hobbies \u2013 none of them truly enjoyed during his darker days \u2013 are emerging again. He reads \u2013 mostly fiction \u2013 and doodles; he'll wander around the suburbs and hike through whatever woods can be found. He can find enjoyment laying spread eagle on grass, staring at the sky. The local communities have him fascinated, and he'll mingle every now and again. He visits the zoo at least once a week. H usually studies with his study group, though sometimes he prefers to do it alone, usually at the library. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Other notes</b></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">His relationship to his parents is strained. They focused more on furthering their own careers, rather than family life. They weren't really there for him - sure, they had vacations and the occasional family outing, fancy dinner at restaurant, and he does love them, but there's a definite distance between them. In many ways, Oscar fears he was a mistake in their carefully planned life, and sometimes it seems like they would love nothing more than to tell him that. They do care, though, as they had no hesitation to let him study abroad while paying for his tuition and rent. He might have a sibling or two. Currently undecided.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Character links (still WIP)</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>LGBT:</b> Oscar is bisexual. He never really thought about his sexuality, but he's a curious fella. He's also a bona fide virgin. Not much for the partying scene, though, maybe bear scene? He isn't reserved, but he probably will wait for the right person for his first go. Might end up promiscuous (though let's not get too detailed about that). Considering the potential cast, it's a natural fit. That, and Thyrsus. Primal. Passionate. Yeah... LGBT is an easy link.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>LITERATURE:</b> Oscar likes (or liked, rather) to read in his youth \u2013 his passion faded away after the forest incident. After having Awakened, though, he now spends about an hour every evening catching up on fiction and fantasy (after he's half-arsed his way through studies, of course). It wouldn't be out of place for him to spend some time at the library either.</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>WILDLIFE:</b> </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Zoos. Parks. Forests. He's a Thyrsus. When he isn't studying or reading, he's exploring. He'll wander neighbourhoods, he'll check out streets and bars, shops and what have you, but most of all, he'll check out places where animals frequent. Bonding with somebody who'll do a morning jog through some forest trails or the park is a possibility.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Individual characters:</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>RAGNAR: </b>I believe we agreed on University as the primary link. LGBT study group, and Ragnar is the TA to Vo's FYS class. Probably the closest bond. Lynx might be studying Comparative Literature, strengthening that bond even further. All subject to Ragnar/Haberdasher's approval, obviously.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>MOONSTONE: </b>There's no predetermined link. If they met, LGBT scene? I can't think of anything else.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>DR. ASPHODEL / Vo: </b>Participant in her FYS class. At U of Chicago.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>PHOENIX: </b>No predetermined link yet. Dojo, library, LGBT scene, Binder's bookstore...</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>BINDER / Marlin: </b>As MagicSwordsman suggested, Lynx probably has visited his bookstore, or they've met at the library. </span></span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Status</b></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px