ar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":".  Unlocked High Speech. 12-18-2016, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:45:14-07:00","id":923358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923346#post923346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I know you said overlap isn't an issue, but since we've got like 4 acanthus and 0 mastigos, I could rework Moonstone as mastigos. That path would really suit him and the trigger for his Awakening just as well, and I was planning to get Mind anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I read through his Awakening, I was sure he'd end up as a Mastigos myself. It would be a good fit, I agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:47:04-07:00","id":923359,"title":"","content":"So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> if this seems familiar, it's b/c im c+p this from GitP so others can see it :P<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">So my only making an Awakening is actually kind of a thematic choice. To James, the before doesn't matter as much. He doesn't hold any ties to his former life, why should it when it was a rut which tied him down to one destiny. His Awakening is, ultimately him saying that he was the master of his own ship, captain of his own soul. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">That being said I can create a backstory if you want. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As for what happened post Awakening, another twist of fate this one a deliberate action on Zosimus' part. Just as he walked into his boss' office, wouldn't you know it, but the artist of the painting herself came to the office. She apparently had received the wrong address for an appointment. His boss, actually a genuine fan of art, recognized her and Zosimus was quickly dismissed. Does that sound contrived? It should, Fate is fun that way :P</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Anyway a week later, once the hunt for the painting had died down, James Wells his job. Now Zosimus makes a living day trading, using his Awakened gifts for sustinace. After all, a starving Mage is no help to anyone. He tried to obscure his talents, occasionally buying a stock which would lose him money and he ensures he never makes too much, but eventually he was discovered none the less. Approached by a masked man, the figure offered him a job. The masked man was growing old and wanted to train an apprentice. And so it was that Zosimus joined the Guardians of the Veil, on the path to become an Interfector, after all who better to investigate the past than a man who had rejected his own.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As for ways for other characters to meet him, I'll take a leaf out of Beans book and say,</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Local Consilium</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: As his mentor is an Interfector, Zosimus spends alot of time in Consilia chambers and meetings learning after his mentor. Furthermore given how Interfectors cover a broader area generally a whole Cacus or Convocation, it explains why Zosimus is in Chicago now rather than Detriot (I figure they are close enough that being in the same GotV Cacus is feasible)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Library</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: While he has access to his mentors collection of tomes, their variety is..</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Limited. Thus Zosimus regularly visits the local libraries to brush up on ancient mythic symbolism as well as occult traditions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Starbucks</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: Starts every day off with it, even months after his Awakening, its affect on his sleep patterns is still felt and some days the caffine is the only thing keeping him standing.<br /> <br /> As for characters who Zosimus would know, I think its possible he knew our former Hunter friend. Perhaps his mentor had been training him by keeping tabs on him to make sure he didn't become a Banisher? Once he finally accepted magic, Zosimus revealed himself and the two became fast friends?<br /> <br /> <b>Preferred Game Style</b>: I would love a mix of intrigue, mystery, and occasional combat. My ideal chronicle would basically be a Dresden Files novel, I love the series and it just screams Mage to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: As for the LGBT trend, I love it! Zosimus is still in the process of discovering himself but I can definitely see him appreciating the beauty of both sides of the coin <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","user":"ChaosArchon","date":". 06-29-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:19:24-07:00","id":923377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923346#post923346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I know you said overlap isn't an issue, but since we've got like 4 acanthus and 0 mastigos, I could rework Moonstone as mastigos. That path would really suit him and the trigger for his Awakening just as well, and I was planning to get Mind anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'm totally cool with that. It's also something we can decide after the final party is selected. I'm deciding mostly based on character concepts and narrative write-ups first, and Path second. I'll consider you as Mastigos for now, but we can discuss further if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:28:22-07:00","id":923382,"title":"","content":"Good luck with the selection process!<br /> <br /> Everyone else, feel free to ask all sorts of questions about Lynx (or me) if you want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:28:41-07:00","id":923383,"title":"","content":"If it is of any help, the first thing I though about Linx was something similar to Phoenix, a kind of father figure. Bardo is very paternal despite (or due to) having no child, so he can develope that kind of relationship with almost any younger character given the circumstances. I think he is the oldest of the bunch at a 45-50 years old mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:29:09-07:00","id":923384,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> also, and this is likely much furthermore down the line, but I'm hoping to pick up Walkers in Mists as Zosimus' legacy as I think the concept is pretty damn cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T12:35:56-07:00","id":923419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=922990#post922990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> - I appreciate the added information. It's giving me a little more to go off of, but I still don't feel like I know much more about your character. What's he doing in Chicago? He can choose to make &quot;cryptid hunter&quot; an Obsession and focus of his Awakened life, but what else is there to him besides that? I can see the direction you'd like him to go in, but I'm asking instead for everything leading up to that point. The rest will come through roleplay and in-game experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...<br /> There's family, likely estranged by his (pre-Awakening) antics. There're hunting buddies (he's likely to grow distant, now - I expect his Sleeper life to gradually wash away, until only his job remains). There's his job as a dietician. His hobbies include country music - he's a (still mediocre) banjo player (Expression 1). He's a scolar first and a hunter second - not just in stats: his thrill for knowledge is stronger than his thrill for the hunt. He actually lives in La Grange - he recently returned from a trip to Enfield, where he Awakened. Favorite season is early autumn. Favorite color is green. Favored food - canned pork. Single. Had some unfulfilling swings with either sex. Feel free to involve any exes.<br /> Is this satisfactory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T12:56:18-07:00","id":923430,"title":"","content":"Vo's probably gone to bars and stuff before the divorce, so I'm sure she's at least seen her fellow queer mages there before. She could easily be teaching anyone who's taking physics classes, and people in the neighborhood could have seen her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T13:03:18-07:00","id":923433,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna keep my eyes on things, see if I make it in, and then do more about checking ties with other players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T16:18:55-07:00","id":923549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923254#post923254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm definitely noticing that in the last few days, more and more players are adding or updating character backgrounds to make themselves part of the LGBT community. I am in full support of the LGBT community and view myself as an ally for people who identify as LGBT. I also want to be clear that you don't need to make your character gay/bisexual, etc. to fit in with the other characters. I want to ask...are people feeling pressured to add this to increase their chances of being picked? Or did recent conversation or other players' ideas pique your interest in exploring this with your character?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, Phoenix is bi simply because I am. It's just the whole writer familiarity thing, nothing more. Though I must say I too am loving the idea of an all/near-all LGBT cabal. Makes sense when you think about it, especially if there's some straight Seers running around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T16:36:24-07:00","id":923562,"title":"","content":"I will fix my application tomorrow I had things to take care of today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T17:24:58-07:00","id":923581,"title":"","content":"Oooooook.<br /> <br /> After reviewing all of the submissions repeatedly today, and taking into consideration all of the info that everyone provided, I have a final list of characters I would like to invite to play in the game. I want to preface this by saying that there were SO many good submissions. This wasn't easy for me. Obviously I would rather give everyone the chance to play, but I just don't think it's feasible for a single cabal.<br /> <br /> Due to the strength and overall quality of these submissions, I decided to keep 6 players:<br /> 1. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> - Dr. Asphodel, Moros theoretical physicist<br /> 2. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Moonstone, Mastigos Sleepwalker-turned-mage<br /> 3. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - Lynx, Thyrsus animist/college student<br /> 4. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Phoenix, Obrimos Hunter-turned-mage<br /> 5. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - Ragnar, Acanthus Renaissance man<br /> 6. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Binder, Mastigos bookstore owner/family man<br /> <br /> Having a cabal of 6 PCs will potentially introduce some challenges for me as a ST, so I'll ask in advance again for your patience as I tackle that learning curve. However, it also means you can potentially split up during certain story points or scenes, which gives me some neat options for adding conflict to the game and offering unique roleplay opportunities.<br /> <br /> As long as the 6 of you are good with this final selection, I will post more tonight or tomorrow with info about what I'd like to do next to get the game up and running!<br /> <br /> To the other 5 players who submitted characters: I really enjoyed your submissions. Once this game gets underway, depending on how it goes and how much free time I have, I might be able to create a separate game for you and ST that one as well. Alternatively, if any of the active players from this game drop out or need to leave the game for whatever reason, I would be looking at this list next to see if anyone wants to join the full game. If anyone has further questions or concerns, please send me a private message.<br /> <br /> Really looking to getting the show on the road with this! Thank you to everyone for your patience. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:12:24-07:00","id":923601,"title":"","content":"Here are some additional ideas I had in mind while reviewing the PCs, now that the party has been selected:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - The rest of the party includes another Acanthus and another Mastigos. Consequently, I think you should pick whichever Path would be the most fun for you to play. Just let me know what you think before you start character creation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> - I would suggest that we say that Vo has been asked to teach the occasional &quot;first-year seminar&quot; kind of college class, one geared towards freshman and transfer students to help orient them to the college experience and to make sure they have at least basic knowledge of the academic skills expected of incoming freshmen. Vo may see this as a frustrating chore and waste of her academic skills, or maybe she loves teaching new students and stepping outside of her academic specialty.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - I think we should make Oscar a student at the University of Chicago. It makes a lot more sense to me that an international student would apply and go there. You can still live in La Grange and commute, just like Vo (if she in fact decides to continue pursuing her academic career after Awakening). And we can say that you took/are taking Vo's first-year seminar class, so you know her. The degree to which you know her, and how hard you would have worked during that class, would be up to you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - By having the rest of your Hunter cell suddenly die at the moment of your Awakening, we might be missing out on a really prime opportunity for plot hooks! I have 2 alternate suggestions for tweaking this. First, we could say that the other Hunters in your cell were all severely injured or maimed, mentally traumatized, <i>or</i> killed, but not all of them died. Or, I'd like you to add that your Hunter cell worked with another one in the Chicagoland area, and they've been trying to figure out what precisely happened to you after the Awakening event. Suffice to say that they're <i>very</i> curious about the things they've been able to figure out so far, and they're looking for you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - How would you feel about making Ragnar a grad student at the University of Chicago? Per Google, they have Ph.D. program in Comparative Literature, or one in English Language and Literature. You could have run into Vo and/or Oscar at some point during a campus event, possibly a LGBT-related event or guest speaker seminar.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Your character has some very unique facets to his background that I am really interested in exploring with you. First, you're the only character who seems to be in a committed relationship or with kids. You're also the only hetero member of the cabal. The way Marlin feels about the LGBT community may influence how easy it is for him to come together with the others to form a cabal. If this feels forced for you, or if you don't have any particular reason for Marlin to meet up with the others, we can also say that he has met some of them (probably Ragnar at least) at a guest author seminar hosted by the University of Chicago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:20:00-07:00","id":923605,"title":"","content":"Vo probably is not the biggest fan of teaching FYS, but she does it and her students get used to the stammer. Hopefully. They're sort of stuck with her.<br /> <br /> I'm happy for her to have met others through the college, obviously, including through teaching FYS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:26:44-07:00","id":923609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923605#post923605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vo probably is not the biggest fan of teaching FYS, but she does it and her students get used to the stammer. Hopefully. They're sort of stuck with her.<br /> <br /> I'm happy for her to have met others through the college, obviously, including through teaching FYS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! Of course, if Lynx would have had any reason to take an introductory physics course, he could have you for that class instead. Assuming he's ok with the UChicago idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T20:41:42-07:00","id":923674,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Yes, Ragnar being a grad student in the Comparative Literature program would be pretty appropriate. Being an Acanthus, I think he would be very interested in seeing how cultures can approach the same story and change the context to suit their cultural mores and theology; it could really give him some insight into how he could use Fate and Time to subtly alter chains of events. Being a grad student, he's almost certainly working as a T.A. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a>, What do you think of Ragnar being a T.A. in the FYS that Vo is teaching, with Lynx taking it? Alternatively, Ragnar is a T.A. for Vo, and Ragnar and Lynx met through a LGBT student group? I did some research on University of Chicago, and apparently there is a student group called The Agenda, which is specifically for gay, bisexual, and queer men. Since Ragnar is relatively inexperienced, and Lynx doesn't have any sexual experience either way, I think a group for non-straight male students could be a convenient venue for them to meet at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T23:10:39-07:00","id":923721,"title":"","content":"Well, that's sad, I had high hopes for this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll still read it to see how does Phoenix do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T23:29:08-07:00","id":923731,"title":"","content":"It kind sucks given I was the one who initally asked for the game to begin with but oh well, I guess the rules are different off GitP forums...now to begin again the month and a half long wait for a Mage ST!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T00:22:20-07:00","id":923745,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, waking up to this pretty much made my morning. Thank you.<br /> <br /> I don't mind having Lynx going to UChicago at all. I think a FYS would probably fit better than an introductory physics course for him. As Haberdasher suggests, Ragnar could also be a T.A. at the FYS, which means Lynx would know (of) the both of them.<br /> <br /> While we're on the subject, since I haven't actually decided what Lynx would study abroad yet, Comparative Literature would be a good fit, I think. Could also strengthen his and Ragnar's bond.<br /> <br /> I'm down with Lynx being a part of a LGBT student group too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 06-30-2016, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T00:56:23-07:00","id":923752,"title":"","content":"Thanks for picking me! I'm looking forward to this game. I'll keep thinking on Path, it might depend a little on what Arcana other people are looking at. Binder and Ragnar especially, do you know what you want to focus on?<br /> <br /> Here's an actual concrete connection: Moonstone has stopped into Marlin's Books once or twice for the ol' &quot;see if the occult bookstore has any Real Stuff we need to get our hands on&quot; routine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T01:25:12-07:00","id":923757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923601#post923601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - By having the rest of your Hunter cell suddenly die at the moment of your Awakening, we might be missing out on a really prime opportunity for plot hooks! I have 2 alternate suggestions for tweaking this. First, we could say that the other Hunters in your cell were all severely injured or maimed, mentally traumatized, <i>or</i> killed, but not all of them died. Or, I'd like you to add that your Hunter cell worked with another one in the Chicagoland area, and they've been trying to figure out what precisely happened to you after the Awakening event. Suffice to say that they're <i>very</i> curious about the things they've been able to figure out so far, and they're looking for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the rest-of-cell-death thing was to create a plot hook with whatever killed his comrades while removing any constraints of a Hunter game since this isn't one. Though if you wanna explore a plot hook of how some Hunters familiar with Phoenix from before he Awakened would react to him becoming a mage, well then let's go with the latter alternative.<br /> <br /> In fact, it makes sense. After all, Hunter cells can settle their differences in order to team-up against powerful creatures. A powerful creature could easily take out an entire cell (Phoenix was dead at the time the rest of his cell was killed). I'd like to discuss with Caladriu about the possibility of Hakim being the target of that hunt. Just an idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923721#post923721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's sad, I had high hopes for this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll still read it to see how does Phoenix do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is unfortunate (although kinda funny since before I thought I was the one not getting in). Perhaps they'll meet at a different time/chronicle, who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T03:27:56-07:00","id":923782,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12044_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12044\" data-vbnamecard=\"12044\">ChaosArchon</a> - Like I said, I am very sorry that I couldn't pick everyone who submitted a character. This is my least favorite part of PbP games. The only way to avoid this issue is to take the first few players who apply, but I feel that it is more fruitful to take more player submissions and make decisions after everyone has had a chance to apply. <br /> <br /> As I said in my post, I would be willing to consider running 2 games so everyone has a chance to play. I would need some time to figure out different plot hooks, but that's not the worst thing. I had some ideas of running another game out of the Colorado area, with more of a rural feel. Would that interest you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T05:07:02-07:00","id":923792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923757#post923757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point of the rest-of-cell-death thing was to create a plot hook with whatever killed his comrades while removing any constraints of a Hunter game since this isn't one. Though if you wanna explore a plot hook of how some Hunters familiar with Phoenix from before he Awakened would react to him becoming a mage, well then let's go with the latter alternative.<br /> <br /> In fact, it makes sense. After all, Hunter cells can settle their differences in order to team-up against powerful creatures. A powerful creature could easily take out an entire cell (Phoenix was dead at the time the rest of his cell was killed). I'd like to discuss with Caladriu about the possibility of Hakim being the target of that hunt. Just an idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, it is unfortunate (although kinda funny since before I thought I was the one not getting in). Perhaps they'll meet at a different time/chronicle, who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, it's ironic. I will follow your adventures as a reader, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T05:44:52-07:00","id":923800,"title":"","content":"For the players who weren't selected for the Chicago game (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12044_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12044\" data-vbnamecard=\"12044\">ChaosArchon</a>):<br /> <br /> For the second game I would be willing to consider running, I'm thinking of a setting in Colorado (probably outside the Denver area) in which the Gauntlet is particularly weak, and experiencing odd fluctuations that lead to frequent and temporary Loci opening. There would be a very active and disturbed Werewolf population attempting to investigate and curb spirit-related issues, which would lead to conflict (and, at times, potential alliances) with the Uratha. The PCs would be exploring Mysteries related to the disturbances in the Shadow and Fallen worlds, including other Mages who might seek to take advantage of the local issues to gain power.<br /> <br /> Would that interest you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T06:18:31-07:00","id":923805,"title":"","content":"I would be interested in playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T06:40:54-07:00","id":923816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923752#post923752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for picking me! I'm looking forward to this game. I'll keep thinking on Path, it might depend a little on what Arcana other people are looking at. Binder and Ragnar especially, do you know what you want to focus on?<br /> <br /> Here's an actual concrete connection: Moonstone has stopped into Marlin's Books once or twice for the ol' &quot;see if the occult bookstore has any Real Stuff we need to get our hands on&quot; routine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ragnar's Arcana is giving me a little trouble. I think Ragnar, at this point, sees the universe as made from the interaction of seven of the Arcana: woven from Space and Time, given movement and shape by Forces and Matters, and the drama of life being the cycle of Life and Death; and all six ruled over by the laws and patterns governed by Fate. Not sure seven Arcana is feasible, but I do think it ties into the Renaissance man mentality that Ragnar has: try to know at least one thing about every subject, and try to know everything about at least one subject.<br /> <br /> Besides, when I ask myself, &quot;what do I see Ragnar doing as an acknowledged Master in a consilium?&quot;, he's the quiet type who can basically corral people into doing what he wants them to do, the mentor type who never seems to take direct action, but is actually working feverishly behind the scenes, and if he ever does act directly, he knows a few ways to <i>really </i>mess your day up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 06-30-2016, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T07:04:26-07:00","id":923828,"title":"","content":"Lynx will focus on both Spirit and Life arcana. The original concept of him also had Matter, which tied in with the Lords of the Inanimate legacy. The more I think about him, though, the less I see him focusing on the material aspect of existence - on the other hand, nobody can really deny the efficiency of being able to get the spirit of a computer to just turn itself on and unlock encrypted contents,, or opening a door with a soft murmur, or having a gun eject its clip with a look. But there's no denying that, right now, he's not going to shy away from the ecstasy of flesh nor the spiritual that exists all around. <br /> <br /> We'll figure it out eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T07:47:27-07:00","id":923849,"title":"","content":"Wooo! I got picked <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923601#post923601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Your character has some very unique facets to his background that I am really interested in exploring with you. First, you're the only character who seems to be in a committed relationship or with kids. You're also the only hetero member of the cabal. The way Marlin feels about the LGBT community may influence how easy it is for him to come together with the others to form a cabal. If this feels forced for you, or if you don't have any particular reason for Marlin to meet up with the others, we can also say that he has met some of them (probably Ragnar at least) at a guest author seminar hosted by the University of Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marlin is totally cool with LGBT, but I can't see him participating in the LGBT community, even as an ally. It just wouldn't really be on his mind (at least, until he joined a cabal with 5 non-hets, lol).<br /> <br /> Ideas for connections:<br /> <br /> <b>Vo:</b> If they both went to the U of C, then it's possible that despite winding up with completely different degrees, they ran into each other a couple times, or had a class together. Depending on the timeline, Marlin may have had Vo as a TA or professor? Then putting neighborhood gossip on top of that would give reason for Marlin to have thought of her recently. &quot;Did you hear what happened to Vivian a couple blocks down?&quot; &quot;Wait... Vivian McAllister? I think I had a couple classes with her...&quot; He'd probably write a short letter to show his support since it's more polite than showing up and rubbing it in her face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923752#post923752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an actual concrete connection: Moonstone has stopped into Marlin's Books once or twice for the ol' &quot;see if the occult bookstore has any Real Stuff we need to get our hands on&quot; routine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely! It's possible that Moonstone was even on Marlin's short list of people to invite to his &quot;ritual,&quot; though no one ended up getting actually invited. I also like the idea of them very occasionally playing chess at the park.<br /> <br /> <b>Ragnar/Pheonix/Lynx:</b> It's possible that they came looking into Marlin's small collection of occult books while doing research, or that they met at the library; Marlin would make extensive use of the library even if his wife <i>didn't </i>work there.<br /> <br /> Regarding Arcana, I'm thinking of starting Mind 3, Space 2, Spirit 1, but I'd also eventually like to expand further, into Prime at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:26:27-07:00","id":923864,"title":"","content":"I was hoping to have some down time today to write a more detailed post, but I'm turning out to be really busy today. <br /> <br /> For the 6 PCs: Please start working on your character sheet, using the standard rules for new Mage characters. Try to include skills and merits that you think reflect the character concept you submitted. Let me know if you have questions, and I will help as I can.<br /> <br /> Also, please put the character sheet in your original post with your character concept and background info, in a text format so I can read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 06-30-2016, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:11:23-07:00","id":923891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923800#post923800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the players who weren't selected for the Chicago game (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12044_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12044\" data-vbnamecard=\"12044\">ChaosArchon</a>):<br /> <br /> For the second game I would be willing to consider running, I'm thinking of a setting in Colorado (probably outside the Denver area) in which the Gauntlet is particularly weak, and experiencing odd fluctuations that lead to frequent and temporary Loci opening. There would be a very active and disturbed Werewolf population attempting to investigate and curb spirit-related issues, which would lead to conflict (and, at times, potential alliances) with the Uratha. The PCs would be exploring Mysteries related to the disturbances in the Shadow and Fallen worlds, including other Mages who might seek to take advantage of the local issues to gain power.<br /> <br /> Would that interest you?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty cool, yeah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:17:04-07:00","id":923924,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Since our characters are fairly recently Awakened, do they not have Order status, and with that the rote skills, dot of Occult, and High Speech Merit that they would get with Order status?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:00:33-07:00","id":923965,"title":"","content":"And presumably no rotes, either. But do we get a Praxis since those are free? Also, not that I'm planning to do this myself, but can we exchange merit dots for Gnosis as usual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:09:36-07:00","id":923972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923924#post923924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Since our characters are fairly recently Awakened, do they not have Order status, and with that the rote skills, dot of Occult, and High Speech Merit that they would get with Order status?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great question! I forgot to mention this. Assuming you intend your character to join an Order, go ahead and pick your Order and indicate all of the things that normally provides (i.e., free dot of Order Status, rote skills, 6 dots of rotes, free dot of Occult, High Speech merit). However, you will not have access to any of those features in-game until you are initiated into the Order. This will happen early in the game, with the intention of very quickly getting the PCs together, forming a cabal, being presented to the Consilium, and having the opportunity to join the Order of their choice. Those bonuses will become active once you are in the Order.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Yes, pick Praxes as normal. You can exchange Merit dots for Gnosis per the standard rules. That means you can technically be Gnosis 3, but especially for characters who wanted to have connections with Awakened society before their actual Awakening, it would be harder to pull off while keeping true to your character concept. If someone in that position really wants Gnosis 3, we can talk about it and discuss pros/cons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:09:53-07:00","id":923973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923800#post923800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the players who weren't selected for the Chicago game (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12044_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12044\" data-vbnamecard=\"12044\">ChaosArchon</a>):<br /> <br /> For the second game I would be willing to consider running, I'm thinking of a setting in Colorado (probably outside the Denver area) in which the Gauntlet is particularly weak, and experiencing odd fluctuations that lead to frequent and temporary Loci opening. There would be a very active and disturbed Werewolf population attempting to investigate and curb spirit-related issues, which would lead to conflict (and, at times, potential alliances) with the Uratha. The PCs would be exploring Mysteries related to the disturbances in the Shadow and Fallen worlds, including other Mages who might seek to take advantage of the local issues to gain power.<br /> <br /> Would that interest you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested for sure, but can we create a seperate thread for it? I'd find it hard to seperate the games in one thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:13:40-07:00","id":923975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923816#post923816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ragnar's Arcana is giving me a little trouble. I think Ragnar, at this point, sees the universe as made from the interaction of seven of the Arcana: woven from Space and Time, given movement and shape by Forces and Matters, and the drama of life being the cycle of Life and Death; and all six ruled over by the laws and patterns governed by Fate. Not sure seven Arcana is feasible, but I do think it ties into the Renaissance man mentality that Ragnar has: try to know at least one thing about every subject, and try to know everything about at least one subject.<br /> <br /> Besides, when I ask myself, &quot;what do I see Ragnar doing as an acknowledged Master in a consilium?&quot;, he's the quiet type who can basically corral people into doing what he wants them to do, the mentor type who never seems to take direct action, but is actually working feverishly behind the scenes, and if he ever does act directly, he knows a few ways to <i>really </i>mess your day up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I can see the dilemma. A lot of the Arcana are really neat and provide fascinating abilities and attainments. But don't forget the rules on distribution of dots among starting Arcana (e.g., most spread out allowed could be 2, 1, 1, 1, 1) and the fact that your Path has very important impacts on how Ragnar would understand magic. He can still be a &quot;jack of all trades&quot; if he desires, but his true understanding of magic is always going to be through the lens of his Acanthus Path. There isn't a &quot;universal&quot; Path. If you're stuck, try reading through the Acanthus Path description again and think how the details there might relate to Ragnar's personal philosophy and Obsessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:18:32-07:00","id":923976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923973#post923973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm interested for sure, but can we create a seperate thread for it? I'd find it hard to seperate the games in one thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that was my plan. Just haven't had a chance yet. I can probably set it up in the next day or two, and we can discuss further. Anyone have a neat idea for the game? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:55:18-07:00","id":924000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923800#post923800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the players who weren't selected for the Chicago game (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12044_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12044\" data-vbnamecard=\"12044\">ChaosArchon</a>):<br /> <br /> For the second game I would be willing to consider running, I'm thinking of a setting in Colorado (probably outside the Denver area) in which the Gauntlet is particularly weak, and experiencing odd fluctuations that lead to frequent and temporary Loci opening. There would be a very active and disturbed Werewolf population attempting to investigate and curb spirit-related issues, which would lead to conflict (and, at times, potential alliances) with the Uratha. The PCs would be exploring Mysteries related to the disturbances in the Shadow and Fallen worlds, including other Mages who might seek to take advantage of the local issues to gain power.<br /> <br /> Would that interest you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds Fun. And there's a good excuse to have a Familiar as a starting character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:57:17-07:00","id":924002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923828#post923828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lynx will focus on both Spirit and Life arcana. The original concept of him also had Matter, which tied in with the Lords of the Inanimate legacy. The more I think about him, though, the less I see him focusing on the material aspect of existence - on the other hand, nobody can really deny the efficiency of being able to get the spirit of a computer to just turn itself on and unlock encrypted contents,, or opening a door with a soft murmur, or having a gun eject its clip with a look. But there's no denying that, right now, he's not going to shy away from the ecstasy of flesh nor the spiritual that exists all around.<br /> <br /> We'll figure it out eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Life 2/Spirit 2/Matter 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:13:33-07:00","id":924009,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Thanks! I was doing a little reading, and actually dug up a copy of Awakening 1e. I took a look at the Walkers in Mists, and decided that the druid imagery fit with the Merlin/Dumbledore/Gandalf archetype that I was envisioning for Ragnar down the road. So that cleared up what Arcana I want to focus on: Fate primary, then Space and Time secondary, and finally Life tertiary. I'm also thinking that the th\u00e9archs' religious philosophy is particularly appealing to Ragnar, since a big part of his backstory is not being satisfied with Sleeper religions, and the Silver Ladder's philosophy could be a real &quot;Aha!&quot; moment for him. Plus the Silver Ladder's focus on leadership ties into the Merlin flavor for Ragnar: even if he's not leading the cabal himself, he's definitely throwing his two cents in for the benefit of who ever is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:36:50-07:00","id":924021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924002#post924002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about Life 2/Spirit 2/Matter 2?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's either going to be that or Life 2, Spirit 2, Matter 1, Other arcanum 1. I'll figure it out in time, of course.<br /> <br /> Really looking forward to this now. It'll be strange to be a player, and equally strange to not use the houserules I have in my own games. Hopefully I won't forget anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 06-30-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:47:44-07:00","id":924073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923800#post923800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the players who weren't selected for the Chicago game (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2650\" data-vbnamecard=\"2650\">Retias</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7592\" data-vbnamecard=\"7592\">wtaylorjr2001</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12044_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12044\" data-vbnamecard=\"12044\">ChaosArchon</a>):<br /> <br /> For the second game I would be willing to consider running, I'm thinking of a setting in Colorado (probably outside the Denver area) in which the Gauntlet is particularly weak, and experiencing odd fluctuations that lead to frequent and temporary Loci opening. There would be a very active and disturbed Werewolf population attempting to investigate and curb spirit-related issues, which would lead to conflict (and, at times, potential alliances) with the Uratha. The PCs would be exploring Mysteries related to the disturbances in the Shadow and Fallen worlds, including other Mages who might seek to take advantage of the local issues to gain power.<br /> <br /> Would that interest you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds even more interesting than the former game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Are you sure you can manage two games at once? If so, I would be totally down for it. Bardo would be troubled without easy access to Spirit, but that's a hook unto itself. I also have a nice niche in mind for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:01:00-07:00","id":924118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923976#post923976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, that was my plan. Just haven't had a chance yet. I can probably set it up in the next day or two, and we can discuss further. Anyone have a neat idea for the game? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking maybe we start off in Egypt circa WW2. I think it would be kind of fun to be a group of Allied Mages fighting Nazi Mages and solving strange, ancient mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:14:25-07:00","id":924124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923976#post923976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, that was my plan. Just haven't had a chance yet. I can probably set it up in the next day or two, and we can discuss further. Anyone have a neat idea for the game? :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChaosArchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924118#post924118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking maybe we start off in Egypt circa WW2. I think it would be kind of fun to be a group of Allied Mages fighting Nazi Mages and solving strange, ancient mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, I tried to run a WW2 campaign, only the players were the Nazis / Seers. It began in November, 1939; the group consisted of an Acanthus WW1 Veteran soldier; a Moros scientist working on nuclear warfare; and a female Obrimos Daksha member of the Gestapo. Officially, they were members of the Ahnenerbe - but they were secretly an infiltration cell meant to root out and hunt down Supernal threats to the Reich. <br /> <br /> Sadly, it only lasted a couple of sessions. They went and solved some communication mysteries in Stralsund involving some British Pentacle spies, and there was a monster that was killing greater spirits all over the country. Then the group fell apart because of time commitment issues... <br /> <br /> I'm now running a campaign set in Basque, 1992, in an alternate world where Germany won WW2... Which is ultimately what would've happened if the WW2 campaign had continued. We just finished our 14th session, and I just finished writing today's recap. It ended up 5.5 pages long... Ah, good, tiresome fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:53:37-07:00","id":924150,"title":"","content":"As I'm making Lynx, I realise I've got a minor disadvantage with being a foreign exchange student: I need to spend 1 of my 10 Merit dot on Language (English). I don't really mind doing so, but I'd like to know your opinion on this issue, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>. After all, native language is Norwegian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:17:44-07:00","id":924164,"title":"","content":"I did not mean to triple-post :&lt; I am bad at this.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-lfg-mage-the-awakening-2e?p=923352#post923352\">I've begun on the character sheet</a>. It looks like arse right now, to be honest, but it's better than nothing. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 06-30-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T17:00:43-07:00","id":924176,"title":"","content":"So I definitely had a typo. I meant does anyone have a neat idea for a game title. The story idea I had is in a previous post: rural Colorado, Gauntlet splitting and Loci forming, conflict with Werewolves and other Mages, etc. Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T17:03:31-07:00","id":924179,"title":"","content":"Wolfpack Mountains?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T20:17:35-07:00","id":924259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924150#post924150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm making Lynx, I realise I've got a minor disadvantage with being a foreign exchange student: I need to spend 1 of my 10 Merit dot on Language (English). I don't really mind doing so, but I'd like to know your opinion on this issue, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>. After all, native language is Norwegian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I feel like making you pay a Merit point for English is dumb. You can have the language for free.<br /> <br /> Also, if you end up going Spirit 3, don't forget that you can always bond a spirit as a familiar on your own by getting up to Spirit 4. Depends how important that Arcana will be to your character concept, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T20:23:04-07:00","id":924263,"title":"","content":"For the 5 players who were not selected for the Chicago game: I created a new game thread for the Colorado one. Check it out and tell me what you think. I think it will be easier to come up with certain things for that game because of the info in some other books I have. <br /> <br /> For everyone: Just a reminder that I'll be out of town starting tomorrow (7/1) through Sunday (7/10), so I may not be able to reply quickly. My hope is to type up more about the setting and local Awakened politics, and then get the ball rolling on the actual game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T00:57:53-07:00","id":924340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924259#post924259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I feel like making you pay a Merit point for English is dumb. You can have the language for free.<br /> <br /> Also, if you end up going Spirit 3, don't forget that you can always bond a spirit as a familiar on your own by getting up to Spirit 4. Depends how important that Arcana will be to your character concept, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the free language.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dependent on the length of the campaign, it would take a very, very long time for me to get to Spirit 4. Assuming I start at Spirit 3, I would have to invest 14 exp before I could give myself a familiar - 19 if I don't beeline straight for Spirit 4, i.e., if I go Life 4 (or any other arcanum to 4) first. I also dislike planning my experience purchases ahead of time in such a fashion as well, so I couldn't tell you when, or even if, I'd go for familiar later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 07-01-2016, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T01:27:49-07:00","id":924347,"title":"","content":"Since we're filling sheets out, I've made some character sheets templates on google docs that auto-calculates Advantages and has a space for equipment. I can make a doc for this game with blank Mage sheets to keep all the sheets in one place as well as a status sheet that keeps track of WP, Health, Mana, and temporary Conditions/Tilts.<br /> <br /> On a related note, I've got a chronicle info doc template where one can record general information of the chronicle, like a Beat record and a space to record where players have spent Experiences, and a profile template doc that all the players can use to add all the mechanic-less stuff.<br /> <br /> rwknoll, if you're interested in that, I can make the docs and give everyone the links to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T01:51:16-07:00","id":924354,"title":"","content":"I'm primarily using an interactive pdf as a character sheet. I'll probably link it at the end of my stat block.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T03:32:05-07:00","id":924376,"title":"","content":"You can keep the stats in other additional formats if you like. Unfortunately, because of the firewall at my job, the problem becomes that I can't load a lot of links...including Google Docs and most download sites. So I will need text format like you've already started if I want to be able to view your character sheets at work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is that ok?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T03:35:28-07:00","id":924377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924376#post924376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can keep the stats in other additional formats if you like. Unfortunately, because of the firewall at my job, the problem becomes that I can't load a lot of links...including Google Docs and most download sites. So I will need text format like you've already started if I want to be able to view your character sheets at work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is that ok?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't mind at all, no worries from my end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T04:02:39-07:00","id":924384,"title":"","content":"Also, experience doesn't scale with current dots like it did in 1E. You need 4 XP to go from Spirit 3 to 4, or 20 beats. And that can be a combination of regular and Arcane experience. It won't take nearly as long as you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T04:52:34-07:00","id":924398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924384#post924384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, experience doesn't scale with current dots like it did in 1E. You need 4 XP to go from Spirit 3 to 4, or 20 beats. And that can be a combination of regular and Arcane experience. It won't take nearly as long as you think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You need Gnosis 3 to get an Arcanum to 4 in 2nd Edition, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gnosis limits the upper limit of a mage\u2019s Arcana. A mage\u2019s highest Arcanum can be three dots at Gnosis 1, four dots at Gnosis 3, and five dots at Gnosis 5. That mage\u2019s other Arcana are limited to a maximum of two dots at Gnosis 1, three dots at Gnosis 2, four dots at Gnosis 4, and five dots at Gnosis 6. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T09:32:47-07:00","id":924497,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I was planning to take the Artifact merit as a keepsake taken from Hakim, how does this look?<br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Night (Artifact 5)</b><br /> An archaic hooded traveling cloak, ink-black, with a leaden clasp in the shape of a death's-head moth.<br /> Contains the spells Shadow Flesh (Death 4) and Wards and Signs (Prime 2). Effective Gnosis 3 and Arcana 4. Contains up to 10 Mana. Counts as a Path tool for Moros mages.<br /> Effect 1: Gain [base Potency 4, more with spell factors] Withstand against all spells targeting me specifically for 1 scene. Activated by closing the clasp around the neck. 7 dice before spell factors. (Wards and Signs, 1 reach spent on instant casting, 1 reach on advanced duration, 1 reach spent on changing primary factor from duration to potency.)<br /> Effect 2: Dissolve into a two-dimensional shadow for [base Duration 5 turns, more with spell factors] as per Shadow Flesh. Activated by pulling the hood over the head. 7 dice before spell factors. (Shadow Flesh, 1 reach spent on instant casting.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923757#post923757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, it makes sense. After all, Hunter cells can settle their differences in order to team-up against powerful creatures. A powerful creature could easily take out an entire cell (Phoenix was dead at the time the rest of his cell was killed). I'd like to discuss with Caladriu about the possibility of Hakim being the target of that hunt. Just an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like Hakim being the one who killed Phoenix's cell? I wasn't imagining him being a Scelesti or anything, but I do like the idea that Moonstone's growth is going to involve distancing himself from his mentor and realizing that the relationship wasn't totally healthy and generally being more clear-sighted about him. And I did say that he had a big falling-out with his former cabal that led to him and Moonstone leaving them.<br /> <br /> I don't know what if anything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> had in mind when suggesting that hook, but maybe (being a Moros) Hakim was secretly a Reaper? Or otherwise dabbling with Left-Handed practices that Moonstone was willfully ignorant about. &quot;He's just under a lot of stress at work!&quot; Or at least he was connected to that kind of Bad Magical Shit enough to be a target, even if he was just investigating a cabal and looked from the outside hunter's perspective to be a member. We could leave it uncertain exactly why he was targeted and what the real truth of the situation was, I definitely want the events around his assassination to provoke some larger Mystery and suspicion and thread-unraveling that's fun for the whole party if we look into it in the course of the game. Also I just like the idea of Moonstone getting really huffy and defensive at the suggestion that he doesn't know his mentor as well as he thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:05:09-07:00","id":924723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924497#post924497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like Hakim being the one who killed Phoenix's cell? I wasn't imagining him being a Scelesti or anything, but I do like the idea that Moonstone's growth is going to involve distancing himself from his mentor and realizing that the relationship wasn't totally healthy and generally being more clear-sighted about him. And I did say that he had a big falling-out with his former cabal that led to him and Moonstone leaving them.<br /> <br /> I don't know what if anything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> had in mind when suggesting that hook, but maybe (being a Moros) Hakim was secretly a Reaper? Or otherwise dabbling with Left-Handed practices that Moonstone was willfully ignorant about. &quot;He's just under a lot of stress at work!&quot; Or at least he was connected to that kind of Bad Magical Shit enough to be a target, even if he was just investigating a cabal and looked from the outside hunter's perspective to be a member. We could leave it uncertain exactly why he was targeted and what the real truth of the situation was, I definitely want the events around his assassination to provoke some larger Mystery and suspicion and thread-unraveling that's fun for the whole party if we look into it in the course of the game. Also I just like the idea of Moonstone getting really huffy and defensive at the suggestion that he doesn't know his mentor as well as he thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty awesome, not to mention it'll spark a lot of drama when Phoenix and Moonstone find out the truth, especially if either one finds something out before the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:30:53-07:00","id":924731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924398#post924398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need Gnosis 3 to get an Arcanum to 4 in 2nd Edition, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, totally forgot that part. I like to give out beats and Arcane beats frequently as rewards for good role play, as well as the normal rules for all that stuff, so hopefully it will happen at a good pace. <br /> <br /> I also plan to have NPCs available who will offer mentorship and resources, in exchange for favors and other resources. So it's possible a Mage with Spirit 4 may mentor you and offer to bond a spirit familiar for you, but with strings attached. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Really, really digging the ideas here about deeper plot ties between your characters. I was partially vague about my suggested plot hook there because I'm still formulating ideas about some Mysteries I want to craft for you all to explore. I also want it to be ambiguous now so you can explore it in-game without full OOC knowledge. <br /> <br /> For right now, let's leave it at this: Hakim may have been involved in the death of Phoenix's Hunter cell, but details and presumed motives are unknown. He died relatively soon after, the apparent nature of which will be tied to a series of events that will serve a prominent role in the first story of this game. Sound fair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:35:08-07:00","id":924733,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - The artifact looks really neat, and I like the idea of having something meaningful from your deceased mentor. It also serves as a temporal sympathy, yeah? So that might be helpful to you down the road (especially if you go Acanthus).<br /> <br /> I am re-reading the core Mage 2E book to familiarize myself with the rules, but by my skimming, it looks accurate for the cost. Seems pretty neat.<br /> <br /> For everyone: Please let me know how else I can help with the actual character stat building process. And let me know what you're thinking of for your Nimbus Tilt, too. <br /> <br /> When you have time, to minimize confusion, please feel free to cut references in your character posts to connections/ties with PCs who weren't selected for this game. <br /> <br /> I've flagged the initial post asking for a mod to rename this thread as an OOC thread for the game, so don't be surprised if/when that happens. Not sure if that throws off URLs to posts in the thread? I'll be re-adding those links to your character posts on the initial post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 07-01-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T01:35:09-07:00","id":924816,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>, if you could give your insight on these matters as the storyteller, I would appreciate it immensely. <br /> <br /> <b>FAMILIAR</b><br /> <br /> It would help to know more about how the Familiar would function, I think.<br /> <br /> 2 dots in the merit gives a rank 1 spirit; 4 dots, a rank 2. Each rank has a variable number of attribute dots and numina, i.e., a rank 1 spirit has 5-8 attributes and 1-3 Numina; rank to has 9-14 attribute dots and 3-5 Numina.<br /> <br /> As the storyteller, what's your verdict here? It says I design it per the rules, though I'll do this process with you closely regardless. If I go for a 4-dot familiar, what are my restrictions? Can I go 14 attribute dots and 5 Numina? Would you prefer the minimum? The median?<br /> <br /> In 1st Edition, you could give spirits Numina that corresponded to specific spells, so long that they fit the spirit's Influence; would you allow this in 2nd edition? In this case, I'm thinking of a lynx as a familiar, which could have an Influence referring to knowledge, truth, vision and foresight, spiritual healing... assuming 4 Numina, I can't think of many of the listed ones in the book suiting the familiar. So...Let's say we go for a knowledge angle. Could it then have a Numen or two that would be the equivalent of Knowing of Time, i.e. &quot;Postcognition&quot; or &quot;Divination&quot;, to reflect Knowledge (of the past) and/or Foresight? Or an effect similar to Prime 1 &quot;Pierce Deception&quot;, if we think Truth?<br /> <br /> How would it work in play?. Do I have full domain over its actions? Do I (help) design its personality? Do I play it as a second character, or does it work more like a mentor or retainer, where it is an NPC which will act in my interests and help me to the best of its abilities? I <i>am</i> honestly hoping for the latter in this case, where I ask it if it could do this or this, and then it does, but its methodology and willingness is ultimately subject to your decisions. <br /> <br /> If it's an embodied familiar, how impractical would it be to have a physical lynx as a pet? Sure, it could create some interesting dilemmas, but I don't want to break suspension of disbelief (Why is a lynx following that man!?) or create unnecessary complications. Keeping it as a Fetch would be the most practical solution.<br /> <br /> It would be wicked if it could Materialise in physical form - that would require an Open condition or some physical form of an ephemeral entity. Said Materialisation would also not be permanent. The spirit could do it on its own, since it would have the Materialise Manifestation effect. In the case of an Open condition, if the Resonance Condition is suitable in an area (e.g., knowledge = library), and I created the Open condition on said Resonance, would it then manifest as a lynx?<br /> <br /> A Death 2 mage can use &quot;Create Ectoplasm&quot; and use &quot;Ectoplasmic Shaping&quot; to allow ghosts to materialise; he can also shape Death-attuned ephemera with Death 2 and pull said ephemera out of Twilight with &quot;Touch of the Grave&quot; into the physical realm. <br /> <br /> Would these rules work parallel with Spirit, i.e., could I shape Spirit-attuned Ephemera and pull it out of Twilight to if I wanted to manifest the Lynx into the physical realm (in a shape of my choosing) for a certain amount of time with Spirit 2?<br /> <br /> Which also reminds me - Death 3 &quot;Ghost Gate&quot; allows the mage to shift into Death-attuned Twilight. Spirit 3 &quot;Reaching&quot; allows the mage to cross the Gauntlet - but there is a Spirit-attuned Twilight. I do assume I could cross over to said Twilight with Spirit 3, but I still want to make sure if you agree or not. <br /> <br /> I'm still not a 100% on the rules on Spirits, so if anybody can correct me that would be swell. Or maybe I'm just really overthinking it...<br /> <br /> <b>ARCANA</b><br /> <br /> I'm still undecided if I want Life 3, Spirit 3, or a fourth Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Life 3 would be immensely practical (and think of the possibilities!)! Transform Life to change aspects of one's self, Honing the Form to bolster physical attributes (on both self and others if needed), Knit to heal wounds and stay refreshed... it also would further Lynx's free spirit and, at this point, his budding hedonism. <br /> <br /> Spirit 3 would open up the Shadow as a secondary location for us to explore and use. Is this an opportunity you find desirable, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>? What about the other players? This alone is a world of possibilities, adventure, and danger (Jake English would be proud), and I will go for Spirit 3 without hesitation if the availability to enter the Shadow across the Gauntlet pretty much at will is wanted. <br /> <br /> As for fourth Arcanum... again, possibilities. If we rule out what <i>wouldn't</i> fit, we'd have Mind (inferior), Space, Death and Forces. I've mentioned Matter before, but I can also imagine Time and Prime, for knowledge's sake. But if I were to go for the familiar as above, it would be Lynx's primary Supernal source of information. <br /> <br /> <b>NIMBUS</b><br /> <br /> Appropriately, the ecstatic feeling of truly feeling alive is what comes to mind. The Immediate Nimbus could be a shadow of Lynx's animalistic nature, e.g., his shadow might appear as a wolf, or momentarily he might look an anthropomorphic animal (not necessarily a lynx); and/or a sensation of heightened senses and sensitivity; the lightest touch resonates through the body; a person's nature manifests as odour (someone deceitful by nature would smell foul; someone calm would smell like a quiet pond or glade, something like that); the feeling of being naked, raw, and exposed. <br /> <br /> The Signature would be remnants of fur and/or a distinct odour, I think. <br /> <br /> <b>NIMBUS TILT</b><br /> <br /> I was thinking either +1 Presence, -1 Resolve, to reflect something akin to empowered primal charisma combined with lowered inhibitions; or +1 Empathy, -1 Subterfuge, to reflect Lynx's instinct of reading people, while making those affected more transparent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T05:57:34-07:00","id":924852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924731#post924731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Really, really digging the ideas here about deeper plot ties between your characters. I was partially vague about my suggested plot hook there because I'm still formulating ideas about some Mysteries I want to craft for you all to explore. I also want it to be ambiguous now so you can explore it in-game without full OOC knowledge.<br /> <br /> For right now, let's leave it at this: Hakim may have been involved in the death of Phoenix's Hunter cell, but details and presumed motives are unknown. He died relatively soon after, the apparent nature of which will be tied to a series of events that will serve a prominent role in the first story of this game. Sound fair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, I'm fine with this. However, I do need a bit more detail on Phoenix's perception of what happened. Not asking for what actually went down, just the things that Phoenix knew and saw. For example, who was Hakim from the cell's perspective and why were they hunting him, things like that. The main reason is so I know what to fill in for Phoenix's first Obsession, and it might affect Aspirations, too.<br /> <br /> Speaking of character stuff, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=922641#post922641\">I've changed my intro post into a full character sheet.</a><br /> <br /> It's incomplete, like the Obsession and I haven't put in any of the Order benefits (I've also listed the input for Order and Legacy in parentheses, meaning that I fully intend for Phoenix to join those, but he hasn't yet). By the way, what are the rules for starting equipment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T06:03:20-07:00","id":924854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924852#post924852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of character stuff, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=922641#post922641\">I've changed my intro post into a full character sheet.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That looks wicked good. Mind if I use it as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T06:13:42-07:00","id":924863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=924854#post924854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Vi