(Prime \u25cf)</li> </ul><b><u>Attainments</u></b><ul><li>Precise Force (Forces \u25cf\u25cf)</li> <li>Mind's Eye (Mind \u25cf\u25cf)</li> <li>Universal Counterspell (Prime \u25cf\u25cf)</li> </ul><b><u>Rotes</u></b><ul><li>Kinetic Blow (Forces \u25cf\u25cf, Brawl)</li> <li>&lt;Mental Scan (Mind \u25cf, Occult)&gt;</li> <li>&lt;Mental Shield (Mind \u25cf\u25cf, Intimidation)&gt;</li> <li>&lt;Dispel Magic (Prime \u25cf, Intimidation)&gt;</li> </ul><b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Long-Term</i> - Events play out like a written tale. A college graduate gets the opportunity they needed, a devious businessman gets the comeuppance they deserve, an innocent child is afflicted with tragedy that changes the course of their life forever, the unconnected situations of strangers weave into one another to bring them together.<br /> <br /> <i>Immediate</i> - The skin of the Fallen World cracks as the pure, raw stuff of creation itself pours out. Cracks form wherever the spell was focused. If he cast an Unveiling spell on himself, his eyes would glow and cracks would form around them. If he cast a Fraying spell on someone, cracks would appear on the wound.<br /> <br /> <i>Signature</i> - The cracks shrink into words of High Speech. The High Speech describes the spell\u2019s effect in a classic mythological sense. For the Unveiling spell, the words might read &quot;And illusions were swept aside&quot;. For the Fraying spell, it might read &quot;Tongues of flame had lashed against flesh&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i>Tilt</i> - The elemental force is too much to handle, resulting in a -1 penalty on Composure rolls.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Aspirations</b></u><ul><li>Aid Moonstone in defeating Alux</li> <li>Join an Order</li> <li>Fail to keep the other Hunter cell away</li> </ul><u><b>Obsessions</b></u><ul><li>Find out about Hakim\u2019s death</li> </ul><u><b>Equipment</b></u><ul><li>Machete (Damage 2, Initiative -2, Strength 2, Size 2, Availability 2)</li> <li>First-Aid Kit (Bonus +1, Durability 1, Size 2, Structure 3, Availability 2)</li> <li>Staff of Truth (Damage 1, Initiative -1, Strength 2, Size 4, Two-handed, +1 Defense against unarmed or Size 1 weapons, Imbued: Pierce Deception</li> </ul><u><b>Tools</b></u><ul><li>Palm Tattoos (Dedicated): Unleashing &amp; enhancing potential</li> <li>Staff of Truth (Path): Revelation, dispelling illusions</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Details</b></span></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><b>General</b></u><br /> <b>Age/Birthday:</b> 20/February 20<br /> <b>Gender:</b> Male<br /> <b>Height:</b> 6' 5&quot;<br /> <b>Build:</b> Athletic<br /> <b>Occupation:</b> Martial Arts Teacher<br /> <b>Ethnicity:</b> Mixed<br /> <b>Nationality:</b> American<br /> <b>Hair Color:</b> Grey<br /> <b>Eye Color:</b> Brown<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Bisexual<br /> <br /> <b><u>Background</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Sleepwalking</i> - Timothy was born to an Awakened mother and a Sleepwalking father, who happened to be a former Thaumaturge, in Boston, Massachusetts. Due to this heritage, Timothy was born with a sensitivity for magic and knew of its existence ever since he could remember.<br /> <br /> His father resented magic. Years of practicing the art weighed heavily upon him. More often than not, magic was abused for selfish and depraved ends, causing terrible suffering. Even when using magic for nothing more than to other\u2019s benefit, it still had a price. Save a life, and someone else would die. Prevent a disaster, and it would merely be delayed. Sooner or later, magic would cause pain and suffering. So he decided to abandon magic, believing it to be a force of evil.<br /> <br /> Before then, he married Timothy\u2019s mother. Being Awakened, his mother couldn\u2019t simply abandon magic like her husband had. Even if she could, she wouldn\u2019t leave the world of magic for him. Inevitably, this created a rift that separated the two parents, eventually resulting in divorce when Timothy was seven years of age. They believed that he should have a chance at a normal life, which his Awakened mother just couldn\u2019t provide, so his father took custody.<br /> <br /> Raised by his father alone, Timothy knew full well of his father\u2019s resentment of magic and was taught to resent it himself, but he never really understood why. He was born with the ability to feel magic, so why did he have to reject it? Wasn\u2019t it a part of him, and thus rejecting it meant rejecting himself? Not that it bothered him much. After his mother left, he didn\u2019t feel much magic at all through the years. By the time he was at the tail end of high school, he suddenly felt the presence of magic. At first he didn\u2019t even knew what he was feeling, but as he felt it more and more, the memories of his mother\u2019s magic came back to him.<br /> <br /> The magic came from various people who looked to be members of a cult. Curiosity getting the better of him, he decided to investigate them, which lead him to a basement that set off his magical sense beyond anything he\u2019d ever felt before. He broke in to find jars of organs, journals detailing human sacrifice to gain immortality, and a drawn circle that reeked of blood and gave off ominous magic. That\u2019s when he saw a shadow appear behind him, along with that same magic, but far stronger.<br /> <br /> \u201cNaughty boy, knowing too much,\u201d the lich tsked, then they thrust a knife straight to his heart. They came from a distance long enough for him to respond, so he managed to grab the lich\u2019s arm to keep the knife at bay. However, the lich\u2019s momentum forced him to the ground to fight for his life. After a few minutes struggle, the lich finally gained the upperhand, the knife just above his heart and slowly lowering.<br /> <br /> Just before the knife began to pierce flesh, a gunshot shattered the struggle. The lich slowly looked down to find a hole in their chest, then more holes spawned with blood spatters as more bullets came. The lich fell on top of him, dead. He immediately pushed them off, to then find the barrel of a gun shoved between his eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho are you and what are you doing here?\u201d the gunman barked. Timothy was far too terrified to even speak, he could only manage incoherent stammering. \u201cJust another victim,\u201d the gunman sighed.<br /> <br /> It turned out that the gunman was one of a small Hunter cell who had been chasing the lich all the way from La Grange, and Timothy had helped them find the lich. After he told them that he could sense magic, they saw him as an incredible asset to their cell. Besides, he now knew of the world behind the veil, he couldn\u2019t go back to his former life. So, they offered him a place to stay there among their ranks. He accepted, believing it would be best to be missed than risk getting his friends and family involved.<br /> <br /> At least he understood why his father hated magic so much, it truly was evil. How else could a person commit such terrible acts for selfish gain?<br /> <br /> He was a Hunter for two years, taking on the name Garrick Royce as a code name. He utilized his magic sensitivity to take out those who practiced the forbidden arts. Most of them were gutter mages, and of the few that were Awakened, were usually troublesome rogue mages, Banishers, Scelesti, and the like. Oftentimes, he was used as an unwitting pawn by the Orders to take them out. However...<br /> <br /> <i>Awakening</i> - It all started with a dream. He saw a tall, thin, pitch-black shape jut from the distance. It birthed a light brighter than a thousand suns, frightening his eyes away to hide in his eyelids. He woke up to find the morning sun shining in his eyes. Later that day, he was in a populated cafe when he began to hear voices in his head. Worse, he could sense magic...coming from him. He was reading the thoughts of the ones around him. The message of his dream was clear: Magic had come for him.<br /> <br /> Every day since brought with it another incident. He read invisible words in between the inked ones in his book, he felt the ebb and flow of various energies against him as he walked down the street, his heart broke in the same manner as some stranger who had lost a loved one. Each night came with the same dream. The landscape always varied from windy plains, to thundering storms, to a calm sunset, but the event was always the same. The tower shone its light, blinding him. The only difference was that it got closer and closer every time.<br /> <br /> He refused the tower\u2019s call. Pushing the daily events to the back of his mind, and shouting defiance at the tower even as it blinded him. He would not have magic claim him, he would fight it to his last breath. And he would fight alone, he couldn\u2019t bring the others into this. He fought for as long as he could, but the magic pursued still.<br /> <br /> It all came to a head when the cell began hunting a sorcerer suspected of being a colleague of the lich killed two years prior. The dream collided with the waking world. The tower, now right in front of him, stood over reality along with a dragon who guarded the entrance. He cried rebellion against tower and dragon, to which they responded with burning him alive. Dead for a time in Fallen reality, his comrades mourned his loss, which was cut short by the ending of their own lives.<br /> <br /> He revived in the middle of the tower itself. His stalwart opposition to magic proved his resolve to the Watchtower, and that broke his heart. All this time he had cried defiance and rejection, resisting the temptation of power offered to him, not only was it for naught, but that it was the very key to his failure. The irony weighed down upon his knees as he beat against the wall, sinking into weeping against it. That\u2019s when a long-forgotten part of his soul welled up from his dissolved anger and contumacy.<br /> <br /> It rose with the truth in hand: Magic is a pure force. It did not corrupt those who wielded it for evil ends, they corrupted themselves. Magic could just as easily inspire, enrich, and protect lives. Magic is nothing more than raw potential, how one used it was up to them and them alone.<br /> <br /> As the revelation dawned on him, the Watchtower burned his palms. Instinctively removing his hands from the wall, he saw the word \u201cpotential\u201d written in High Speech on them, as well as on the wall itself when he looked up. Now, he understood. Now, he accepted.<br /> <br /> Now. he Awakened.<br /> <br /> <i>Awakened</i> - Upon returning to the Fallen World, he found all his comrades dead. With no other lead than the sorcerer, he doggedly chased them on the night of the Deathstorm. He couldn\u2019t find them, however, and the trail went cold since then. The next day, the Consilium contacted him, telling him the basics of his new condition. They recommended him to come up with a Shadow Name for protection and a new identity for his new life.<br /> <br /> \u201cPhoenix,\u201d he answered before they could finish explaining, \u201cI died in fire, yet was reborn as something different. Phoenix.\u201d<br /> <br /> When asked if he had any questions for them, he asked if they knew about a mage that killed his comrades. They didn\u2019t know, so Phoenix immediately left, he had nothing more to learn or say. Since then, he\u2019s been drowning his grief in training, teaching, and alcohol. However, that will only get him so far...<br /> <br /> <u><b>Personality</b></u><br /> Phoenix is very much a what-you-see-is-what-you-get type of person. He never wore a mask and probably will never fully understand why some people do that. He was also never one to take anyone's bullshit, no matter how much authority they had. If he feels like punching you in the face for making some snark, well, expect to have a fist in your face then. He's not stupid, though. Experience has taught him that punching authority figures results in lots of trouble. That doesn't mean he'll take things lying down, he'll just counter in a way that gives him less trouble.<br /> <br /> A lover of mythology, quite a bit of his free time is spent in the local library with his nose in a book. His Awakened perspective has not only enhanced his appreciation for the classics, but it's also given him some unique insight into the world. The tale is what's real, not the tired laws of science. He is the Hero of his own story, as is everyone else to theirs. While this perspective does give him a rare degree of compassion, seeing everyone as necessary to fill out their own roles in the world, it does tend to make his thinking rigid. He might make assumptions about how one's story is supposed to go, or certain possibilities about what could happen won't enter his mind.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Daily Life</b></u><br /> Phoenix works as a martial arts teacher at the local dojo (many students who have watched a little too much anime have taken to calling him Royce-sensei). This was very practical as a former Hunter, as it helped pay the bills and he spent his down time training and keeping in shape, not to mention it was one of the things he was good at. The leader of his cell owned the house he lives in. With them gone, their next of kin decided to let him have the house, seeing as he was a good friend to the previous owner and had a job. Unfortunately, the bills are a bit too big for his income to handle all alone, so he\u2019s looking for some roommates.</div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Experience Log</b></span></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Beats:</b> 0/5<br /> <b>Experiences (Unspent/Total):</b> 1/2<br /> <b>Arcane Beats:</b> 2/5<br /> <b>Arcane Experiences (Unspent/Total):</b> 1/1<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dots Purchased - XP Cost</b></u><ul><li>1 dot in Defensive Combat (Weaponry) Merit - 1 Experience</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 07-07-2017, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:50:31-07:00","id":926766,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I think part of how rotes work isn't as clear compared to wording in 1E, so I wanted to clarify this. <br /> <br /> The skill that each Rote is encoded in may or may not be one of your Order's rote skills. I will allow you to pick a different skill than the ones listed as suggestions in the book, but it still needs to be at least loosely related to the symbolism of the spell. For Warding Gesture, for example, I don't think Expression makes sense. Most of the suggested skills have to do with hiding or protecting yourself. Speak with Beasts makes sense to me for Expression, so that one I'm ok with too. But Locate Object I'd also prefer something different. <br /> <br /> If the skill happens to line up with the Order rote skill, you get +1 to the roll. Your standard skill specialties do not apply to the roll, because those refer to mundane skill checks, not spell casting.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I want you to get significant benefit out of using a rote because the experience cost is meaningful. I'll be lenient with letting you pick skills that are a stretch if it lets you have a higher skill bonus. But remember that some other member of your Order is passing down a way of casting that another master created, probably decades or centuries ago, not just using skills that your character is good at or their own spell adding style. Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Typo 07-05-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T19:46:25-07:00","id":926788,"title":"","content":"Oh, my bad, I thought the skill had to be one of the Order's rote skills, which was why everything was Expression! Well that makes this much easier! I'll use Occult for both Warding Gesture and Locate Object, since that's a recommended skill for both rotes. I'll keep Hung Spell as Expression, since that's both a recommended rote skill and an Order rote skill. Sorry for all the difficulties, for some reason I was interpreting the stuff on rotes to be very specific. Would have been a lot easier if I just asked, my bad.<br /> <br /> Yes, that does make sense. Sorry, when I was reading the core book I somehow interpreted the text about rote skills to mean that you <i>have</i> to use one of those skills. Maybe I missed the part where the book explained that isn't the case, but that was the impression I got. Very sorry, that should be the last bit of confusion over rotes that I have! Praxes were much easier for me to understand, for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T19:47:57-07:00","id":926789,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Love the NPC descriptions for Hakim's old cabal! I'll think of ways to incorporate them into the story in some way. One or more may reach out to some of you and offer mentorship. I think some may be initially distant with Moonstone because they associate him with Hakim's seemingly hubristic philosophy. However, i imagine they would ultimately sympathize with Moonstone after his Awakening as a result of pity for him after Hakim's death. Phoenix may learn about Hakim from one of them, after pursuing the Arrow.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Thanks for putting the new character sheet post up. I updated my link on the OP. The info looks great!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - If there are any other NPCs you think would have meaningful relationships with Ragnar, pre- or post-Awakening, feel free to post ideas here. Otherwise, no worries, I think the info you've provided is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T19:57:44-07:00","id":926792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=926788#post926788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, my bad, I thought the skill had to be one of the Order's rote skills, which was why everything was Expression! Well that makes this much easier! I'll use Occult for both Warding Gesture and Locate Object, since that's a recommended skill for both rotes. I'll keep Hung Spell as Expression, since that's both a recommended rote skill and an Order rote skill. Sorry for all the difficulties, for some reason I was interpreting the stuff on rotes to be very specific. Would have been a lot easier if I just asked, my bad.<br /> <br /> Yes, that does make sense. Sorry, when I was reading the core book I somehow interpreted the text about rote skills to mean that you <i>have</i> to use one of those skills. Maybe I missed the part where the book explained that isn't the case, but that was the impression I got. Very sorry, that should be the last bit of confusion over rotes that I have! Praxes were much easier for me to understand, for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, no worries. This has been one of my annoyances with the World of Darkness books in general: I never quite know where to find some critical info because it's not always clear. They may or may not tweak layout stuff with the final (non-advance) PDF version. <br /> <br /> Once we get the game's IC thread up and running, this will be the ideal spot to post questions and clarifications about in-game events. Please always feel free to ask! I hope I've made it clear that my ST style is to encourage players' ideas and make the game fun (but fair) for everyone. If you prefer to ask a question privately, you can always PM me too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T20:34:23-07:00","id":926814,"title":"","content":"I did give Ragnar a Mentor, so I think I should touch on that. <br /> <br /> Dr. Jacob Langley is a stuffy old English professor (as in, actually from England) who teaches art history at UChicago. Ragnar met Langley during orientation week, and Langley took an immediate liking to the young man, which surprised many who know the distant Langley immensely. Ragnar supposes that Langley sees him as an old soul who can appreciate cultural artifacts of by-gone ages. Langley's real passion is antiquities, and possesses a rather shocking breadth of knowledge about them. Additionally, Langley has expressed willingness to help Ragnar get through grad school, and has even offered to lend him aid in other fields as well. In return, Langley asks that Ragnar aid him in his personal research projects, and spend a couple hours a week in the library to help find references to specific artifacts in literature and historical documents. Ragnar sometimes suspects that there is more than meets the eye to Langley, and he sometimes thinks that Langley believes the same about him. <br /> <br /> Mechanically, Langley possess the Crafts and Politics skills, and the Resources merit. The Crafts represents Langley's knowledge of archaeology and antiquities, and the Politics chiefly represents putting in a word where necessary to help Ragnar deal with administration and staff at UChicago. The Resources represents a willingness to lend Ragnar resources and supplies when needed, perhaps even lending an artifact for &quot;independent&quot; studies. I did see Langley as some sort of supernatural being who recognizes or suspects that Ragnar is a mage, and is willing to give him a helping hand for his own reasons. I don't really have any particular kind of being in mind, though. Ideally, I would like Langley's true nature- if he has one, he may just be a Sleeper who has taken a shine to Ragnar- to become an Obsession for Ragnar, or maybe an Aspiration that leads Ragnar to develop an obsession with whatever kind of being Langley ultimately turns out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T21:42:51-07:00","id":926835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=926789#post926789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Love the NPC descriptions for Hakim's old cabal! I'll think of ways to incorporate them into the story in some way. One or more may reach out to some of you and offer mentorship. I think some may be initially distant with Moonstone because they associate him with Hakim's seemingly hubristic philosophy. However, i imagine they would ultimately sympathize with Moonstone after his Awakening as a result of pity for him after Hakim's death. Phoenix may learn about Hakim from one of them, after pursuing the Arrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since Askia is also a self-defense instructor like Phoenix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=926789#post926789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Thanks for putting the new character sheet post up. I updated my link on the OP. The info looks great!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I do try! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hopefully I can update this post and have it seen.<br /> <br /> Little side note, anything within angled brackets (&lt;&gt;) is something that will be added later. So the Order benefits are placed within angled brackets because he hasn't joined the Adamantine Arrow yet. Also, because I'm an artist, I'll be drawing up Phoenix myself, so I'll have a picture up soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T22:14:19-07:00","id":926854,"title":"","content":"Oh, nice! I very much would like to have an image of dear Phoenix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T06:53:05-07:00","id":927023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=926835#post926835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, because I'm an artist, I'll be drawing up Phoenix myself, so I'll have a picture up soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! I never could draw people, it always ended up looking really weird. Hence scouring the internet for pictures of people who look close enough to the image in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T19:13:58-07:00","id":927399,"title":"","content":"Finished off Nimbus details, added Aspirations. Is it alright if I leave Obsession to be filled in during the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T03:49:31-07:00","id":927529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927399#post927399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finished off Nimbus details, added Aspirations. Is it alright if I leave Obsession to be filled in during the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would prefer if you came up with one now, and then if you decide that one fits better or don't like it, I'll let you change it. Obsessions influence social maneuvering, give ways to earn arcane beats and mana, and affect other certain rolls like focused Mage sight for related Mysteries. <br /> <br /> Obsessions could be really straightforward if you're stuck. Maybe gain a new dot of Gnosis or an Arcanum, use focused Mage sight during a Highstorm, or enter another realm other than the material world (e.g., the Shadow).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:02:34-07:00","id":927622,"title":"","content":"OK, in that case I think my starting Obsession will be &quot;Interact with ephemeral entities&quot; (unless you think that that's too generic) and I'll change my first Aspiration to &quot;perform a summoning ritual&quot; (unless that seems to close to double-dipping).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:18:31-07:00","id":927625,"title":"","content":"Works for me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's the only thing I think you had left for your character to be ready that I could see. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Did you decide which Forces 2 attainment you wanted to go with? Otherwise, I think you're all set. <br /> <br /> I think everyone else is all set, too. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> - When you have a chance, please copy/paste the rest of that info to your character sheet post so I can find it more easily. <br /> <br /> I'll try to get more info up today about La Grange, answer any remaining questions, and then we can finally try to get some stuff on the road! Thanks for your patience this week. It's hard to be productive when you're sitting on the beach all day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:11:33-07:00","id":927641,"title":"","content":"Quick questions about Arcanum attainments: the experience chart states that Legacy attainments have an experience cost, but it doesn't mention regular non-Legacy attainments. Does this mean that attainments tied to Arcanum are acquired automatically? And can you only have one Arcanum attainment per dot in each Arcanum (i.e., you can have Precise Force at Force 2 or Force Mage Armor at Force two, but not both)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:23:30-07:00","id":927643,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a>, my take on it is as follows, quoted from the relevant passages, with emphasis mine:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Attainments are available to all mages as their understanding of magic (as measured by the Arcana) increases. As a mage\u2019s rating in an Arcanum increases, she gains access to new Attainments. <u><b>The Orders instruct their members on how to use these abilities</b></u>, but the instruction bears more resemblance to conditioning in athletics or fundamental principles in mathematics. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lesser Utilities <u><b>(i.e., the Attainments gained from 2 dots in an Arcanum)</b></u> are Attainments that fit into the purview of the Arcana, but don\u2019t map to the Practices and rely more on a general understanding of the Arcanum in question than of specific spells. Below are some of the most common Lesser Utilities, <u><b>though the players and the Storyteller may devise others.</b></u> </div> </div> </div>There are no limits to the number of Arcana attainments you can have by default. The fact that they're more like techniques suggests that, when you join an Order, they simply teach you the Attainments in the same way that they teach you Rotes and High Speech. For balancing purposes, I would argue that you would have to pay an experience cost for other Utility Attainments, in the same vein that you'd have to pay for Legacy Attainments, but that's ST's discretion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 07-07-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:59:14-07:00","id":927657,"title":"","content":"My understanding is a little different.<br /> <br /> For non-legacy attainments, you &quot;unlock&quot; all of them for free as you gain new dots in Arcana. You gain each of them for a certain level as indicated. So, for example, at 2 dots you get a Lesser Utility <i>and</i> Mage Armor for that Arcanum. There is no experience cost for these. <br /> <br /> The reason I asked <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> about Phoenix is because he had previously created an alternative Lesser Utility attainment for Forces and asked me if he could use it instead. I don't think he has settled on which of the two he wants, which is why I mentioned it. <br /> <br /> As for having multiple Lesser Utility attainments per Arcanum (or multiple attainments at any new dot level), I don't think that's what the books suggest. I think they mean you can pick alternate effects to substitute for the original ones, kind of like how in D&amp;D some people make alternate class features or design new feats with DM permission. Because attainments are not subject to dissonance and do not provoke paradox, and especially because gaining additional attainments is one of the key reasons to invest in a Legacy, I would prefer not to allow players to create and purchase additional non-legacy attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T10:03:35-07:00","id":927661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927657#post927657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is a little different.<br /> <br /> For non-legacy attainments, you &quot;unlock&quot; all of them for free as you gain new dots in Arcana. You gain each of them for a certain level as indicated. So, for example, at 2 dots you get a Lesser Utility <i>and</i> Mage Armor for that Arcanum. There is no experience cost for these.<br /> <br /> The reason I asked <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> about Phoenix is because he had previously created an alternative Lesser Utility attainment for Forces and asked me if he could use it instead. I don't think he has settled on which of the two he wants, which is why I mentioned it.<br /> <br /> As for having multiple Lesser Utility attainments per Arcanum (or multiple attainments at any new dot level), I don't think that's what the books suggest. I think they mean you can pick alternate effects to substitute for the original ones, kind of like how in D&amp;D some people make alternate class features or design new feats with DM permission. Because attainments are not subject to dissonance and do not provoke paradox, and especially because gaining additional attainments is one of the key reasons to invest in a Legacy, I would prefer not to allow players to create and purchase additional non-legacy attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had forgotten that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> had mentioned doing an alternate attainment, so I thought he was stuck on picking one, and I momentarily wondered if I had grossly misinterpreted the text again like I had with rotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T10:28:15-07:00","id":927673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927657#post927657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is a little different.<br /> <br /> For non-legacy attainments, you &quot;unlock&quot; all of them for free as you gain new dots in Arcana. You gain each of them for a certain level as indicated. So, for example, at 2 dots you get a Lesser Utility <i>and</i> Mage Armor for that Arcanum. There is no experience cost for these.<br /> <br /> The reason I asked <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> about Phoenix is because he had previously created an alternative Lesser Utility attainment for Forces and asked me if he could use it instead. I don't think he has settled on which of the two he wants, which is why I mentioned it.<br /> <br /> As for having multiple Lesser Utility attainments per Arcanum (or multiple attainments at any new dot level), I don't think that's what the books suggest. I think they mean you can pick alternate effects to substitute for the original ones, kind of like how in D&amp;D some people make alternate class features or design new feats with DM permission. Because attainments are not subject to dissonance and do not provoke paradox, and especially because gaining additional attainments is one of the key reasons to invest in a Legacy, I would prefer not to allow players to create and purchase additional non-legacy attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perfectly reasonable.<br /> <br /> I have to ask though, where does it say that Legacy attainments don't provoke Paradox or incite Quiescence? I know that was the case in 1st Edition, but I can't find the passage for this in 2nd Ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:32:52-07:00","id":927706,"title":"","content":"I'm having a hard time finding good info on my phone, because I don't have a search feature. But attainments aren't spells, and paradox is only caused by spellcasting or reaching. I'm pretty sure dissonance and quiescence only apply to spells, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:07:54-07:00","id":927723,"title":"","content":"I think what frustrates me is the lack of clarity in the book - or maybe I'm just daft. It does say that a Legacy Attainment is, paraphrased, &quot;invoking an internalised Praxis from her reshaped soul, rather than reaching into the Supernal&quot; - and spellcasting is invoking the Supernal directly. So you're right that Legacy Attainments can't invoke Paradox. I wish the rulebook could spell it out more clearly, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Curse strikes a Sleeper when she sees obvious magic, either during the spell\u2019s casting or encountering its effects later. </div> </div> </div>Page 298. A blatant Legacy Attainment, e.g., a Tamer of Fire's manipulation of fire, could be defined as &quot;obvious magic&quot; - yet, as mentioned above, it is an effect from a reshaped soul, rather than drawn from the Supernal... <br /> <br /> This frustrates me. I'll not dispute your ruling either way, and I appreciate the insight. <br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to the campaign! Got an ETA on when it kicks off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:13:21-07:00","id":927728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927723#post927723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what frustrates me is the lack of clarity in the book - or maybe I'm just daft. It does say that a Legacy Attainment is, paraphrased, &quot;invoking an internalised Praxis from her reshaped soul, rather than reaching into the Supernal&quot; - and spellcasting is invoking the Supernal directly. So you're right that Legacy Attainments can't invoke Paradox. I wish the rulebook could spell it out more clearly, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Page 298. A blatant Legacy Attainment, e.g., a Tamer of Fire's manipulation of fire, could be defined as &quot;obvious magic&quot; - yet, as mentioned above, it is an effect from a reshaped soul, rather than drawn from the Supernal...<br /> <br /> This frustrates me. I'll not dispute your ruling either way, and I appreciate the insight.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to the campaign! Got an ETA on when it kicks off?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> said that he was on vacation until the 11th. So I'm assuming some time after that. Can't wait to get this Chronicle started, so excited!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:14:23-07:00","id":927729,"title":"","content":"If I find a clearer explanation I'll let you know, and if it contradicts my current ruling, I'll change it accordingly. <br /> <br /> Aiming to start the game in a few days at best. Right now it looks like everyone is waiting on me. I just need to add some more info about La Grange, double check that everyone is all set, and start the IC thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:18:10-07:00","id":927731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927728#post927728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I remember correctly, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> said that he was on vacation until the 11th. So I'm assuming some time after that. Can't wait to get this Chronicle started, so excited!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, still that long, huh... the anticipation is keeping me tense.<br /> <br /> Lynx has only been in Chicaco for a couple of days now - I believe Oscar has met Simon through the FYS, but I don't know if Lynx has met Ragnar. Got any thoughts about that, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927729#post927729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I find a clearer explanation I'll let you know, and if it contradicts my current ruling, I'll change it accordingly.<br /> <br /> Aiming to start the game in a few days at best. Right now it looks like everyone is waiting on me. I just need to add some more info about La Grange, double check that everyone is all set, and start the IC thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appreciated! You have my trust either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:18:29-07:00","id":927755,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> Looking over the section on Mage Sight, Active Mage Sight is required to see another mage's Nimbus flare, and unless Lynx does something that catches Ragnar's Peripheral Sight, I don't think Ragnar would have cause to scrutinize Oscar with Focused Sight. At this point, I think the only things that put Oscar on Ragnar's radar are the fact that Oscar is a student in the FYS that Ragnar is T.A. for, and that he might find Oscar attractive.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to a point that I've been meaning to run by everybody, but been hesitant to bring up: out of all our entire cabal, there is one straight male, a lesbian, a queer male, two bisexual males, and a gay male. How does everybody feel about doing romance in this Chronicle? Specifically, between PCs and NPCs or even between cabal-mates? I don't think that would be an issue for Dr. Asphodel or Binder, since one is a divorced lesbian dealing with the fallout from her divorce and Binder is a straight family man, but in-universe, I don't see anything stopping Lynx, Moonstone, Phoenix, or Ragnar from developing an interest in each other and wanting to act on it.<br /> <br /> So I would like to hear from all the other players and our ST about comfort levels dealing with this subject matter, and what everybody thinks is okay and not okay.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm fine with any of the members of the cabal participating in romantic scenes. I think if it's done right, it could add some drama to the Chronicle. I would even be fine with romances between PCs developing. That said, I don't want the game to get bogged down in romance, and I would be uncomfortable with having to get into nitty-gritty details- if there's intimacy, I would be perfectly content with scenes &quot;fading to black&quot; where necessary and picking back up when the deed is done. Some of the best Chronicles I have read involved PCs exploring their feelings for other characters, including romantic feelings, and never once did those scenes rise above anything that I would consider PG or at most, PG-13.<br /> <br /> Of course, I could be committing a major faux pas even discussing this, so if I am, I'm sorry. I just know from reading the core books for the 2e games that romantic and sexual relationships, including LGBT ones, do get touched on fairly frequently in the books. I don't mean for this to sound like a demand on my part- &quot;Romance or I'm out!&quot; or something- but it was just a scenario that crossed my mind- &quot;Hey, should we talk about the possibility of romance?&quot;- and I wanted to express how I felt about it and see how everybody else felt, and then make a decision. So to recap: I'm not opposed to romance being an element in the Chronicle, and I would not be opposed to roleplaying a romantic scene between Ragnar and a ST character- or another PC, if the other player was willing and didn't feel uncomfortable with the prospect. I do, however, think that romance, if included, should be used as a tool to get characters to reveal elements of themselves and to establish connections with other characters -i.e., to explain their motivation to another character in an organic way, or to establish or deepen a connection with that character- and I don't want romance to become the focus of the Chronicle. I'm also unwilling to role-play scenes once they get beyond talk, and would want those scenes to politely &quot;bow out&quot; and pick up later.<br /> <br /> That's my position on the issue. How does everybody else feel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":".  Edited to clarify position 07-07-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:53:55-07:00","id":927771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927755#post927755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my position on the issue. How does everybody else feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm OK with pretty much anything. Obviously I think Binder will probably be only interacting romantically with Daisy and I don't expect he'll be involved in anything explicit. I'm OK with things being more explicit (as long as the scene has a point and it isn't just pornographic roleplaying) but I'm also OK with the bar being set lower if it's what makes people more comfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:56:02-07:00","id":927772,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with romance as part of the story, whether PC/NPC or PC/PC, as long as it's used to enrich the story and/or characters involved. I agree that things should fade to black before it gets too heavy.<br /> <br /> In Vo's case, it would take some time for her to become open to romance again, but that could be a fruitful area of character development should it happen.<br /> <br /> Also, I'll try to get my sheet post updated tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T14:24:07-07:00","id":927777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927755#post927755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking over the section on Mage Sight, Active Mage Sight is required to see another mage's Nimbus flare, and unless Lynx does something that catches Ragnar's Peripheral Sight, I don't think Ragnar would have cause to scrutinize Oscar with Focused Sight. At this point, I think the only things that put Oscar on Ragnar's radar are the fact that Oscar is a student in the FYS that Ragnar is T.A. for, and that he might find Oscar attractive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oscar does use his magic, but not a lot - and not (much) in public. Unless <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> objects, though, I think it would be interesting if they find out they have magic in common in-character as part of the first chapter or plot - maybe as Oscar does use magic for the first time around Ragnar...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927755#post927755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to a point that I've been meaning to run by everybody...<br /> <br /> ...That's my position on the issue. How does everybody else feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind romance as part of the campaign, so long as it's a tool for character development.<br /> <br /> I agree that romance shouldn't be focal - this isn't 50 Shades of La Grange or Twilight: Supernal Suburbia Edition (I hope...). If it seems like something's blossoming between two characters, the players can discuss it behind the scenes - through private messages or some other means - relay the development to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> so he can take it into account, and then let it play out through in-character interactions. If the scene's going somewhere sexual, it probably should just fade to black.<br /> <br /> I don't think you made a faux pas, by the way. I appreciate you bringing it up. It's best that we're all on the same page, after all.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a>: since Vo teaches Oscar's FYS and they've met that way, does she know Oscar's Awakened? Does she know Ragnar is as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 07-07-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:14:29-07:00","id":927822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927625#post927625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Did you decide which Forces 2 attainment you wanted to go with? Otherwise, I think you're all set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I chose Precise Force. I also changed the Rote Skill of Mental Scan to Occult from Empathy, mostly because I plan on raising Occult since it's so useful for mages to have and makes perfect sense for Phoenix to learn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927755#post927755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to a point that I've been meaning to run by everybody, but been hesitant to bring up...<br /> <br /> ...That's my position on the issue. How does everybody else feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering when this was gonna be brought up. The reason I didn't is because to be frank, I don't really care about it all that much. That said, I'm all for romance as a means of exploring the characters and story. I personally don't mind reading XXX material so long as it's tasteful and has an actual purpose (same thing goes for things like gore, insanity, and other mature subjects). Although, if others would rather those scenes simply &quot;fade to black&quot;, I'm okay with that, too.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to second KKV on you not making a faux pas. It is a legitimate subject to bring up. Think about it, if it was a faux pas to bring up romance and sex, yet it's somehow not so to bring up extreme violence, depraved acts, horrifying revelations, and other horror elements, it would be kinda hypocritical.<br /> <br /> Anyways, from Phoenix's end, he just lost his comrades. It's also quite likely that he's had romantic feelings for one of them (I haven't thought too far on the cell as characters, mostly because I wanna keep Phoenix's hunting part of his storyline open for another game). He's grieving, and he's still in the denial stage because he's burying his feelings in work, exercise, and alcohol. So, he can either: shut off from romance completely due to shutting off his emotions, or he could be too eager to get into the game as another means of burying his grief.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure which one to go for. The first one would be easier to roleplay, but it could possibly shut off plot hooks. The second one would make Phoenix more dynamic in that particular area, but it might be inappropriate. Any thoughts on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:36:04-07:00","id":927832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927822#post927822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, from Phoenix's end, he just lost his comrades. It's also quite likely that he's had romantic feelings for one of them (I haven't thought too far on the cell as characters, mostly because I wanna keep Phoenix's hunting part of his storyline open for another game). He's grieving, and he's still in the denial stage because he's burying his feelings in work, exercise, and alcohol. So, he can either: shut off from romance completely due to shutting off his emotions, or he could be too eager to get into the game as another means of burying his grief.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure which one to go for. The first one would be easier to roleplay, but it could possibly shut off plot hooks. The second one would make Phoenix more dynamic in that particular area, but it might be inappropriate. Any thoughts on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both? 8D<br /> <br /> Seriously, though: sober Phoenix is all apathetic work and exercise, the drunk one all too eager to find something resembling happiness in a self-destructive manner - y'know, the Jekyll/Hyde approach, the perfect solution if you want a trainwreck of sizable proportions?<br /> <br /> <br /> If it's one or the other, though, I see merit in both. If I consider Lynx's perspective, seeing somebody who essentially represses himself in denial and grief would definitely make him want to try to help - drama ahoy! The second option is, of course, more dynamic. Again, from Lynx's perspective, indulgence is great and all, but I think he would be able to tell that Phoenix's doing it to compensate, and will, in turn want to help. If it's an issue of propriety, I reckon we'll communicate if it goes too far, and you'll adjust accordingly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:53:36-07:00","id":927836,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - I really appreciate you bringing this up and the maturity with which you asked to discuss it. This actually is on my list of things I wanted to discuss before we got the IC thread up and running (more on that in a minute).<br /> <br /> I would prefer to limit &quot;on screen&quot; interactions to PG-13 or R at most. I appreciate that CoD games are adult in nature, and I know there are going to be adult themes (violence, murder, sexuality) throughout the game. But I'm personally not comfortable with X-rated scenes and would prefer the &quot;fade to black&quot; approach. <br /> <br /> If characters want to be involved with each other romantically, as with all other significant drama related to the PCs, I'm fine with it as long as all players involved are fine with it OOCly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:14:01-07:00","id":927843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927777#post927777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a>: since Vo teaches Oscar's FYS and they've met that way, does she know Oscar's Awakened? Does she know Ragnar is as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a yes to Oscar; not 100% sure on Ragnar, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:17:40-07:00","id":927846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927843#post927843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a yes to Oscar; not 100% sure on Ragnar, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. How'd you figure she knows a student's Awakened, but not her TA?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:19:21-07:00","id":927847,"title":"","content":"Good point, now that you bring it up---sorry, brain's a little fried today. Probably she'd know both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:34:29-07:00","id":927863,"title":"","content":"Vo having Prime 1 would make it logical that she knows Oscar is Awakened. That doesn't necessarily mean she's approached him outside of lectures... though you're the professor and he's a student. Lynx wouldn't know how to find other Awakened, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T18:51:17-07:00","id":927892,"title":"","content":"I don't have an issue with including romance/relationship elements in the game, although I'm not personally interested in playing that with another PC. For Moonstone, his main thing is the weird and unlabeled &quot;It's Complicated&quot; relationship he had with Hakim, and I'd definitely like to have that as an issue he's working through and look back on it with Time or Mind. Actually, in line with his fractured perceptions, I keep thinking it would be an interesting little Mystery if he has a few memories of their time that appear differently through Postcognition and Perfect Recall. Either his mind has been messed with or the record of Time has, or both, really. I'm interested in playing someone who firmly holds a belief even when it's not supported by the evidence, defiantly and desperately rejecting reality in the way that mages do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T19:23:57-07:00","id":927904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927836#post927836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - I really appreciate you bringing this up and the maturity with which you asked to discuss it. This actually is on my list of things I wanted to discuss before we got the IC thread up and running (more on that in a minute).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Thank you. It just kind of flashed into my head that romance could be an element of the Chronicle, and I figured I may as well bring it up since we were getting close to starting the Chronicle. PG-13 sounds sufficient. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> I'm thinking that a situation in which Lynx, Ragnar, and Asphodel are forced to use magic in front of each other could work: the spells would trip their Peripheral Sight, and when they attempt to use Active Sight, they would realize that they are all mages- and forced to make a snap decision on how to react to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T19:46:23-07:00","id":927914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927904#post927904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Thank you. It just kind of flashed into my head that romance could be an element of the Chronicle, and I figured I may as well bring it up since we were getting close to starting the Chronicle. PG-13 sounds sufficient. <br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I'm thinking that a situation in which Lynx, Ragnar, and Asphodel are forced to use magic in front of each other could work: the spells would trip their Peripheral Sight, and when they attempt to use Active Sight, they would realize that they are all mages- and forced to make a snap decision on how to react to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was already thinking about this, too. Most likely I will have them encounter something supernatural that demands a response when they're just getting out of class. <br /> <br /> You've all created a lot of neat ideas for plot hooks. The reason I asked everyone to have some kind of association with other PCs is so it makes it easier to facilitate this part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:10:57-07:00","id":928191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927904#post927904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that a situation in which Lynx, Ragnar, and Asphodel are forced to use magic in front of each other could work: the<br /> spells would trip their Peripheral Sight, and when they attempt to use Active Sight, they would realize that they are all mages- and forced to make a snap decision on how to react to this.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927914#post927914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was already thinking about this, too. Most likely I will have them encounter something supernatural that demands a response when they're just getting out of class.<br /> <br /> You've all created a lot of neat ideas for plot hooks. The reason I asked everyone to have some kind of association with other PCs is so it makes it easier to facilitate this part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I approve of this suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 07-08-2016, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:40:20-07:00","id":928221,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty rad to me---is this to be played out in-game, or something that already happened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:53:43-07:00","id":928264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=928221#post928221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds pretty rad to me---is this to be played out in-game, or something that already happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why waste the opportunity to let us get a chance to test our spells? I say we play it out! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:39:45-07:00","id":928442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=928264#post928264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why waste the opportunity to let us get a chance to test our spells? I say we play it out! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would plan to do it in-game and make it very early on, probably one of your first scenes for those characters if not the very beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:20:16-07:00","id":928464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927904#post927904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> I'm thinking that a situation in which Lynx, Ragnar, and Asphodel are forced to use magic in front of each other could work: the spells would trip their Peripheral Sight, and when they attempt to use Active Sight, they would realize that they are all mages- and forced to make a snap decision on how to react to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could then possibly have Moonstone, Binder, and Phoenix meet up in their own scene, then another scene connecting both groups of three together.<br /> <br /> No doubt Phoenix would be looking for Hakim, it's his Obsession after all. However, with the trail cold, he'll be looking for clues anywhere he could possibly find them, so that leads him to Binder's occult shop with Binder and Moonstone there. Then a situation occurs forcing them all to use magic and discover they're all mages, yadda yadda blo blah blah.<br /> <br /> Then, it turns out the two situations are interrelated, leading the two groups of three to each other and all finding each other out. Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:24:56-07:00","id":928467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=928464#post928464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We could then possibly have Moonstone, Binder, and Phoenix meet up in their own scene, then another scene connecting both groups of three together.<br /> <br /> No doubt Phoenix would be looking for Hakim, it's his Obsession after all. However, with the trail cold, he'll be looking for clues anywhere he could possibly find them, so that leads him to Binder's occult shop with Binder and Moonstone there. Then a situation occurs forcing them all to use magic and discover they're all mages, yadda yadda blo blah blah.<br /> <br /> Then, it turns out the two situations are interrelated, leading the two groups of three to each other and all finding each other out. Just an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking about that: Dr. Asphodel, Lynx, and Ragnar handling a situation at UChicago, and Binder, Moonstone, and Phoenix handling a situation either somewhere in Chicago or La Grange, and then the two trios following the trail from their respective incidents and bumping into each other, and then trying to work together to handle the source of the incidents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T16:04:14-07:00","id":928483,"title":"","content":"I don't know what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> has in mind, but that initial split sounds appealing to me. It occurs to me that one way of getting the two groups together as soon as possible would be that Moonstone and Ragnar both have Time, and might use Divination to ask &quot;where is all this leading/what are the implications of this?&quot; and end up in the same place.<br /> <br /> If Phoenix, Binder and Moonstone were all at his bookshop, an interesting wrinkle is that all three of us have at least Mind 2, which might color what we run into or how we deal with it. We also all have some knowledge of the occult already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T17:53:06-07:00","id":928535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=928483#post928483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> has in mind, but that initial split sounds appealing to me. It occurs to me that one way of getting the two groups together as soon as possible would be that Moonstone and Ragnar both have Time, and might use Divination to ask &quot;where is all this leading/what are the implications of this?&quot; and end up in the same place.<br /> <br /> If Phoenix, Binder and Moonstone were all at his bookshop, an interesting wrinkle is that all three of us have at least Mind 2, which might color what we run into or how we deal with it. We also all have some knowledge of the occult already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ragnar has Divination as a rote, so he wouldn't be able to cast it as such right off the bat. He and Moonstone could, however, both cast it as an improvised spell. It's just that Ragnar would get an additional reach on it because he's Fate 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T18:16:11-07:00","id":928541,"title":"","content":"I have ideas to get everyone together, and we'll get there soon! :P Don't worry about your magic &quot;spoiling&quot; or causing issues with the plot, the whole idea of Mage is that you should be able to do amazing things -- but with a potential cost for overreaching. <br /> <br /> I do have a question that I would like everyone's feedback on. How do you want to handle dice rolls?<br /> <br /> My preference for actually getting the numbers would be for people to use any online site that archives results, so you can direct perma-link to the results. I've used Coyote Code roller for this, but lately my favorite has been <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/?action=roll\" target=\"_blank\">Orokos</a> because I know I can load it at work.<br /> <br /> Some of the dice rolling issues can be discussed more easily in real time, like when a ST tells you what to subtract for Defense on a roll before you make it. For PbP games, I can tell you what to subtract before I have you roll. I can do Withstand effects for spell effects after the roll results without revealing what the withstand effect is, but I'll have to make Defense obvious. Is that ok? Does anyone else have any suggestions for rolling conventions for PBP games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T18:28:34-07:00","id":928544,"title":"","content":"Orokos is good for me.<br /> <br /> IMO a good way to deal with Defense and other dicepool penalties, if you haven't called for a roll yourself and told us what they are, is to ignore the last X dice in our pool (and tell us that you're doing that.) Like if we're in the middle of a scene and I spontaneously say &quot;I want to roll Wits+Politics (Consilium) to see if I know something about this guy&quot;, I would just roll 6d10 or whatever and post the results: 4, 8, 1, 1, 9, 2. Two successes.<br /> <br /> When you reply, you could then say &quot;Actually your Consilium specialty does not apply and there's a -1 penalty due to the obscurity of the information, so your dicepool would be 4d10 and the last two dice don't count.&quot; My result would be treated as 4, 8, 1, 1. Just the one success. Conversely you could also apply a bonus to the roll that I wasn't aware of, and roll 1 or 2 more dice yourself.<br /> <br /> The main advantage to doing things that way, at least having the option to do it that way when we suggest a roll ourselves, is to streamline things for PbP and have less back and forth. On the other hand, some players don't like the GM &quot;altering&quot; their result once they've already rolled, and that's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T18:41:10-07:00","id":928546,"title":"","content":"Since I've never down a PbP game before, I have no real preference. Some GMs tell their players to factor in bonuses and maluses for their own rolls, some GMs add or subtract from the rolls after the player rolls. We could try one and change to the other if we feel that it's not working to our satisfaction. <br /> <br /> All of the PbP games I've read include links to the rolls within the post itself to verify the roll. I take it you want that as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T19:12:36-07:00","id":928553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=928546#post928546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the PbP games I've read include links to the rolls within the post itself to verify the roll. I take it you want that as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that is what I would prefer. You make a good point though, we can always change it if necessary. As Caladriu pointed out, posting the direct link makes it easier to adjust rolls as needed. <br /> <br /> I would personally prefer to give you modifiers in advance and have you roll with them included, but I also like the idea of modifying rolls after the fact in some situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T03:16:36-07:00","id":928668,"title":"","content":"I've no real experience with PbPs and dice rolls outside of Paizo's forums. The suggestions thus far all seem appropriate, and I'll most likely be fine with whatever method chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T05:08:13-07:00","id":928691,"title":"","content":"I'm almost back home from my vacation. I have a wedding today and more driving tomorrow, but will hope to have some more info up for you tonight or tomorrow. Haven't had the time to put things up because I can do it much faster on a computer than my phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T07:33:04-07:00","id":928727,"title":"","content":"The &quot;drop the rightmost dice for unannounced penalties&quot; is how I've seen it done in the past, too. Obviously the best thing is when you can tell us which attribute+skill-penalty to roll, but sometimes its best if players can just toss a &quot;I roll to sneak&quot; without having to go back and forth about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T20:03:52-07:00","id":929027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=927832#post927832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both? 8D<br /> <br /> Seriously, though: sober Phoenix is all apathetic work and exercise, the drunk one all too eager to find something resembling happiness in a self-destructive manner - y'know, the Jekyll/Hyde approach, the perfect solution if you want a trainwreck of sizable proportions?<br /> <br /> If it's one or the other, though, I see merit in both. If I consider Lynx's perspective, seeing somebody who essentially represses himself in denial and grief would definitely make him want to try to help - drama ahoy! The second option is, of course, more dynamic. Again, from Lynx's perspective, indulgence is great and all, but I think he would be able to tell that Phoenix's doing it to compensate, and will, in turn want to help. If it's an issue of propriety, I reckon we'll communicate if it goes too far, and you'll adjust accordingly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking on it, the &quot;Jekyll/Hyde&quot; approach makes perfect sense (especially for someone who doesn't mind what package he's dealing with) and makes him even more dynamic in the area. Damn, that's a really nice idea. Thanks KKV! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for dice rolling, I don't mind signing up to Orokos, though I do want to refrain from signing up now because I don't want to make an account for something and then not use it. As for handling dice rolls, it's generally done as others have stated so far: make the roll, take dice away or make another roll adding to it if need be. Not much I can add to that, I'm afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:05:15-07:00","id":929041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=929027#post929027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thinking on it, the &quot;Jekyll/Hyde&quot; approach makes perfect sense (especially for someone who doesn't mind what package he's dealing with) and makes him even more dynamic in the area. Damn, that's a really nice idea. Thanks KKV! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for dice rolling, I don't mind signing up to Orokos, though I do want to refrain from signing up now because I don't want to make an account for something and then not use it. As for handling dice rolls, it's generally done as others have stated so far: make the roll, take dice away or make another roll adding to it if need be. Not much I can add to that, I'm afraid.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> Reading this, I'm starting to think that the three younger members of the cabal could have some really interesting chemistry. All three of them have the potential to really help each other grow or emotionally devastate each other, whether or not they get involved with each other. Phoenix is the guy who jumps in bed with you and then ignores you the following day because he doesn't know how to process it; Ragnar has basically been conditioned to take what he can when he can, but is afraid of screwing up a chance for something better; and Lynx is the eager young guy who doesn't really know any better. Three boys who know enough to go after what they want, and not enough to know not to go after it so greedily. <br /> <br /> Of course, their carrying-on would also affect the rest of the cabal: Dr. Asphodel and Moonstone watching their own experiences play out before them, and Binder trying desperately to keep the cabal from imploding.<br /> <br /> Could be fertile soil for some juicy character stuff, what do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 07-10-2016, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T03:52:46-07:00","id":929155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=929027#post929027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thinking on it, the &quot;Jekyll/Hyde&quot; approach makes perfect sense (especially for someone who doesn't mind what package he's dealing with) and makes him even more dynamic in the area. Damn, that's a really nice idea. Thanks KKV! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for dice rolling, I don'