"edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 07-11-2016, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:41:22-07:00","id":929944,"title":"","content":"Aaaaand <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\">IC thread is up</a>! Feel free to post whenever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You don't have to use Orokos if you don't want. Coyote code roller works too, or any dice roller that archives rolls.<br /> <br /> Please keep your character's name at the top of each post. I'll show a sample format later of what would help me keep your posts organized when I have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:03:42-07:00","id":929954,"title":"","content":"Gettin' on that posting. Also, Viv's address is 635 Mason Dr, La Grange, IL 60525 for whatever that's worth.<br /> <br /> Hope it's not too godmoddy of me to say that Lynx happens to be the one near the light switch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 07-11-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:49:31-07:00","id":929980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=929954#post929954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope it's not too godmoddy of me to say that Lynx happens to be the one near the light switch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind in the slightest, as I've just responded to that. <br /> <br /> Going to take a while for me to really get into PbP, so if my roleplaying is awkward, I blame newbie jitters. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:46:39-07:00","id":930057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=929524#post929524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - What do you want the name of your dojo to be? And just to clarify, do you go by Garrick Royce at the dojo? How many other instructors do you want there to be (if any)? What type of martial arts do you practice/teach? And does anyone there know Phoenix's sympathetic name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to my complete unfamiliarity with martial arts, I decided to look up actual martial arts schools in La Grange and found <a href=\"http://yonginmusa.com/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">YongIn Martial Arts</a> (not sure if there's supposed to be a space there, but that's how it's typed on the website). He goes by Garrick Royce there (as well as everywhere else in Sleeper society). There's a list of instructors on the website (though I'm not sure who works at which branch, considering the website is for both branches in the Chicago metropolis and La Grange, but for our purposes it's just a name list). The school teaches tae kwon do (emphasis on kicks, agility, and speed), hap ki do (emphasis on countering various types of attacks on reflex), and kum do (sword-fighting with a <i>reeeally</i> unfortunate name), Phoenix acts as a &quot;poly-filler&quot; instructor for each of these (Brawl 4 and Weaponry 3, but only Status 1). No one there knows of his sympathetic name.<br /> <br /> Reading the provided schedule, classes start from late afternoon to mid-evening on weekdays, with Saturday classes starting from late morning to mid-afternoon (no classes on Sunday). I can always give specific times if needed, but that should do for the most part.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I added the link on the character sheet for ease of reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 07-11-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:20:44-07:00","id":930072,"title":"","content":"And we're off! I've been waiting for this moment for a while. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T20:04:11-07:00","id":930134,"title":"","content":"Oh, bit of a side note, there's this webcomic based on a Mage chronicle that was also based in the Chicago area. It's called <a href=\"http://morphe.thewebcomic.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Morphe</a>, and it's an interesting read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T21:12:09-07:00","id":930155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=930072#post930072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we're off! I've been waiting for this moment for a while. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Me too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A few things I wanted to comment on now that I've got IC up and running. <br /> <br /> Please post at your own speed as your schedule allows, and don't feel obligated to post on any given day if you don't have time. I will generally try to post a few times a day, or at least daily, but that won't always be realistic for all of us at any given time. I encourage you to post at least once weekly just to keep things moving. If it feels like we're moving too slowly, I may move us along.<br /> <br /> I like what you've all done with the spoiler tag for rolls and OOC info, so I'll do that too. <br /> <br /> I am still learning the 2E rules. I'll try to take time to reference them before posting, but if I mess something up, please post in the OOC thread and let me know! I'm hoping to pick it up quickly but there is a lot to know. <br /> <br /> For Orokos dice roller, make sure your dice expression is set correctly. Normally it's xd10o10h8, where x=dice pool. If you have the 9- or 8-again property or rote quality on a roll, adjust the hX part or oX part accordingly. KKV, I think you had yours set to count 7s as a success. And anyone can ask for help if you need it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Periodically I will ask for feedback about my storytelling style and how you feel about the game overall. Please don't hesitate to give constructive criticism. I'm trying to grow as a ST here. I know from experience that I sometimes lean more naturally towards running sandbox kind of games than clear plot/story arcs, even when I'm trying to do the latter, but I'm trying to improve on how I create drama and conflict and clear antagonists. Please speak up or send a PM if you don't like something. <br /> <br /> In your posts, under your name, please add a line to include current spells you have active (even if none currently), and another line for conditions/tilts. On one of those lines you might also want to note when you have active or focused Mage sight on. This will help a lot in active conflict or combat situations, but also helps me remember what extra information you might pick up. <br /> <br /> My current plan for NPC rolls is to not post them here, but I'll still use Orokos. Is that ok with everyone, or would you prefer I post for transparency's sake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:28:57-07:00","id":930203,"title":"","content":"I will happily let you know if something's up or give any feedback I have! Don't worry, I think everyone is just happy to play. I appreciate the writing work you've done to describe just Mage Sight and the experience of spellcasting, it really sets the mood! I find it hard to do that consistently in person, I really like reading it and immersing myself a little.<br /> <br /> When you have any Active sight up, you can see what Arcanum a spell being cast is, so you're right with Phoenix seeing Time. I believe it also tells you generally what the spell is (&quot;a Time spell cast on himself,&quot; &quot;a Life spell cast on the guy she's fighting&quot;), because you have the opportunity to counterspell and I assume you're not meant to do that blind, but I'm not 100% sure.<br /> <br /> I'm totally okay with you not posting NPC rolls here to keep your posts clean, but it would be nice if they're on Orokos just to keep you honest. I trust you, do whatever!<br /> <br /> Also a note for the record now that I have a picture and description up in my sheet: Moonstone does look a bit younger than he should thanks to being around Life mages, but he's Marlin's age. I was thinking that when you described him as the young man at the library- the description's fine, just FYI, he's not in the college squad or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T01:24:27-07:00","id":930240,"title":"","content":"I could've sworn I had put an 8 there and not a 7. My bad, I'll be more vigilant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T14:14:02-07:00","id":930521,"title":"","content":"How many rolls are we permitted to make in a turn/post? Let's say I want to try and calm the class, and also make a Perception check to see if Ragnar notices that Dr. Asphodel is studying Lynx. Would that be permissible?<br /> <br /> Edit: Consulted the scorebook, looks like only one action per turn. I'll just try to pacify the class for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 07-12-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T16:47:40-07:00","id":930588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=930521#post930521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many rolls are we permitted to make in a turn/post? Let's say I want to try and calm the class, and also make a Perception check to see if Ragnar notices that Dr. Asphodel is studying Lynx. Would that be permissible?<br /> <br /> Edit: Consulted the scorebook, looks like only one action per turn. I'll just try to pacify the class for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think I am more flexible than that, especially with PbP games. Rather than letting the game slow down because you want back and forth for rolls, I'm ok with you including more than one action per post. If time or turns start to matter, I'll jump in and ask you to wait for something before you can take the second action, or call for initiative.<br /> <br /> Also, unless there's specifically something you're waiting on me to reply to in your post, you all are welcome to interact with each other in a back and forth fashion without me stepping in. We don't all have to post at a 1-to-1 ratio.<br /> <br /> On a related note in terms of game time: I'll indicate scene transitions, as that may matter for things like willpower costs for Mage Sight, etc. I'll also be breaking up chapters into reasonable chunks based on story arcs rather than game sessions, for obvious reasons. I'll sometimes grant beats or arcane beats mid-scene; if that gives you enough for a full experience or arcane experience point, you can spend it any time but the effects will kick in after the scene ends. In the case of things that need some kind of in-game time commitment, like some Merits (e.g., Resources), I may require you to wait until time between chapters. I'm planning to give &quot;interlude&quot; downtime between some chapters to indicate longer periods of down time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T17:55:36-07:00","id":930620,"title":"","content":"For everyone: Some of you have contacted me or noted it on your character sheet, but if there is an appropriate persistent Condition you'd like to have in effect on your character for purposes of adding drama and conflict to the game, feel free to do so. If there's one that you think would make sense but doesn't show up in the sample list in Appendix Three in the MtAw book, post here and let me know what you're thinking.<br /> <br /> Also, am I reading it correctly that <i>every</i> time you see someone cast a spell while having active Mage Sight on, you're affected by their nimbus tilt if potency is equal to or greater than your Resolve? I keep having to pull up everyone's character sheet to double check, and so far it hasn't been an issue, but I was curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T22:11:47-07:00","id":930717,"title":"","content":"Won't be able to post until tomorrow night due to things, sorry team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T22:19:30-07:00","id":930721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=930620#post930620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, am I reading it correctly that <i>every</i> time you see someone cast a spell while having active Mage Sight on, you're affected by their nimbus tilt if potency is equal to or greater than your Resolve? I keep having to pull up everyone's character sheet to double check, and so far it hasn't been an issue, but I was curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's right. At least, with how it's written. Though perhaps if it would get a little tedious, you could just limit being affected by the Tilt to once per scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T05:51:42-07:00","id":930803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=930721#post930721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's right. At least, with how it's written. Though perhaps if it would get a little tedious, you could just limit being affected by the Tilt to once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, if one of us is going to start throwing around spells that we know are probably going to inflict Nimbus Tilts, we could advise everybody else to look away or temporarily drop Mage Sight- you know, how sometimes people with guns tell people standing next to them to cover their ears. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> Do you want to pause our scene until Beans can get back to us? A day of posting shouldn't put us too far behind the others, and besides, Lynx and Ragar are waiting on Dr. Asphodel's orders to leave the room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T06:35:06-07:00","id":930823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=930803#post930803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> Do you want to pause our scene until Beans can get back to us? A day of posting shouldn't put us too far behind the others, and besides, Lynx and Ragar are waiting on Dr. Asphodel's orders to leave the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think so. I don't mind the delay either, so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a>, don't worry about it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","v