alue":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T00:19:16-07:00","id":941743,"title":"","content":"I actually laughed out loud because it was adorable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T04:08:42-07:00","id":941816,"title":"","content":"The Doc may or may not ship it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:00:00-07:00","id":941876,"title":"","content":"Ragnar and Lynx, Supernal Suburbia's first OTP. Go get that mushroom, Ragnar!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:53:13-07:00","id":941911,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - I'd like to slow down here for a second and back up on your most recent post. There's a few things going on that either I don't understand what you're trying to accomplish, or you're misunderstanding something about the rules -- which is totally understandable for our game's first attempt at casting sympathetically!<br /> <br /> First, Moonstone wants you to use his hair as a sympathetic Yantra to be able to track him and cast spells on him from a distance. In mechanical terms, per p. 173, when used as a sympathetic Yantra his hair counts as a Strong connection. However, because you don't know Moonstone's sympathetic name, the Withstand rating is 2. Any spell you cast on him will thus have -2 Potency, so it needs to be at least Potency 3 to work on him at a distance. (On a tangent, this is why I asked <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> to pick a sympathetic name.) Remember that using an item as a sympathetic Yantra allows you to cast at sympathetic range with your Space 2 attainment, but it still counts as one of your possible Yantra for the spell casting and doesn't confer a dice bonus for the roll. If you want to use another Yantra, such as a tool, you can't cast reflexively and will need at least 2 turns to do so. That might matter when we're in initiative.<br /> <br /> Second, the Borrow Threads spell essentially allows you to siphon sympathetic connections from someone else, which can allow you to do a number of useful things, but it's not necessary to cast on Moonstone sympathetically. For instance, you could transfer the connection from his hair sample to yourself, so now <i>you</i> have a direct Strong link to Moonstone for the duration of your spell. Or, you could steal the connection from Moonstone to gain a stronger connection to one of his close friends or mentors, which would then let you cast at sympathetic range more easily on that other person. In this particular example, I don't think Borrow Threads does anything useful for you. If you just want to cast sympathetically, you can already do that.<br /> <br /> Third, according to the Sympathetic Range attainment (p. 193), you only need to be casting at sensory range. The extra reach to cast at someone you're viewing remotely would be if you used Scrying to see someone, and then wanted to cast on them directly; that would require the extra reach, but not the normal requirements for sympathetic casting.<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume from your post that your goal here is simply to Scry on Moonstone, using his hair as a sympathetic Yantra and your Shadow Name as a Persona Yantra, and you want to make it Potency 3 and last for one scene. With Space 2, that will take 2 instant actions and the following roll: 1 (Gnosis) + 2 (Space) + 1 (Persona Yantra) - 2 (Potency +1) = 2d10. It requires 1 mana (for sympathetic range) and a total of 4 reach (casting time, sensory range, advanced duration, and swap primary factor to potency). That means you only roll Paradox 3, as this is your first paradox-risking spell in the new scene. Based on your roll, that means you rolled 3 successes on the Paradox roll, not 4, but the spell still fails.<br /> <br /> Please let me know if I got all of that right before I reply to your IC post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 08-02-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:10:04-07:00","id":941918,"title":"","content":"Just for fun, I'm going to roll Composure to see if the Doc can keep herself from giggling about the cute moment.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/423771\" target=\"_blank\">Amazingly, she passes with flying colors.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:12:20-07:00","id":941920,"title":"","content":"I was considering making a Resolve + Composure check to see if Ragnar kept his head, but I figured it would be more interesting if he didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:27:51-07:00","id":941925,"title":"","content":"I think I'm gonna have the Doc attempt the Discern Composition spell on the shrooms. Lemme just figure this out here...<br /> <br /> Okay, so Matter 2 + Gnosis 1 is my base. The spell is Matter 1, so Vo gets 2 Free Reach. One will be spent on instant casting; the other... the spell's given Reach options don't seem necessary, so she may just not use the other Reach.<br /> Vo has two Yantra slots for a spell. I don't think there's Paradox risk in the first place, so her Cane won't be used as a Dedicated Tool in this instance. It will be used as a Path Tool to add 1 die.<br /> Now, I know the environment adds a +2 Environment Yantra for Death, but this is Matter, so unless it also adds any Matter aid, that's not relevant.<br /> It's not Duration-based so I can't use Concentration. Would using her glasses as a Tool count, since they're a pretty obvious symbol of perception?<br /> If so, I'm at 5 dice (Matter 2 + Gnosis 1 + Tool [Cane] 1 + Tool [Glasses] 1). If not, 4 dice.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, I have the Shadow Name merit. &quot;Dr. Asphodel&quot; sounds like the sort of persona fit for studying things in the deathzone, so if the Glasses tool can't be used, could I use the Persona for +1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 08-02-2016, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:53:58-07:00","id":941941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=941911#post941911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - I'd like to slow down here for a second and back up on your most recent post. There's a few things going on that either I don't understand what you're trying to accomplish, or you're misunderstanding something about the rules -- which is totally understandable for our game's first attempt at casting sympathetically!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can see why it took me so long to get this post up lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=941911#post941911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, Moonstone wants you to use his hair as a sympathetic Yantra to be able to track him and cast spells on him from a distance. In mechanical terms, per p. 173, when used as a sympathetic Yantra his hair counts as a Strong connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking when we were first making this plan, but it seems to actually be tougher than that.<br /> <br /> Yes, the hair has a Strong connection to Moonstone, but as far as I can tell, using the hair as a Sympathetic Yantra <i>doesn't</i> allow me to use it's sympathetic connection. Under Sympathetic Tools on page 122, it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;the Yantra represents the subject of the spell, allowing the mage to ... use <i><b>her own</b></i> sympathetic connection to the subject in order to cast across Space or Time&quot; </div> </div> </div>So while the hair allows me to cast sympathetically at Moonstone, it doesn't actually provide it's own Strong connection to the spell. Rather, I only have my own Weak connection to use. (Were I not casting sympathetically, it <i>would</i> work as a +2 Yantra, though.)<br /> <br /> Instead of using the Weak connection, I used <i>Borrow Threads</i> with the lock of hair as a target. I mistakenly thought it was a Connected connection (with a Withstand of 5) rather than a Strong connection (Withstand 3), but ultimately I don't think I'm on anything better than a chance die anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=941911#post941911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, because you don't know Moonstone's sympathetic name, the Withstand rating is 2. Any spell you cast on him will thus have -2 Potency, so it needs to be at least Potency 3 to work on him at a distance. (On a tangent, this is why I asked <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> to pick a sympathetic name.) Remember that using an item as a sympathetic Yantra allows you to cast at sympathetic range with your Space 2 attainment, but it still counts as one of your possible Yantra for the spell casting and doesn't confer a dice bonus for the roll. If you want to use another Yantra, such as a tool, you can't cast reflexively and will need at least 2 turns to do so. That might matter when we're in initiative. <br /> <br /> Second, the Borrow Threads spell essentially allows you to siphon sympathetic connections from someone else, which can allow you to do a number of useful things, but it's not necessary to cast on Moonstone sympathetically. For instance, you could transfer the connection from his hair sample to yourself, so now <i>you</i> have a direct Strong link to Moonstone for the duration of your spell. Or, you could steal the connection from Moonstone to gain a stronger connection to one of his close friends or mentors, which would then let you cast at sympathetic range more easily on that other person. In this particular example, I don't think Borrow Threads does anything useful for you. If you just want to cast sympathetically, you can already do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, this is all correct, and was taken into account in my casting of <i>Scrying</i>. The only other thing is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=941911#post941911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, according to the Sympathetic Range attainment (p. 193), you only need to be casting at sensory range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the default range is <i>touch </i>(or aimed). I need to Reach for sensory then Reach again for sympathy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, for clarification, my post had me first casting <i>Borrow Threads</i> on the lock of hair with a chance die, using my knife and Shadow Name (which was a 2 turn affair each time), then casting <i>Scrying </i>sympathetically (using only the knife so that it would take 1 turn of <i>Borrow Threads</i>' duration) (also I couldn't think of a way that Binder's Shadow Name would work for a <i>Scrying</i>). Anyway, that's my understanding of the rules, but ultimately you're the Storyteller and if you disagree with my interpretation, I'm happy to re-do it! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Ironically, I think we did this exactly the wrong way around. I should have given <i>my</i> hair to Moonstone, scryed on that, then cast another <i>Scrying</i> through the window at Moonstone.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:01:07-07:00","id":941947,"title":"","content":"The confusion here might come a little bit from me based on Moonstone's IC advice. I was under the impression that to do sympathetic casting, you need two separate things:<br /> 1. The caster needs to have their own sympathetic connection to the subject.<br /> 2. Actually casting the spell requires a sympathy yantra, some physical token (or just knowledge of their sympathetic name.)<br /> <br /> I was under the impression that Binder would probably need to cast Borrow Threads because he has a weak sympathetic link, if any, to Moonstone at this point. The lock of hair has Strong sympathy to Moonstone, but it doesn't automatically grant that level of sympathy by being used as a yantra.<br /> <br /> I could be way off here, but I thought this situation was exactly what Borrow Threads was for, and it's a basic Space utility spell you'd expect to cast as frequently as Supernal Vision or Speak with Dead or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 08-02-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:09:02-07:00","id":941954,"title":"","content":"It was what I had been thinking and your in-character advice made me more certain I was correct","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:46:31-07:00","id":941972,"title":"","content":"Ok. I reviewed the rules and tried to skim through some posts online to get a better grasp on the rules for sympathetic casting. I think we are both right and both wrong about different things. I think I'm mistaken about the range and sympathy, because I'm probably thinking back to how things worked in 1E.<br /> <br /> Because Binder has cast spells on Moonstone and communicated with each other, I'll say they have a Weak sympathetic connection together. The hair can be used as a symbolic sympathetic Yantra, and it also has a Strong connection to Moonstone.<br /> <br /> So, you were right about the fact that the Sympathetic Range attainment uses <i>your</i> sympathetic connection (Weak, currently). You <i>can</i> use Borrowed Threads to steal the Strong sympathetic connection from the hair. It is Withstood at 3, so to be able to transfer a single sympathetic connection, you need a net Potency of 1 (so base Potency 4). I'll say that you can make those repeated rolls to get it to work, as you originally put in your IC post. As you wrote, this means it lasts for 2 turns, and you use one of them up by attempting (and failing) your spell.<br /> <br /> However, I was right about the reaches. Casting on someone whom you are viewing remotely is different than casting on them sympathetically. Viewing remotely would include something like trying to trigger a heart attack in someone that you're currently watching on a live news channel. You don't need any sympathetic connection or sympathetic Yantra to cast that spell. For example, you could open a Scrying window at Moonstone's location, and then cast something on Phoenix by using 2 reach to boost from touch range to remote viewing range, as long as you can see him through the Scrying window. You wouldn't need any sympathetic Yantra, nor would you need to have any sympathetic connection to Phoenix (although you have a Weak one with him as well).<br /> <br /> Once you get Space 3, you can use Web-Weaver to temporarily boost sympathetic connections, so you could just directly enhance your own Weak connection to a stronger one. But in the meantime, borrowing one will have to suffice.<br /> <br /> Based on this, I think nothing changes. You have 1 turn left to attempt a spell on Moonstone with a Strong connection. What you do in your next turn, however, will likely be impacted by what's about to happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:52:52-07:00","id":941982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=941925#post941925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm gonna have the Doc attempt the Discern Composition spell on the shrooms. Lemme just figure this out here...<br /> <br /> Okay, so Matter 2 + Gnosis 1 is my base. The spell is Matter 1, so Vo gets 2 Free Reach. One will be spent on instant casting; the other... the spell's given Reach options don't seem necessary, so she may just not use the other Reach.<br /> Vo has two Yantra slots for a spell. I don't think there's Paradox risk in the first place, so her Cane won't be used as a Dedicated Tool in this instance. It will be used as a Path Tool to add 1 die.<br /> Now, I know the environment adds a +2 Environment Yantra for Death, but this is Matter, so unless it also adds any Matter aid, that's not relevant.<br /> It's not Duration-based so I can't use Concentration. Would using her glasses as a Tool count, since they're a pretty obvious symbol of perception?<br /> If so, I'm at 5 dice (Matter 2 + Gnosis 1 + Tool [Cane] 1 + Tool [Glasses] 1). If not, 4 dice.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, I have the Shadow Name merit. &quot;Dr. Asphodel&quot; sounds like the sort of persona fit for studying things in the deathzone, so if the Glasses tool can't be used, could I use the Persona for +1?</div> </div> </div> </div>The environment does not add to Matter spells, correct. You can go ahead and use the glasses as a Path Tool in this case, because the lenses are close enough to a mirror (they're slightly reflective) and relate to sight/perception. So feel free to roll at 5 dice, which takes 2 turns (irrelevant currently since you're not in initiative).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:00:15-07:00","id":941987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=941972#post941972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Casting on someone whom you are viewing remotely is different than casting on them sympathetically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know lol. I'm basing it on this (p. 193) (shoulda quoted in my previous post):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To use this Attainment, the mage must be casting a spell <i>at sensory range</i>, use a sympathy Yantra, and spend one Mana. </div> </div> </div>But I definitely think the intention is confusing because it seems weird to say it only requires one Reach and kind of stealthily actually require two?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what's about to happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Haha, oh man XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:10:13-07:00","id":941994,"title":"","content":"On p. 112, under common reach effects:<br /> \u2022 Move the spell from touch/self to <b>sensory </b>range<br /> \u2022 If at <b>sensory </b>range, allow the mage to cast on a subject she is <b>viewing remotely</b><br /> <br /> So, one reach increases from touch to sensory range. Sensory range would be casting at someone you can physically see, but might be a fair distance away -- like half a mile or something, if it's light out and you have clear line of sight. Remote viewing, as I mentioned earlier, would be like targeting someone you're talking to via Skype/Facetime, watching on live television, or viewing through a Scrying window. Casting on someone remotely requires 2 reach, but no mana.<br /> <br /> As you quoted, casting sympathetically only requires a sensory range. It thus needs 1 reach, and 1 mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:22:01-07:00","id":942001,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> - I totally forgot to mention that Matter doesn't apply here. Only works on non-living objects; living objects, including fungi, fall under Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:34:16-07:00","id":942013,"title":"","content":"Lynx's Life might be a better go-to for studying the mushrooms - though at the moment he's too preoccupied making sure Ragnar's okay to really think about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:39:55-07:00","id":942017,"title":"","content":"Whooooooops.<br /> Can I have her switch to looking at the stone instead, or would I need to recast for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:41:31-07:00","id":942018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=942017#post942017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whooooooops.<br /> Can I have her switch to looking at the stone instead, or would I need to recast for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Just edit your post and indicate which stone you're looking at. You could potentially use that extra Reach to use advanced scale and study multiple objects, too. Once you edit your post, I'll update mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:50:00-07:00","id":942022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=934807#post934807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>A bruised and tired young Vietnamese woman in a hospital bed, being prompted to sign some paperwork while a nurse holds her newborn. An adolescent girl furiously shaving her head in the bathroom as her parents pound on the locked door. Watching a 9th grader threaten to do terrible things to another 9th grader, walking away and saying nothing. Pawning Mom's jewelry for drug money. A dance instructor shoving her finger in his red and puffy face and telling &quot;Amelia&quot; that she is lazy, ungraceful, and too fucking fat to be in this Intermediate Ballet II classroom in anything but a tree costume. Homeless in Chicago, getting the shit kicked out of him at the bus terminal. Being fired as a Wal-Mart greeter (incompetence+customer complaints, &quot;too friendly&quot;). Realizing that he is never, ever going to have children.<br /> <br /> Improperly preparing the wards for a summoning ritual, being severely injured by the angry spirit along with the rest of the Knights, Askia refusing to heal him magically: &quot;That scar is your idiot tax. That's what this costs you personally.&quot; Rose of Sharon rolling her eyes and waving off an incident where he embarrassed the cabal in front of a Consilium gathering: &quot;No one was expecting better from you.&quot; Practicing with a blade in the mirror the way Ghost Dog taught him, and sternly giving himself imagined instructions: &quot;Now remember, Moonstone, when you're on the battlefield, Hakim is what matters. <b>You don't matter.</b>&quot; Bowing his head obediently: <b>&quot;I don't matter.&quot;</b> Talking and humming and singing to himself, alone in the sanctum, pretending he's a mage. The facial expressions at the individual moments when each of the Knights decide that he is not going to Awaken.<br /> <br /> Watching Hakim court various women and laugh and smile and be happy with them. Feeling shame and physical pain at how poisonous his jealousy is. Sitting on the edge of Hakim's bed, half-dressed, ugly crying. Hakim saying: &quot;You make it hard to love you.&quot; Hakim saying: &quot;You aren't thinking straight right now, that's your symptoms talking.&quot; Hakim saying: &quot;Just because I say something once doesn't mean I feel the same way forever.&quot; Hakim saying: &quot;There need to be boundaries between us.&quot; Hakim saying: &quot;I do not love you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of these he remembers as he watches them, but there's one extended scene that he doesn't remember at all:<br /> A closed door behind which he and Hakim are having a mild argument about some regrettable thing Hakim did that escalates quickly into Moonstone screaming and shattering picture frames. Hakim is kind and patient and increasingly scared as he fails to explain the situation and calm him down. A blade is shoved through the closed door, followed by the door being pushed open and Moonstone stalking out alone, breathing hard and clutching an ornate enchanted sword and streaming tears. He swings in a frenzy, tearing at the walls of the sanctum, slices wide and deeply cuts his own arm and yelps and falls to his knees. Ghost Dog rushes in, shouts something. Hakim stumbles through the door, clutching his abdomen, and says <b>&quot;Undo today.&quot;</b> Ghost Dog chants in the High Speech, draws his own blade, and deftly cuts through Time-</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I could add my opinion here, Hakim sounds like an emotionally abusive ableist jerk. D:"