 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm intrigued to see what these rolls are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:11:15-07:00","id":967699,"title":"","content":"Not sure what stats you'd run for the broom, but I'd suggest a modified spear. 0 damage modifier instead of 2, and a -1 initiative penalty instead of -2 (this causes Phoenix's.initiative to fall to 12, which means he goes after Monnstone since his initiative mod is lower), everything else stays the same, including the fact that it grants +1 Defense (so long as the opponent is either unarmed or has a weapon with a Size of 1). However, Phoenix is using his regular Defense for this one so it's a Defense of 5, not 7 (7 is when he's fighting unarmed due to his Defensive Fighting Merit for Brawl). This would makes Phoenix's total Defense 6, so the Abyssal gets another die to work with (or 2, if the Defense boost doesn't apply).<br /> <br /> Phoenix reflexively employs Forces Armor of 2, which means that unless that extra die(ce) rolls more successes, he takes no damage. By the way, I'll need to know Defense before making an attack. That, and I'm wondering how you'd handle a trip attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T03:58:25-07:00","id":967854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=967699#post967699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what stats you'd run for the broom, but I'd suggest a modified spear. 0 damage modifier instead of 2, and a -1 initiative penalty instead of -2 (this causes Phoenix's.initiative to fall to 12, which means he goes after Monnstone since his initiative mod is lower), everything else stays the same, including the fact that it grants +1 Defense (so long as the opponent is either unarmed or has a weapon with a Size of 1). However, Phoenix is using his regular Defense for this one so it's a Defense of 5, not 7 (7 is when he's fighting unarmed due to his Defensive Fighting Merit for Brawl). This would makes Phoenix's total Defense 6, so the Abyssal gets another die to work with (or 2, if the Defense boost doesn't apply).<br /> <br /> Phoenix reflexively employs Forces Armor of 2, which means that unless that extra die(ce) rolls more successes, he takes no damage. By the way, I'll need to know Defense before making an attack. That, and I'm wondering how you'd handle a trip attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds fair to me. +0L weapon, -1 initiative, +1 defense, two-handed. Still size 4 and I'll say you need 1 Str to wield (which isn't an issue for you). I'll roll the extra 1d10 and modify my post. Looks like you still take 2 bashing damage...sorry. :P<br /> <br /> This Abyssal entity has defense 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 09-12-2016, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:33:51-07:00","id":967891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=967854#post967854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like you still take 2 bashing damage...sorry. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Geez, it's like that Abyssal broke the 4th wall and said &quot;Fuck your character's Forces armor, I deal 2 bashing, I'mma gonna deal 2 bashing, goramit!&quot;. No need to apologize, the dice rolled that way.<br /> <br /> I think it's safe to say Moonstone spends the turn running, so I'll make a post on Phoenix's action. I'd still like to know how you'd handle a trip attack, assuming you'd allow it in the first place that is (IE only allowed it as part of a combat Merit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:57:25-07:00","id":967901,"title":"","content":"Phoenix is fighting the shard of an Abyssal god with naught but a broom. Ever the hero, kid. Respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T07:15:40-07:00","id":967911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/fo