ref=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9b62PRo8hKs\" target=\"_blank\">Have an appropriate quote from an appropriate character</a>. Let's do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:58:52-07:00","id":978777,"title":"","content":"Are there established rules for ties on initiative? Seriously I've looked like 5 times now and can't find it...Based on initiative modifier as first tiebreaker, but then what?<br /> <br /> FYI, Mathias actually had a 16 overall, not 15, that's why I edited his total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:02:36-07:00","id":978778,"title":"","content":"In my game when I have a tie, I either have them re-roll (seems like a needless trouble in play-by-post) or just do alphabetical order/arbitrary whim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:15:36-07:00","id":978782,"title":"","content":"Gah, ninja'd! Yeah, alphabetical sounds fine to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:47:19-07:00","id":978892,"title":"","content":"I did a 2E conversion of the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind, the Legacy I'm thinking Moonstone might join. Check it out! <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...the-demon-wind</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Is that something you'd be open to having in the game? At the very least, Hakim's former cabalmate Ghost Dog is meant to be a Ronin.<br /> <br /> I'm so pleased with how it went that I'm planning to do some more conversions just for fun. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> I'm already looking at the Walkers in Mists. I also have an updated Thrice-Great that I did for my own chronicle, just because they're my faves, and I'm planning to do the Choir of Hashmallim as well.<br /> <br /> Are there any Legacies that you guys would be interested in seeing 2E versions of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:14:50-07:00","id":978944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=978572#post978572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It penalizes rolls, not your current initiative count. So, no, stick with your initiative from before.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, since Phoenix is no longer holding the broom, his initiative is 13, not 12.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=978572#post978572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally forgot about that timing with the scene, sorry. I actually meant for the new scene to start for you and Moonstone after leaving the portal, so that was a clerical error on my part putting it in the post earlier when I did.<br /> <br /> Let's do this: Armor was active at the time, so don't take any more damage. But it's not currently active. We'll treat it like you're in a new scene now for purposes of armor. Fair compromise</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:57:09-07:00","id":978951,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I was thinking about giving some Legacies a conversion, especially the Walkers in Mist, but I guess using one of my own conversions might be cheating! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:16:22-07:00","id":978956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=978778#post978778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game when I have a tie, I either have them re-roll (seems like a needless trouble in play-by-post) or just do alphabetical order/arbitrary whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea, works well for me. Since I'll do it as a second tiebreaker, it hopefully won't be that relevant all the time anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=978892#post978892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a 2E conversion of the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind, the Legacy I'm thinking Moonstone might join. Check it out! <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...the-demon-wind</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Is that something you'd be open to having in the game? At the very least, Hakim's former cabalmate Ghost Dog is meant to be a Ronin.<br /> <br /> I'm so pleased with how it went that I'm planning to do some more conversions just for fun. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> I'm already looking at the Walkers in Mists. I also have an updated Thrice-Great that I did for my own chronicle, just because they're my faves, and I'm planning to do the Choir of Hashmallim as well.<br /> <br /> Are there any Legacies that you guys would be interested in seeing 2E versions of?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=978951#post978951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I was thinking about giving some Legacies a conversion, especially the Walkers in Mist, but I guess using one of my own conversions might be cheating! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of people helping to craft or convert Legacies to 2E, even if it's one you want to join (especially if you want to join it!). Honestly, Legacies were something I never really got to explore or deal much with in 1E. I didn't really understand the purpose or benefit of them and didn't get the chance to learn, because I never had the chance to really play Mage 1E.<br /> <br /> I can review the drafts you have and give feedback, in case there's anything that I think is unfair.<br /> <br /> If someone could take a stab at <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Storm_Keeper\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>, that would be handy...considering Mathias is one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:24:20-07:00","id":978959,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Oh my. If I wasn't already set on the Walkers in Mist, I would go for these guys so hard. But they are very thematically resonant for Ragnar's philosophy on magic and the world. I think Mathias has found himself a protege... whether he wants one or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:31:26-07:00","id":978961,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Just realized I never answered one of your questions. Yes, use Rank for Withstand rating on the Abyssal entity, until or unless I find some other ruling or explanation suggesting otherwise.<br /> <br /> Question for anyone else who might know better...Maybe this is a dumb question, and I didn't think to consider it earlier when Binder used Mind magic on the Abyssal entity he encountered. Are spirits or spirit-like creatures supposed to be immune to Mind spells? I think of them as sentient, but maybe that takes away from the Spirit Arcanum, so I don't know.<br /> <br /> If anyone else has any other questions or something you need input from me about, let me know. I sometimes forget to reply to thinks and don't want to leave you hanging. Working on IC post now, will hopefully have up in a little bit unless something comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:47:09-07:00","id":978965,"title":"","content":"I haven't thought about Legacies yet, in that I am still establishing Lynx's character. I'll get there in due time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, Legacies were something I never really got to explore or deal much with in 1E. I didn't really understand the purpose or benefit of them and didn't get the chance to learn, because I never had the chance to really play Mage 1E. </div> </div> </div>Legacies in 1E had two major mechanical advantages. Firstly, their Attainments were often rolled with a dice pool much like a Rote's dice pool, i.e., Attribute + Skill + Arcana; it was also bound to the Fallen World, so Sleepers were not subject to Quiescence, nor would they erode the Attainment. This did mean that if you have a shapeshifting Attainment, you could become a bear in the middle of the streets, and people wouldn't go mad, wouldn't be subject to Breaking Points, and your spell wouldn't diminish - making it a Guardian's nightmare, obviously.<br /> <br /> Secondly, they had access to better Oblations than 2E's, in that they regained mana equal to successes, rather than being limited to dots in Ruling arcanum.<br /> <br /> As for purpose, it is the mage's Journey and Method used to find the ultimate Truth. The mage shapes her soul into the expression and embodiment of her magical style and beliefs, or integrates the tradition that most resonates with her, if taught an established Legacy. The soul becomes a lens through which the Supernal can be expressed in the Fallen World. In essence, the reason Legacies don't incite Quiescence is that the mage's Attainments are comparable to natural law: it's part of reality, whether or not you like it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not a fan of 2E's legacies. They're cleaner, sure, but they also feel more tacked on than in 1E. They feel weaker. I also find converting them to 2E is difficult, personally. I enjoy the reduced Gnosis requirements, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I've been doing it all wrong, but y'know. That's my take on Legacies in 1E, as taught by my M:tAw mentor, Lankin, some odd 4 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 09-30-2016, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:13:35-07:00","id":978972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=978961#post978961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for anyone else who might know better...Maybe this is a dumb question, and I didn't think to consider it earlier when Binder used Mind magic on the Abyssal entity he encountered. Are spirits or spirit-like creatures supposed to be immune to Mind spells? I think of them as sentient, but maybe that takes away from the Spirit Arcanum, so I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div><s>I believe Dave clarified that they are supposed to be affected, but I can't cite my source.</s><br /> <br /> Edit: Double-checked, found the thread, and I was misremembering. Dave has not reported on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 09-30-2016, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:51:17-07:00","id":978986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=978972#post978972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <s>I believe Dave clarified that they are supposed to be affected, but I can't cite my source.</s><br /> <br /> Edit: Double-checked, found the thread, and I was misremembering. Dave has not reported on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, for now I'll do what I did with the last one: It's a sentient spirit and can be affected by Mind spells, but they may not work as effectively or have the same outcome as they would on Goetia or a human.<br /> <br /> Everyone: Minor thing, but can you represent bashing damage as a B rather than / in your health bar? The slashes are hard to count when they're next to each other. Also, please make sure your post header includes whether you have Peripheral vs. Active Sight if it's not already there...I want to be able to provide extra info to people who have Active Sight, but I can't remember if anyone has that up currently.<br /> <br /> Also remember that seeing others cast spells using Active Sight may lead you to be affected by their Nimbus, which could influence some of your dice pools depending on the nature of their Nimbus and your own attributes/skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:46:45-07:00","id":979175,"title":"","content":"Quick question: if we are improvising a spell, do we need to be touching the person we wish to affect? I'm just asking, cause I don't want to have to try and touch the gulmoth to hit it with a spell. And it would be nice to not have to run around to touch people to help them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:19:18-07:00","id":979190,"title":"","content":"You've got options.<ul><li>You can touch the target.</li> <li>You can &quot;throw&quot; the spell, which requires a reflexive Gnosis+(Athletics or Firearms)-Defense roll immediately after you finish casting the spell. &quot;Aimed Spells&quot; on p.115</li> <li>Or, you can spend 1 Reach to cast it at sensory range, no roll or touching necessary.</li> </ul><br /> If I remember right, the gulmoth has Defense 6. Go wild!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:34:22-07:00","id":979264,"title":"","content":"Hm. That sounds like a &quot;thrown&quot; spell would get reduced to a chance die, and there's always the possibility for a dramatic failure with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:21:31-07:00","id":979285,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> Concentration probably wouldn't be a great Yantra for the spell you're thinking of, because the spell ends when you take an instant action (like attacking).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:26:55-07:00","id":979290,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Speaking of 2E Legacy conversions, the Fixed Reach element has given me a particular headache when making the Attainments for them. So I devised a house rule where they had instant casting without taking a Reach, or you got 1 extra Reach to work with if it had ritual casting time. Yes, this effectively means that you got 1 extra free Reach, but considering Rotes can give you anywhere from 0 to 4 extra free Reach, and that's their main draw for spending the Experience on them, I think giving just 1 extra ain't that big of a deal. That, and a lot of the 2E Legacy conversions I've seen tend to give a the extra Reach anyways. Mostly because I think it's simply impractical otherwise for most Attainments.<br /> <br /> That said, up to you on what rules you wanna go with. I'll devise a 2E conversion on Tamers of Fire once I know what ruling you're going with (inb4 someone points out the conversion thread for the Legacy, I'm perfectly aware of its existence, I'm going to be posting my own version on there soon and I'll link it on here once I've posted it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979285#post979285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> Concentration probably wouldn't be a great Yantra for the spell you're thinking of, because the spell ends when you take an instant action (like attacking).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, forgot about that. Well, I can use the Dedicated Tool for a +1, Kinetic Blow does enhance the potential of attacks, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 09-30-2016, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:33:16-07:00","id":979294,"title":"","content":"Today is really an off day for me. I can't even read properly. The amount of oddities I've misheard today is beyond hopeless. Rat of Gods (Wrath of Gods), do you have Taylor Swift, Plastic sex, random insertion of the word lube in conversation...keep dropping things too. I've edited my actions, and will be waiting for either Phoenix and/or Ragnar to leave the aura - horray for overprotectiveness and inability to actually fight - or for both of them to say they're not leaving. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:49:42-07:00","id":979297,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> Don't you need to cast take advantage of that boon on this turn? I didn't up the duration any. <br /> <br /> Hm, sounds like a &quot;thrown&quot; spell would get reduced to a chance die, and there's always the possibility for a dramatic failure with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:06:14-07:00","id":979442,"title":"","content":"Several of you have made some choices or used rules that I think are in error. I know I myself had to look up rules a lot earlier today because I was rusty on a few things, but I wanted to make sure you all remembered some stuff<br /> <br /> Haberdasher: First, you can't spend Reach to boost Potency like that. You can make it advanced potency, but that only helps Withstand against dispellation. Also, you can only use Concentration as a yantra on spells with a duration more than 1 turn long. Your spell only has duration of 1 turn by default. That means you would need something like a Path tool instead; however, it's a moot point because even dropping to +1 yantra instead of +2 wouldn't affect the outcome of your casting roll. You are correct that if Phoenix does not make a mundane roll this turn (such as attacking), your spell will run out of duration and expire. Finally, if you only have one free Reach, I'm assuming you spent it on instant casting?<br /> <br /> Caladriu: In order to cast a touch spell in combat, you actually also need to succeed on a Dexterity + Brawl roll. -2 aura applies, but Defense does not. See chapter 5 for details. You can either keep the action and add that roll, or change your action. As with aimed spells, this roll is reflexive and takes place <i>after</i> rolls for spell casting and Paradox; failure means it misses and the spell fails. I will say that I think it satisfies your Naive Vice but does not count as an act of hubris; you're trying to understand and communicate with it for now, not make a deal or reason with it. I will share my thoughts on how it affects Moonstone if you decide to keep the action and succeed on the touch attack. <br /> <br /> KKV: Not directly related to your post, but your header you've been copy/pasting still shows that you have 3 active spells right now. Can you clarify which are still active (and can drop any reflexively that you don't want anymore) by editing your header?<br /> <br /> Crapcarp: As pointed out, concentration means your spell will end by taking a non-reflexive action, so it's not worth it for you because the spell will end before you get to use its benefit. Sounds like you will use the dedicated tool as both a tool yantra and for the Paradox reducing function, right? So yeah, casting this turn, then actually roll for casting next turn, then you can attack the turn after that. Let me know if I'm missing something there. <br /> <br /> Let me know what your thoughts are about these things. Once we clear up those actions I'll find the time to put up the next post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 09-30-2016, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:32:00-07:00","id":979453,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Don't worry about it, getting the rules straight makes things go smoother in the future.<br /> <br /> Like for instance touch attacks in Moonstone's current state. Here's what Shadow Flesh says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage transforms the subject\u2019s body and all her personal<br /> possessions into a mass of moving and animated shadows. The<br /> mage may choose to make the subject a three-dimensional or<br /> a two-dimensional shadow. Three-dimensional shadows still<br /> have no apparent mass or substance, and cannot interact with<br /> physical objects. Two-dimensional shadows may move through<br /> cracks and crevices, though are still bound by the laws of gravity<br /> and must remain touching the floor, even if moving on walls.<br /> <br /> <b>The subject retains all of her Attributes and Skills, but may<br /> not take physical actions other than to move, though she can<br /> still cast spells.</b> She is immune to attacks or damage, but not<br /> Supernal magic, while in her shadowy form. She is effectively<br /> invisible in natural or supernatural darkness, though she can<br /> see in them herself. </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it, this probably means that I can't do touch range spells while wearing the Cloak, in or out of combat, because Moonstone simply isn't capable of making physical contact.<br /> <br /> Can I revise my action and instead do it as a sensory range casting, with the Reach and Paradox that would entail?<br /> <br /> Also, I might be misreading you, but if I'm making a terrible mistake here (by which I mean my spell would be disruptive to the game and unfun), just say the word and I can do something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:53:05-07:00","id":979461,"title":"","content":"Totally forgot to consider how Shadow Flesh would interact with that here, you're right. I think that interpretation is fair. That revision sounds good to me! Go ahead and roll for the Paradox then. <br /> <br /> And you're totally cool to try this. I meant I don't want to say what conditions/tilts you may or may not get until after you confirm decision to cast. I was giving the option to revise while trying to minimize meta gaming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:56:38-07:00","id":979466,"title":"","content":"Okay, so Reach is not used to increase Potency, I just choose to increase Potency and take a -2 per additional level of Potency beyond the first, which is implied. I think I've got it!<br /> <br /> Yes, I'll go ahead and use the free Reach for an Instant Casting time. And looking at the boon section under fate, I can mix and match boons, with one boon per level of Potency. So instead of a +2 dice to two rolls, since one of those rolls is going to be wasted for duration, I would like to change one of those boons to granting Phoenix the Inspired Condition (resolving that won't get you a Beat upon resolving).<br /> <br /> So he gets +1 dice to a roll on his next turn, and the Inspired Condition for the turn. If that's acceptable, I'll update my post. <br /> <br /> Also, the spell cannot affect spell casting rolls, since I didn't go for that Reach option. Crapcarp, you would probably be better off just whacking it with the staff to get the benefit of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-01-2016, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:54:36-07:00","id":979499,"title":"","content":"Updated my action to cast at sensory range and incorporate a Paradox roll, otherwise stayed the same.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Not to give you a dozen things on your plate, but there's a spell I was thinking about casting this scene with Creative Thaumaturgy. It's modeled on Fate 2 &quot;Shifting the Odds&quot; which temporarily grants [Potency] dots of Social Merits for [Potency] uses until they fade again. Here's what I want to do, does it look alright?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Glory Days (Time 2+Mind 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> <br /> By strengthening his temporal sympathy to a certain period in his own life, the subject can temporarily act at the level he imagined he could in his prime. The subject gains temporary dots in one Merit equal to Potency. The mage may benefit from the Merit a number of times equal to Potency during the spell's Duration before it fades.<br /> <br /> The Merit must be strongly related to a specific time in the character's life, not made up from whole cloth. It can only grant mental instincts and reflexes, not significant physical changes or external circumstances: Pusher would be acceptable, but Resources would not. For a character like Moonstone with formal combat training, this might be used to recreate the fighting ability of an especially intense sparring session. A character who remembers himself as a young lothario might instead draw on memories of fast-talking social graces.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The subject may divide Potency between dots in an additional Merit. This effect may be selected multiple times. </div> </div> </div>---<br /> <br /> Also, in case anyone is interested, here's an update I did for the Choir of Hashmallim Legacy: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...bout-summoning</a><br /> <br /> I mentioned an NPC in Hakim's old cabal who practices this Legacy, so it's relevant for that at least!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:52:37-07:00","id":979576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979442#post979442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KKV: Not directly related to your post, but your header you've been copy/pasting still shows that you have 3 active spells right now. Can you clarify which are still active (and can drop any reflexively that you don't want anymore) by editing your header?</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies. I've edited out the Analyse Life that should've been gone ages ago. Lynx has Body Control up still, for Dr. Asphodel, Ragnar and himself; and Heightened Senses for himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:31:37-07:00","id":979586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979466#post979466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so Reach is not used to increase Potency, I just choose to increase Potency and take a -2 per additional level of Potency beyond the first, which is implied. I think I've got it!<br /> <br /> Yes, I'll go ahead and use the free Reach for an Instant Casting time. And looking at the boon section under fate, I can mix and match boons, with one boon per level of Potency. So instead of a +2 dice to two rolls, since one of those rolls is going to be wasted for duration, I would like to change one of those boons to granting Phoenix the Inspired Condition (resolving that won't get you a Beat upon resolving).<br /> <br /> So he gets +1 dice to a roll on his next turn, and the Inspired Condition for the turn. If that's acceptable, I'll update my post. <br /> <br /> Also, the spell cannot affect spell casting rolls, since I didn't go for that Reach option. Crapcarp, you would probably be better off just whacking it with the staff to get the benefit of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so you've almost got it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For Potency, yes, you pick what you want it to set it to and take -2 per extra level required to get it up there. But don't forget that Potency is the primary spell factor of Exceptional Luck, not duration, so you can make it Potency 2 for free because you have Fate 2.<br /> <br /> The problem is still duration. As written, your spell still ends on his next turn. Since your roll already accounted for a -2 penalty to boost Potency that you don't need to pay, I recommend just saying that -2 was to boost duration to 2 turns. That allows you to use Concentration as a yantra on the spell (because it can only be used for spells with a duration longer than 1 turn), and the boon will still be active on his next turn if Phoenix chooses to make a roll then. <br /> <br /> To clarify in regards to the boons: If you want to pick the option of giving a dice bonus to certain actions/skills, you don't pick which rolls count, you just pick the skill; the target gets to choose when to apply the bonus. Similarly, for condition boons, you just pick which ones to grant and the target can choose when to resolve them. You get to &quot;spend&quot; the Potency on these options by mixing and matching what you want. <br /> <br /> So with Potency 2, you can use 1 Potency to grant +1 die bonus to 1 Weaponry roll, which can be used by the recipient any time before the spell duration ends. You can also use the other Potency to grant one beneficial condition, such as Inspired. Given all the penalties Phoenix has right now due to injuries and the aura, I would probably recommend Steadfast: he can resolve it to guarantee 1 success on a failed roll, or turn a chance die into a normal 1d10 roll. Means he can have a better shot at landing a hit.<br /> <br /> It's worth pointing out that you can also give 9-again on a number of mundane rolls equal to Potency as another boon, which don't have to be specified in advance by you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:34:39-07:00","id":979587,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Can you clarify for me, did Phoenix actually pick up the staff? Or is it lying on the ground? Matters for purposes of initiative and which skill you would need to hit, since our Fate mages here are looking to give you boons on rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:47:09-07:00","id":979591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979499#post979499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated my action to cast at sensory range and incorporate a Paradox roll, otherwise stayed the same.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Not to give you a dozen things on your plate, but there's a spell I was thinking about casting this scene with Creative Thaumaturgy. It's modeled on Fate 2 &amp;quot;Shifting the Odds&amp;quot; which temporarily grants [Potency] dots of Social Merits for [Potency] uses until they fade again. Here's what I want to do, does it look alright?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Also, in case anyone is interested, here's an update I did for the Choir of Hashmallim Legacy: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...bout-summoning</a><br /> <br /> I mentioned an NPC in Hakim's old cabal who practices this Legacy, so it's relevant for that at least!</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell looks good to me, probably only needs Mind 2 honestly because you can gain Social Merit dots with just a Ruling spell. But you could incorporate past memories of skills with Time 2 and add that flavor to the Imago if that's what Moonstone would do and what you want, sure. I think spells requiring multiple arcana is less necessary in 2E.<br /> <br /> I'll check out the Legacy that you and others have posted here when I'm done reviewing that section in the core book and have time to process it all. I will probably try to make one of my own first, to get some practice with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:13:03-07:00","id":979598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979586#post979586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with Potency 2, you can use 1 Potency to grant +1 die bonus to 1 Weaponry roll</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that would actually be a +2. &quot;Grant a dice bonus equal to Potency on certain actions (usually a single Skill) for a number of rolls equal to the Potency of the spell during its Duration.&quot; (p. 134).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979587#post979587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Can you clarify for me, did Phoenix actually pick up the staff? Or is it lying on the ground? Matters for purposes of initiative and which skill you would need to hit, since our Fate mages here are looking to give you boons on rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's lying just ahead of him. Would grabbing it be an instant action, or could he scoop it up while charging towards the enemy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-01-2016, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:29:05-07:00","id":979608,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on how you choose to distribute it. Also per p. 134: &quot;As with hexes, Potency can be used to mix and match the above effects, boons that affect the same Skill do not combine their effects (only the highest bonus counts), and no character can have multiple instances of a Condition unless they apply to two different and specific things.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you have Potency 2 and create a boon, you could give 2 conditions. Or you could give 1 condition and 1 use of 9-again, or 2 uses of 9-again, or +2 on 2 skill rolls, etc. That's how I thought it worked?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:17:37-07:00","id":979639,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Sheesh! These spell casting rules are kinda tricky. So Potency can be set to your dots in that Arcana for free, and anything beyond that requires a -2 to the role. Sure, let's use the -2 I threw in there to bump Duration to two rounds. Phoenix gets a +1 to 1 Weaponry role that he makes within the next two turns, and I'll change Inspired to Steadfast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:38:23-07:00","id":979825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979598#post979598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, it's lying just ahead of him. Would grabbing it be an instant action, or could he scoop it up while charging towards the enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's what the CofD rulebook says on page 88:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lining up a shot or hefting a baseball bat takes more<br /> effort than just swinging a fist. When a character is using a<br /> weapon, apply its Initiative penalty for as long as she\u2019s got<br /> the weapon ready. The only way to avoid this modifier is to<br /> sling it or drop it. Dropping a weapon is a reflexive action,<br /> but picking it back up takes an instant action, as does just<br /> drawing a weapon normally. </div> </div> </div>Quick Draw is a 1 dot merit for situations like these, it lets you reflexively draw/equip a weapon or firearm.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> ALSO: what do we think those two rolls that our all-knowing ST called for when we each left the otherspace were for? I'm pretty sure that one of them is to remember what happened in the other world and the other one is to determine whether we brought back a Highstorm Artifact, but I can't figure out which.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-01-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:07:58-07:00","id":979875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979608#post979608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it depends on how you choose to distribute it. Also per p. 134: &quot;As with hexes, Potency can be used to mix and match the above effects, boons that affect the same Skill do not combine their effects (only the highest bonus counts), and no character can have multiple instances of a Condition unless they apply to two different and specific things.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you have Potency 2 and create a boon, you could give 2 conditions. Or you could give 1 condition and 1 use of 9-again, or 2 uses of 9-again, or +2 on 2 skill rolls, etc. That's how I thought it worked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a +2 on a skill roll and 1 Condition/9-again. I don't see how that differs from what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979639#post979639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Sheesh! These spell casting rules are kinda tricky. So Potency can be set to your dots in that Arcana for free, and anything beyond that requires a -2 to the role. Sure, let's use the -2 I threw in there to bump Duration to two rounds. Phoenix gets a +1 to 1 Weaponry role that he makes within the next two turns, and I'll change Inspired to Steadfast.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell's primary spell factor is Potency, then yes. Same deal if it's Duration. As for the Skill, considering it's going for only two turns and not three, Phoenix doesn't have time to pick up the staff, and so he's just coming in with fisticuffs.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the two-turn spell, I'mma gonna have to speed things up and just cast the spell now. So I'll only use 1 Yantra for just the Paradox penalty. Last post has been edited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:14:41-07:00","id":979882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=979875#post979875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the spell's primary spell factor is Potency, then yes. Same deal if it's Duration. As for the Skill, considering it's going for only two turns and not three, Phoenix doesn't have time to pick up the staff, and so he's just coming in with fisticuffs.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the two-turn spell, I'mma gonna have to speed things up and just cast the spell now. So I'll only use 1 Yantra for just the Paradox penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll miss out on the +1 dice boon unless rwknoll allows me to change that boon to Brawl, unless I'm forgetting about a merit you have that allows you to keep it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:40:16-07:00","id":979893,"title":"","content":"This action hasn't been resolved yet, I'm sure you can just change it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:45:27-07:00","id":979895,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll go ahead and do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T03:06:09-07:00","id":980179,"title":"","content":"A few miscellaneous things here...lots of bookkeeping needed for this fight, haha. <br /> <br /> I reviewed the Body Control spell and forgot that it adds to initiative. That means Ragnar and Lynx should be at +2 initiative until the spell ends. <br /> <br /> Ragnar, I forgot to let you know that you should lose your bashing damage. It's healed by now, that was from inside the portal and before you took the train here. <br /> <br /> Picking up items is an instant action, yes. Feels kind of costly to me, but there are several ways to get around it (merit or probably an improvised spell).<br /> <br /> I realized in re-reading boons/hexes that it references Potency of the <i>spell</i> versus Potency of the <i>boon/hex</i>. Anything that references spell potency is based on the full potency, which can be allocated to different bonuses such that the total potency of the boon equals the spell's potency. I posted in the general Mage forum here asking for clarification, but I believe that means you should get a +1 bonus to Brawl on 2 rolls during the spell's duration. This is because Ragnar cast a Potency 2 spell and granted two types of boons: Skill bonus (Potency 1 boon) and condition (Potency 1 boon).<br /> <br /> Lynx, because you waited on characters to listen to you but neither followed your advice, it looks like you lose your instant action for this round. Unless someone remembers whether he can just delay to a certain point in initiative and go again now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T05:56:02-07:00","id":980205,"title":"","content":"I don't mind losing my action, don't worry. I think being confused and indecisive when faced with something so primordially terrifying is perfectly logical. That being said, I'll do an actual action on this next turn. I'd like to see what Ragnar and Phoenix do beforehand, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T07:03:30-07:00","id":980227,"title":"","content":"Quick question: assuming Alux decides to try and skewer me, can I activate Fate Armor like Mathias did to add it to my defense on the attack roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:12:05-07:00","id":980249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage can only benefit from one form of Mage Armor at a time, but can spend Mana to change between Arcana as a reflexive action. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't actually state what action is required to activate it, so you might need an instant action to activate it in the first place, but that quote makes me believe activating it is a reflexive action. So yes, you should be able to activate Fate Armour in case you're about to become a shish kebab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:59:02-07:00","id":980267,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> Um, what are the effects of Mind Over Matter? I can't seem to find it in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:09:53-07:00","id":980272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=980267#post980267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\