">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T15:14:33-07:00","id":985098,"title":"","content":"Well that escalated quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:07:05-07:00","id":985136,"title":"","content":"This just got a lot more interesting. All we need is for Boomer, Binder, and Lynx to show up. <br /> <br /> Quick question: what is the threshold for overcoming a target's Withstand Attribute? Do you just need a number of successes equal to the Withstand Attribute?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:26:10-07:00","id":985147,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Yay, my first Experiences! Which leads me to ask the question: How exactly is spending Experiences going to be handled?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985017#post985017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still struggling with grief IRL, and that might reflect on Lynx in a rather emo way, so I apologise for that in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>My condolences as well. I hope Phoenix isn't acting too awfully unrealistically. I've never gone through grief myself, so I'm just feeling it out as best I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985098#post985098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that escalated quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and I'm lovin' it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985136#post985136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question: what is the threshold for overcoming a target's Withstand Attribute? Do you just need a number of successes equal to the Withstand Attribute?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, if a spell is Withstood, it reduces the spell's Potency. If a spell has 0 Potency, the spell's still cast and is there (in terms of scrutinizing, spell count, etc.) but it's effect is nullified, so a spell has to have a Potency higher than the Withstanding Attribute in order to take effect. In Ragnar's case, Psychic Dominion has to have a Potency of 3 (which it does).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-10-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:44:39-07:00","id":985158,"title":"","content":"After we resolve the rolls for the grappling, I would like to pause the action in that scene. Mathias would have replied or intervened by now, but I haven't had time tonight to post. Loving the conflict and action, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:28:53-07:00","id":985185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985168#post985168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"center\"><b>Moonstone</b></div>Clearly I'm biased, but I think Defense applies here. Moonstone talked to Phoenix 10 seconds ago, he's totally aware that he's present and just broke his spell, and it's clearly a tense situation so he'd be on guard. Moonstone has Defense 7, so Phoenix would either fail or roll a chance die for the grapple, depending on how <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> handles it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I still think Phoenix still has the element of surprise, it doesn't actually matter because I just remembered Phoenix can do an all-out attack, leaving 2 dice and coming up with 1 success, so I'll just edit the post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T22:08:18-07:00","id":985268,"title":"","content":"Ok, posted. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a>, are you around and interested in commenting on this scene too? Just want to make sure we're not forgetting you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:23:48-07:00","id":985304,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://media3.giphy.com/media/AT6LbRAazEoPm/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>Way to go, Moonstone!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T01:05:01-07:00","id":985312,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've ever experienced a more intense scene in all my years of RP, which is also frustrating, as I literally have no idea how to respond to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T02:52:59-07:00","id":985331,"title":"","content":"Turns out Lynx's response is to snap as well.<br /> <br /> What a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T03:52:01-07:00","id":985344,"title":"","content":"Ok, pause the IC action again.<br /> <br /> So I'm having a couple of thoughts here. <br /> <br /> On one hand, I think Moonstone is acting in line with his character's values and beliefs. He is clearly thoughtful and you're role playing him very well, and the scene is more vivid and realistic because of that. <br /> <br /> At the same time, I'm concerned as a ST because your character appears to be well on his way to writing himself into a corner in which he is the enemy of the other PCs. His earlier actions have been questionable but accepted by the others due to them giving Moonstone a few free passes. But so far Moonstone has caused Phoenix, Lynx, and Ragnar to feel outraged. I need Moonsfone to be accepted by the others enough that they would allow him to join their cabal, which requires a level of trust and intimacy I don't feel is there right now. Phoenix would like to bash your head in, Lynx seems like he is questioning whether he even wants to join mage society in total, and the others haven't posted their reactions yet so I'm not sure if I'm reading into it too much or not.<br /> <br /> I can see this going one of several ways. Moonstone would need to come down from his high seated horse to a reality check, and feel genuinely remorseful for how he is behaving, to the point that others pity him enough to accept him but not to the point of loathing him.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Shields of Dawn may intervene. Because they are built around positive morals, they most likely would rescind your welcome and eject you from their sanctum. Moonstone would be on his own, and the rest of the cabal would likely move on without him. I don't like this option because I like your character depth and history, and I think it screws you over majorly. But my NPCs are not inclined to befriend you here.<br /> <br /> I think I can come up with a response that would help us move forward, but before I do, I'd like to hear the group's thoughts to make sure I'm not reading into this way more than everyone else. Looking for input on how to address issues of cabal unity before the cabal is formed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T04:04:42-07:00","id":985346,"title":"","content":"Lynx is just upset and tired. Not having willpower, having watched Ragnar get mauled by an entity to that degree, having caused apparently a chain reaction of grief? It's a hard case of reality interfering with his euphoric idea of what the magical world is like. Having people he feels close to by virtue of being the first Awakened he's ever met clash over something he considers insignificant? Of course he's angry.<br /> <br /> I think his issue is that he can't really resonate with the Shields of Dawn - the best way to resolve this IC is, once the dust settles, they find a Thyrsus that he can talk to. As for Orders, the idea is Mysterium, but I think he's a little bit uncertain at the moment. I have full intent on having him join Mage Society, but this scene isn't making a great impression on him. But you mustn't forget, his Vice is Gluttonous, though admittedly I'm not playing that very well. He wants more magic. He wants more of the Awakened world. He <i>wants</i> to meet others, to get to know the rest of the group, and the Shields of Dawn.<br /> <br /> As for Moonstone, Lynx is angry with him, yes, but I have no intentions of letting that go out of hand. The easiest solution here is that Lynx and Moonstone talk about it on their own, I think. Moonstone did ask Lynx to heal the others and himself in a kind way, and Lynx doesn't think Moonstone's evil, just... a little too vain and proud at the moment. If Moonstone were to apologise for the things he said, or at least admit that he was wrong about what happened with the Gulmoth, that would go a long way - but I don't want Caladriu to be forced into doing that if he feels that would be the wrong direction to take.<br /> <br /> Lynx also knows that it was dumb of him to yell like that, so he's inclined to apologise for that if necessary.<br /> <br /> Rest assured, Lynx is going to join Mage society - maybe with more scepticism - and he isn't going to stay mad at Moonstone, nor will this truly affect his relationship with him, I don't think. At worst, Lynx will be a little wary around him, but the Thyrsus knows what it's like to get dragged into the torrent of passion and emotion. That doesn't mean Moonstone's actions are acceptable, but Lynx won't begrudge him that.<br /> <br /> Hope that eases your mind, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>.<br /> <br /> Let's hope the outburst gets Lynx into some trouble, though. Would be nice to get Willpower from his Passionate Virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-11-2016, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T04:20:39-07:00","id":985348,"title":"","content":"Phoenix is unsure of what to think of Moonstone at the moment. Here's the thing: Phoenix's thinking boils down primarily to the belief of an overarching narrative. It's where his Rigid Vice comes from, he tends to see things in black and white. This extends to people, he sees them as characters starring in their own individual stories and play their roles in other people's.<br /> <br /> So right now he simply doesn't know what role Moonstone is playing. Is he an outright villain, or is his journey just being a little bumpy at the moment? Phoenix wants to find out and see where things go. He's certainly enraged at Moonstone for his hubris, but if he accepts he has done wrong and makes up for it, Phoenix can certainly forgive him (Compassionate Virtue, yo).<br /> <br /> That said, he's certainly ain't trusting Moonstone with the staff, and will demand to have it regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T05:42:55-07:00","id":985364,"title":"","content":"Ragnar's just in damage control mode. He's not happy that Moonstone did a Mind spell on him, but he's the long-suffering type (Patience Virtue for the win!), and he now has some inkling of Moonstone's feelings for Hakim. No successes on a role to talk Mathias and Moonstone down, though, but maybe I didn't need them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:34:34-07:00","id":985471,"title":"","content":"Sorry, was a little preoccupied this weekend (which included Monday for me, haha).<br /> <br /> I think everything will turn out OK as long as not every interaction turns into a spiral of emotions overrunning judgement and lashing out at each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:04:14-07:00","id":985517,"title":"","content":"Ok, sounds like I might've just been reading into it too much. The feel I had from the posts here was that there was some pretty intense conflict, and since I know these are some of your characters' earliest impressions of each other, I was worried it would be a big deal. But I'll just focus on making the NPCs reply in a way as fitting of their personalities as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:17:36-07:00","id":985530,"title":"","content":"Will post in just a minute with some of my thoughts on clearing the air, don't update just yet please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:21:34-07:00","id":985534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985530#post985530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will post in just a minute with some of my thoughts on clearing the air, don't update just yet please!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok! Basically we can assume that Mathias is stunned and seething with barely-contained anger. Go ahead and post, but then really I think it makes sense for Mathias to reply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:22:56-07:00","id":985536,"title":"","content":"Oh no, I meant I'll post in the OOC thread here<br /> <br /> e: response number 666 #spooky #halloween","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-11-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:25:52-07:00","id":985599,"title":"","content":"So as an ST, I totally sympathize with your concern about party unity and wanting to test the waters before we go ahead here. Things got a little tense yesterday, and I definitely made that worse by doing a Mind spell on Ragnar- that was me just having time for a quick post and thinking &quot;how could Moonstone counter this social maneuvering attempt, aren't there a lot of Mind spells about that? Oh, I know!&quot;<br /> <br /> I really was not at all intending for this to blow up into a huge PvP thing that the other PCs got involved in, seriously. I mainly just wanted to play out the Duel Arcane rules with an NPC. I was (perhaps naively) hoping we'd be able to quickly resolve the duel and move on yesterday if you were around for most of the day. I definitely would like to minimize party conflict, and I honestly wasn't anticipating the other characters (except maybe Ragnar) reacting so strongly in the negative.<br /> <br /> For purely in-character motives, I decided right after the Alux fight that I wanted Moonstone to challenge Mathias to a duel. I don't want to lean too heavily on this as a roleplaying aid, but a common symptom of borderline personality disorder (which is what Divergent represents, I might change the name of that to make it less numinous and vague and more concrete) is the person potentially being very sensitive to perceived betrayal and forming strong opinions about people that can change relatively quickly, and that's what was on my mind. From Moonstone's point of view, he doesn't remember what happened in the portal and the specifics of the summoning (which are pretty egregiously irresponsible), just that it's &quot;his fault&quot; in a vague way- but he does know that he laid the killing blow on Alux, with minimal help from Mathias' Fate spells, and the others (Mathias, Phoenix, Ragnar) responded to that with hostility and he doesn't understand why. Also like- in my opinion, Moonstone is overreacting, but he's not wrong. Physical violence was unwarranted in the circumstances, and the Duel Arcane exists for mages to resolve disputes without violence, even over seemingly petty things. Winning the Duel is his way of proving that he's Mathias' equal and not to be trifled with, which he has a huge complex about after spending years as a Sleepwalker and second-class citizen in Awakened society. This is an unWise but entirely plausible situation for the Duel Arcane. Dueling as an idea is foolish, messy, personal, and not the first resort of reasonable people. Mages are not reasonable people.<br /> <br /> More out of character: my experience running Mage with my current group has been that my players are quite passive and friendly and almost always go out of their way to avoid offending NPCs and find a diplomatic solution, even when (from my POV) I'm presenting a clear opportunity for action and conflict. That's all well and good, but I do find it a little boring sometimes, and so I personally really enjoy playing a character who's more dynamic and aggressive and doesn't always act in their own best interests, as long as it doesn't break things for the other players. When I think of the fiction for games like Mage, it's full of characters who act foolishly and take things personally, because reasonable people don't tend to get into dramatic conflicts very often. I feel like Obsessions and grudges and personal drama are meant to drive mages into conflict, but in a way that's fun or exciting for the group as a whole. IE: PCs in conflict with NPCs is preferable to intra-party conflict.<br /> <br /> More broadly about the Shields of Dawn: I think they're perfectly fine, but I personally don't really like feeling that my character is obligated to be friends with an NPC who's introduced for that purpose. I would really be okay with there being ongoing hostility and tension or just aversion/avoidance between Moonstone and Mathias or the Shields of Dawn as a whole, <i>as long as it didn't hurt the other PCs. </i>Picking up on what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> said about meeting a Thyrsus, I think I'd prefer to seek out other mages of a similar (or interestingly different) temperament to be allies and mentors and friends. Chicago is a big city, there's got to be more options than just these guys- although it's perfectly fine for them to be big recurring NPCs whom other PCs have close ties to. I just don't want there to be a single designated &quot;friend cabal&quot; of NPCs, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Here's a few ways I could see this scene proceeding.</b><br /> <br /> My strong preference would be for the Duel to go ahead, and determine who wins as per the normal rules. I'm totally okay with Moonstone losing (although of course I would like him to win) and I think Mathias' stakes would be great for moving forward and promoting party unity. If Moonstone wins, he's going to be relieved and happy and overjoyed that he defended his honor, not vindictive at all toward the rest of the PCs. I would suggest that if defeated, a humbled but level-headed Mathias could take the other PCs aside and personally ask them to bury the hatchet and take Moonstone into their cabal, because from his POV he's clearly on a path to ruin, and he would consider it a personal favor if they would let Moonstone help them in their endeavors so he doesn't fall through the cracks and become Left-Handed. I feel like, if everyone is willing to accept that in-character, we can move forward from there. As the book says in the Mage Society chapter, cabals aren't always or totally built on deep personal friendship, they can be very pragmatic: &quot;I'll help you with your Obsessions if you help me with mine, and we all stand together against outsiders.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whoever wins or loses, here's what can happen to make peace within the party. Moonstone can apologize sincerely to Ragnar- he passed the Act of Hubris check, which means he knows what he did was wrong and wants to make restitution. Moonstone can have a heart-to-heart with Lynx and soothe the hurt there by getting to know each other a little better. And Moonstone can formally gift the Artifact staff to Phoenix as a peace gesture between them, which would kill two birds with one stone since Phoenix wants the staff anyway.<br /> <br /> We can also clear the air by Moonstone casting Perfect Recall and/or Postcognition to learn what actually happened in the portal (if that's possible? could be a Mystery going forward if mages can't easily recover their lost memories from that place) and see how specifically he's at fault. Whether he sees what happened or not, Moonstone still has the Guilty condition about summoning Alux, and he can resolve that by fully acknowledging what he's done to the other PCs and apologizing sincerely for his hubris and etc. So there's a path there.<br /> <br /> <b>If you don't think that's doable and don't want to proceed with the duel, here's another possibility. </b>Mathias is a Disciple of Time. He could cast Time 3 &quot;Shifting Sands&quot; to go back in time a few turns to the moment when Moonstone was about to challenge him in the hallway, and defuse the situation by apologizing to him before he gets hostile. I would be okay with that outcome as well, although again, I would prefer to duel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:44:51-07:00","id":985734,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the insight and will try to post tonight or tomorrow morning on the IC thread. <br /> <br /> The thing is that from an OOC perspective, pretty sure you would win the Duel. You have 4s in Attributes whereas Mathias is more well rounded, and a condition you're requesting that lets you win a round, and more WP (so more Doors). From a practical standpoint, it's Moonstone's smartest way to beat an opponent who could outclass him in a straight magical fight. <br /> <br /> The part I just need to decide is whether Mathias would consider that, and whether he's ok with the stakes you proposed. The issue is that Mathias' terms are really quite mild, whereas Moonstone's could cost him an incredible amount of reputation among the entire Consilium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:21:50-07:00","id":985760,"title":"","content":"Here's my hot take:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985734#post985734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that from an OOC perspective, pretty sure you would win the Duel. You have 4s in Attributes whereas Mathias is more well rounded, and a condition you're requesting that lets you win a round, and more WP (so more Doors). From a practical standpoint, it's Moonstone's smartest way to beat an opponent who could outclass him in a straight magical fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the idea, yeah. Unlike say, research or persuasion, this is a challenge that Moonstone is well equipped to win. And I cast Know Nature to learn his stats with this duel in mind. Mages are at their best when they prepare ahead of time!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The part I just need to decide is whether Mathias would consider that, and whether he's ok with the stakes you proposed. The issue is that Mathias' terms are really quite mild, whereas Moonstone's could cost him an incredible amount of reputation among the entire Consilium. </div> </div> </div>Unless Mathias or Valentine cast a spell like Know Nature or Divination, which would be Withstood by his Cloak (again, prep) in addition to the usual rating, I don't know how they would consider his stats or his likelihood of victory. On the face of it, he's a newly Awakened mage with a head too big for his shoulders, and Moonstone got an exceptional success on a roll to goad Mathias into dueling out of Pride, his Vice, which Moonstone also took the time to discover in-character. Even if his stakes are unreasonable, how could Mathias possibly lose? He's an Adept going against a Disciple.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, the outcome of a duel is that the winner gets the Triumphant condition and the loser gets the Defeated condition, which I intended Moonstone's stakes to model. They're absolutely intended to be punitive, but as the Storyteller, you also decide exactly what the fallout entails. I don't know what you have in mind for your setting, but as I imagined it, this kind of thing happens all the time in a Consilium. Mages duel each other over points of honor and petty rivalry and gain or lose face.<br /> <br /> And even if Moonstone wins and Mathias loses a huge amount of reputation...okay? He's an NPC. The actions of a player character will have affected the setting in a meaningful way, and it will add an interesting dynamic to Mathias' relationship with Ragnar as a mentor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:53:04-07:00","id":985818,"title":"","content":"You know, that's a really good point. I want to reinforce you as a player for doing something cool. And I need to remember that Mathias is an NPC, not my character. I've been RPing each of the NPCs as if I were playing them, but that takes away my attention from the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T19:31:32-07:00","id":985890,"title":"","content":"I agree that Moonstone fighting- and beating- Mathias in a Duel Arcane would be interesting. But I'm sure that narratively, once the dust settles, the cabal will find a way to gel and come to terms with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:35:17-07:00","id":985970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985818#post985818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, that's a really good point. I want to reinforce you as a player for doing something cool. And I need to remember that Mathias is an NPC, not my character. I've been RPing each of the NPCs as if I were playing them, but that takes away my attention from the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for understanding! I'm sorry if I came off a little thorny. In my opinion, it's perfectly cool to be fond of your NPCs, it's just that they're unlike player characters in that the ST has a whole stable of them whereas the players have one persistent character which they're loyal to, and that colors how to use them.<br /> <br /> I think your read of the Duel Arcane rules is the same as mine, I wish they had been more clear about some things in the errata. Only things I would add: I don't see anything about not being able to spend Willpower on your roll, but if you'd like to run with that restriction I'm okay with it. Also, what happens if one party tries all 3 of their Arcana against a Door and fails with each one? I assume that means you can't open that Door with an attack and have to try Negotiate instead, and can try again if the Door opens that way.<br /> <br /> I'll keep my IC posts brief and quick, I strongly agree about not slowing things down. I don't want to own the spotlight or cause a snarl here, any more than I already have at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-12-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:03:49-07:00","id":986287,"title":"","content":"I'll leave it up to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> whether the memory of Hakim particularly resembles Anubis, I would lean towards no because Phoenix and Moonstone are already at rock bottom right now and this probably isn't the best time to drop that bomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:14:30-07:00","id":986333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=985970#post985970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your read of the Duel Arcane rules is the same as mine, I wish they had been more clear about some things in the errata. Only things I would add: I don't see anything about not being able to spend Willpower on your roll, but if you'd like to run with that restriction I'm okay with it. Also, what happens if one party tries all 3 of their Arcana against a Door and fails with each one? I assume that means you can't open that Door with an attack and have to try Negotiate instead, and can try again if the Door opens that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that Willpower is reflected in Doors; the loser of the Duel loses all of their Willpower, reflected in all of their Doors being opened during the Duel Arcane. Because Willpower is quantified in this fight in your health, allowing Willpower on the rolls seems to give a very unfair advantage to whoever happens to have highest Resolve + Composure. Perhaps that's the point? But if so, that means Moonstone could stand toe to toe with just about any mage, because you only need 1 success to open a Door. That doesn't seem to make sense to me thematically.<br /> <br /> I'm going to post on the Mage forums here and see if I can get more ideas to make this more interactive. I would rather not change the rules mid-Duel unless you prefer it, and instead apply it to Duels in the future. But yeah, it seems pretty non-interactive.<br /> <br /> The other issue I'm seeing quickly is that because you can only open 1 Door per turn, we're going to need a <i>lot</i> of back and forth here to end the Duel unless someone concedes. Works great in person, not as much in PBP. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:35:04-07:00","id":986352,"title":"","content":"I think the fun of an in-person duel is trading Imago descriptions back and forth and rolling dice in real time, which doesn't translate as well in this medium. I've seen some permutations that draw on the Social Maneuvering and Chase systems and create Fighting Styles just for dueling, but it's a little thin on the ground, yeah.<br /> <br /> Here's a suggestion: in the name of moving things along, we could abstract the exchange a little bit. Perhaps I could roll my actions for 3 turns at once on the next volley, and you could respond with 3 rolls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:39:09-07:00","id":986356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986352#post986352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the fun of an in-person duel is trading Imago descriptions back and forth and rolling dice in real time, which doesn't translate as well in this medium. I've seen some permutations that draw on the Social Maneuvering and Chase systems and create Fighting Styles just for dueling, but it's a little thin on the ground, yeah.<br /> <br /> Here's a suggestion: in the name of moving things along, we could abstract the exchange a little bit. Perhaps I could roll my actions for 3 turns at once on the next volley, and you could respond with 3 rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that sounds great. Still leaves room for Defending or Negotiating after that salvo.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, let's make it 2 rolls because Mathias is already at 3/6 Doors and he would eventually start defending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-12-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T17:48:12-07:00","id":986493,"title":"","content":"&quot;You can't just keep dueling away from your problems, Moonstone!&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://poorlydrawnlines.com/comic/jetpack/\" target=\"_blank\">But he totally could, and it was awesome.</a><br /> <br /> (sorry, I missed your edit about 2 rolls rather than 3. i really wasn't expecting that exchange to end it, but i'm glad it didn't drag on too long!)<br /> <br /> e: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-sT4HZR9Pc4\" target=\"_blank\">Moonstone and Mathias</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:47:53-07:00","id":986554,"title":"","content":"The official text color for Nicki Minaj in this chronicle is <span style=\"color:#DDA0DD\">Plum.</span> This is canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:55:31-07:00","id":986560,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Yep, sure, take a Beat for the Aspiration and then replace it with a new one! Forgot about that one. Same goes for other people here - tell me if you think you satisfied an Aspiration/Obsession and I'll let you know what I think. It's hard for me to keep those all straight without reminders, but you deserve the Beats.<br /> <br /> Question: Am I missing something here? What does Moonstone mean by this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Oh- don't get up. Tell the people what he's won, Mathias.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I figured you might want to interject here but didn't want to slow the scene down, so I just included all of Mathias' comments in one paragraph. We can assume he would pause for you long enough to speak up and taunt him.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I forgot to state it explicitly, but Moonstone gains the Triumphant condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-12-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T21:10:14-07:00","id":986568,"title":"","content":"That line just stuck in my mind as a gameshow host type thing to say, haha. He's referring to himself in the third person, and inviting Mathias to say what he says in your post.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that's done with quickly and we can get back to the other characters, to be honest! Maybe +1 Beat or Arcane Beat for everyone else would be in order, to reflect witnessing a Duel Arcane for the first time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-13-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T23:51:47-07:00","id":986609,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a>, I...I read that response post, and I honestly have no idea what's the proper reaction here. It's refuge in audacity. I can't help but chuckle. Moonstone is a narcissistic twat, and I'm loving him for it. To quote:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Never do anything by halves if you want to get away with it. Be outrageous. Go the whole hog. Make sure everything you do is so completely crazy it's unbelievable.&quot;</i> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">\u2014 Matilda</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> As for Lynx... I don't think he's impressed with anyone or anything. I'll have to sort out his feelings as well. Fucking hell, this campaign is gold. Thank you, everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:14:48-07:00","id":986644,"title":"","content":"It's been a pleasure even only reading it. Can't wait to hop in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:08:21-07:00","id":986687,"title":"","content":"Oh, Moonstone. He gives me strength. <br /> <br /> I think my solution to the staff ownership question should be satisfactory to both parties. And I think Ragnar's going to try and draw up a contract or bill of rights for the cabal once everybody has joined in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:22:47-07:00","id":986693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986687#post986687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my solution to the staff ownership question should be satisfactory to both parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my eyes, it seems reasonable. But, Phoenix is not only extremely pissed at Moonstone, he's also a bit paranoid of the guy. That, and he's an Obrimos, and once an Obrimos makes up their mind...<br /> <br /> Sorry to say, but Phoenix ain't havin' it. He will insist Moonstone either gives it up or fights for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:30:29-07:00","id":986695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986644#post986644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a pleasure even only reading it. Can't wait to hop in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Won't be long! I'm going to be ending this Chapter in just a little bit, once the action settles and everyone's ok with moving on.<br /> <br /> Before we move on to the next chapter, everyone is going to have a few in-character days to take care of personal errands, explore their own agenda, and maybe introduce some other NPCs to plant some seeds for future events or potential plot hooks. Once this scene is over, we'll be moving towards that, and that is when I'd like to introduce Ouroboros Ophis.<br /> <br /> Before we can do that, I still need you to add an updated backstory to your character post (which I have linked <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=984363#post984363\">here</a>; let me know if you are going to be using a different post as your primary character sheet).<br /> <br /> Here are a few issues or decisions I'd like you to address in your backstory:<br /> <br /> 1) Ophis is newly Awakened in the past week. He would have met Mathias and/or other members from this cabal sometime in the past few days, who would have given a lot of the same basic information about mage society as the others received in this scene (e.g., basics of Paths, Arcana, Orders, Consilium politics). Please decide who you would've met, and the circumstances under which they met. (If you don't want to pick this, let me know -- really doesn't matter, I'm just giving you more leeway to decide events relevant to your PC).<br /> <br /> 2) Your character would be involved in the University of Chicago in some capacity. He could be a teacher at the UofC medical school, a full-time clinician, or perhaps a retired colleague or previous employee depending on the age you choose for him. He would be contacted by a Dean this week with a plea to cover a FYS class for the semester due to Dr. McCallister unexpectedly leaving her post (more to come on this for everyone!). Given Ouroboros Ophis' personality and interest in mentoring the younger generation, I think Ophis would love the chance to do this. But maybe he's annoyed it's taking him away from his medical work; include in your backstory how he feels about it.<br /> <br /> 3) Can you clarify what you mean by your long-term Aspiration to &quot;regain his life&quot;? The wording is vague to me.<br /> <br /> 4) Let me know if you have any other questions or need help adapting the backstory you've previously included to fit the game now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:40:21-07:00","id":986700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986687#post986687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Moonstone. He gives me strength.<br /> <br /> I think my solution to the staff ownership question should be satisfactory to both parties. And I think Ragnar's going to try and draw up a contract or bill of rights for the cabal once everybody has joined in.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986693#post986693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my eyes, it seems reasonable. But, Phoenix is not only extremely pissed at Moonstone, he's also a bit paranoid of the guy. That, and he's an Obrimos, and once an Obrimos makes up their mind...<br /> <br /> Sorry to say, but Phoenix ain't havin' it. He will insist Moonstone either gives it up or fights for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think it makes a lot of Phoenix to not be putting up with any shit from Moonstone right now, and he will see the artifact as his. And as they'll learn more about the local laws on recovering artifacts, Phoenix does have a rightful claim to the object. Mathias would've been the one to talk about it in more detail, but he's a little preoccupied with moping at the moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:57:42-07:00","id":986707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986695#post986695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Ophis is newly Awakened in the past week. He would have met Mathias and/or other members from this cabal sometime in the past few days, who would have given a lot of the same basic information about mage society as the others received in this scene (e.g., basics of Paths, Arcana, Orders, Consilium politics). Please decide who you would've met, and the circumstances under which they met. (If you don't want to pick this, let me know -- really doesn't matter, I'm just giving you more leeway to decide events relevant to your PC).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just brainstorming here. <br /> <br /> Both Lynx and Ophis Awakened after the Deathstorm. I think this is an opportunity. Would it be possible to have his Awakening having somehow coincided with Lynx's? Maybe they happened simultaneously (down to the exact minute - spooky!) or they met (or were close to meeting) during their experiences? Though Lynx had a Mystery Play, and I don't know how Ophis experienced his. Would be an interesting take on fate and destiny and timing if a Mastigos, Obrimos and Acanthus also Awakened in the same moment - a sort of tug of war between player agency and whether or not Fate should be followed at every turn.<br /> <br /> Up to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:20:04-07:00","id":986857,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> I get that you're roleplaying and Phoenix would be mad or whatever, but can you please dial back on the physical hostility and cursing? I'm a femme guy and I get a lot of verbal and physical shit from masculine guys, particularly in the dating world, and it legitimately makes me pretty uncomfortable to read that stuff in a game that I'm playing for fun.<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-13-2016, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:20:57-07:00","id":986886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986857#post986857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> I get that you're roleplaying and Phoenix would be mad or whatever, but can you please dial back on the physical hostility and cursing? I'm a femme guy and I get a lot of verbal and physical shit from masculine guys, particularly in the dating world, and it legitimately makes me pretty uncomfortable to read that stuff in a game that I'm playing for fun.<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry about that. I'll be sure to note that in the future. Phoenix is a <i>very</i> masculine guy and playing him is quite a power trip for me, but I should be able to take it down a notch when interacting with Moonstone.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> How was my last post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:37:42-07:00","id":986957,"title":"","content":"That's totally fine, thanks for understanding!<br /> <br /> Similar to the power trip you mention- I really like playing Moonstone because, with this thing with Mathias for example, it's fun to play a character who absolutely doesn't tolerate being hurt or abused, and has the resources to come out on top when he challenges someone on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-13-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:57:49-07:00","id":986967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986695#post986695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Won't be long! I'm going to be ending this Chapter in just a little bit, once the action settles and everyone's ok with moving on.<br /> <br /> Before we move on to the next chapter, everyone is going to have a few in-character days to take care of personal errands, explore their own agenda, and maybe introduce some other NPCs to plant some seeds for future events or potential plot hooks. Once this scene is over, we'll be moving towards that, and that is when I'd like to introduce Ouroboros Ophis.<br /> <br /> Before we can do that, I still need you to add an updated backstory to your character post (which I have linked <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=984363#post984363\">here</a>; let me know if you are going to be using a different post as your primary character sheet).</div> </div> </div> </div>Will do!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here are a few issues or decisions I'd like you to address in your backstory:<br /> <br /> 1) Ophis is newly Awakened in the past week. He would have met Mathias and/or other members from this cabal sometime in the past few days, who would have given a lot of the same basic information about mage society as the others received in this scene (e.g., basics of Paths, Arcana, Orders, Consilium politics). Please decide who you would've met, and the circumstances under which they met. (If you don't want to pick this, let me know -- really doesn't matter, I'm just giving you more leeway to decide events relevant to your PC). </div> </div> </div>Only a week, I see... Well, I was thinking he actually awakened shortly after the death of his parents and moving from New England to Chicago. I think, maybe Valentine is a good first contact with the Awakened community. He might have help him set up shop as a doctor and surgeon for &quot;especial clientele&quot;. Then the Deathstorm hit and he lost his wife in the debacle. He then focused on his job and his magical persona to an unhealthy degree, so maybe that's why they will introduce to rest of the characters, to ground him a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Your character would be involved in the University of Chicago in some capacity. He could be a teacher at the UofC medical school, a full-time clinician, or perhaps a retired colleague or previous employee depending on the age you choose for him. He would be contacted by a Dean this week with a plea to cover a FYS class for the semester due to Dr. McCallister unexpectedly leaving her post (more to come on this for everyone!). Given Ouroboros Ophis' personality and interest in mentoring the younger generation, I think Ophis would love the chance to do this. But maybe he's annoyed it's taking him away from his medical work; include in your backstory how he feels about it. </div> </div> </div> Nice. Maybe pushing him to interact with students was another step in taking him from the path he was set in, leaving almost everything behind as a copping mechanism. It will feel weird at first for him, but as you said, is something old Marvin used to love (he's 40)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Can you clarify what you mean by your long-term Aspiration to &quot;regain his life&quot;? The wording is vague to me. </div> </div> </div> My bad. Basically having a regular ( or as regular as it can be) social life outside of the magic community, like he had previous to his hermitage after the lost of his wife.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Let me know if you have any other questions or need help adapting the backstory you've previously included to fit the game now. </div> </div> </div>Not much, except for the dissapearance of his wife in the Deathstorm. He has a small clinic where mages (maybe other strange things) go when they need medical atention, and want to keep the Veil intact and little else. He and Phoenix knew each other from before, but, at least Ophis, was not a mage by then. He will sure be quite shocked, in a good way, when he sees him, he had a soft spot for the kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-13-2016, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T23:43:17-07:00","id":987119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=986857#post986857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> I get that you're roleplaying and Phoenix would be mad or whatever, but can you please dial back on the physical hostility and cursing? I'm a femme guy and I get a lot of verbal and physical shit from masculine guys, particularly in the dating world, and it legitimately makes me pretty uncomfortable to read that stuff in a game that I'm playing for fun.<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I also want to say that I'm sorry if my posts or Mathias' actions also caused distress for you as the player.<br /> <br /> I want to make it clear that Mathias' actions after the fight with Alux were fueled by his backstory and personal demons, which were hinted at but not fully divulged in this scene. But even with that history, he and the other Shields of Dawn have the temperaments that oppose pointless violence or brute forced methods. <br /> <br /> The reality though is that some other mages in this game setting could easily enjoy using their superior Arcana mastery to ruin Moonstone's day in a way that might evoke similar feelings of being threatened or controlled against his will -- things like being violently blasted away with magic, mind controlled, or humiliated by other magical means. This to me is an illustration of how access to real power can corrupt people, which is a core theme in this game. Do you think that might be a problem for you as well? Or are you asking that we avoid or minimize use of graphic physical violence related to acts of forced submission specifically?<br /> <br /> I also want to make sure that as a ST that I'm allowing each of our players to get the spotlight and feel successful and satisfied with their characters. I have no issue with PCs attacking or RPing through conflict together, especially in heated situations like what has happened here. Sometimes that leads to people arguing over which PC would be able to get the upper hand, and in my opinion, the most fair way to resolve that is to use the game mechanics (like attack/defense stats and rolls) inherent in this system. This is why Moonstone was able to evade Phoenix's attack earlier even though crapcarp wanted him to hit you, and why I agree that Moonstone should be able to escape his grab again now. Rules help arbitrate these conflicts. Do you have an issue with that approach to the game, or was it more specifically about the narrative used in his post when he tried to grab Moonstone (or something else altogether)?<br /> <br /> Basically I just need to know that if Phoenix or any NPC want to (and have the capacity to) get comeuppance against Moonstone that we're on the same page about it, because this issue is likely to come up again. Power and control are parts of this game system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-14-2016, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:17:23-07:00","id":987399,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean to make it a big problem, let me be a little more clear. I pretty much don't have an issue with things NPCs do, because that's more easily resolved. I do sort of prefer explicitly magical/supernatural/fantastical threats (being trapped in a Space ward, banished to the Shadow, attacked by dude with flaming sword, pursued by demon monster, Mind control in small doses, etc) over totally mundane and grounded harm (being mugged or beaten up in a dark alley, using slurs, etc). Like in my home game, there was initially a focus on racialized gang violence in the background, until the group decided that wasn't fun and we replaced those elements with more fantastic Jet Set Radio/The Warriors style gangs.<br /> <br /> But the actual issue isn't so much the fictional content as that it was coming from a PC rather than an NPC. I can try to solve or just endure something coming from an NPC in a variety of ways, but I don't want there to be a status quo of open hostility and fighting with another PC where we're both going to be working together. That and the language used for Phoenix's narration about Moonstone read to me as kind of over-the-top cruel and demeaning in a way that was a little too close to home. Like, because of the fact that we're in a group together, Moonstone isn't just going to bug out and leave if there's an issue with another PC, and what's unfun for me is being in a position where there's a problem that might cause OOC tension if it were resolved with game rules. I just want everybody to be friends!<br /> <br /> That's all! Again, not meaning to make it a huge concern, it's just something that had been bothering me for a little while that I decided to state openly instead of ignoring. Thanks for being accommodating!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-14-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:22:59-07:00","id":987548,"title":"","content":"Gotcha, that makes a ton of sense and I appreciate the extra input and insight. <br /> <br /> FYI, I'm out of town this weekend so I may have limited opportunity to post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T06:26:00-07:00","id":988222,"title":"","content":"We're about to wrap up this scene and move into a bit of individual stuff before the chapter ends. If you have time or know what you'd like to do with a few in-character days, please post here and let me know. It will help keep us all on the same speed and be able to move into the next chapter. This includes Ouroboros Ophis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:31:01-07:00","id":988277,"title":"","content":"I think we decided Lynx has a roommate, so Lynx will definitely want to get to know that NPC a bit. He'll call his parents after his first week in the US of A and express his excitement - or they'll call him. He'll want to get to know the suburb as well as the city, so he'll ask the other PCs to show him around and hang with them so long as he doesn't neglect his studies too much. He'd also check out the woods and (if prompted), the LGBT community. He'll try to get a hold of Dr. Asphodel and make sure she's okay too. <br /> <br /> He's itching to meet somebody else who understands the Wild, though, so finding another Thyrsus (or somebody else attuned to the Wild) is his main focus. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:19:04-07:00","id":988299,"title":"","content":"Moonstone's plan for the next few days: recover from his resistant Lethal damage at an Arrow sanctum, and hopefully get in touch with Hakim's former cabal just to say that he's Awakened, he might have a new cabal, and he'd like to be in touch with them going forward.<br /> <br /> Go to Rumors Nightclub, or some other semi-classy space that does cabaret and burlesque shows, and start talking to an organizer about dancing as part of a showcase. Ideally this would be Social Maneuvering to impress the lady/dude/person in charge and get on the list.<br /> <br /> Get the name of an Adept of Mind who might be willing to do some goetic summoning and Familiar binding for him, preferably one who respects the name of Hakim.<br /> <br /> Spend some time out around town collecting good sacraments for spellcasting, hopefully stuff suitable for a +2 Sacrament yantra. Old watches for Time, transit maps of the area for Space, crosswords and dream journals for Mind, etc. I was thinking I could make a Skill roll now and then treat my total successes as a pool that I can spend in the future to have the perfect sacrament on hand for a given spell.<br /> <br /> Also there's some specific spells I want to cast, possibly ritual cast some of them as long as we're hanging out at a proper sanctum.<ul><li>Divination to learn when and where Alux will return from hibernation. There's also a Time/Space spell from Banishers that I want to adapt which lets you learn the perfect time and place to attack someone, and gives bonuses/penalties if you do so (maybe modeled on Fate boons/hexes.)</li> <li>Attempt Postcognition to see what happened in the scene Moonstone and Phoenix spent in the otherworld. I assume this will be more complicated than that because the portal exists in a weird place relative to Time, but I want to see what happens. Also try Perfect Recall for a similar effect.</li> <li>Dream Reaching to see what Mathias is dreaming about, just from sheer voyeuristic curiosity and looking for insight into things the prophet sees on the horizon.</li> <li>Correspondence as a ritual casting to further his Obsession. I want to boost Potency as high as possible and cast it on Hakim with the Reach options to follow a trail and see a specific type of connection (those related to the Deathstorm, if they exist). Moonstone has three hypotheses right now: either all victims of the Deathstorm have Sympathy to one another directly, or they each individually have Sympathy to a single person/entity/place/thing that embodies the storm, or there is no shared Sympathy and it's a null result.</li> <li>Attempt to use Focused Mage Sight during Postcognition to scrutinize/reveal Alux. I'm thinking of targeting it during the 3 turns where it was manifested in the alley, and seeing what I can uncover.</li> <li>Do some experimentation with Sympathy, and learn whether or not he can effectively create a Symbolic-level sympathy yantra by acting as/impersonating someone (Manipulation+Expression) and recording the result. The image of Moonstone spending an hour alone, repeatedly trying to imitate someone's voice and the way they move, is deeply weird and unsettling and appealingly Mage-y to me.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-16-2016, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:46:51-07:00","id":988345,"title":"","content":"After this scene ends, Ragnar's probably going to head home (which would introduce Patty, his eccentric Comp Sci and Sleepwalker roommate), and maybe hop on a dating or hookup app to indulge his Vice and get a point of Willpower back. Other than that, he'll be attending classes (possibly represented with one or more Intelligence + Academics rolls to see how he's doing in his classes?), and might start working on his Obsession or one of his Aspirations. <br /> <br /> He might also play around with Time to review the events of the day, especially with regards to the fight with Alux and the events that followed after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:38:50-07:00","id":988894,"title":"","content":"The main thing I can think of are to start making the bookstore more appropriate as a sanctum, which may involve casting some spells. Probably will be looking into changing the store's name now that he knows having his sympathetic name on the door might be risky.<br /> <br /> He'd also try to start at getting a feel for the local spirits, as limited as his ability there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:04:01-07:00","id":988989,"title":"","content":"Other than starting getting the gist of the classes and maybe getting a pet snake, I don't know what I want Ophis to do before meeting the cabal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:14:02-07:00","id":989169,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks all! I was waiting to see if anyone else had lingering IC questions to ask or comments to make before finishing this scene, and then we'll move into the individual stuff. Let me know if you're done with this scene.<br /> <br /> My plan for wrapping up the chapter was to use broader narrative perspectives and summaries, with maybe one &quot;mini-scene&quot; per PC, but if the things your characters would like to do require multiple locations/settings and dice rolls, we can do that too. I'll experiment with it and will solicit feedback after we do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-17-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:15:52-07:00","id":989170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=988989#post988989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than starting getting the gist of the classes and maybe getting a pet snake, I don't know what I want Ophis to do before meeting the cabal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do hope you realize that Ragnar's going to unleash his full powers of snark one he finds out the guy with the snake-themed Shadow Name is looking to get a pet snake. Assuming Moonstone doesn't beat him to the punch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:33:44-07:00","id":989189,"title":"","content":"Its only fair you do. It is related, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:53:55-07:00","id":989196,"title":"","content":"I think everyone's done with the scene, yeah. I can condense most of my downtime actions to one post that's just broadly &quot;several things Moonstone did over the next few days&quot; without requiring extensive detail, and follow up on any consequences in another post or two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=989170#post989170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do hope you realize that Ragnar's going to unleash his full powers of snark one he finds out the guy with the snake-themed Shadow Name is looking to get a pet snake. Assuming Moonstone doesn't beat him to the punch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;More like Ouroboros <i>Ophiuchus </i>at this rate, am I right???&quot;<br /> <br /> [silence]<br /> <br /> &quot;i'm sorry, about your dead wife <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot; <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-18-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T22:47:16-07:00","id":989223,"title":"","content":"Unless something happens that Phoenix would respond to, I'm done with the scene.<br /> <br /> As for down time stuff, Phoenix'll still be trying to find Anubis. Should I roll for it? Other than that, Phoenix will train with the staff. To represent this mechanically, I'll spend 1 Experience on the Defensive Combat Merit for Weaponry.<br /> <br /> The Consilium meeting is going to be played out, or at least be dealt with in some way, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:25:19-07:00","id":989234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=989196#post989196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think everyone's done with the scene, yeah. I can condense most of my downtime actions to one post that's just broadly &quot;several things Moonstone did over the next few days&quot; without requiring extensive detail, and follow up on any consequences in another post or two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;More like Ouroboros <i>Ophiuchus </i>at this rate, am I right???&quot;<br /> <br /> [silence]<br /> <br /> &quot;i'm sorry, about your dead wife <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot; <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, hopefully she's not dead, just missing. We'll see.<br /> <br /> I figure we will all get together at the Consilium meeting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T04:59:24-07:00","id":989292,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think Ragnar's accomplished all he needs or wants to in this scene. He'l broach the topic of apprenticeship to Mathias at the Consilium meeting Saturday- no point talking to him when he's trying to get over losing the Duel Arcane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:32:42-07:00","id":989892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=989223#post989223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Consilium meeting is going to be played out, or at least be dealt with in some way, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, we will be starting the new chapter around the time of the meeting at that location. The Shields of Dawn will meet up with your group shortly before it starts to go over a couple of things.<br /> <br /> As for the downtime stuff, I will include in the IC thread which things I'm requesting rolls for. Just need to type it up and it'll make more sense.<br /> <br /> For everyone: Hoping to get that post up today, work has been slower today. I'm going to be experimenting with the narrative/storytelling style for this kind of scene in which things are moving at a faster time pace. I still want you to be able to roleplay or have meaningful interactions with people if that's what you'd want to do. I'm just trying to do a more fast-forward kind of approach here to save time. If we were playing in person, this is the kind of scene where I'd give each of you a couple of minutes to summarize what you're doing with downtime, make rolls, and tell you what happens based on those efforts. It's a little harder to capture in PBP format but I think it'll be fine. Let me know what you think once we're past it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T00:57:03-07:00","id":990322,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking the time to write a long post for us!<br /> <br /> I made a long post in response, but it might have been too long because it didn't go through yet. I only need some quick feedback from you before I do the rest of my plans: getting a Condition from dramatic failing Divination, signing off that my Yantra gathering rolls are okay, and moving on with the Social maneuvering.<br /> <br /> Here's what I had in mind for the Condition, which could be a good template for other spellcasting dramatic failures in the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cut Off</b><br /> The future is closed to you. You cannot cast &quot;Divination&quot; or other spells affecting the future. In addition, you take -2 and an automatic +1 Paradox die on all Time spells.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Successfully cast a spell using the Time Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T03:59:54-07:00","id":990364,"title":"","content":"I think the forums ate your post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Did you by any chance save it somewhere else or have a way to pull up a draft?<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, if anyone wants an NPC introduced that's related to your character (like Patty or Ewan) and you have a picture that you really like, post a link! I enjoy finding ones for NPCs but if it's your NPC, I want you to be able to help create the game universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:08:53-07:00","id":990394,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Since we're in downtime mode IC, I was wondering what you think about spellcasting in downtime? If the spell to be cast doesn't require answers from the DM (e.g. Fate or Time spells) and doesn't have any consequence of failure, is there a reason to roll for them or can I just say the spell was cast eventually over the course of a morning hour or similar?<br /> <br /> E.g., Lynx wanted to cast Life 2 &quot;Body Control&quot; on himself the next morning. With free reach he'd have Advanced Duration and Instant Casting, and to keep the dice pool above 0, he can do Potency 2. He'd have a paradox risk-free spell with 2 dice. Since regular failure would give no consequences at all, can I say Lynx manages to cast and maintain the spell, or do I have to do the rolls in character?<br /> <br /> EDIT: With my Exceptional success from the Empathy roll earlier, don't I also get a Condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-20-2016, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:34:24-07:00","id":990404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=990394#post990394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Since we're in downtime mode IC, I was wondering what you think about spellcasting in downtime? If the spell to be cast doesn't require answers from the DM (e.g. Fate or Time spells) and doesn't have any consequence of failure, is there a reason to roll for them or can I just say the spell was cast eventually over the course of a morning hour or similar?<br /> <br /> E.g., Lynx wanted to cast Life 2 &quot;Body Control&quot; on himself the next morning. With free reach he'd have Advanced Duration and Instant Casting, and to keep the dice pool above 0, he can do Potency 2. He'd have a paradox risk-free spell with 2 dice. Since regular failure would give no consequences at all, can I say Lynx manages to cast and maintain the spell, or do I have to do the rolls in character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great question, and one I don't think we've addressed here yet. If you're in a tense or time-limited situation, you can make consecutive attempts on a roll but at -1 penalty for each consecutive attempt. However, you don't get penalized for rolls that are free of time pressure.<br /> <br /> Let's go with this: If the spell is instant cast and does not risk Paradox, and the dice pool is above 0, I'd like you to at least roll it on the dice roller once. If it fails, you can &quot;take 1&quot; -- basically assume you eventually cast it with 1 success, or keep rerolling if preferred. If the spell is cast as a ritual, I'd like you to roll each time; you'll take -1 consecutive rolls on the ritual because it takes up time, so there's time pressure and implications of failing the roll. For spells that risk Paradox, I'd like you to roll each attempt because of the cumulative bonuses to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> Spells that fit multiple categories above use both sets of rules. So for example, instant-cast spells that risk Paradox will have the additional +1 Paradox per roll, but no cumulative -1 penalty to the roll itself. Ritual-cast spells that risk Paradox will have cumulative -1 penalty to the spell casting roll and +1 Paradox.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With my Exceptional success from the Empathy roll earlier, don't I also get a Condition? </div> </div> </div>Yes, you do! Go ahead and pick a beneficial condition of your choosing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:47:43-07:00","id":990405,"title":"","content":"That makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> I'll go for Steadfast as a condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:19:28-07:00","id":990419,"title":"","content":"Split my draft into two posts. I think I probably had too many HTML links in one post?<br /> <br /> Thanks for clarifying the spellcasting for this, that's helpful!<br /> <br /> I might get some NPC pictures together. Also, would you mind if I put together simple character sheets for the named members of Hakim's cabal using that XP template I posted in the other thread? Of course you could change them as you like, this is just to give a model of their important stats. I was thinking that they're Gnosis 4 so they have access to some Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:56:36-07:00","id":990443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=990419#post990419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Split my draft into two posts. I think I probably had too many HTML links in one post?<br /> <br /> Thanks for clarifying the spellcasting for this, that's helpful!<br /> <br /> I might get some NPC pictures together. Also, would you mind if I put together simple character sheets for the named members of Hakim's cabal using that XP template I posted in the other thread? Of course you could change them as you like, this is just to give a model of their important stats. I was thinking that they're Gnosis 4 so they have access to some Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I've already incorporated your NPC building suggestions into my ST notes for the campaign. I was going to stat them at some point but that saves me time. Using your guidelines, I would either make them 2-dot NPCs and then pay to advance Gnosis to 4, or make them 3-dot NPCs, whichever you think is most appropriate. I'll use that as a starting point and tweak as I see fit. If you could, please post the stats in text format so I can copy/paste, rather than uploading a file (e.g., Dropbox, Google Drive) -- otherwise I won't be able to access at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:00:53-07:00","id":990447,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I admire how you're fleshing out the world and your background in your posts. Moonstone feels very established as a character. I have no idea how to replicate that myself - Lynx feels a little...feeble in comparison. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I've changed Lynx's &quot;Get to know the group&quot; Aspiration to &quot;Get to know a Thyrsus&quot; - is that appropriate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:05:15-07:00","id":990448,"title":"","content":"Dang it, I was totally thinking about dipping out of the mage meeting early to pick up Forest from school but decided against it since I didn't actually have any indication of what time it was XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:11:53-07:00","id":990473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=990447#post990447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I admire how you're fleshing out the world and your background in your posts. Moonstone feels very established as a character. I have no idea how to replicate that myself - Lynx feels a little...feeble in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfft, I disagree about your assessment of Lynx! You've created an NPC and gave me ideas on your vision for him, you're including details about his actions and goals, and I think his character voice is also strong and developing. I think Moonstone's strength of personality and comfort with the Supernal is largely a reflection of the PC's knowledge of mage society, as well as clear experience on Caldriu's part as a Mage player and storyteller. Lynx's voice is developing and I really like him as a character, and you'll find more ways to develop him and your character concept through playing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I've changed Lynx's &quot;Get to know the group&quot; Aspiration to &quot;Get to know a Thyrsus&quot; - is that appropriate? </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. It's a good reflection of his current goal and further communicates to me what Lynx's priorities are right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:13:32-07:00","id":990474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=990448#post990448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dang it, I was totally thinking about dipping out of the mage meeting early to pick up Forest from school but decided against it since I didn't actually have any indication of what time it was XD</div> </div> </div> </div>This is mostly for character development and further creating inter- and intrapersonal conflict for Binder. I really like the idea of him having to learn how to navigate the boundaries around his Sleeper and Awakened lives. Since he didn't ask to leave early, I thought it was a great way to showcase that in this scene.<br /> <br /> That being said, if Binder would have committed to leaving and would've prioritized picking up his son, and it was just you as the player who forgot to ask about that, let me know. We can retroactively change the scene if you want, it's really no big deal. He may have missed some of the conversation and consequently missed out on some of their last-minute advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:24:28-07:00","id":990590,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's fine. This is literally one of my aspirations after all, haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T20:34:17-07:00","id":990776,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna drop this here so it doesn't get lost in an edit: Moonstone instant casts a Space 1 Knowing spell, Potency 2, to ask two questions about his own Sympathy: <i>do I have Weak or Medium sympathy to Alux? </i>And, <i>can I use &quot;Alux&quot; as that entity's Sympathetic Name?</i><br /> <br /> Gnosis 1, Space 2, tool +1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447817\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a><br /> <br /> With that I should have all the mechanical stuff I need for spellcasting city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T01:37:32-07:00","id":991308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ragnar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]some muscly closeted guy who's going to UChi too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dear. Does this mean what I think it means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T02:50:42-07:00","id":991320,"title":"","content":"Could it actually be your roomate? I also thought that inmediately. It would explain why is so self conscious about nudity before you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-22-2016, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:35:24-07:00","id":991337,"title":"","content":"Sorry Thorbes, didn't see your post until just now. I'll give some more info for you today or tonight when I have time! Out of town again this weekend and wanted to get the rest of the post up at least.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, added something for you. Wasn't sure what other input you needed for now? Let me know if I missed something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-22-2016, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:15:32-07:00","id":991347,"title":"","content":"Don't worry at all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, It is confirmed, your roomate is a closeted gay, Linx <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:04:49-07:00","id":991359,"title":"","content":"Sorry for a bit of an absence, I'll rectify that now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> If the down time's 4 days, wouldn't we recover 4 Willpower?<br /> <br /> As for NPCs connected to Phoenix, there's the other staff for the martial arts center (the website linked on the character sheet has some photos), which on Tuesday he would be late to attend. They're not unfamiliar to violence though, so it can be reasonably assumed that they've been in quite a few scuffles and therefore know when someone's been in a very serious fight. Result, they would be concerned over what happened, and Phoenix would try to brush them off as much as he could. I'll come up with a roll for that, feel free to have it changed if you see fit.<br /> <br /> Besides the staff, there's the whole student angle as well. Perhaps one could look up to him, think he's the coolest of the teachers there, and therefore be closer than other students. They'd probably be one of the people to check and try out the staff.<br /> <br /> Another area are other Hunters, and in particular, the cell that helped with trying to take out &quot;Anubis&quot;. Now would be a good time to bring that little plot hook in, I think. You'll see what I mean in my next IC post. As for stats, pictures, and all that stuff, I'll leave up to you, or I can handle it if it's too much work for you.<br /> <br /> The final area can think up of for now is the new roommate. I don't have much in the way of that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 10-22-2016, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T08:39:36-07:00","id":991405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You either need to use a different spell to let you speak with them and understand them, or use your Spirit 2 Attainment if you want to interact with them. Either way, take an Arcane Beat for your first chance to really study spirits and attempts to interact with them. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exorcist's Eye</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first spell most Spirit mages learn, this spell allows the mage to perceive and speak with spirits in the physical world, whether they are roaming freely in Twilight, slumbering within an object (including discorporated spirits in hibernation), or possessing a living being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have I misunderstood something here, or...?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=991347#post991347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry at all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, It is confirmed, your roomate is a closeted gay, Linx <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>: D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 10-22-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:03:15-07:00","id":991630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=991359#post991359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for a bit of an absence, I'll rectify that now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> If the down time's 4 days, wouldn't we recover 4 Willpower?<br /> <br /> As for NPCs connected to Phoenix, there's the other staff for the martial arts center (the website linked on the character sheet has some photos), which on Tuesday he would be late to attend. They're not unfamiliar to violence though, so it can be reasonably assumed that they've been in quite a few scuffles and therefore know when someone's been in a very serious fight. Result, they would be concerned over what happened, and Phoenix would try to brush them off as much as he could. I'll come up with a roll for that, feel free to have it changed if you see fit.<br /> <br /> Besides the staff, there's the whole student angle as well. Perhaps one could look up to him, think he's the coolest of the teachers there, and therefore be closer than other students. They'd probably be one of the people to check and try out the staff.<br /> <br /> Another area are other Hunters, and in particular, the cell that helped with trying to take out &quot;Anubis&quot;. Now would be a good time to bring that little plot hook in, I think. You'll see what I mean in my next IC post. As for stats, pictures, and all that stuff, I'll leave up to you, or I can handle it if it's too much work for you.<br /> <br /> The final area can think up of for now is the new roommate. I don't have much in the way of that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, should be 4 days. I forgot that in 2E you get WP every time you wake up on a new day. I miscounted days. So everyone will get 4 WP over this time period, not 3. Good catch!<br /> <br /> For the NPCs: what would help me the most would be names, brief summaries of personalities, and any special requests/ideas you have for the NPCs. For example, Patty is a Sleepwalker, but Ragnar doesn't know that yet. Give me some ideas on the personalities, like how Caladriu did for the Knights of Alhambra, and I have no issue taking it from there.<br /> <br /> How about this: You focus on some of the people at the dojo, and I'll create an NPC for you as your potential roommate. I'll include more info in my next IC post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-22-2016, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:04:10-07:00","id":991632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=991405#post991405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I misunderstood something here, or...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, I'm dumb. Totally missed that from the spell description. I'll edit the scene, sorry!<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, added the stuff about the spirit's interaction with you. Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-23-2016, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:25:08-07:00","id":991687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=991308#post991308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh dear. Does this mean what I think it means?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't precisely intend for it to be Ewan. In my mind, it might be him, it might not be. I tried to keep the post as IC as possible so that our dear ST could interpret it as he wanted to. Heck, it could still be a red herring. But if Ragnar did do it with Ewan... well, it's going to make things very interesting, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T01:47:24-07:00","id":991770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=991687#post991687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't precisely intend for it to be Ewan. In my mind, it might be him, it might not be. I tried to keep the post as IC as possible so that our dear ST could interpret it as he wanted to. Heck, it could still be a red herring. But if Ragnar did do it with Ewan... well, it's going to make things very interesting, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it would be. All the drama! ...but in a good way!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:09:12-07:00","id":991939,"title":"","content":"Phew. Sorry for that super-long string, I broke it up into multiple chunks so the forum wouldn't get mad at me for having too many HTML links in one post. I was working on bits of that in my free time over the last couple days. I'll try not to write that much at once in the future, I just had a big cumulative laundry list of stuff I'd been wanting to do when we got some downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:30:10-07:00","id":992121,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> How do you want me to handle Scrutinize rolls? Can I make multiple rolls per turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:49:14-07:00","id":992223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=992121#post992121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> How do you want me to handle Scrutinize rolls? Can I make multiple rolls per turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not under time pressure in the traditional sense, so you can make as many as you want. Just use the dice roller for each because there are consequences for failing rolls after the first few attempts; see the rules on Scrutiny for a refresher.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be clear, scrutiny is an extended action on which you can make new roll attempts every turn. So, when you're out of initiative, you can ignore the time limitations but need to be mindful of the consequences of failing after making multiple rolls (e.g., increased Opacity). Because you cast Postcognition using Advanced Duration and the option to &quot;scrub&quot; the feed, you have no time limitations on your roll. Does that make more sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Clarification 10-24-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T06:02:53-07:00","id":992344,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> - I may not have made this clear because you joined us mid-game, but I would like your character to not be initiated into an Order yet. I'll introduce an NPC that I will say you have met, someone from the Free Council who encouraged you to join the Order shortly after your Awakening, but I'd like the Order initiation process to happen on-screen for you as it will for everyone else (probably in the next chapter about to begin). As a result, you would not yet have access to your Order benefits: that includes the extra dot in Occult, Order Status, Rotes, or the High Speech merit.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - I think you've made some Occult rolls using that extra dot, so make sure to adjust accordingly until you're properly initiated. I won't go back and edit results of previous rolls. Ignore me if I'm wrong on the math.<br /> <br /> Going to reply to Thorbes' post and then I <i>think</i> that I'm up to speed on everyone in terms of ST input. If you're waiting for me to reply to something before you can move forward, please let me know. I might've missed something in the past few days.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Wanted to double check on you since Binder has been quiet, do you need any input from me or something else before we move forward?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:30:14-07:00","id":992530,"title":"","content":"I'll avoid unnecessary rolls in the future, sorry! It seemed to make sense before first attempting something new and arcane, I was surprised to get so many successes.<br /> <br /> I <i>think</i> I have the Occult pool right so far. Moonstone has Occult 4 and a seemingly relevant Specialty, and will get 5 once he joins an Order. I'll double-check next time I roll it though.<br /> <br /> Checking in with my Contact is the last action I wanted to take during downtime, I'm good after this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:44:06-07:00","id":992537,"title":"","content":"Cool. I want your characters to excel at the things you want to excel at! That's an aspect of these tabletop games that many people find so enjoyable, and I don't want to take that away. Rolling just doesn't always need to be there. Reminds me of earlier when Lynx rolled to &quot;safely harvest the mushrooms&quot; (tass) that I was offering to their group -- appreciate the PC's hesitation, but rolling seemed silly there. :P<br /> <br /> You're right, I totally forgot about the skill specialty. My bad!<br /> <br /> Thanks again for helping bring this game's setting to life. I really like your contributions, and appreciate your patience as I try to grow as a Storyteller. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:05:01-07:00","id":992904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=992344#post992344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Wanted to double check on you since Binder has been quiet, do you need any input from me or something else before we move forward?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry! Will be posting today!<br /> <br /> I have some ideas for things that Binder will want to pursue, but they're probably best saved for <i>after</i> he's initiated into an order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 10-25-2016, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:33:23-07:00","id":993009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=992904#post992904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry! Will be posting today!<br /> <br /> I have some ideas for things that Binder will want to pursue, but they're probably best saved for <i>after</i> he's initiated into an order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally fine, it's your call! Just wanted to make sure I wasn't missing anything, I'm trying to be helpful and responsive here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Didn't want you to miss out on opportunities for Binder's personal growth or RP, that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:30:55-07:00","id":993165,"title":"","content":"Just to be certain, the crow or raven oogling Lynx, is that a spirit or a physical bird?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:37:21-07:00","id":993219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=993165#post993165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be certain, the crow or raven oogling Lynx, is that a spirit or a physical bird?</div> </div> </div> </div>Physical bird. Neither your Peripheral Sight nor your Exorcist's Eye spell suggest a spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T11:49:48-07:00","id":994133,"title":"","content":"A bit of a bookkeeping update: In the document I use for tracking Storyteller notes and NPC stuff, I added a table to help me track everyone's Aspirations/Obsessions and which Beats and Arcane Beats you've earned in a given scene. This will help me better track how we're doing with experience economy, and I can help encourage or motivate players who are behind in Beats/Arcane Beats to do things that will earn those.<br /> <br /> It looks like fewer people resolved a Condition, either mundane or supernatural, this scene. I also see that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> is the only one who has consistently taken dramatic failures on both mundane and spellcasting rolls. Remember that you can take that option once per scene to earn extra experience!<br /> <br /> I'll be much better about this moving forward, so I apologize if the next bit here is redundant. If I've already told you to do the following, please ignore.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Gain an Arcane Beat for spending time and effort pursuing information about &quot;Anubis&quot;, which is your Obsession.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - Take an Arcane Beat for attempting to move forward with your Obsession about finding the Great Lynx, and making progress by learning about different types of spirits and how they interact with mages.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - Take a Beat for completing your Aspiration to investigate supernatural occurrences in your apartment complex. Replace it with another short-term Aspiration. Also, your long-term Aspiration is particularly long-term, in the sense that it would take a lot of time for Ragnar to graduate in game time. I'm going to try and provide more opportunities for you to continue pursuing that Aspiration, such as adding more meaningful scenes or references to your UChi course work or graduation requirements. However, if you would like to replace your long-term Aspiration now that you know more about your character and his personality, please feel free to do so and mention it in this thread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> - Can you please add your character's background to the post I have linked where you're keeping your current character sheet? I have the link cross-referenced on the first page of the IC and OOC threads. I want to be able to see your background and reference it periodically so I can keep thinking about ways to weave it into the main story and NPC relationships. Also, in case I didn't say it before, take an Arcane Beat for a meaningful interaction with supernatural creatures (ghosts) in this scene.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Still waiting to hear your thoughts on the Aspirations. One of them is supposed to be long-term, meaning that you get Beats for making headway towards it just like the long-term Obsession. I suggested keeping the long-term Aspiration for &quot;keeping magic secret from family&quot;, but wanted to see what you thought about that. Also wanted to remind you that there are lots of opportunities for Beats/Arcane Beats that you're missing, so feel free to do more this scene or just be mindful of those options in future scenes!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Can you double-check whether I gave you an extra Arcane Beat this scene? Wanted to confirm that you only took 1 Arcane Beat for resolving a Condition from spellcasting/Paradox. Otherwise, you're already done a great job at taking advantage of options to earn Beats and Arcane Beats, and have been doing so consistently across scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:33:02-07:00","id":994162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=994133#post994133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of a bookkeeping update: In the document I use for tracking Storyteller notes and NPC stuff, I added a table to help me track everyone's Aspirations/Obsessions and which Beats and Arcane Beats you've earned in a given scene. This will help me better track how we're doing with experience economy, and I can help encourage or motivate players who are behind in Beats/Arcane Beats to do things that will earn those.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good idea! I might steal that.<br /> <br /> Went back and checked where I got beats/arcane beats this scene.<ul><li>AB: spellcasting dramatic failure (Divination), took Irritable condition</li> <li>AB: risked Wisdom loss</li> <li>B: resolved Aspiration</li> <li>B: mundane dramatic failure (Scrutiny), attracted the attention of a Demon of Pandemonium</li> <li>B: resolved Steadfast condition (from mundane roll)</li> <li>AB: advanced Obsession</li> <li>AB: resolved Irritable condition (from spellcasting)</li> </ul><br /> That's pretty much all of the categories, actually. I guess Moonstone could still go on a Paradox-containing bender and take damage in his rightmost health box, but he's already learned his lesson about respecting his body and his magic this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-27-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:57:19-07:00","id":994169,"title":"","content":"I am rather out of IRL at the moment. Not sure when I'll get around to an update.<br /> <br /> At the moment I should have 2 beats and 4 arcane beats, but I don't remember exactly where I got all those beats from. I <i>think</i> it's something like this:<ul><li>1 beat and 1 arcane beat from resolving Conditions</li> <li>1 beat and 1 arcane beat from story progress</li> <li>1 arcane beat from encountering a new mystery (the spirits)</li> <li>1 arcane beat from progressing on Obsession</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:14:58-07:00","id":994175,"title":"","content":"Done, boss! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:32:34-07:00","id":994184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=994133#post994133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Still waiting to hear your thoughts on the Aspirations. One of them is supposed to be long-term, meaning that you get Beats for making headway towards it just like the long-term Obsession. I suggested keeping the long-term Aspiration for &quot;keeping magic secret from family&quot;, but wanted to see what you thought about that. Also wanted to remind you that there are lots of opportunities for Beats/Arcane Beats that you're missing, so feel free to do more this scene or just be mindful of those options in future scenes!.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I am gonna take your advice on keeping &quot;keep magic a secret,&quot; though way back when I didn't actually intend it to be. At first I thought it was kind of weird as a long-term aspiration, since there's no distinct end goal, but after some contemplation on the matter I decided that it does make sense, as it's a thing that is supposed to be continually coming up for Marlin (and would be anyway, even without the Aspiration).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure exactly how I'm missing out on potential Beats? I guess I'm not rolling for stuff or doing very much, haha.<br /> <br /> Will try to get a post up tonight (I'm still all out of whack; I used to plan and make posts at work, but my new job is busier than my old job, so I've got less time to do that and I haven't gotten used to devoting time in the evenings for it)<br /> <br /> EDIT: OK, so messing with Aspirations and Obsession. Here's what I'm thinking:<br /> <br /> Short-term: Join a cabal<br /> Short-term: Be inducted into an Order.<br /> Long-term: Keep magic a secret from his family.<br /> <br /> Obsession: Discover a cure for the Sleeping Curse.<br /> <br /> Obviously Binder isn't the first mage to try and look into this, and I'm 99% sure he can't accomplish it, but it reflects what's on his mind and his naivete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 10-27-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:41:55-07:00","id":994195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=994184#post994184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I am gonna take your advice on keeping &quot;keep magic a secret,&quot; though way back when I didn't actually intend it to be. At first I thought it was kind of weird as a long-term aspiration, since there's no distinct end goal, but after some contemplation on the matter I decided that it does make sense, as it's a thing that is supposed to be continually coming up for Marlin (and would be anyway, even without the Aspiration).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a neat idea even though it doesn't have a long-term goal. I think the idea is that eventually they could find out, at which time you lose the Aspiration and replace it with another one. Kind of like Phoenix's long-term Aspiration to keep the other Hunter cell away, even though they are going to be increasingly suspicious about his behaviors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure exactly how I'm missing out on potential Beats? I guess I'm not rolling for stuff or doing very much, haha. </div> </div> </div>Everyone gets 1 Beat at the end of each Chapter. That's coming up and I will announce it.<br /> <br /> In addition, you can earn Beats for <b>each </b>of the following per <b>scene</b>:<br /> 1) Resolve or make significant headway towards an Aspiration<br /> 2) Resolve a Condition (except those caused by spellcasting, Paradox, or magical source; see below)<br /> 3) When you fail, you can optionally make it a dramatic failure<br /> 4) Any major or dramatic event in the story, at my discretion<br /> 5) Take damage (bashing or lethal) in your rightmost health box<br /> <br /> You can earn Arcane Beats for <b>each </b>of the following per <b>scene</b>:<br /> 1) Fulfill or make significant headway towards an Obsession<br /> 2) Resolve a Condition from spellcasting, Paradox, or magical source<br /> 3) When you fail a spellcasting roll, you can optionally make it a dramatic failure<br /> 4) Risk an Act of Hubris and make a Wisdom degeneration roll<br /> 5) Participate in Legacy tutoring<br /> 6) Any meaningful and new encounter with the supernatural, at my discretion<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will try to get a post up tonight (I'm still all out of whack; I used to plan and make posts at work, but my new job is busier than my old job, so I've got less time to do that and I haven't gotten used to devoting time in the evenings for it) </div> </div> </div>Totally understand -- I'm in the same boat. Hoping to post later tonight, or sometime tomorrow during the day. Sorry for everyone waiting on me!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (If it's alright, I'd like to switch out &quot;perform a summoning&quot; for &quot;Join an Order&quot;; I'll re-add the summoning after Binder learns a little bit more about the process in character) </div> </div> </div>Yep, sounds perfect. Thanks for the heads up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-31-2016, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:24:24-07:00","id":994220,"title":"","content":"After spending, what, 2 days? trying to decide what to do about the phone call, I realized that Marlin would do exactly the same thing and putz around the bookstore overthinking it XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:53:25-07:00","id":994254,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> So is the staff an Artifact, or simply an Imbued item? Also, what spell does it have? I know it has to do with revelation or something, but I forget the exact spell and I find it anywhere. I wanna know for listing it on the character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:35:18-07:00","id":994659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=994254#post994254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> So is the staff an Artifact, or simply an Imbued item? Also, what spell does it have? I know it has to do with revelation or something, but I forget the exact spell and I find it anywhere. I wanna know for listing it on the character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a weak artifact, adapted from the rules in the core book for the Artifact Merit. It's essentially a 1-dot Artifact, rather than the 3+ dot merit on p. 99. Some of the items you receive may be Imbued items, but the ones you received were all artifacts. I gave the stats and details on the artifacts <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=984830#post984830\">in this post</a> (see the spoiler when Boomer is talking). The staff has the Pierce Deception spell (Prime 1, p. 165). It also has slightly better stats than a standard staff, compared to the stats on the broom you used in the Highstorm portal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:30:08-07:00","id":994751,"title":"","content":"Ok, a regular beat, then. That puts me at 3/5 beats and 3/5 arcane beats, if I remember correctly. I'll probably make headway on my obsession to investigate Sleeper worship areas for Supernal elements tomorrow IC, since the Consilium is meeting in a church if I understood Valentine correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:49:20-07:00","id":994909,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> So what about the Death mage Phoenix is interacting with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:10:24-07:00","id":994924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=994909#post994909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> So what about the Death mage Phoenix is interacting with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crap, sorry! I'll add that as soon as I have time. Busy at the moment, sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:48:33-07:00","id":994976,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Something I was thinking about given how often Moonstone risks Wisdom loss. The Chronicles of Darkness book has this system:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD 75</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Meditation</b><br /> A character can improve her chances of resisting<br /> a breaking point by meditating. Meditation is an<br /> extended action with a pool of Composure + Wits,<br /> target successes of 4, and an interval of 30 minutes.<br /> After successfully meditating, the character gets a<br /> +1 bonus to her next breaking point roll. Once this<br /> bonus is used or the character sleeps, it disappears,<br /> and must be regained by meditating again.<br /> <br /> Soothing music or relaxation tapes can provide a<br /> +1 to +2 equipment bonus. A dedicated meditation<br /> room, perhaps in the character\u2019s Safe Place, provides<br /> +3. Loud noises, an uncomfortable environment, or<br /> lack of sleep inflict a -1 penalty each. Lack of food<br /> inflicts a -1 to -3 penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can that be applied to Act of Hubris rolls as well? It seems to make sense given that Wisdom is about control and foresight and thinking about your actions in advance. Maybe it could be used only if you meditate on the act you intend/expect to commit and what its consequences might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T03:51:18-07:00","id":995142,"title":"","content":"I have taken &quot;Join a Cabal&quot; as the new Aspiration. Also noted the two last Beats from the resolved Aspiration and Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T06:10:11-07:00","id":995168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=995053#post995053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eventually, you see it happen: Mrs. Parks stops walking. She smiles and sighs, &quot;Henry, <i>there</i> you are.&quot; With Dante's spell, you see a dark, mysterious doorway appear and open, and Mrs. Parks steps through. The door vanishes a moment later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sneaking in a little Being Human reference there, are we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cu