rbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:36:05-07:00","id":995452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=995429#post995429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am done with my scene, unless you want me to finish it with a post of my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you want to. I'm curious about how Ouroboros Ophis would react to this scene, but I can probably make some educated guesses. Totally your choice.<br /> <br /> That still leaves Lynx (whom I think is almost done?), Binder (if he would respond at all to Falling Blossom's offer to meet), and Phoenix (needs his Social Maneuvering roll and any other interaction with the Hunters).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T18:49:58-07:00","id":995468,"title":"","content":"Good point. I'll make a reaction and closing scene post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T04:14:11-07:00","id":995578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=994976#post994976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Something I was thinking about given how often Moonstone risks Wisdom loss. The Chronicles of Darkness book has this system:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can that be applied to Act of Hubris rolls as well? It seems to make sense given that Wisdom is about control and foresight and thinking about your actions in advance. Maybe it could be used only if you meditate on the act you intend/expect to commit and what its consequences might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, just realized I never replied to this. <br /> <br /> I'm on the fence about it. On one hand I totally get the case in favor of letting you do this. Seems to make sense that meditating like this would help you stay present in a way that you don't lose sight of reason when casting spells.<br /> <br /> At the same time, it seems like mundane meditation should not sufficiently protect you from the temptations of hubris. Against the very real power that you're drawn to when you use Awakened magic, meditating seems like it would be a paper shield.<br /> <br /> Personally I think the simplest answer is to go with no for now, but I might change my mind after thinking about it more. The CoD core book is really intended for mortals, not mages, so I don't think it makes sense to apply mundane actions to supernatural character rules. The things I'm ok with using from that book are rules on mundane actions and equipment, like Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:17:37-07:00","id":996049,"title":"","content":"Happy Monday everyone!<br /> <br /> There is a very good possibility (but not guarantee) that I'll have a pretty quiet day today. As this scene wraps up, I will try to quickly prep the next part and introduce us to the next chapter. I don't want to railroad you all, so let me know if there are more things you'd like to accomplish soon, but I will try to provide some structure and opportunities for more individual and group RP. Just waiting on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a>'s last post and reaction to the Hunters, and then I think we're all done with this scene.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - Unless I missed it, I still need a new short-term Aspiration from you, and would like you to update your character sheet. I have your current aspirations as joining an Order (short), and graduating from UChi (long).<br /> <br /> I've been trying to portray this in-character, but my understanding is that Pentacle mages are very quick to seek out newly Awakened mages such as yourselves. Mages are uncommon enough and rely on social groups, so they look to newly Awakened mages as potential recruits and ways to increase their own social currency. This is why everyone has been quick to befriend you and tried to convince you to join their Orders.<br /> <br /> My plan for the next Chapter is to give you opportunities to join mage society in Chicago so you can get your first tastes of the local politics. Because the Order initiation process can take up to a few weeks for some, I'll be fast-forwarding at some point during this Chapter again, so you'll have chances to pursue individual Aspirations/Obsessions again as needed.<br /> <br /> Now that this first Chapter is wrapping up, I'd like to again solicit some feedback on how things are going! Please either PM me or comment here with your general thoughts, things you liked/disliked, or any questions or concerns about the game. I'm still a developing Storyteller, and I want you to enjoy the game, so please let me know if you're not. I hope you are, though! I'm certainly enjoying the chance to write and create ideas and bring this universe to life, and I'm really digging all of your characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-31-2016, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T07:34:48-07:00","id":996062,"title":"","content":"I've wrapped up the downtime events for Lynx's next couple of days, until Saturday. I'm satisfied thus far with events unfolding.<br /> <br /> Lynx is a little isolated unlike the others. Since he's been in the US now for only a week though, it's not as though he's had time to establish anything remotely similar to a social network the same way all other characters have their jobs, friends, and families, which I think is a good thing. <br /> <br /> It's also unusual for me to see players have narrative control, e.g. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> dictating a lot of their day to day life (seemingly) without <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>'s input. I'm always afraid of overstepping my boundaries in that regard. <br /> <br /> I'm enjoying this campaign rather a lot, though. It's got a good pace for me, what with IRL being a pain in the arse these days (grief and injuries, oh my), yet it doesn't feel like it stagnates. I look forward to updates and I'm enjoying playing Lynx as a character. I appreciate the effort you've put into this, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>, and I think you're doing great thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:57:27-07:00","id":996100,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - Thanks for the feedback! Glad to hear you're enjoying it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Personally I like to be the one &quot;at the helm&quot; for NPCs, such as leading conversations, etc., but I really like the idea of players being able to introduce NPCs relevant to your characters. In a PBP game where I can't give immediate feedback or respond to questions as quickly, I am perfectly comfortable with players taking more control of the reigns, with the understanding that I can retroactively change a scene or veto a decision as I deem necessary.<br /> <br /> Take Dante for example. I created the character and introduced his personality, and whenever a conversation has happened, I've been the one writing his lines. But Thorbes added details about how he and Ouroboros Ophis met up later to talk about ghosts and the Supernal, and I'm totally cool with that. If I had decided that Dante would not have been so accommodating, I would've edited the scene as needed.<br /> <br /> If you ever want to introduce an NPC or add more drama/conflict regarding NPCs you already know, let me know and we can work it out! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:14:15-07:00","id":996134,"title":"","content":"It was easy, as you had already set his personality and it seemed fitting. I am also very much enjoying this game (had before as a reader and now as player) I don't have any suggestions for now, because I like how things are developing. If something occurs to me , I will let you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:09:30-07:00","id":996153,"title":"","content":"A+ game so far; I'm very impressed by the amount of detail you've put into the world and NPCs and the amount of effort you put into drawing everyone in, even a player like me who tends to kind of sit back and let things happen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:35:15-07:00","id":996211,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> l'll take &quot;figure out if Patty is a Sleepwalker&quot; as my next Aspiration. I'll update my character sheet today.<br /> <br /> I've really been enjoying the game so far. Some great conflict, great character building, and even some genuinely amusing moments. I also like how we basically created our own villain so early on.<br /> <br /> I can't remember if I've got this right or not, but aren't I at 1 Experience? I noticed that I didn't add a beat after completing Ragnar's Aspiration to investigate the apartment complex, and after getting a beat for the end of the chapter, that should put me at 1 normal Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 10-31-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:31:56-07:00","id":996232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=996211#post996211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> l'll take &quot;figure out if Patty is a Sleepwalker&quot; as my next Aspiration. I'll update my character sheet today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's right, I think you mentioned that earlier in the thread. Thanks for the reminder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've really been enjoying the game so far. Some great conflict, great character building, and even some genuinely amusing moments. I also like how we basically created our own villain so early on. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback! Glad to hear you're enjoying it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't remember if I've got this right or not, but aren't I at 1 Experience? I noticed that I didn't add a beat after completing Ragnar's Aspiration to investigate the apartment complex, and after getting a beat for the end of the chapter, that should put me at 1 normal Experience. </div> </div> </div>Sure, sounds right to me. I haven't been tracking all of these that closely. I'm going to be doing a better job tracking it on a scene-by-scene basis, just to help you all with bookkeeping. But I haven't gone back to check if that math adds up. I'd trust your judgment on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:34:21-07:00","id":996233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=996134#post996134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was easy, as you had already set his personality and it seemed fitting. I am also very much enjoying this game (had before as a reader and now as player) I don't have any suggestions for now, because I like how things are developing. If something occurs to me , I will let you know.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=996153#post996153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A+ game so far; I'm very impressed by the amount of detail you've put into the world and NPCs and the amount of effort you put into drawing everyone in, even a player like me who tends to kind of sit back and let things happen!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, thanks everyone! Glad you're having a good time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As always, I do encourage you to provide feedback on anything that you feel isn't going well, if that comes up. I like to think that I'm a pretty accommodating person, so I hope you feel like you can share those concerns as needed.<br /> <br /> I've been working today on miscellaneous stuff to get us ready for the next scene, including creating NPCs, etc. Hoping to make it interesting and immersive for you all! I'll aim to put up the start of the scene tonight or tomorrow as my time allows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T05:35:23-07:00","id":996538,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - So I was browsing through old posts in the thread and just found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=926814#post926814\">this post</a> in which you introduced an NPC for your academic mentor. I completely forgot you had created this NPC and that you had 3 dots in the Mentor merit! Sorry about that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll try to find a way to introduce him sometime in the next few scenes, and use him as a way to help you pursue your long-term Aspiration.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else create an NPC or have some other great idea that I completely forgot to comment on??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T05:51:15-07:00","id":996542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=996127#post996127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, try to think of things Phoenix would do in consistent patterns or routines that he leans back on to avoid stressful situations, or when he doesn't know how to move forward on a problem. Especially if that behavior would put stress on another relationship or cause problems for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean exactly? Can you think of any examples for what you're thinking of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:11:07-07:00","id":996568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=996542#post996542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean exactly? Can you think of any examples for what you're thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, great question. Here are some possible examples I can think of:<br /> <br /> 1) Let's say that Phoenix is disciplined and has a steady routine for when and how he trains at the martial arts studio. Maybe something comes up that unexpectedly prevents him from following that routine, so he gets irritable towards someone that day when he can't go.<br /> <br /> 2) Maybe he thinks in more black and white terms about people based on first impression, and someone's mean to him at first encounter. The next time they try to offer him help with something or ask a favor, he shoots them down because of how they treated him before, so he misses out on a chance to improve the relationship or get some help with something.<br /> <br /> 3) Phoenix has a rough day and doesn't know how to tackle a problem. He decides to fall back on a certain routine he's done before (e.g., train at the dojo, talk to an old friend) rather than face the actual problem.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if these fit with what you had in mind for Rigid, but there the kinds of examples I'm thinking of. If you find that it's hard to think of examples or feel like you aren't being given enough opportunities to invoke his Vice, you can also pick a new one and edit your character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:43:07-07:00","id":996924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=996538#post996538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - So I was browsing through old posts in the thread and just found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=926814#post926814\">this post</a> in which you introduced an NPC for your academic mentor. I completely forgot you had created this NPC and that you had 3 dots in the Mentor merit! Sorry about that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll try to find a way to introduce him sometime in the next few scenes, and use him as a way to help you pursue your long-term Aspiration.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else create an NPC or have some other great idea that I completely forgot to comment on??</div> </div> </div> </div>Naw, it's fine. Dr. Langley wouldn't have been really relevant for the first chapter. Besides, it gives an opportunity for the world to unfold more slowly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:21:22-07:00","id":997123,"title":"","content":"FYI, I have never actually been to some of the places I'm referencing in Chicago like this particular church. I just used Google Maps to find something that already existed to fit my ST needs. But I'm enjoying the approach to using real-life places and events as fodder for this game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If anyone has any questions or issues about the game or story stuff, just let me know! Hope your week is going well so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T00:16:42-07:00","id":997584,"title":"","content":"I poked around the area in Street View myself, it's kinda fun! I don't have anything particularly on my mind. Hope you're also doing well.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, since they're probably going to be onscreen soon, here's stats for the Knights of Alhambra. I built them as Rank 3 NPCs using those guidelines, feel free to adjust or change them however you like!<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Dog</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/D87z1mp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Concept: Modern Samurai<br /> Virtue: Just<br /> Vice: Violent<br /> Path: Mastigos<br /> Order: Adamantine Arrow<br /> Legacy: Brotherhood of the Demon Wind (Attainments: Dew of Evening, Choosing Death, Chasing the Wind)<br /> <br /> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Initiative 6, Defense 7, Speed 11<br /> <br /> Crafts 1, Investigation 1, Occult 3 (Demon Wind)<br /> <br /> Athletics 2, Drive 1, Larceny 2, Stealth 2, Weaponry 4 (Daisho)<br /> <br /> Expression 3 (Poetry), Intimidation 1, Streetwise 3<br /> <br /> Merits: Status (Arrow) 2, High Speech. Adamant Hand 2, Quick Draw (Weaponry) 1, Taste (Poetry) 1, Defensive Combat (Weaponry) 1, Style: Armed Defense 3, Style: Light Weapons 3, Language (Japanese) 1, Occultation 2, Shadow Name 2<br /> <br /> Gnosis 4<br /> Mind 3, Space 3, Time 4<br /> Wisdom 8 (Enlightened)<br /> <br /> Rotes: Co-Location (Space 3, Weaponry 4), Clear Thoughts (Mind 3, Expression 3), Choose the Thread (Time 1, Weaponry 4)<br /> Praxes: Prophecy (Time 4) [others converted into attainments]<br /> <br /> Experience expenditures: Gnosis 1&gt;4 (free), Space 2&gt;4 (8a), Time 1&gt;3 (2a,6), Wisdom 7&gt;8 (2), Armed Defense 3 (3), Arrow Status 1&gt;2 (1), Occultation 1&gt;2 (1), Shadow Name 2 (2).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Rose of Sharon</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/31kXqho.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Concept: Skeptical Visionary<br /> Virtue: Faithful<br /> Vice: Unforgiving<br /> Path: Obrimos<br /> Order: Adamantine Arrow<br /> Legacy: Choir of Hashmallim (Attainments: Eyes to See/Ears to Hear, Aetherial Cleansing, Aetherial Avatar)<br /> <br /> Intelligence 4, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> Initiative 4, Defense 3, Speed 9<br /> <br /> Academics 4 (Religion), Investigation 3, Occult 5 (Abyss, Rituals)<br /> <br /> Athletics 1, Firearms 1, Stealth 2<br /> <br /> Empathy 2, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 2, Socialize 1<br /> <br /> Merits: Status (Arrow) 2, High Speech. Artifact 5, Library (Academics) 2, Destiny (Bane: Eye of the Storm) 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Abyss) 1, Summoner\u2019s Soul (Aether) 2<br /> <br /> Gnosis 4<br /> Prime 4, Forces 4, Matter 2<br /> Wisdom 8 (Enlightened)<br /> <br /> Rotes: Apocalypse (Prime 4, Academics 4), Supernal Dispellation (Prime 4, Occult 4), Craftsman\u2019s Eye (Matter 1, Investigation 3), Shaping (Matter 2, Persuasion 2)<br /> Praxes: Find the Balance (Matter 2), Levitation (Forces 4), Control Weather (Forces 2), Platonic Form (Prime 3)<br /> <br /> Experience expenditures: Gnosis 4 (free), Prime 2&gt;4 (5a,3), Forces 2&gt;4 (5a,3), Wisdom 7&gt;8 (2), Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (1), Summoner\u2019s Soul 2 (2), Legacy Attainments (3), Rote (1)<br /> ---<br /> Aetherial Avatar: A Light Shining in Darkness<br /> <br /> A mighty figure that vaguely resembles the Statue of Liberty, carrying a torch in one hand and a burnished shield in the other. Supernal entity, see Choir of Hashmallim Legacy for full rules and the Summoner's Soul merit.<br /> <br /> Rank 1<br /> Power 2, Finesse 2, Resistance 2<br /> Spells: Aetheric Winds, Universal Counterspell (works on Abyssal Influences and Numina)<br /> Ban: Must attack any Abyssal entities within sensory range<br /> Bane: A soul stone of Path Obrimos<br /> ---<br /> Artifact 5 left to ST to define as desired.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Askia</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"http://www.tabletmag.com/wp-content/files_mf/kehinde_wiley_030712_620px.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\"