 I'm just being shitty. Sometimes it gets hard for me to set aside the time to post, that has nothing to do with me getting busy or depression or anything, it just gets tough for me to <i>sit down and do</i> something. Seems to have an inverse relationship to how long a post I'm planning to make, too...<br /> <br /> I'm still super suspicious about this cat, when maybe I shouldn't be. Can I confirm that 1) if there had been a spirit, my mind spell would have detected it, and 2) if the cat had any kind of magic on it, I would have seen (or clashed) with my mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:37:49-08:00","id":1050074,"title":"","content":"Well, I have returned, and with quite the post, I might add. This should make the rest of this fight easier. Hopefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T04:15:21-08:00","id":1050940,"title":"","content":"Had a crazy work week because my colleague is on vacation and I've been covering some of his duties at work. I also have a friend visiting from out of town this weekend. I do have Monday off though, so expect a post by Monday at the latest! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T05:44:36-08:00","id":1051474,"title":"","content":"Great! I will, for the sake of convenience and time, edit my post with several more Scrutiny rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:30:31-08:00","id":1052154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1048203#post1048203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still super suspicious about this cat, when maybe I shouldn't be. Can I confirm that 1) if there had been a spirit, my mind spell would have detected it, and 2) if the cat had any kind of magic on it, I would have seen (or clashed) with my mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Mind 1 spell would not be able to detect spirits, as that falls under the Spirit Arcanum. You could add Spirit 1 to your spell to allow it to detect them, probably.<br /> <br /> Life Sight does not reveal the presence of Life spells; it only reveals their physical condition. Prime Sight can detect spells. Nothing caused a Clash of Wills","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:18:14-08:00","id":1052315,"title":"","content":"Well this guy's day is about to get much, much worse. I also could have sworn there was something about a dice penalty if you had a certain number of active spells, must've been a mistake. I already have Inspired, but I think I would like Steadfast. That's the one where you can make a Failure a Success, right? I think his lack of combat ability is weighing on him- he brought it up before the fight with Alux- but this spell confirms to him that he can, in fact, hold his own against other mages in a fight. Though he's definitely going to be asking Mathias to help him get to Fate or Time 3 as quickly as possible so that he can start using Fraying spells when the chips are down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:54:50-08:00","id":1053991,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the long wait of my post. I'm currently in the middle of moving, so there was a point where I simply didn't have the time. I'll try to post more frequently from now on, though.<br /> <br /> Anyways, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> is the Bonded Tool Merit allowed, not, or are you still thinking on it? If you did confirm it, I either missed it or it wasn't terribly clear before (I think mainly because I went into a little back and forth with MagicSwordsman about it). Just making sure because I'm thinking of spending my 1 banked Experience on the first dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T04:07:01-08:00","id":1054258,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> Hopefully that translates into decent whack. But even assuming that it does full damage, that's only three. Remember, I haven't made so much as a scratch on the guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T11:24:32-08:00","id":1054381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1052154#post1052154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Mind 1 spell would not be able to detect spirits, as that falls under the Spirit Arcanum. You could add Spirit 1 to your spell to allow it to detect them, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so the ruling you're going with is that Mind doesn't work on Spirits or Ghosts? I remember it was ruled that Mind had incomplete/unpredictable effects on abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1052154#post1052154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life Sight does not reveal the presence of Life spells; it only reveals their physical condition. Prime Sight can detect spells. Nothing caused a Clash of Wills</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang, it's been too long since I last looked at the Mage Sight rules... Prime is looking better and better all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 02-24-2017, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:54:16-08:00","id":1054454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1054258#post1054258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hopefully that translates into decent whack. But even assuming that it does full damage, that's only three. Remember, I haven't made so much as a scratch on the guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the next move I'm planning is forcing the Beaten Down Tilt on him using a Mind spell. All he needs to suffer is 1 lethal (or bashing that exceeds his Stamina) for it to come in under normal circumstances, so I figure if I meet that, the Mind spell can force it (it's possible rwknoll isn't gonna make it work like that, but here's hoping).<br /> <br /> All that's left for him after that is to either surrender, or spend a Willpower for every action to fight off three mages. I don't think he'd have much of a chance with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:01:15-08:00","id":1055176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1053991#post1053991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the long wait of my post. I'm currently in the middle of moving, so there was a point where I simply didn't have the time. I'll try to post more frequently from now on, though.<br /> <br /> Anyways, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> is the Bonded Tool Merit allowed, not, or are you still thinking on it? If you did confirm it, I either missed it or it wasn't terribly clear before (I think mainly because I went into a little back and forth with MagicSwordsman about it). Just making sure because I'm thinking of spending my 1 banked Experience on the first dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I forgot to go back and actually review it. I don't have a firm answer yet. I like the idea behind it but I want to investigate further to make sure the math is fair, and also consider how it might affect Artifacts and items recovered from Highstorms. Sorry I haven't gotten to that yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1054381#post1054381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so the ruling you're going with is that Mind doesn't work on Spirits or Ghosts? I remember it was ruled that Mind had incomplete/unpredictable effects on abyssal entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the confusion. I think I'm having a hard time wrapping my head around the best way to rule the uses of spells against creatures not traditionally under their purview. I asked on the Mage forums about it just now to get some input, I'll try to think about it more and give you a clearer and fair answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dang, it's been too long since I last looked at the Mage Sight rules... Prime is looking better and better all the time. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's pretty useful. Active Sight of any kind is great for seeing and interacting with spells as they're being cast, but actually seeing and interacting with them later is what Prime is for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1054454#post1054454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but the next move I'm planning is forcing the Beaten Down Tilt on him using a Mind spell. All he needs to suffer is 1 lethal (or bashing that exceeds his Stamina) for it to come in under normal circumstances, so I figure if I meet that, the Mind spell can force it (it's possible rwknoll isn't gonna make it work like that, but here's hoping).<br /> <br /> All that's left for him after that is to either surrender, or spend a Willpower for every action to fight off three mages. I don't think he'd have much of a chance with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:43:17-08:00","id":1055195,"title":"","content":"Ok, got a response and it makes way more sense to me now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1055183#post1055183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind can detect and control any sentient being. However, while Mind could be used to control the actions of a ghost or a spirit it can't control the more fundamental aspects of their being the way that their respective arcana can. You also wouldn't be able to actually see the entities or into their respective Twilight or access their adjacent realms (Underworld/Shadow) except indirectly. I know some people house rule this so that Mind doesn't work on ghosts and spirits because Mind has a lot going for it already.<br /> <br /> Lure and Repel wouldn't work on spirits because they're not biologically alive and that's the principles that that spell works on. Life doesn't work on ephemerals except as a conjunction with another arcana or when the ephemeral has become housed in flesh.<br /> <br /> Basically, if a thing falls under an Arcana's purview it can be affected by that Arcana, and most things fall under multiple Arcana's purview in one way or another. Some Arcana will be better at more direct manipulation than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here's what I'm thinking. For ephemeral entities that are capable of sentient thought, like spirits and Abyssal creatures, mind control and Mind spells that influence their thinking will work. But that's because thoughts and thinking are under the purview of Mind. But I like the idea of requiring Spirit to actually detect spirits, just like you need Prime to detect existing spells. <br /> <br /> KKV, because the wolf spirit is not fettered to a living creature, your Life spell won't affect it. But you can improvise a Spirit 2 spell to do the same thing if you like. I will let you edit your post if you like.<br /> <br /> Does this sound more fair and make more sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:53:01-08:00","id":1055198,"title":"","content":"I'll edit it. Let's see if I have any luck this time.<br /> Edit: Edited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 02-26-2017, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:31:16-08:00","id":1056157,"title":"",