bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - FYI, you can only scour your Pattern to get mana by targeting a physical attribute (Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina); you can't use Presence.<br /> <br /> For everyone else: crapcarp is right, I forgot to mention that only Binder and Ouroboros Ophis would have regenerated Willpower during the night. As far as I can see from the rule book, you only regain a point of Willpower if you had a restful, peaceful night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T21:08:27-07:00","id":1096157,"title":"","content":"New post is up!<br /> <br /> FYI, this always amused me when I was in the area, but La Grange Park is a town, not a park. And it's distinct from La Grange...sort of. People tended to lump the two together. So, you're all meeting in a subdivision of a suburban neighborhood, not a literal park.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T04:18:46-07:00","id":1096227,"title":"","content":"The more you know.... <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T04:56:41-07:00","id":1096233,"title":"","content":"And knowing is half the battle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T20:53:22-07:00","id":1096587,"title":"","content":"Put up a new post. A few corrections/comments/clarificatons:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> - In interest of saving time in a PBP game, you can go ahead and describe/roll for any spell that you would offer to cast. Anyone who wouldn't let you cast the spell can just mention so in their next post, or post here. I'm assuming you're looking at something like Speak with the Dead?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - You actually wouldn't be able to see Moonstone's familiar at all, at least not unless you use some spell effect to be able to observe ephemeral entities in Twilight. The ability to detect Goetia with your Peripheral Sight (and actually see the Goetia in Twilight using Mind Sight) is a benefit from the Mind 2 attainment, so that means that Binder is the only other mage here who would sense the familiar without a spell effect. Also, the ability to extend your Sight to other non-superior Arcana by spending 1 mana is still limited to other Arcana that you have at least 1 dot in. So, for 1 mana you could add either Life or Space Sight to your Active Sight, but you can't pick Death or Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T05:18:52-07:00","id":1096676,"title":"","content":"Noted. I will keep that in mind from now on. I'll edit my post right away! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T09:25:54-07:00","id":1096766,"title":"","content":"My post has also been amended.<br /> <br /> So I'm guessing the flowers are either the source of the Mana (hence why the spirits are congregating around it), or they are the reason why the houses are so quiet. I'm also wondering if there's a rampant Tranquility spirit (in which case, we have an opportunity to collaborate with some werewolves), or if this is a mage's work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 05-25-2017, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T10:33:53-07:00","id":1097173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1096766#post1096766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm guessing the flowers are either the source of the Mana (hence why the spirits are congregating around it), or they are the reason why the houses are so quiet. I'm also wondering if there's a rampant Tranquility spirit (in which case, we have an opportunity to collaborate with some werewolves), or if this is a mage's work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gosh, so many possibilities. What a...Mystery! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T11:49:31-07:00","id":1097202,"title":"","content":"By the way, if you tell me the Opacity of the dandelions (only in mage you get to say such things, don't you love it?) I will add a Revelation roll to my last post. That was the idea behind adding Life to the active Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T06:14:28-07:00","id":1098085,"title":"","content":"Paging <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a>, in case you want to get in on some of this action too. I'm assuming Binder and Phoenix would have some valuable information to add here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:32:51-07:00","id":1098119,"title":"","content":"I love your description of divination as the smoke and brimstone of Pandemonium swirling off into the past and future! I need to get back in the habit of thinking about magic as being filtered through the Supernal world, it really adds a ton of color to Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:42:34-07:00","id":1098123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1098119#post1098119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love your description of divination as the smoke and brimstone of Pandemonium swirling off into the past and future! I need to get back in the habit of thinking about magic as being filtered through the Supernal world, it really adds a ton of color to Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm trying to make the descriptions colorful and unique to each of you instead of just saying &quot;You get the following info&quot;, etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:19:03-07:00","id":1098136,"title":"","content":"Playing Persona has got me really excited about having a goetic familiar, I'll probably invest in a more permanent and less weird one in the future. Here's the stats I'm using for Moonstone's Fear, I can change stuff if needed:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moonstone's Fear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 5, Resistance 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 15<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Familiar<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Fear 2<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Counterspell, Drain, Hallucination, Reveal Flaws<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must spend 1 Willpower to act against someone who successfully resisted a fear attack.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Physical contact with the real Alux.<br /> <br /> Moonstone's Fear lurks hazily in Mind Twilight as a human-sized and slightly more humanoid version of Alux. Toothsome, amorphous, light-consuming. Moonstone has nightmares that Alux can fly, and so Fear can fly.<br /> <br /> <b>Counterspell: </b>As it specifically represents Moonstone's fear of the Abyss consuming and nullifying his magic, Fear can counter Awakened spells by injecting fear and self-doubt into the caster's Imago. When Moonstone perceives a spell being cast in Active Sight, spend one Essence to activate this Numen, which recreates the Prime 2 &quot;Universal Counterspell&quot; Attainment. Fear rolls Rank+Influence in the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Drain: </b>As written. When used on Moonstone, Fear may choose to take only 1 success on its activation roll, effectively letting him steal its own Willpower- if he's at least minimally strong.<br /> <br /> <b>Hallucination: </b>As written, with an eye towards nightmarish hallucinations drawn from Moonstone's subconscious.<br /> <br /> <b>Reveal Flaws: </b>Fear draws a target's hidden faults to the surface, literally writing words such as &quot;weak&quot; or &quot;greedy&quot; or &quot;liar&quot; on their skin in Mind Twilight. This Numen costs one Essence, is resisted by Resolve+Composure+Gnosis, and lasts until Fear has used another Numen or Influence. For each net success Fear achieves, the target suffers a -1 penalty on its next contested roll, such as Numen resistance or Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Special: Goetic Struggle. </b>As the embodiment of a specific complex drawn from Moonstone's unconscious, Fear can use its Influence to help its owner potentially resist fear. When Moonstone would otherwise be affected by a supernatural fear effect (such as Awe, Emotional Aura, certain Mind and Life spells, the Nightmare Discipline, etc) it triggers a Clash of Wills. Roll Gnosis+Mind against the goetia's Rank+Influence. If Moonstone succeeds, the supernatural fear effect fails and he gains 1 Willpower. If Fear succeeds, Moonstone is affected by the power as if the attacker rolled an exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to think of other cool Mastigos stuff I can do to weaponize Moonstone's complexes and issues. As I'm re-reading the Path description, I really like the idea of not denying your passions and Vices, but mastering them and using them for power. Maybe some kind of ritual that gives him an additional benefit when he fulfills an Aspiration, or &quot;scouring&quot; his own sympathetic connections for a Yantra boost or Willpower/Mana. I suppose it hasn't been that long in-character, but I'm about ready for Moonstone to stop pining for Hakim and start pivoting into his own scary magical self. Starting with joining the Guardians!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T04:12:31-07:00","id":1098394,"title":"","content":"Maybe your Persona's Incubus 8D . Low level, got Evil Touch for that Fear status effect, and it's certainly a deviant one with that horn between its legs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T21:57:47-07:00","id":1098660,"title":"","content":"I'd rather steer clear of anything from Kamoshida's Palace. I'm holding out for Satanael :P<br /> <br /> Thanks for the spell clarification <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a>, Pathfinder is a good model. Asking a question like that seemed to be in the purview of Space, but I do remember you ruled against a similar spell for seeing where Alux would manifest in the previous chapter. Chalk it up to Moonstone not knowing what his magic is capable of. How about this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Where To? (Space \u2022)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Streetwise, Survival<br /> <br /> Warlocks know that people exist on lines, not points. When cast on a target, this spell gives the mage an intuitive sense of where they are currently going. If the destination is within the spell's Area, the mage has an innate sense of what it is. If not, the mage only knows which direction to go, similar to the Pathfinder Numen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew I should have cast Mental Shield on everyone, I almost did, but I figured &quot;oh no, waste of a spell slot, we won't need it.&quot; Don't touch ghosts without wearing gloves, everybody!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 05-31-2017, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T04:09:34-07:00","id":1098725,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> - Yes, that seems great to me. And if you disagree about a ruling, you can always tell me, and we can talk about it. I honestly don't always remember what I've said before about things, and my understanding of the mechanics is always growing (I hope). I just thought that using Space that way should require you to either account for the Area or some kind of Withstand. Knowing their destination without Area seems more like something a Mind spell would be useful for, like just scanning their surface thoughts to see the image or intent in their mind.<br /> <br /> @KKV - Well, oops, I forgot that Lynx forgot about that. But I like the way you're role playing it out as something like a repressed memory resurfacing. Go with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T04:22:28-07:00","id":1098727,"title":"","content":"Repressed memory? Or something else? DUN DUN DUN.<br /> <br /> It's fun either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T08:04:58-07:00","id":1099528,"title":"","content":"Finally thought of something I can do to contribute this scene!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T06:38:51-07:00","id":1100425,"title":"","content":"Hello, long time no post, and just after I said I'd commit to posting regularly. Reason this time? I needed a time out from the forums for...another thread I made a little while ago. Maybe you've seen it, maybe you haven't, I'd rather not bring it up in a public thread. I'm open to PMs if anyone's curious, but here let's just say I opened up and got hurt when I was vulnerable, let's leave it at that.<br /> <br /> As for Phoenix, given his lack of participation during this scene, perhaps we can explain this away by saying he didn't arrive until now. As for what caused the delay, his younger half-sister called him. Just came up with her as another aspect of Phoenix's character, she doesn't have to come in to this chronicle in any way, she's just in his life is all. Though, if you'd rather he's been there the whole time and been quiet, I can go with that, too (I just don't think Phoenix would stand ideally by with all this going on, he's not the mellow sort, after all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T08:57:54-07:00","id":1100462,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, just wanted to tell you that my posting opportunities will be very limited for the foreseeable. Should be no longer than a couple weeks, but may be no longer than a couple days. Just proceed as normal, Ragnar will tag along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T19:48:12-07:00","id":1101088,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> - Hey, no worries at all. I'm glad you're back, and sorry to hear that you didn't receive the response you were hoping for in your other discussion. You are definitely appreciated and valued here in our threads! Thanks for all the neat ideas and entertainment you've brought to this game.<br /> <br /> In regards to Phoenix's silence, I love the idea of him arriving late due to personal issues with a new angle. When you have time and feel so inclined, I would love you to flesh out that idea and describe it here. I don't think you've introduced her concept before, right? What's her name, what is Phoenix's relationship with her, and which biological parent do they share? Also, what do you want to say that he and his sister were talking about that caused the delay?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> - Totally understand! Let us know when you're back on a regular schedule. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - Maybe this isn't your role play style, but I honestly think Binder is an incredibly fascinating character and he enhances the depth of our scenes just by hearing what he has to say in response to the situation and in regards to other characters. Binder is a family man, married and straight, with different experiences and perspectives than some of the others; if you want to contribute but aren't sure what to do, just try some dialogue with the other characters.<br /> <br /> Also, can you believe that this game has been up for almost a full <i>year</i> now? I am so glad and grateful that you all have stuck around for so long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T00:00:01-07:00","id":1101130,"title":"","content":"Wow, it's been a year already? Time does fly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T02:32:47-07:00","id":1101896,"title":"","content":"Nom nom nom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T04:42:15-07:00","id":1101923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1101088#post1101088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to Phoenix's silence, I love the idea of him arriving late due to personal issues with a new angle. When you have time and feel so inclined, I would love you to flesh out that idea and describe it here. I don't think you've introduced her concept before, right? What's her name, what is Phoenix's relationship with her, and which biological parent do they share? Also, what do you want to say that he and his sister were talking about that caused the delay?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo, I haven't introduced her, and that's because I just came up with her for this very purpose. It fleshes Phoenix's character out even more, after all.<br /> <br /> \u200bHer name is Layla Klasina Kemp, she's his sister from another mother,his father remarried after the divorce with his mother. Since Phoenix had a very strong relationship with his mother, and considering his father remarried a measly 3 years later (the engagement started getting serious less than 1 year), and the new couple had a kid only about a year later. Needless to say, Phoenix felt abandoned and his half-sister reminded him of that abandonment every time he saw her face, and this was going on just before he hit puberty (he was 7 when his parents divorced, so he was 11 when she came along). The onset of his teenage years made the problem even worse and he ended up claiming that he hated her for several years, even going so far as to say it right in her face on a few occasions (though he didn't really hate her, he was just angry with her, and even then, it was mostly the anger with his father that he directed at her). Naturally, this created a rift between the two.<br /> <br /> Once Phoenix left the nest, it didn't take very long of her being out of his life that he saw how much of a dick he was being, so he made amends. He promised her that they'd stay in touch, so they both call each other fairly regularly. Unfortunately, he's recently neglected that obligation, what with all that's happened, and she's letting him have it with the call. She has a lot more catching up to do than the usual, so the call takes him more time than he initially expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T03:20:01-07:00","id":1103064,"title":"","content":"Grab bag of ideas to deal with this Essence storm situation:<ul><li>Death/Prime/Spirit: study it with Mage Sight to see what's happening</li> <li>Time: Postcognition to study the scene when the cloud formed and see what caused it, possibly with Mage Sight or a ghost/spirit seeing spell active if it was something invisible</li> <li>Mind: Psychic Domination to make the swarming spirits and ghosts destroy each other and discorporate, or just send them away before the Essence dries up</li> <li>Spirit or Death: Cap the Well to keep the spirits from feeding on the Essence, maybe Shadow Walk (or Prime, Supernal Veil) to keep them from seeing it at all. Death might be able to do similar for ghosts.</li> <li>Prime or Spirit: Study it (ley lines? node?) with Sacred Geometry. Prime or Spirit Unveiling spells could ask what the cloud's Resonance keyword is.</li> <li>Forces/Prime: Control Weather with a Prime 2 requisite to turn the mystical weather effect into a clear day</li> <li>Life or Death, plus Fate: large-scale Bruise Flesh or Rotting Flesh effect to kill all the dandelions in the neighborhood at once. Might need Ragnar to cast Warding Gesture first.</li> <li>Nothing: it's free Mana! Think of all the spells we can power and Paradox we can ignore! Forget about the Sleepers, they'll be fine, probably.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T06:52:58-07:00","id":1103788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1103064#post1103064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grab bag of ideas to deal with this Essence storm situation:<ul><li>Death/Prime/Spirit: study it with Mage Sight to see what's happening</li> <li>Time: Postcognition to study the scene when the cloud formed and see what caused it, possibly with Mage Sight or a ghost/spirit seeing spell active if it was something invisible</li> <li>Mind: Psychic Domination to make the swarming spirits and ghosts destroy each other and discorporate, or just send them away before the Essence dries up</li> <li>Spirit or Death: Cap the Well to keep the spirits from feeding on the Essence, maybe Shadow Walk (or Prime, Supernal Veil) to keep them from seeing it at all. Death might be able to do similar for ghosts.</li> <li>Prime or Spirit: Study it (ley lines? node?) with Sacred Geometry. Prime or Spirit Unveiling spells could ask what the cloud's Resonance keyword is.</li> <li>Forces/Prime: Control Weather with a Prime 2 requisite to turn the mystical weather effect into a clear day</li> <li>Life or Death, plus Fate: large-scale Bruise Flesh or Rotting Flesh effect to kill all the dandelions in the neighborhood at once. Might need Ragnar to cast Warding Gesture first.</li> <li>Nothing: it's free Mana! Think of all the spells we can power and Paradox we can ignore! Forget about the Sleepers, they'll be fine, probably.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Ragnar and Moonstone study the Cloud with Ophis' spell, and one that Lynx casts on them to see when the spirits got involved. Then I think our 3-dot characters go to town on the flowers after we try to limit the collateral damage with Warding spells on the houses and people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T05:11:57-07:00","id":1106970,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Phoenix isn't using Forces for Active Sight, he's using Mind. And the only reason he's using that was because he sensed the passive presence of Moonstone's Goetia due to Mind's Eye. That said, it's not really important now, he's going back to Peripheral Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T20:14:49-07:00","id":1107192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1106970#post1106970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Phoenix isn't using Forces for Active Sight, he's using Mind. And the only reason he's using that was because he sensed the passive presence of Moonstone's Goetia due to Mind's Eye. That said, it's not really important now, he's going back to Peripheral Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're thinking of Focused Sight. Active Sight automatically uses multiple Arcana, and then you can spend extra mana to include other Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p. 90-91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Active Mage Sight requires more concentration from the mage, and overlays the mage\u2019s perception with the Supernal World of her Path. It automatically uses the mage\u2019s two Path Ruling Arcana, has no cost to add any third Ruling Arcanum, and costs one point of Mana per scene to include a Common or Inferior Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you get Forces and Prime automatically, and then pay extra to see Mind, but you still get all three. It's like...going to a movie in 3D. You pay extra to wear the 3D glasses, but you still have color and 2D perceptual abilities, because those come naturally to you.<br /> <br /> Focused Sight, in contrast, involves staring intently at a specific subject through the filter of a single Arcanum, and adding any additional Arcana actually interferes with your ability to succeed on the roll (&quot;Permutations Arcana&quot;, p. 93).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T01:04:53-07:00","id":1107569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1107192#post1107192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're thinking of Focused Sight. Active Sight automatically uses multiple Arcana, and then you can spend extra mana to include other Arcana.<br /> <br /> So you get Forces and Prime automatically, and then pay extra to see Mind, but you still get all three. It's like...going to a movie in 3D. You pay extra to wear the 3D glasses, but you still have color and 2D perceptual abilities, because those come naturally to you.<br /> <br /> Focused Sight, in contrast, involves staring intently at a specific subject through the filter of a single Arcanum, and adding any additional Arcana actually interferes with your ability to succeed on the roll (&quot;Permutations Arcana&quot;, p. 93).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAh, I stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:29:24-07:00","id":1109661,"title":"","content":"I am assuming sharing an specific Arcanum for Mage Sight with another as Ragnar asked is a simple Unveiling spell. I will make a simple post with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T03:39:42-07:00","id":1109678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1109661#post1109661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am assuming sharing an specific Arcanum for Mage Sight with another as Ragnar asked is a simple Unveiling spell. I will make a simple post with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the spell you cast that lets everyone see and interact with ghosts was essentially what Ragnar was asking for, so he already has Death covered. He was asking for help with seeing phenomena from other arcana. <br /> <br /> Also, just wanted everyone to know that I'm sorry I haven't been very active this week. My wife and I closed on our new house on Monday! So we have been a little busy with moving. I'm also leaving for a week-long vacation tomorrow, but I'll have more down time than usual so it shouldn't prevent me from posting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T03:41:49-07:00","id":1109680,"title":"","content":"Lynx helps Ragnar with the Spirit Arcanum. I figure he can take a single success, as there is no risk of paradox, and he'll try to use the Concentration yantra just long enough for Ragnar to observe what's necessary. I'll make a more substantial post later, as IRL is being a pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:42:51-07:00","id":1112380,"title":"","content":"Casting Divination to try and keep this from turning into the stereotypical &quot;let's split up in the haunted house&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T00:10:30-07:00","id":1112536,"title":"","content":"Hello, I doubt it is possible but do you have an open slot for a character? I'm new to mage, I want to play but have not had much luck, so I thought I would try my hand at play by post. If you do I can discuss a character with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:32:47-07:00","id":1112695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1112536#post1112536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I doubt it is possible but do you have an open slot for a character? I'm new to mage, I want to play but have not had much luck, so I thought I would try my hand at play by post. If you do I can discuss a character with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but we are full at the moment. I have had several others ask to join a Mage game as well. Your best bet is probably to start a recruitment thread here on the boards seeking a group and a Storyteller. If enough people are interested, I bet you can find someone willing to be a Storyteller. If there still isn't someone willing to step up, i might be willing to revive my old game that died (Mountains of Shadow) as a Storyteller. But I would also rather have the chance to play my own character than to ST for a second campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:33:19-07:00","id":1112964,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> You have both a player and a PC who are Shakespeare fans, so you need to get up pretty early in the morning to slip a potential &quot;no man born of woman&quot; situation past Ragnar and me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T18:48:51-07:00","id":1113042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1112964#post1112964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> You have both a player and a PC who are Shakespeare fans, so you need to get up pretty early in the morning to slip a potential &amp;quot;no man born of woman&amp;quot; situation past Ragnar and me!</div> </div> </div> </div>I...actually don't know what you mean. I'm a bit rusty on my Shakespeare references.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:18:04-07:00","id":1113052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1112695#post1112695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but we are full at the moment. I have had several others ask to join a Mage game as well. Your best bet is probably to start a recruitment thread here on the boards seeking a group and a Storyteller. If enough people are interested, I bet you can find someone willing to be a Storyteller. If there still isn't someone willing to step up, i might be willing to revive my old game that died (Mountains of Shadow) as a Storyteller. But I would also rather have the chance to play my own character than to ST for a second campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I have that thread up<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1113048-recruitment-new-mage-the-awakening-2e-player-seeks-game-or-to-start-one\"> right here</a> for you. Feel free to say you'd like to play, having an experienced player there with me would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:50:02-07:00","id":1113064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1113042#post1113042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I...actually don't know what you mean. I'm a bit rusty on my Shakespeare references.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a line from <i>Macbeth. </i>When Macbeth goes to the Weird Sisters for information, they say that &quot;no man born of woman&quot; can kill him. He takes this to mean that he's immortal, but at the end of the play, Macduff comes to get revenge for his wife and son, and reveals that he was &quot;from my mother's womb untimely ripped,&quot; which scholars generally interpret to mean that he was delivered via C-section or his mother died in labor and he was removed from her corpse, thus he was not &quot;born.&quot; Macduff then kills Macbeth in a duel. <br /> <br /> Fun fact, this &quot;cop out&quot; was what inspired J.R.R. Tolkien to have Eowyn kill the Witch-King in <i>\u200bThe Return of the King: </i>he had gone to see a production of Macbeth as a child, and had assumed that the twist in the prophecy was going to be the Macbeth would be killed by a woman. Hence the similar terms of the prophecy. <br /> <br /> The more you know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T09:25:56-07:00","id":1113276,"title":"","content":"In a bit of a rut IRL. Will make a post when able. Play on Lynx's Distracted condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:29:05-07:00","id":1115486,"title":"","content":"Update: My wife and I are finally moving all of our stuff out of our apartment into our new house on Saturday. We have been swamped this week with last minute packing and cleaning, and I have been busy and tired at night when I often work on my posts. <br /> <br /> I will try to get up another IC post soon, I'm guessing that another Storyteller post with info on what you're seeing in the house will help others know how to respond and act. Thanks again for your patience!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/9