818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T04:16:47-07:00","id":1152456,"title":"","content":"Hey all, sorry I haven't posted in the past few days. Had a few things going on with personal stuff, we had guests this weekend and I've been busy at work too. I'll try to get a post up today so we can keep up the momentum. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T23:46:46-08:00","id":1157888,"title":"","content":"I've got enough XP to buy up Arcana/Gnosis. Is that something I can just do at a dramatic moment, reaching beyond Moonstone's limits, or would it be better to wait until a longer break?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T18:10:59-08:00","id":1158730,"title":"","content":"Guyyyyys I am the worst. I'm so sorry I've been absent. This has been lower on my priority list lately and I have totally slacked off, and our momentum has been poor because of that. <br /> <br /> I really do like this game and want it to keep moving. Work has been crazy busy so I haven't had down time there to work on posts either. But I'll try to make this more of a priority and keep things going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T03:29:54-08:00","id":1158847,"title":"","content":"I mean, is a game after all, of course there are a lot of things that will take precedence over that (family and work chief amongst them) so I totally understand. I will welcome the continuity of the game so much though, it's been helping me get my mind off certain issues that one should not dwell in.<br /> <br /> In short, don't worry about it and welcome back when you are ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T05:49:52-08:00","id":1158905,"title":"","content":"I Second that notion. We at mountains of shadow wish you well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T19:52:06-07:00","id":1411737,"title":"","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> Tagging everyone who has been an active player in this game in the past:<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a><br /> <br /> I hope that you all see this, and I hope that it finds you well. I have a lot of things that went through my mind as I was preparing this post, and I'm still not sure of how to organize them all. But the main thing I wanted to say is that I desperately miss this game and I would love to see if there are enough of you still active on these boards and still interested in this game that you'd be interested in resurrecting it.<br /> <br /> I was talking a few weeks ago with one of my best friends IRL about some of the tabletop RPGs I've played in or run, and this game is still near the top of my list. Despite being a PBP game, I loved the thoughtfulness, creativity, and social interaction that went into this game, both on the OOC and IC threads. I still have not been able to play a Mage game in person in the past few years; I've been part of a regular D&amp;D 5e game for going on just over 2 years, but still haven't found the personal time and a group of interested players to play something like this.<br /> <br /> I feel that I owe all of you an apology for my communication when we stopped playing. Around the time I went dark on the forums, I was grappling with several personal issues, involving marital problems, adjustments to more responsibilities at work, and a lot of other things demanding my time and attention. On top of that, Onyx Path forums and Orokos were both added to the firewall at my work, so I wasn't able to quickly type up something on my breaks anymore. As my availability waned, I started feeling more pressure to keep up with quality posts and I just really fell behind. It got to a point where I let the guilt affect my ST approach and so I just ghosted you all. In reviewing the entire IC thread and most of the OOC thread in the past few days, I've been reminded of how appreciative, supportive, and patient you all were, so I'm sorry for not being honest and just sharing how I was feeling.<br /> <br /> This is really unorthodox, and I honestly know that it's a long shot. But if even 4 of you are still around and want to get this game up and running again, I would love to breathe some life back into it.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest and up front about the fact that I don't think my life has necessarily gotten much quieter in the past 3 years. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have an 18-month-old daughter who keeps me on my toes. Work is busy, but on a whim I checked and saw that OP Forums is off the firewall list again, so I can access the forums more easily (although I will still need to use my phone browser to do dice rolls or find another online dice roller that works with CoD mechanics).<br /> <br /> So: Who's with me? Anyone? Please let me know sometime in the next few days so we can talk shop and figure out the logistics. I'll dust off my ST notes and brainstorm some plot hooks to finish off this Chapter and start the next one, but I'd rather wait to do that until I know that this could actually happen.<br /> <br /> Also, in case anyone asks or was curious: I have no intentions of resurrecting my other PBP game here, Mountains of Shadow. I might steal some ideas I had come up with for that campaign, but I just don't have the desire or motivation to run that. I want to put all of my time and creativity into one game, and this one specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 09-04-2020, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T23:53:00-07:00","id":1412014,"title":"","content":"I'm interested. To be honest, I have been checking in on this thread quite a few times over the years, wondering if something would happen. <br /> <br /> Question though, would we pick up from where we were, or will we do some sort of soft reboot / reset? It's been a long time and I don't know if I'll be able to connect to Lynx as a character in media res. A lot has happened in my life as well. <br /> <br /> Hope to hear from you all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T04:56:27-07:00","id":1412053,"title":"","content":"So good to hear from you!!<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve put a lot of work into creating the world, so I like the setting a lot and would prefer to still use it. I\u2019m flexible with whatever makes it more fun for everyone else. It would probably depend on what everyone wants to do, assuming at least a few people are still interested.<br /> <br /> If you have time, you can do what I did and reread the IC thread from start to finish. It might help you come up with ideas or find Lynx\u2019s \u201cvoice\u201d again. If you decide you would rather change parts of his character, either his actual character sheet or his backstory, we could edit or retcon whatever we need to in order for this to be fun. Or if you want to make a new character, we could introduce one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T10:58:17-07:00","id":1412116,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll try to find time to do that. Let's see if the others show up first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T12:00:40-07:00","id":1412628,"title":"","content":"Said this in PM but figured I'd say it here too; I'm grateful for the thought, but in the intervening years I've just lost my capacity for forum-based play. Discord PBP is about all that works for me. However, given the fact that the ability to access this site at work was a factor that impacted the game's original hiatus, I'm not coming in expecting that Discord PBP would be a convenient method for our ST. So most likely I'll be bowing out, but I hope the rest of you can enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T05:22:09-07:00","id":1413361,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> - Totally understand, and I appreciate the prompt answer. I\u2019m not able to do Discord very easily. I can access it on my phone during the work day but I would have to do almost all the typing on my phone, unless I routinely email it to myself and then copy/paste, which feels convoluted. However, I\u2019m really curious how a PBP game looks on Discord. How do you save messages for easy reference? Can you have persisting links to old posts? I thought the chat was just a running list of messages. That doesn\u2019t strike me as super easy for PBP games but I\u2019m really curious what that could look like. Also, does Discord have a built in dice roller? That would be convenient but I wasn\u2019t sure if it is a feature. <br /> <br /> Everyone else: I\u2019m still here and interested. Not sure who else might be but let me know. If we could at least get 3 players, preferably 4, that would be ideal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T10:45:13-07:00","id":1416012,"title":"","content":"I thought I sent this earlier but the forum may have eaten it.<br /> <br /> TL;DR Discord has a feature allowing you to pin messages, and its search feature is pretty robust. It definitely helps to make use of multiple IC channels if you're going to have people split off into different groups or by themselves. You can incorporate dicebots into a server (which generally are best confined to a single dice-rolling channel, with perhaps a second hidden one for secret ST rolls if you want) and one, Dicecord-CoD, is made specifically for Chronicles of Darkness rolling.<br /> <br /> I've been in a long-running Exalted 3e PBP game via Discord and it works really well for us. Having OOC, IC, and rolling all in the same server (with personal, hidden channels for discussion between the ST and each individual player in turn) is pretty convenient.<br /> <br /> Now, none of that fixes the issue of your capacity to access and post on Discord during your work hours, but I didn't want to leave you hanging any more than I already did. I will say, it might benefit y'all to have a discord just for OOC, as it helps with coordinating and that probably isn't as restricted by only being phone-accessible to you during work hours since you're not having to do big IC posts there.<br /> <br /> Best of luck in any case!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T11:22:22-07:00","id":1416881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1416012#post1416012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I sent this earlier but the forum may have eaten it.<br /> <br /> TL;DR Discord has a feature allowing you to pin messages, and its search feature is pretty robust. It definitely helps to make use of multiple IC channels if you're going to have people split off into different groups or by themselves. You can incorporate dicebots into a server (which generally are best confined to a single dice-rolling channel, with perhaps a second hidden one for secret ST rolls if you want) and one, Dicecord-CoD, is made specifically for Chronicles of Darkness rolling.<br /> <br /> I've been in a long-running Exalted 3e PBP game via Discord and it works really well for us. Having OOC, IC, and rolling all in the same server (with personal, hidden channels for discussion between the ST and each individual player in turn) is pretty convenient.<br /> <br /> Now, none of that fixes the issue of your capacity to access and post on Discord during your work hours, but I didn't want to leave you hanging any more than I already did. I will say, it might benefit y'all to have a discord just for OOC, as it helps with coordinating and that probably isn't as restricted by only being phone-accessible to you during work hours since you're not having to do big IC posts there.<br /> <br /> Best of luck in any case!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks so much for sharing the ideas and the input. I never realized that some of these features existed, and others I realized were there but never considered how they could be utilized. Thanks for sharing! On a related subject, is it possible to direct link to a specific post, or is searching the best? Just trying to figure out if there's an easy way to create a &quot;table of contents&quot; post within Discord.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - Unfortunately, it looks like no one else from the original crew is available right now. A few have logged on but never replied to my PM or posted here, so I'm going to assume at this point that they aren't interested for now. The others just haven't logged on in the past few months; they might come back, but no idea if/when that might happen.<br /> <br /> I have a few ideas on what we could do if you are still personally interested in playing:<br /> <br /> (1) I could run the game solo for you as Lynx, and if/when other players decide to rejoin, they could do so. I have some IC ideas on reasons for their absence. I would introduce new NPCs for you to hang out with, or have you spend more time with Raven and The Shields of Dawn on screen.<br /> (2) I could run the game solo for you as another character, if Lynx is no longer interesting to you and you'd like to try something different. If/when other players decide to rejoin, you could keep playing as the new character or switch back to Lynx if you like.<br /> (3) I could NPC some/all of the other players, and let them take over if/when they decide to rejoin. I don't love this because it's messier if others show up later.<br /> (4) We could recruit additional characters, and you could continue as Lynx with a new cabal. Trickier to deal with if more of the original crew come back, but it would get the game moving again.<br /> (5) We could keep this game on hiatus, and I could start a new PbP game in a new setting, and invite you as a player. I would recruit more players and start from scratch. If enough players from this game show back up in the future, we could run this game separately at that time.<br /> (6) We could do nothing for now and leave this game on hiatus. If/when others show up in the future (ideally at least 3 players), we could restart it.<br /> <br /> Let me know if you like any of these options, and what you would like to try!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T15:35:02-07:00","id":1416906,"title":"","content":"You can in fact get direct links to posts, which I just realized, which is good! You could definitely make a table of contents with that, I think. The links can cross channel and category bounds as well, so you can provide links to posts in different channels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T17:39:50-07:00","id":1416914,"title":"","content":"FWIW Beans, I PMed rwknoll a little while back about potentially filling a vacancy. I've been meaning to post, but unfortunately life is insanely busy right now. If you transition to another game, I'd love to jump in, especially if it's Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T12:06:32-07:00","id":1417032,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I think I'd prefer something like a soft reboot. I still want to play Lynx, though my perception of him has changed over the years (does that even make sense). I also think recruiting new players would be better than waiting, if this is going to ever kick off. I'd probably respec Lynx anyway. So I guess a mix of 4 and 5? Honestly, the character would probably be completely different at this point anyway, same name but different character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T12:21:34-07:00","id":1417036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417032#post1417032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I think I'd prefer something like a soft reboot. I still want to play Lynx, though my perception of him has changed over the years (does that even make sense). I also think recruiting new players would be better than waiting, if this is going to ever kick off. I'd probably respec Lynx anyway. So I guess a mix of 4 and 5? Honestly, the character would probably be completely different at this point anyway, same name but different character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok! I can totally work with that. I really have enjoyed this setting and I've put a lot of thought into creating the NPCs and some of the Mysteries involved.<br /> <br /> It makes a lot of sense that over the past few years you would've thought about Lynx and reflected on whether or not he matches the type of character you would enjoy playing, or the concept you've created for him. My own interest in which Path/Order I would like to play if I was ever a Mage player has changed, so I can imagine that your own vision of Lynx could change as well.<br /> <br /> A few questions:<br /> - Do you still think you would want to play Lynx as a Thyrsus, or has that changed?<br /> - Do you think it would be more fun to play a recently Awakened mage and still RP through the Order initiation process, or do you think it would be more fun/easier to assume that you're already in an Order and that the cabal has already formed?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it might be simpler to fast forward through the Order initiation and do a more standard character creation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2021\" data-vbnamecard=\"2021\">MagicSwordsman</a> - I know you've been on the forums recently but I haven't heard back. Totally understand if you don't want to play in any campaign related to this one or in a game I'm running, but if you are, you're welcome to join us. Please let me know before Monday; if I haven't heard from you by then, I'll assume you aren't available.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - I would be glad to have you aboard. I'd love to hear your pitch of what kind of character you would like to play, even if you just have general inklings for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T12:33:40-07:00","id":1417039,"title":"","content":"I'll have to give it a bit of consideration, but it'd probably still be Thyrsus with the animist angle, yeah. <br /> <br /> I also agree it's probably easier to just go with the assumption that we're already initiated and have formed (or start with the forming of) the cabal, though I'm happy to let you or the others decide on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T12:48:00-07:00","id":1417042,"title":"","content":"My initial thought had been a Moros who sees ghosts, goetia, spirits as being manifestations of a larger occult world and is actively seeking to overcome the fact Spirit is their Inferior Arcana, but its a very rough idea, so I could go with an entirely different concept if that doesn't fit so much. <br /> <br /> Also, agreed with just jumping to the point the Cabal is already formed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T03:53:26-07:00","id":1417123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417042#post1417042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial thought had been a Moros who sees ghosts, goetia, spirits as being manifestations of a larger occult world and is actively seeking to overcome the fact Spirit is their Inferior Arcana, but its a very rough idea, so I could go with an entirely different concept if that doesn't fit so much. <br /> <br /> Also, agreed with just jumping to the point the Cabal is already formed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a neat idea. Probably lends itself to Obsessions about interacting with a variety of ephemeral entities, which makes it easier for me to introduce some for plot hooks. <br /> <br /> I think what we can do is have the story pick up around the time as this one went on hiatus, maybe just after the Consilium meeting. The NPCs I have introduced will still be in the game, but depending on the new PC cabal composition, the Shields of Dawn may or may not be the de facto mentors for your characters.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m giving the rest of the original players until Monday to join and then I\u2019ll open up for recruitment again. Gives me a few days to start brainstorming some plot ideas and larger Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T04:31:04-07:00","id":1417130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417042#post1417042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial thought had been a Moros who sees ghosts, goetia, spirits as being manifestations of a larger occult world and is actively seeking to overcome the fact Spirit is their Inferior Arcana, but its a very rough idea, so I could go with an entirely different concept if that doesn't fit so much.<br /> <br /> Also, agreed with just jumping to the point the Cabal is already formed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be a good link with Lynx, who sees spirits in everything. He'd definitely have motivation to help you understand the spiritual aspect of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T08:40:40-07:00","id":1417327,"title":"","content":"For you two who are already committed to the &quot;soft reboot&quot; we are planning, here are some additional details regarding character concepts and creation.<br /> <br /> We will continue to use the existing OOC and IC threads for the game. It's easier than starting from scratch in a new thread, I think.<br /> <br /> Follow normal character creation rules, with the following exceptions: Begin with Gnosis 2 instead of Gnosis 1. However, you cannot spend extra merits to begin with Gnosis 3. This essentially gives you 5 extra merit dots (if I recall correctly), but you can start with a little better control over magic without sacrificing merits to flesh out your character background. Use the merits from character creation to better flesh out and reflect your character concept. This will hopefully give you more flexibility with making your character's background match the concept you want to create, but without forcing you to start with Gnosis 1.<br /> <br /> Feel free to suggest alternative Virtues/Vices than what are listed in the book. If you do, please list a few examples of situations that you think would qualify for satisfying the Virtue/Vice so I can make sure that I know how to reward you for following these in-game.<br /> <br /> My ideal player group size is 4-6 characters, including the two of you. If we move to recruitment, I will not automatically add the first few people to reply; instead, I'm looking for players who appear to be thoughtful, mature, and friendly. I think these qualities are necessary to make the gaming experience better for everyone, and although I've had very few concerns about the caliber of people posting on these forums, there have been some who have given me concern or may not be a good fit for my game in my opinion.<br /> <br /> If you have any questions/concerns, feel free to post here. I have some extra time today to help out, as I telework from home on Thursdays and it's easier for me to post during the day from my personal computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T15:52:12-07:00","id":1417573,"title":"","content":"While I do appreciate the welcoming back, I'm unfortunately going to have to decline. I've simply moved on and playing live games. PBP was a means of playing when I couldn't play that way. Now that I am, I've found I don't really like PBP that much. Nothing in particular about this game, I just don't like PBP in general. That said, I wish y'all luck in this chronicle. Thanks for the fun times while they lasted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T16:06:24-07:00","id":1417574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417573#post1417573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do appreciate the welcoming back, I'm unfortunately going to have to decline. I've simply moved on and playing live games. PBP was a means of playing when I couldn't play that way. Now that I am, I've found I don't really like PBP that much. Nothing in particular about this game, I just don't like PBP in general. That said, I wish y'all luck in this chronicle. Thanks for the fun times while they lasted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Totally understand! Thanks so much for letting me know. Hope all has been well with you these past few years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T12:05:18-07:00","id":1417863,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>: I have officially opened up the game for recruitment again! If you know of anyone else who you think would like to join, please talk to them and ask them to consider submitting a character concept.<br /> <br /> At your convenience, can the two of you please also post character ideas with the following information? And anyone else reading this who would like to submit a character, please provide this same information.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept: </b>Summarize your character concept in one phrase or short sentence.<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name:<br /> Shadow Name:<br /> Path:<br /> Order:<br /> Legacy:</b> (If you have one in mind)<br /> <b>Virtue:<br /> Vice: </b><br /> <b>Background:</b> Please provide a brief narrative summary of the character concept, taking into consideration how your background may fit into the greater Mysteries described in the introductory post in this thread. You can also include information about the character's Awakening.<br /> <br /> KKV, you are welcome to change as little or as much about Lynx as you like, or you can even submit an entirely brand new character concept if you like.<br /> <br /> I don't have a deadline for recruitment, it really depends on how many other people post here and the quality of their submissions. If you two can try to have something posted within the next few days, though, that will help me start to brainstorm some story hooks and Mysteries that might help us get the game started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:59:10-07:00","id":1417973,"title":"","content":"<b>Concept: </b>Multi-Level Marketing Executive / Conwoman<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name: </b><b>Hannah</b>Kaczkowski<br /> <b>Shadow Name: Morganna<br /> Path: Mastigos<br /> Order: Silver Ladder<br /> Legacy:</b> (If you have one in mind)<br /> <b>Virtue: Just <br /> Vice: Deceitful</b><br /> <b>Background:</b> It's all a lie, literally. What is true is that Hannah graduated from the University of Illinois Champlain with a degree is business, that she served 18 months in Club Fed (Federal minimum security) for making materially false statements to the FBI and that her ex-husband got custody of the kids. Since then she's been trying to make ends meet. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T00:30:00-07:00","id":1417994,"title":"","content":"Legal Name: Hannah Kaczkowski<br /> Shadow Name: Morganna<br /> Virtue: Just<br /> Vice: Deceptive<br /> Order: Silver Ladder<br /> Path: Mastigos<br /> Concept: Soccer Mom / Con-Woman<br /> Age: 32<br /> <br /> Background: Hannah came from a small town in Illinois and attended the University of Illinois, at Champlain. If she cheated her way through business school, well many of her classmates did the same. After graduation, she worked in a number of less than savory business ventures. Ironically, it wasn\u2019t some scam that landed her in jail. Instead it was going legit. Hannah snagged a position at a drug company, only to find that they had hidden the addictive and dangerous nature of one of their blockbuster products. When Hannah tried to, anonymously, report the situation to the authorities she instead found herself fired and under investigation. Ultimately, she spent 18 months in a federal (minimum security) prison for lying to the FBI.<br /> <br /> While awaiting trial, Hannah began working for a cultlike multi-level marketing firm \u2013 Pentacle Supply, actual a Silver Ladder front. Hannah\u2019s awakening as a Mastigos formed a mystery play taking part at the same time as her release from prison.<br /> <br /> Hannah is now back on the outside. While on the inside her husband (Mat) divorced her, getting custody of the couple\u2019s two kids (Lucy, 10 and Max 8).<br /> <br /> Needless to say Hannah, is frightened to discover the supernatural is real. Looking to stop being scared, she took the name Morgana, after Morgana le Fey \u2013 one of the central villains of Arthurian lore.<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Be Less Scared (Short Term), Pull a Con on a Supernatural Entity (Long Term), Don\u2019t Forget to Pickup Lucy\u2019s Scout Uniform from the Cleaners (Short Term)<br /> <br /> Obsessions: Find out what\u2019s happening to the kids at the high school.<br /> <br /> Long Term Conditions: Ex-Con (Non-Violent)<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 3<br /> Wits : 2<br /> Resolve: 3 (2+1)<br /> <br /> Str: 1<br /> Dex: 3<br /> Sta: 2<br /> <br /> Prs: 2<br /> Mnp: 3<br /> Cps: 3<br /> <br /> Skills:<br /> Academics: 1 (Business)<br /> Politics: 1<br /> Occult: 3 (Astral Realms)<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> <br /> Athletics: 3<br /> Firearms: 3 (Pistols)<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> <br /> Empathy: 1<br /> Persuasion: 4 (Confidence Scams) (Rote Skill)(Asset Skill)<br /> Socialize: 1<br /> Streetwise: 1<br /> Subterfuge: 4 (Rote Skill)(Asset Skill)<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 2<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> <br /> Arcana:<br /> Mind: 3<br /> Space: 2<br /> Prime: 1<br /> <br /> Praxis:<br /> Pierce Deception (Prime 1)<br /> Enhance Skill (Mind 3)<br /> <br /> Rotes:<br /> Goetic Summons (Mind 3)<br /> Augment Mind (Mind 3)<br /> Psychic Assault (Mind 3)<br /> <br /> Dedicated Tool: A small statue of justice that sat on the window of her cell.<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> High Speech<br /> Silver Ladder Status 1<br /> Shadow Name: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Mystery Cult Initiation: Avalon Supply MLM<br /> * Specialty (Occult, Astral Realms)<br /> ** Striking Looks: 1<br /> *** Extra Skill Dot (Occult)<br /> **** Astral Adept 3<br /> ***** Resources 2, Mentor 1<br /> <br /> Professional Training (Conwoman)<br /> Asset Skills: Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> * Contacts (Criminals, High Society)<br /> ** 9 Again on Persuasion and Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Gear:<br /> Studio Apartment<br /> Mini-Van<br /> 9mm Glock (might be illegal to own, purchased at a gun show).<br /> Kevlar Vest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","user":"DrSteve","date":". 10-15-2020, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T02:04:22-07:00","id":1418001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417863#post1417863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KKV, you are welcome to change as little or as much about Lynx as you like, or you can even submit an entirely brand new character concept if you like.<br /> <br /> I don't have a deadline for recruitment, it really depends on how many other people post here and the quality of their submissions. If you two can try to have something posted within the next few days, though, that will help me start to brainstorm some story hooks and Mysteries that might help us get the game started.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've looked over Lynx a bit the last couple of days, and I'm still a little uncertain which direction to take Lynx. I might play up the spiritual aspect to complement <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a>, so I'd like some feedback there. Am thinking one dot of Dream merit, and some changes to rotes and praxes. Virtue and vice are also currently undecided. Since we're officially starting at 2 gnosis now, I assume that also means we get 2 praxes?<br /> <br /> <b>Concept: </b>Foreign exchange student and (probably) animist. (otherwise something something spiritual caretaker)<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name: </b> Oscar Dalberg. <br /> <b>Shadow Name: </b> Lynx<br /> <b>Path: </b> Thyrsus<br /> <b>Order: </b> Mysterium<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Undecided<br /> <b>Virtue: </b> Passionate (subject to change)<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Gluttonous (subject to change) <br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> (short summary of original story, which may be altered be altered, but the gist is there) Born in Norway to ambitious parents; emotionally neglected during large parts of childhood; rebelled as a teenager by running from home, which triggered the beginning of his Mystery Play, a journey into the Primal Wild; however, retreated from the calling due to fear. Mystery Play lingered as Oscar's fear slowly turned to curiosity, and adopted spiritual practises in an attempt to reconnect, but it became an obsession that made him largely withdraw from society. One day, wanderlust struck, and he suggested studying abroad to his parents, who agreed on condition that he take the studies seriously. After applying to universities and colleges around the world, one stood out to him: a college near La Grange. When he landed in the US, his Mystery Play resumed in full force. He journeyed through the Primal Wild, this time without fear, and embraced it as he, once Oscar, now Lynx, arrived to his new home. <br /> <br /> Links to greater mysteries: The fluctuating gauntlets of the Brookfield Zoo, and the Uratha and Hallows of the Bemis Woods are the two most natural links to the supernal points of interest in La Grange. From a more earthly perspective, the Rumors Nightclub is something Lynx is very curious about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T11:00:36-07:00","id":1418070,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - Interesting character concept, thanks for expressing interest in the game!<br /> <br /> I have a few questions looking at the overall character sheet and the background.<br /> <br /> (1) What is Hannah's new relationship with her ex-husband and children now that she has Awakened? Do they still live in the Chicago metro area? Your aspirations suggest that she still sees her children, but I wasn't sure from your background what her new relationships might be with her former family. I also wonder if there is anything else that ties Hannah to Chicago specifically; did she move here after getting out of prison? Do you think she would have known about the Highstorms or other local Mysteries before moving here?<br /> <br /> (2) Regarding skills: I think these all make sense, except I'm thinking Persuasion 5 might be excessive considering the context. 5 dots in a skill implies &quot;absolute mastery of the discipline&quot; per the core book, and you also picked skills that overlapped with both rote and asset skills. You're going to be *the best* at these skills, but I might suggest moving some of your skills around to have a little more utility in other settings. Would it make sense to move Persuasion down to 4 and bump Empathy or Occupt up to 2, or putting 1 dot in Investigation?<br /> <br /> (3) Can you explain to me more about the rationale for Mystery Cult Initiation for an Awakened mage? I have not seen that for PCs except when the merit is being used as a substitute for Order Status for a Nameless Order. Since you have only the free starting dot in Silver Ladder status, unless I'm misunderstanding the MCI merit, the allocation you have picked paints the picture of a mage who is deeply invested as a <b>subordinate </b>member in a cult for Sleepers that is influenced behind the scenes by another th\u00e9arch, but has not moved to being in a place of influence yet within that cult. I wonder if <b>Mystery Cult Influence</b> (p. 103) is a better option? Alternatively, I think having higher dots in Silver Ladder status could represent a great level of influence over an existing Mystery Cult run by the th\u00e9archs. Finally, can you explain your thoughts on how Astral Adept and Shadow Name fit into the Mystery Cult symbolism? I'm not opposed to these choices, but I'm wondering how they relate specifically to the cult involvement. On a related note, what type of symbolism do you think the Shadow Name of Morgana should hold, or what types of spells or Imagos do you think fall within its purview?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T17:19:12-07:00","id":1418122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418070#post1418070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - Interesting character concept, thanks for expressing interest in the game!<br /> <br /> I have a few questions looking at the overall character sheet and the background.<br /> <br /> (1) What is Hannah's new relationship with her ex-husband and children now that she has Awakened? Do they still live in the Chicago metro area? Your aspirations suggest that she still sees her children, but I wasn't sure from your background what her new relationships might be with her former family. I also wonder if there is anything else that ties Hannah to Chicago specifically; did she move here after getting out of prison? Do you think she would have known about the Highstorms or other local Mysteries before moving here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well she is not going to send a goetia to eat her ex-husbands face in the middle of the night. When she went to prison, he divorced her, married a younger woman, took most of the assets and the kids. He's from a political family and is gearing up to run for office. Her shadow name is Morganna, the sorceress who actively worked to bring down Camelot.<br /> <br /> The judge gave her some time with her kids but not much, probably one or two weekends a month. She hasn't seen them much and is trying to reconnect. It doesn't help that she's hearing that things out there might want to randomly kill her (no sanctum or safe place merit), so she's worried about being around the kids too much.<br /> <br /> She lived in the Chicago area with her family before her arrest, one of the reasons that she's back. She knows about the mysteries that a sleeper would be aware of (kids disappearing) but I can't really see her knowing about the highstorms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (2) Regarding skills: I think these all make sense, except I'm thinking Persuasion 5 might be excessive considering the context. 5 dots in a skill implies &quot;absolute mastery of the discipline&quot; per the core book, and you also picked skills that overlapped with both rote and asset skills. You're going to be *the best* at these skills, but I might suggest moving some of your skills around to have a little more utility in other settings. Would it make sense to move Persuasion down to 4 and bump Empathy or Occupt up to 2, or putting 1 dot in Investigation? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was going to ask if could retcon Medicine for Investigation. What do you mean by Occupt? (Occult? Occupational Skill?). I'm not able to find the dot rating equivalents in the Mage 2nd Ed book. Is academics 1 highschool or is it an undergraduate degree? If I accidentally gave her an MBA, then it might be best to drop it a dot and move that dot into Occult.<br /> <br /> In agreement about persuasion. It got bumped up a dot because of the mystery cult initiation, but persuasion 4, probably makes more sense for the chronicle (5 being about the level that you get out of jail and announce your run for Congress). Would Empathy or Socialize be the more useful skill to move a dot into?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (3) Can you explain to me more about the rationale for Mystery Cult Initiation for an Awakened mage? I have not seen that for PCs except when the merit is being used as a substitute for Order Status for a Nameless Order. Since you have only the free starting dot in Silver Ladder status, unless I'm misunderstanding the MCI merit, the allocation you have picked paints the picture of a mage who is deeply invested as a <b>subordinate </b>member in a cult for Sleepers that is influenced behind the scenes by another th\u00e9arch, but has not moved to being in a place of influence yet within that cult. I wonder if <b>Mystery Cult Influence</b> (p. 103) is a better option? Alternatively, I think having higher dots in Silver Ladder status could represent a great level of influence over an existing Mystery Cult run by the th\u00e9archs. Finally, can you explain your thoughts on how Astral Adept and Shadow Name fit into the Mystery Cult symbolism? I'm not opposed to these choices, but I'm wondering how they relate specifically to the cult involvement. On a related note, what type of symbolism do you think the Shadow Name of Morgana should hold, or what types of spells or Imagos do you think fall within its purview? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that mystery cult initiation 5 is still considered a subordinate role. Signs of Sorcery did have some mechanical incentive for a mage to use mystery cult initiation as it can be used as a Yantra (Level/2 rounded up) but that's a bit cheesy for what is already a powerful merit. [Edit - on the other hand, Morgana getting a Yantra bonus for breing a priestess of Avalon. . . ] (Also see how Ars Magica handles Mystery Cults).<br /> <br /> That said, I kind of like the idea of somebody that just awakened two weeks ago being in a cult run by another th\u00e9arch. One of the issues is how to get a dot of striking looks onto the character sheet (part of the riff on suburbia). How about dropping Alternative Identity 1 for Striking Looks 1 [edit - some kind of hedge magic glamour] and swapping out Shadow Name 3 for Resources 2, Mentor 1 as the Mystery Cult 5 benefit. I'm also swapping the * benefit for an Occult specialty in astral realms, making the group more supernatural focused (the skill dot probably needs to remain in persuasion, it is a MLM cult after all). [Edit - changed the name of the group to Avalon Supply to go all in on the Arthurian theme.] That gives us an MLM selling cosmetics and yoga mats [and Renfest supplies] where some of the marketing hype actually brings participants closer to awakening -- basically playing on the theme of consumerism in suburbia.<br /> <br /> At some point during play Mystery Cult Initiation can be swapped for Mystery Cult Influence (she'll take over the cult for the other (th\u00e9arch). (Astral Adept can be used by both awakened and sleepers so it fits in with the idea of cult who's practices actually work). Shadow name becomes a non-mystery cult merit. But um, lets work out in the Signs of Sorcery Investiture Yantra is going to apply. It may be a bit cheesy, but there is a balancing drawback of requiring more involvement than mystery cult influence.<br /> <br /> Morgan(n)a is one of the most complicated characters in Arthurian lore <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan_le_Fay\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan_le_Fay</a> for a Mastigos the name would be some take on a Renaissance-era witch with Arthurian overtones.<br /> <br /> In some stories, Mogranna is supposed to have learned magic from Merlin so skill enhancing magic like Enhance Skill would be covered (as would some applications of the time spell that allows the creation of a temporary background). The association with second sight probably covers all Unveiling spells, but at the least should cover Pierce Deception (as well as the one dot spirit and death sight spells). The association with Morgana the Lady of the Lake, and the fact that Excalibur was forged on Avalon in the earliest stories, means that the Prime based crafting abilities should be included (probably all of them as long as they can be done with a witchy flavor).<br /> <br /> For Mind magic, a couple of things are obvious. Mind based illusions, mind reading / manipulation, Goetia (at least when featuring either Faeries or Demons) and stat-boosting (numerous stories of various potions). Not covered would be psychic blast and other mental attacks as well as puppet master type spells (don't really appear in Arthurian literature).<br /> <br /> For Space it would include basically all the sympathetic magic spells, scrying, dowsing (locate object), wards and effects meant to release physical bonds (such as removing chains or oppening cells) but not the teleportation or extra deminsional spaces.<br /> <br /> Now if you wanted to make the situation really twisted - have her ex be a werewofl pack leader. Now you have Arthur and his knights in a complicated relationship with Morgana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","user":"DrSteve","date":". 10-15-2020, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T19:22:32-07:00","id":1418285,"title":"","content":"Keeping with the Arthurian theme, since her mentor is only *, how about an Obrimos with a shadow name of Vivian (another name for the Lady of the Lake). Gnosis 4, Forces 4, Prime 3, Mind 3, Spirit 2 (many of her Goetia are Angels to Morgana's demons). Probably similarish stats to Morgana but Prs 3, Mnp 2 (so an Obrimos who tries to get things done with force of personality where Morgana is more manipulative). Maybe with Expression 4, Persuasion 3 and Subterfuge 3. She's no slouch in the social department, but Morgana is both slightly better and more professional. The mentor/student relationship is not always one way.<br /> <br /> Edit- Actually after thinking about it over night, I&quot;m going to move the bonus skill dot from the mystery cult from Persuasion into Occult and pull a dot from somewhere else to keep persuasion at 4. That's a bit different from a frightened soccer mom who suddenly discovered the supernal but gives somebody who had minimal understanding of the occult (occult 1) ;and who's scared as her life keeps betting more bizarre (occult dots from mystery cult initiation and awakening but not from an organic buy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","user":"DrSteve","date":". 10-15-2020, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T08:29:08-07:00","id":1418532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418122#post1418122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well she is not going to send a goetia to eat her ex-husbands face in the middle of the night. When she went to prison, he divorced her, married a younger woman, took most of the assets and the kids. He's from a political family and is gearing up to run for office. Her shadow name is Morganna, the sorceress who actively worked to bring down Camelot.<br /> <br /> The judge gave her some time with her kids but not much, probably one or two weekends a month. She hasn't seen them much and is trying to reconnect. It doesn't help that she's hearing that things out there might want to randomly kill her (no sanctum or safe place merit), so she's worried about being around the kids too much.<br /> <br /> She lived in the Chicago area with her family before her arrest, one of the reasons that she's back. She knows about the mysteries that a sleeper would be aware of (kids disappearing) but I can't really see her knowing about the highstorms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love these additions to the background. Thanks for taking the time to flesh this out. I think they offer a deeper, richer perspective on Hannah/Morganna's personality and history.<br /> <br /> As far as the local setting goes, Sleepers would not know anything about the supernatural components of the Highstorm, but in my Awakened Chicago, Sleepers are aware of the very unusual weather patterns and have basically just grown accustomed to &quot;freak weather&quot; events. Most of them probably just take it in stride or even take pride in their ability to live in a city with such weird phenomenon. Their &quot;other&quot; mentality for out-of-towners and tourists is likely accentuated compared to the real world. I imagine that Sleeper cults regarding the weather are particularly common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I was going to ask if could retcon Medicine for Investigation. What do you mean by Occupt? (Occult? Occupational Skill?). I'm not able to find the dot rating equivalents in the Mage 2nd Ed book. Is academics 1 highschool or is it an undergraduate degree? If I accidentally gave her an MBA, then it might be best to drop it a dot and move that dot into Occult.<br /> <br /> In agreement about persuasion. It got bumped up a dot because of the mystery cult initiation, but persuasion 4, probably makes more sense for the chronicle (5 being about the level that you get out of jail and announce your run for Congress). Would Empathy or Socialize be the more useful skill to move a dot into? </div> </div> </div>I meant Occult, sorry about that. Per Mage p. 208, &quot;Skills with a single dot reflect a cursory training. Two dots is sufficient for professional use. Three is a high level of competency. Four is outstanding, and five is absolute mastery of the discipline.&quot; See p. 31 of the Chronicles of Darkness book for additional guidelines about Academics, as well as comments on the fact that someone with no degree but advanced self-training would have higher dots, whereas someone with an advanced degree but little interest in topics outside of their niche may actually have fewer dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure that mystery cult initiation 5 is still considered a subordinate role. Signs of Sorcery did have some mechanical incentive for a mage to use mystery cult initiation as it can be used as a Yantra (Level/2 rounded up) but that's a bit cheesy for what is already a powerful merit. [Edit - on the other hand, Morgana getting a Yantra bonus for breing a priestess of Avalon. . . ] (Also see how Ars Magica handles Mystery Cults).<br /> <br /> That said, I kind of like the idea of somebody that just awakened two weeks ago being in a cult run by another th\u00e9arch. One of the issues is how to get a dot of striking looks onto the character sheet (part of the riff on suburbia). How about dropping Alternative Identity 1 for Striking Looks 1 [edit - some kind of hedge magic glamour] and swapping out Shadow Name 3 for Resources 2, Mentor 1 as the Mystery Cult 5 benefit. I'm also swapping the * benefit for an Occult specialty in astral realms, making the group more supernatural focused (the skill dot probably needs to remain in persuasion, it is a MLM cult after all). [Edit - changed the name of the group to Avalon Supply to go all in on the Arthurian theme.] That gives us an MLM selling cosmetics and yoga mats [and Renfest supplies] where some of the marketing hype actually brings participants closer to awakening -- basically playing on the theme of consumerism in suburbia.<br /> <br /> At some point during play Mystery Cult Initiation can be swapped for Mystery Cult Influence (she'll take over the cult for the other (th\u00e9arch). (Astral Adept can be used by both awakened and sleepers so it fits in with the idea of cult who's practices actually work). Shadow name becomes a non-mystery cult merit. But um, lets work out in the Signs of Sorcery Investiture Yantra is going to apply. It may be a bit cheesy, but there is a balancing drawback of requiring more involvement than mystery cult influence. </div> </div> </div>My expectation of players is that they will help to make the story more engaging and rewarding, and that they will prioritize the shared experience over power-gaming or &quot;cheese.&quot; I think your general suggestions and edits make sense, but I'll need more input from you as we play on how to incorporate the Mystery Cult because I am less familiar with Ars Magica and have only recently obtained Signs of Sorcery, so I have more work to do to better understand these mechanics and incorporate them into the story in a meaningful way. I want players to feel powerful and excited about their characters, and in a game of Mage, I am totally fine with characters being &quot;awesome&quot; or exceptional -- but I will provide opportunities for conflict built around the theme that power corrupts and that there are ramifications for your actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Morgan(n)a is one of the most complicated characters in Arthurian lore <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan_le_Fay\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan_le_Fay</a> for a Mastigos the name would be some take on a Renaissance-era witch with Arthurian overtones.<br /> <br /> In some stories, Mogranna is supposed to have learned magic from Merlin so skill enhancing magic like Enhance Skill would be covered (as would some applications of the time spell that allows the creation of a temporary background). The association with second sight probably covers all Unveiling spells, but at the least should cover Pierce Deception (as well as the one dot spirit and death sight spells). The association with Morgana the Lady of the Lake, and the fact that Excalibur was forged on Avalon in the earliest stories, means that the Prime based crafting abilities should be included (probably all of them as long as they can be done with a witchy flavor).<br /> <br /> For Mind magic, a couple of things are obvious. Mind based illusions, mind reading / manipulation, Goetia (at least when featuring either Faeries or Demons) and stat-boosting (numerous stories of various potions). Not covered would be psychic blast and other mental attacks as well as puppet master type spells (don't really appear in Arthurian literature).<br /> <br /> For Space it would include basically all the sympathetic magic spells, scrying, dowsing (locate object), wards and effects meant to release physical bonds (such as removing chains or oppening cells) but not the teleportation or extra deminsional spaces. </div> </div> </div>These are all awesome, and I really dig it. Thanks for being intentional about semiotics. I think Shadow Name is often overused and takes some of the challenge out of incorporating Yantras thoughtfully if the ST and player don't t set boundaries around the merit's use. I just wanted to make sure that you were thinking about when it does and doesn't apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now if you wanted to make the situation really twisted - have her ex be a werewofl pack leader. Now you have Arthur and his knights in a complicated relationship with Morgana. </div> </div> </div>Mmmmm...Now we're talking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keeping with the Arthurian theme, since her mentor is only *, how about an Obrimos with a shadow name of Vivian (another name for the Lady of the Lake). Gnosis 4, Forces 4, Prime 3, Mind 3, Spirit 2 (many of her Goetia are Angels to Morgana's demons). Probably similarish stats to Morgana but Prs 3, Mnp 2 (so an Obrimos who tries to get things done with force of personality where Morgana is more manipulative). Maybe with Expression 4, Persuasion 3 and Subterfuge 3. She's no slouch in the social department, but Morgana is both slightly better and more professional. The mentor/student relationship is not always one way.<br /> <br /> Edit- Actually after thinking about it over night, I&quot;m going to move the bonus skill dot from the mystery cult from Persuasion into Occult and pull a dot from somewhere else to keep persuasion at 4. That's a bit different from a frightened soccer mom who suddenly discovered the supernal but gives somebody who had minimal understanding of the occult (occult 1) ;and who's scared as her life keeps betting more bizarre (occult dots from mystery cult initiation and awakening but not from an organic buy). </div> </div> </div>I'll get back to you on the mentor stuff, I need to review the merit and consider how to flesh them out. I actually wonder if it might be an interesting idea to have your mentor be the th\u00e9arch who is in charge of Avalon Supply. So that would make the Obrimos another Silver Ladder member, and given that your Order Status is so low and her Gnosis and Arcana are so much higher, I'm pretty sure Vivian is definitely not going to view the mentor as bidirectional (even if Morganna, of course, may see it differently).<br /> <br /> When you have time, can you find pictures to add for Morganna and Vivian?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T07:37:41-07:00","id":1418659,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - Just wanted to say that you\u2019re officially in, in case that wasn\u2019t clear. Looking forward to playing with you!<br /> <br /> I have also posted a recruitment post on the RPG.net forums. It seems like they are way more active. Hoping that draws some more interest.<br /> <br /> If I am somehow able to access RPG.net from work, I might suggest that we migrate there to play the game. I\u2019ll let you know if I suggest that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T08:41:57-07:00","id":1418665,"title":"","content":"I'm interested, but quite busy today - hope I can figure out a good thumbnail before this fills up ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T09:02:38-07:00","id":1418667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418665#post1418665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested, but quite busy today - hope I can figure out a good thumbnail before this fills up ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, glad to hear you are interested! No rush, like I said in the recruiting post, if there is more interest than openings, I\u2019ll be selecting players who have the most interesting ideas and seem like the best fit for the group. Let me know if you have any questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T13:27:24-07:00","id":1418698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418659#post1418659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - Just wanted to say that you\u2019re officially in, in case that wasn\u2019t clear. Looking forward to playing with you!<br /> <br /> I have also posted a recruitment post on the RPG.net forums. It seems like they are way more active. Hoping that draws some more interest.<br /> <br /> If I am somehow able to access RPG.net from work, I might suggest that we migrate there to play the game. I\u2019ll let you know if I suggest that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good, keep us updated.<br /> <br /> Do you need anything specific from me at the moment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T13:46:41-07:00","id":1418701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418698#post1418698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good, keep us updated.<br /> <br /> Do you need anything specific from me at the moment?</div> </div> </div> </div>All I need from you right now is to update your character sheet so it matches the changes you were thinking of making. If you want to change your background at all as well, consider what changes you want to make and enter those as well. If you can\u2019t make those yet until our other members have entered drafts of their sheets, that\u2019s ok too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T03:27:39-07:00","id":1418792,"title":"","content":"I have a concept in mind, though I might be a bit inactive due to college reasons. Nevertheless, I'll post my character here once I have them all lined up in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T03:40:29-07:00","id":1418794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418792#post1418792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a concept in mind, though I might be a bit inactive due to college reasons. Nevertheless, I'll post my character here once I have them all lined up in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi, thanks for expressing interest! Due to my own personal life and work obligations, the reality is that we probably aren\u2019t going to be moving at any breakneck speed. I would like people to be able to post on average ~2-3 times per week, or at least weekly during times when you\u2019re really busy. If you think that is unrealistic with your schedule, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T03:45:34-07:00","id":1418795,"title":"","content":"That's good actually, twice a week is more than fine. Especially since I've just gone past mid-semester tests. Finals are a few months out at least.<br /> <br /> Also, a question. Would it be alright for my character's brother to be a Changeling? At least one still in his Durance? I made a bunch of crossover characters for fun a while back and one of them is a brother sister pair of Mage and Changeling. Not including him would be okay, but might shift a few things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T03:58:04-07:00","id":1418799,"title":"","content":"I would say sure, pitch the character concept in a way that sounds the most fun for you. If you want the sibling NPC to be more influential or available to help you out, make sure that you take an appropriate number of dots in a relevant merit, such as Allies, Retainer, and/or True Friend.<br /> <br /> I will say that I know very little about Changeling so I\u2019ll need to read up on it more if you end up joining us. But I\u2019m all for crossovers when implemented thoughtfully and tastefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-18-2020, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T17:37:16-07:00","id":1418918,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1096_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1096\" data-vbnamecard=\"1096\">squidheadjax</a> - Just a reminder in case it was lost in the past few pages, but when you have time, please use the following format to pitch your character concept.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept: </b>Summarize your character concept in one phrase or short sentence.<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name:<br /> Shadow Name:<br /> Path:<br /> Order:<br /> Legacy:</b> (If you have one in mind)<br /> <b>Virtue:<br /> Vice: </b><br /> <b>Background:</b> Please provide a brief narrative summary of the character concept, taking into consideration how your background may fit into the greater Mysteries described in the introductory post in this thread. You can also include information about the character's Awakening.<br /> <br /> You can go back and edit your post later to add more details. At the very least, if you have an idea on which Path(s) most interests you, that would be helpful to know for the other players working on character creation. I'm not opposed to having multiple players of the same Path, but I do think the cabal and the game would benefit if most/all of the Paths were covered, or at least most of the Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T00:55:49-07:00","id":1418959,"title":"","content":"Obviously WIP, but wanted to get it out there before sleeping...<br /> <br /> <b>Concept: </b>Magical Private Eye<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name: </b>Sylia Swift, PI<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> TBD (Trying to come up with one that would sound like an obvious spy codename or something)<br /> <b>Path: </b>Acanthus<br /> <b>Order: </b>Free Council<br /> <b>Legacy::</b> undecided<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Generous<br /> <b>Vice: </b> Vindictive<br /> <b>Background:</b> Disillusioned former cop falls down the rabbit hole, comes out determined to use magic to help people even if she usually can't let them know that's what's going on.<br /> <br /> Fate 3 Time 2 Prime 1, most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T06:13:09-07:00","id":1418997,"title":"","content":"Here's mine, it's a bit pretentious, but bear with me here:<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b>: Heavy is the Head That Wears the Crown of Wisdom<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name: </b>Rene Fraser<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Fatewise<br /> <b>Path: </b>Acanthus<br /> <b>Order: </b>Mysterium<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Something with Mind Ruling<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Steadfast<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Curious<br /> <b>Background</b>: She never <i>asked </i>to be Awakened, to wake from the comforting dream and know true reality does to people. What it did to her brother. But she does See, she does Know. And she won't let something like that happen without her knowing ever again.<br /> <br /> She'll have something like Fate 3, Time 1, Prime 2 for the Universal Counterspell Attainment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:25:54-07:00","id":1419020,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe I should come up with a moros instead...<br /> <br /> (I do have the idea already, it was competing with the Acanthus. A thief who no lock will gainsay...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 10-19-2020, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T08:00:49-07:00","id":1419162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418959#post1418959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously WIP, but wanted to get it out there before sleeping...<br /> <br /> <b>Concept: </b>Magical Private Eye<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name: </b>Sylia Swift, PI<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> TBD (Trying to come up with one that would sound like an obvious spy codename or something)<br /> <b>Path: </b>Acanthus<br /> <b>Order: </b>Free Council<br /> <b>Legacy::</b> undecided<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Generous<br /> <b>Vice: </b> Vindictive<br /> <b>Background:</b> Disillusioned former cop falls down the rabbit hole, comes out determined to use magic to help people even if she usually can't let them know that's what's going on.<br /> <br /> Fate 3 Time 2 Prime 1, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat ideas as a start. Do you see this character as having a professional background in law enforcement before becoming a PI? Or is that a new role or idea since she Awakened? As you work on fleshing out the background more, please also think of ways her interests and background might tie in with the Chronicle-specific setting details in the introductory OOC and IC threads. <br /> <br /> Is Sylia the sympathetic name or did you mean Sylvia?<br /> <br /> You are welcome to keep her as Acanthus, but I\u2019m curious, what are your thoughts about Moros? Definitely would lend itself well to detective work with regards to investigating crime scenes or homicide cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T08:09:12-07:00","id":1419165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418997#post1418997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's mine, it's a bit pretentious, but bear with me here:<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b>: Heavy is the Head That Wears the Crown of Wisdom<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name: </b>Rene Fraser<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Fatewise<br /> <b>Path: </b>Acanthus<br /> <b>Order: </b>Mysterium<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Something with Mind Ruling<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Steadfast<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Curious<br /> <b>Background</b>: She never <i>asked </i>to be Awakened, to wake from the comforting dream and know true reality does to people. What it did to her brother. But she does See, she does Know. And she won't let something like that happen without her knowing ever again.<br /> <br /> She'll have something like Fate 3, Time 1, Prime 2 for the Universal Counterspell Attainment</div> </div> </div> </div>Not pretentious, but I am very interested to learn more about Rene\u2019s history before her Awakening. Your character concept emphasizes how she will view Supernal truths and the Fallen World now that she has Awakened, but who was she before? What was her relationship with her brother before their respective changes, and how is it now?<br /> <br /> Remember that the characters will all be newly awakened, essentially within the past few weeks. So I really want to see characters with really well defined backstories. Bonus points to relationships with characters I can use as NPCs to easily bring in plot hooks. <br /> <br /> Also, if you do have interest in a Legacy with Mind as the ruling arcanum, have you considered starting with at least Mind 1? Or was it intentional to start without that? Just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T09:44:32-07:00","id":1419180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419162#post1419162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neat ideas as a start. Do you see this character as having a professional background in law enforcement before becoming a PI? Or is that a new role or idea since she Awakened? As you work on fleshing out the background more, please also think of ways her interests and background might tie in with the Chronicle-specific setting details in the introductory OOC and IC threads.<br /> <br /> Is Sylia the sympathetic name or did you mean Sylvia?<br /> <br /> You are welcome to keep her as Acanthus, but I\u2019m curious, what are your thoughts about Moros? Definitely would lend itself well to detective work with regards to investigating crime scenes or homicide cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, ex-cop, and that would have been the correct spelling of the name. I'd mostly planned to lean heavily on Postcognition, Supernal Vision, Lucky Number and Shifting the Odds to do the magically supercharged detective stuff. Not sure about shifting that idea over to Moros... aside from being able to ask dead people what killed them in a variety of ways, it doesn't really have the sort of tools I would have wanted to use. Easily get into places and sneak around and stuff, but, eh. Been having a 'Lady Thief' idea that uses those tools in more fun ways for me. Not finished baking... not particularly sure about her Awakening, but I can probably tie it into the goings-on that have been going on.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b>: Enlightened 'Lady' Thief<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name</b>: Syrine Summers<br /> <b>Shadow Name</b>: TBD<br /> <b>Path</b>: Moros<br /> <b>Order</b>: Guardians<br /> <b>Legacy</b>: Any Forces-related Moros out there? <br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Generous<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Addictive<br /> Background: Relatively well-off suburban girl starts shoplifting and other petty thievery for the thrill of it, assuages her conscience by redistributing some of what she takes to people in need, starts getting enmeshed in more and more weirdness until she comes out the other side of the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> Matter 2, Forces 2, Death 2. Can get through any sort of mundane security, stay unseen, and wipe all traces of her passing, in addition to throwing a surprisingly mean right hook when she gets into trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T17:02:56-07:00","id":1419261,"title":"","content":"Hey, if you would rather play an Acanthus, please don\u2019t feel obligated to pitch a Moros character concept. I would rather not have more than 2 of the same Path but if the Acanthus character you pitched is who you are more interested in playing, then work on fleshing out that background more. <br /> <br /> Both characters seems really cool and could find ways to fit in with the CofD Chicago setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T21:36:40-07:00","id":1419293,"title":"","content":"I am in conundrum, because I am more attached to that idea than I thought I would be, but it's looking like there's going to be quite a bit more overlap than just Path there.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> , what sort of stuff were you actually planning on doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T21:56:21-07:00","id":1419297,"title":"","content":"Also trying to tag <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - any idea of at least which Path you might want to play? Assuming you're still interested in the game and able to play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T22:09:01-07:00","id":1419299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419165#post1419165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not pretentious, but I am very interested to learn more about Rene\u2019s history before her Awakening. Your character concept emphasizes how she will view Supernal truths and the Fallen World now that she has Awakened, but who was she before? What was her relationship with her brother before their respective changes, and how is it now?<br /> <br /> Remember that the characters will all be newly awakened, essentially within the past few weeks. So I really want to see characters with really well defined backstories. Bonus points to relationships with characters I can use as NPCs to easily bring in plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Also, if you do have interest in a Legacy with Mind as the ruling arcanum, have you considered starting with at least Mind 1? Or was it intentional to start without that? Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rene is a high school student/recent graduate; haven't figured exactly how old she is, but its somewhere around there and her brother Jack is around there as well. She met her brother quite recenntly, since because their parents decided to get married. They started off ambivalent to each other but got closer as time went on.<br /> <br /> Then Jack got kidnapped by the True Fae.<br /> <br /> Rene got suspicious of the Fetch as soon as he crossed the door. She became more distant, feeling like Jack turned into a stranger overnight. She watches him out of the corner of her eyes, trying to figure out why she felt like this.<br /> <br /> Eventually, one of two things happened: either Rene finally managed to see through the Mask somehow, or Jack managed to come home, changed by his Durance.<br /> <br /> This is what prompts her Awakening.<br /> <br /> If Jack is still in Arcadia, then she would be trying to find out as much as she can about the Fae and what the hell happened to the real Jack. If not, then Rene is struggling to help her brother out. She doesn't understand what happened to him, but damn it if she doesn't try.<br /> <br /> Not quite sure what would be more interesting, but I'm leaning towards Jack being out.<br /> <br /> As for Mind, I kinda wanted Prime 2 for the Counterspell though. Maybe I'll move a point from Fate...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T22:10:17-07:00","id":1419300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419293#post1419293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am in conundrum, because I am more attached to that idea than I thought I would be, but it's looking like there's going to be quite a bit more overlap than just Path there.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> , what sort of stuff were you actually planning on doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I have a few other concepts that I can change around to fit the mage theme instead of Rene if you really need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T23:25:36-07:00","id":1419312,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I'll sleep on it. You seem to have things already pretty fleshed out with the brother and stuff, and I'm mostly still in advanced brainstorming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T06:08:06-07:00","id":1419363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419297#post1419297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also trying to tag <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - any idea of at least which Path you might want to play? Assuming you're still interested in the game and able to play?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am, just very busy between work, drafts, and oral surgery. Moros or Thrysus would be the ways to go for me, depending on the rest if the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T14:47:54-07:00","id":1419447,"title":"","content":"I think I'm good with the Moros thief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T21:13:02-07:00","id":1419508,"title":"","content":"...actually I'm finding she works better as a Obrimos. Wish there was an Guardian Obrimos Matter Legacy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T23:48:37-07:00","id":1419522,"title":"","content":"<b>Concept</b>: Enlightened 'Lady' Thief<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name</b>: Michelle Bianchi<br /> <b>Shadow Name</b>: Caligniosa ('Callie' will do)<br /> <b>Path</b>: Obrimos<br /> <b>Order</b>: Guardians<br /> <b>Legacy</b>: (Want one, might have to make it... an Obrimos/Guardian/Matter legacy would probably metaphorically relate to the walls of the Labyrinth...)<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Generous<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Addictive<br /> <b>Arcana</b>: Forces 3, Matter 2, Prime 1<br /> <b>Background</b>: <br /> (bullet points for now because no way I'm finishing a paragraph writeup before I pass out)<ul><li>Grew up well-off in La Grange, but got into various forms of theft for the thrill of it and got repeatedly caught, largely because she tried to go Robin Hood and pass out stolen stuff she didn't need</li> <li>'Hung out with' (was dating, not that she could tell her parents) Libby Price, who was one of the La Grange kids who up and disappeared. She didn't come back.</li> <li>Went to college in Chicago, kept it up and now she wasn't a minor, so got kicked out but also hooked up with contacts through fences at pawn shops</li> <li>The crew she fell in with was <i>weird</i>, like she could swear Mickey Jim didn't even pick some of the locks he got through. And they usually hit up places after weird weather, for some reason. And the partying was <i>intense</i>. Something always kept feeling <i>wrong</i>, though, like there were always whispers and strange shadows around.</li> <li>On the night of the Deathstorm, Mickey Jim disappeared and the cops raided the flophole she was staying in, so she bolted out and into a maze of alleys she was sure weren't where she actually had been. (<b>I'm not clear on whether the Deathstorm was still just one week ago, or there's more time. If just one week I'll probably have to move that back.)</b> The idea is she was getting groomed by a Seer pillar, but didn't actually fit in, and the Guardians made a more persuasive offer after she Awakened.</li> <li>What she came to understand once she finally escaped the maze of convoluted reality and stolen the knowledge at its heart, was that there were a whole lot of things out of place in this world, and now she had the power to put them back. (Besides realizing I wanted Forces primray, this seems more like an Obrimos sort of revelation).</li> <li>Now she's back in La Grange after getting initiated in the Mysteries, so she can prove herself to the Guardians with fewer of the... <i>distractions</i> that Chicago provides.</li> <li>Her tasks from the Guardians, for now, mostly are concerned with retrieving dangerous magical items from the possession of Sleepers and less Wise mages.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 10-22-2020, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T06:59:31-07:00","id":1419574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419522#post1419522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Concept</b>: Enlightened 'Lady' Thief<br /> <b>Sympathetic Name</b>: Michelle Bianchi<br /> <b>Shadow Name</b>: Caligniosa ('Callie' will do)<br /> <b>Path</b>: Obrimos<br /> <b>Order</b>: Guardians<br /> <b>Legacy</b>: (Want one, might have to make it... an Obrimos/Guardian/Matter legacy would probably metaphorically relate to the walls of the Labyrinth...)<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Generous<br /> <b>Vice</b>: Addictive<br /> <b>Arcana</b>: Forces 3, Matter 2, Prime 1<br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> (bullet points for now because no way I'm finishing a paragraph writeup before I pass out)<ul><li>Grew up well-off in La Grange, but got into various forms of theft for the thrill of it and got repeatedly caught, largely because she tried to go Robin Hood and pass out stolen stuff she didn't need</li> <li>'Hung out with' (was dating, not that she could tell her parents) Libby Price, who was one of the La Grange kids who up and disappeared. She didn't come back.</li> <li>Went to college in Chicago, kept it up and now she wasn't a minor, so got kicked out but also hooked up with contacts through fences at pawn shops</li> <li>The crew she fell in with was <i>weird</i>, like she could swear Mickey Jim didn't even pick some of the locks he got through. And they usually hit up places after weird weather, for some reason. And the partying was <i>intense</i>. Something always kept feeling <i>wrong</i>, though, like there were always whispers and strange shadows around.</li> <li>On the night of the Deathstorm, Mickey Jim disappeared and the cops raided the flophole she was staying in, so she bolted out and into a maze of alleys she was sure weren't where she actually had been. (<b>I'm not clear on whether the Deathstorm was still just one week ago, or there's more time. If just one week I'll probably have to move that back.)</b> The idea is she was getting groomed by a Seer pillar, but didn't actually fit in, and the Guardians made a more persuasive offer after she Awakened.</li> <li>What she came to understand once she finally escaped the maze of convoluted reality and stolen the knowledge at its heart, was that there were a whole lot of things out of place in this world, and now she had the power to put them back. (Besides realizing I wanted Forces primray, this seems more like an Obrimos sort of revelation).</li> <li>Now she's back in La Grange after getting initiated in the Mysteries, so she can prove herself to the Guardians with fewer of the... <i>distractions</i> that Chicago provides.</li> <li>Her tasks from the Guardians, for now, mostly are concerned with retrieving dangerous magical items from the possession of Sleepers and less Wise mages.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I love this so much! I think this is an awesome character concept and will really help to bolster the group.<br /> <br /> I don't have many questions, and I imagine that you'll answer most of them as you further flesh out the character more.<br /> <br /> I'll look through old print sources to see if I can find an Obrimos Guardian Legacy with Matter ruling. If you have a particular desire for a Legacy that we can't find in other print sources, we can always create one together, and just say there are only a handful of members in the local Consilium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":".  Typos 10-22-2020, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T11:06:14-07:00","id":1419616,"title":"","content":"It looks like recruitment has been slower this time around than a few years ago, so I'm not really expecting many more people to hop on here to pitch a character concept. All of you have offered interesting ideas and seem excited and open about how to fit those characters into the current setting, so unless we suddenly have a bunch of more applicants come out of the woodwork, it looks like we have our party starting to form:<br /> <br /> 1. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923352#post923352\">Lynx</a>, Thyrsus animist/college student<br /> 2. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - TBD, Moros or Thyrsus<br /> 3. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417994#post1417994\">Morganna</a>, Mastigos soccer mom / con-woman<br /> 4. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418997#post1418997\">Fatewise</a>, Acanthus high school grad with supernatural family problems<br /> 5. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1096_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1096\" data-vbnamecard=\"1096\">squidheadjax</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419522#post1419522\">Caligniosa</a>, Obrimos enlightened 'lady' thief<br /> <br /> If we get any more submissions, I'll consider making room for one more person, otherwise we will stick with 5.<br /> <br /> Here is what I need from each of you to help us get the game started:<br /> <br /> <b>Everyone:</b><br /> Now that the party is starting to form, start thinking about ways your characters might have connections to the others (or not). Assume that the Deathstorm occurred ~3 weeks ago, and that you all Awakened after it, but all within that week (so you've all been Awakened for at least 2-3 weeks, but not more than that). It need not have occurrred on the exact day of the Deathstorm, perhaps within the next few days or even a week later, but all after it happened. In that time, you came across at least one mage who welcomed you into Awakened society, and you found your home within an Order. In terms of the cabal itself, I'm going to say that you all have met each other within the past week or so; various members of the Orders did some networking and your mentors encouraged you to join a cabal given your shared experience of Awakening shortly after the Deathstorm. You do not need to have even agreed upon a specific cabal name yet; that could be determined &quot;on screen&quot;, or you could discuss it in the OOC thread here. Regardless, you would have been presented at a recent Consilium meeting.<br /> <br /> I would also like each of you to identify a mentor. You can look through the NPC list in the IC thread, or you can create a new NPC mage who would be your main mentor. They would most likely be from your Order. Remember that if you do not take any dots in the Mentor merit (p. 106) that your mentor might have a pleasant relationship with you, but will not routinely offer free time or resources to help you out more actively. You do not need to flesh out the mentor's actual stats or character sheet unless you take dots in the Mentor merit, in which case feel free to include your suggestions on your character sheet.<br /> <br /> Please also note somewhere in your background or character sheet where your character resides, taking into consideration whether you have the Safe Place or Resources merits. If you take Safe Place or Sanctum, note whether that is also where you live, or if your sanctum is in a separate location than your home. If you have neither of these merits, you don't have to be homeless per se, but you probably live in a public place that is not great (e.g., cramped studio apartment in a not so great part of Chicago; living in the basement or garage of a friend or family member's house or apartment). Starting equpiment is equally limited to standard rules for the Resources merit.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a><br /> I need an updated draft of your character sheet with any changes to the character concept, background, Arcana, merits, etc. that you would like to make. Please let me know when you have finished making these edits so I can look at the sheet and help review it. Also let me know if you are just going to edit the original post with your character sheet (linked above), or make a new post altogether so I can update the link on the introductory posts for the OOC and IC threads.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a><br /> I probably need the most for you. Totally understand that RL stuff has been keeping you busy - trust me, I do get it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Do you have an idea of what a reasonable goal might be for when you'd be able to put up at least a character concept like the others, or a full draft of an actual character sheet? With regards to Path, I am still open to any Path that you might be interested in as long as the character concept is fleshed out. That being said, if you pick Moros, you will help complement the party really well because all of the other Paths are represented.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a><br /> You already have a great draft of a character background and character sheet. As you have time, work on adding other polish to the character sheet with details like a picture, additional ideas about how Morganna fits into the local Consilium, information requested of everyone above, and fleshing out the stats for your mentor. Let me know if you have any questions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a><br /> As your time allows, Please flesh out the character background more, decide how you want your relationship with Jack to appear, and then put in a draft of actual stats for your full character sheet. You have a great start to your character concept; work next on getting the character &quot;game ready.&quot; Also see if you can find a picture you like to represent your character.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1096_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1096\" data-vbnamecard=\"1096\">squidheadjax</a><br /> Finish working on the character background more as you have time, including a picture and other details as requested above, and then work on creating an actual character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-22-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T14:13:58-07:00","id":1419641,"title":"","content":"Ahh, Resources. Yeah, Michelle's pretty much getting by with whatever she can steal (...which is rather a lot, really). I could easily spend 5 or 10 more Merit dots if we had them!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19PBoyZPoV7yX9h5mENlCXNKgM28whvcX/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet is actually mostly done, in my google drive</a> (still subject to change as I complete it). I keep waffling on whether I really should keep professional training or put it in some other stuff. Realizing I should probably drop something for alternate identity. Hmm.","signatur