e('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Michelle's natural look:<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/236x/63/8b/6e/638b6e10365f9bf0155b95800e8def0a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The wig she wears as part of her Shadow Name:<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/44/0f/e8/440fe89cba1a45472667e39882de1206.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The hoodie she wears for 'blending in' as Caliginosa (without her wig, here):<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/236x/54/ce/97/54ce97233f1ac48766f4f89590187512.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> When she's more concerned with magical matters, and also wants to be able to conceal larger stuff she picks up without having to re-cast Invisibility:<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/e6/7a/30/e67a30e465dbfb7792845538c9f5233f.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b><u>Background</u></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Before Awakening, Michelle was a 'professional' thief, more or less. She didn't grow up poor or anything like that; it just came naturally to her. (Call her a kleptomaniac and you're asking for a grumpy spark from a nearby wall socket, but she'll grudgingly agree with you too.) Privilege and her parents' money kept her from catching worse than community service when she was caught while still a minor, but they never chose to confront whatever the actual problem was and just assumed their daughter would grow out of it, and at least she hadn't run off god-knows-where* like that Price girl she'd hung out with**. It's not like she was some hardened criminal, they figured, since one of the ways she kept getting caught was passing the goods on to someone she thought needed it more. (The other way was that she really couldn't lie with great skill.)<br /> <br /> *Libby Price is one of the recent La Grange children to vanish without a trace, and one of those who (as of yet) haven\u2019t come back.<br /> **Dated, actually, not that she felt she could tell her parents.<br /> <br /> Of course she didn't grow out of it, and when she went into Chicago for university she was soon getting into the same habits, and then quickly figured out which pawn shops nearby were truly in the business of fencing. Accordingly, she got the attention of the locals - both those of the criminal persuasion and the police (to the extent that didn\u2019t overlap) - which is why she got kicked out of uni before ever deciding a major. Michelle couldn\u2019t really just <i>go home</i> at that point, not to the disapproval <i>at best</i> that would await her. She managed to keep up enough \u2018income\u2019 to pay for a shitty hotel room with cash week-to-week, as long as she only ate what she could get away with shoplifting. Which\u2026 wasn\u2019t really tenable. A pawn shop owner knew a guy who knew a guy and they were looking for some people. She was afraid it was going to be the Mafia or something, but she needed work. As it turned out, the Mafia would have been a lot less <i>weird</i>.<br /> Mickey Jim\u2019s* crew lived large, to an extent that positively mystified Michelle, especially with how few actual jobs they pulled. And she was never entirely sure if the worship toward the golden bull statue in the center of their \u2018hideout\u2019 was real or just debauchedly ironic. Or if that girl she spent a night with really had darkly prismatic wings, or if that was just the Ecstasy. And they only ever ran jobs right after whatever freaky weather Chicago sometimes had. It all seemed strangely normal and yet surreal at the time. She also didn\u2019t get why most of the crew just seemed to be desperate hangers-on, passing money up from whatever small jobs they did and getting used for crappy, risky roles like lookouts, couriers, and such in exchange for basking in the revelry while she was brought into the core who seemed to actually do things.** And the jobs were\u2026 weird. Mickey Jim didn\u2019t even seem to pick the locks he opened some of the time, and seemed to always know what the keycodes and combinations were.. Ivy could just slip her way through any security with perfect timing. Benny talked to security guards, mob enforcers and police who were getting ready to break knees to shoot like they were old friends. Mercy had these nurses\u2026 well they gave the impression of being nurses anyway, sort of\u2026 to patch people up while she just waited. And despite being ostensibly criminals, they carried themselves like they ruled the world.<br /> <br /> *Michelle never figured out how he got that moniker, which is probably for the best.<br /> **In retrospect, she figures her Awakening was already starting, and the Pylon was trying to guide it and groom her.<br /> Maybe if she\u2019d had more time to be drawn in, she would have ended up staying\u2026 but the Deathstorm happened. Mickey Jim and Benny disappeared, Mercy\u2019s nurses went berserk, and Ivy apparently knew in advance to make herself scarce. Michelle felt something like a wall coming down or a rubber band snapping, and then the police were raiding the hideout. In a panic, she escaped through a door that she didn\u2019t remember, into\u2026 nowhere.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>Awakening</i> - A maze of alleys, unlike any actual place in Chicago. Doors, all locked doors. A maze\u2026 a labyrinth. And all she really had with her were her lockpicks. But\u2026 doors. She could do doors. With lockpicks. But sometimes she\u2019d pick a door, and just come out in a mirror of the alleys she was just in. Sometimes she\u2019d end up\u2026 somewhere else. Bright and searing, like her mother\u2019s disapproval. Or a swirling haze of heat like she\u2019d felt when she first kissed Libby. Or the cold, clammy fear of knowing she\u2019d been caught again.<br /> Sometimes they opened somewhere she\u2019d been in before. The museum where that statue was waiting. It shouldn\u2019t have been there, but it shouldn\u2019t have been where they took it, either. Michelle knew that now. The doorways curled back on themselves, halls twisting and churning to bring her back to that storage room where the brass thing had screamed as Mercy touched it. But that\u2019s not what happened. Not what she remembered. Mercy hadn\u2019t even been\u2026 she hadn\u2019t\u2026 she had. The memories overlapped, what her mind insisted happened but she knew wasn\u2019t true, and what her mind insisted was impossible but it was burned into the world, breaking through to her awareness like cracks forming in a pipe about to burst. More impossible memories, more wrongness, more sin against the world that could and should be but was held in barbed chains of iniquity\u2026<br /> She curled up against one of those treacherous doorways, crying and screaming. \u201cI don\u2019t want this! I\u2019m not this! I\u2019m not-\u201d<br /> And she fell back through the open door, into the wide open park, in the middle of the day. Lincoln Park? Or somewhere else? She wasn\u2019t sure. There\u2019d been some big charity thing for\u2026 kids with cancer or whatever. She\u2019d palmed a roll of 20s into the collection box. It had felt\u2026 good. Oh. Right. This was the day it rained frogs. Lots of screaming children. She\u2019d been told to catch as many frogs as she could. Which\u2026 made no sense at all. But it was what it was. All she\u2019d gotten was a pile of squirming, broken bodies. No, this time one of the frogs was fat, far too fat, and the poor thing\u2019s skin split to disgorge a pearl. It\u2019s murky, grey, not like a pearl should be. The world is grey, foggy, twilight, but with more and more light growing blinding. All the park is gone now, except\u2026 is that a statue plinth? It\u2019s calling to her. Something\u2026 She feels the urge to scratch her name into it, with her lockpicks. It\u2019s a name that\u2019s not her name, something cloudy, hard to see.<br /> And then, she woke up, and there was a man standing over her. Immaculately dressed, especially in comparison to her grubby, torn hoodie. \u201cA pleasure to meet you. My name is Valentine.\u201d<br /> It wasn\u2019t hard to recruit her into the Guardians, particularly in the role of retrieving things from people that shouldn\u2019t have them. Like the crew she\u2019d been running with before. She could set all the wrongness\u2026 right.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>Awakened</i> - [insert history since Awakening]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Daily Life</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Michelle is back in La Grange\u2026 or rather, Candice Fergusson is. She\u2019s renting a small basement apartment on Kensington Street, paid in cash, to a little old lady who doesn\u2019t particularly care what sort of callers she has as long as they\u2019re not loud. As a newly minted Guardian, this posting back home is more or less a chance to prove herself worthy of actual mentorship, sweeping up after the issues and Supernal debris left by the Lie Zones. With not much in the way of logistical support for now, she\u2019s having to steal to pay for the apartment (she could try to get a lower-stakes job with her fake ID, but that\u2019d still be a risk). Stealing from Sleepers isn\u2019t particularly hard, though safely laundering stolen items into cash is a little harder and rate-limiting. It helps that she can screw with the serial numbers and other ways to track what she steals, but overdoing it as a one-woman crime wave will cut off options.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Modus Operandi</b></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Magical thief Caliginosa is a persona pretty thoroughly divorced from her old life, as well as her fake Sleeper identity. The main costume elements are a grey hooded garment - either a hoodie, to look more normal, or a cloak, to have better options to conceal big stuff - and a frosted silver wig, a theme of shadowy grey overall. She can draw on it for pretty much anything sneaky or spooky; she\u2019s not going to be standing in the middle of town and tossing fireballs around Harry Dresden style as long as she has a choice, anyway. Her Dedicated Tool is her lockpick set - sometimes waving a pick like a magic wand, or often lightly scratching symbols into something. With those and High Speech at her disposal, she doesn\u2019t dive deeply into other tools much, though she keeps a pocket mirror and knives with her at all times.<br /> <br /> As she\u2019s living entirely on stolen cash, disposable income isn\u2019t really a thing right now. She has two prepaid phones (one for the Cabal and the Guardians, one for outside business so she can burn it if need be), her lockpicks, a few knives, and that\u2019s basically it.<br /> <br /> While Michelle\u2019s not a warrior, she can defend herself. She first learned some fighting from dealing with her two brothers, but her parents insisted she take self-defense classes. The stripmall dojo they picked out taught Krav Maga. It\u2019s good for close-in situations and fighting dirty to escape, at least. Between her kinetic energy rote and her preference to stay invisible and silent when she expects a fight, she can supercharge that into a disabling blow.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Character links</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>LGBT:</b> Michelle is gay, and her parents' attitude towards that is one of the several reasons she won't be revealing herself to her family again any time soon.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>FAMILY:</b> ...unless something threatens her family, especially her little brother George or her Pop-pop and Nan who also live nearby.</span></li> <li><b><b>CRIME:</b></b> She's working on a rep in the Sleeper criminal world... maybe she can even eventually found a mystery cult that's, like, the good version of the Pylon that tried to take her in.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Individual characters (TBD):</b></span></span><ul><li><i>Lynx</i>: she probably thinks 'loud and judgy', which is less than fair and will probably change.</li> <li><i>Eurydice's Heir</i>: she's not a fan of being confrontational about things... but she's going to want to learn Death magic (great for covering mundane evidence!), so likely to try and be ingratiating.</li> <li><i>Fatewise</i>: perceptive enough to make Callie a little instinctively anxious. She might also think Rene is leaning into the 'witch' thing a little too dramatically, but that's very pot-and-kettle.</li> <li><i>Morganna</i>: What Callie thinks of her will partly depend on how much of her background she reveals. Respect for her as an ex-con, and also as a thief for actually being successful in a MLM. Callie is probably also an embarassingly easy mark where Morganna is concerned, especially with those Striking Looks (btw, in 2e it's only 1 dot per level, so she'd have level 2).</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Status</b></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Health:<