2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Praxes</b></u></span></span><ul><li>Shifting the Odds (Fate \u25cf\u25cf)</li> <li>Supernal Vision (Prime \u25cf)</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b><u>Attainments</u></b></span></span><ul><li>Counterspell (Fate, Mind, Prime, Time \u25cf)</li> <li>Conditional Duration (Fate \u25cf\u25cf)</li> <li>Targeted Summoning (Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b><u>Rotes</u></b></span></span><ul><li>&lt;Exceptional Luck (Fate \u25cf\u25cf, Occult)&gt;</li> <li>&lt;Pierce Deception (Prime \u25cf, Occult)&gt;</li> <li>&lt;Divination (Time \u25cf, Investigation)&gt;</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b><u>Nimbus</u></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>Long-Term</i> - Great bouts of luck, both good and bad, become more common and more intense. Rather than just finding a penny or a dollar on the ground, people find entire wallets without identification in them. Rather than just tripping, people would trip down several flights of stairs. Misfortune rarely results in actual death, but injuries are fair game.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>Immediate</i> - Random events appear to fall into place at just the right moment to further or distrupt Rene's actions. Golden strings of light can casionally be seen criscrossing the space around her, guiding things to their fate.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>Signature</i> - Golden strings that surround the subject, pulling them and being pulled in turn.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>Tilt</i> \u2013 Those affected by Rene's Nimbus can somewhat see the golden strings that occasionally surrounds her. This grants +1 to Wits, +1 to Investigation, and 8-Again to Investigation. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Aspirations</b></u></span></span><ul><li>Get to know fellow Cabal members. (Short)</li> <li>Research fellow Cabal members. Just in case. (Short)</li> <li>Subvert other's expectations of youurself. (Long)</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Obsessions</b></u></span></span><ul><li>Figure out what's going on with your brother.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Equipment</b></u></span></span><ul><li>A smartphone.</li> <li>A pair of knitting needles.</li> <li>A crystal ball she bought upon finding out she's some sort of witch.</li> <li>A silver goblet her father had lying around. Possibly a family heirloom.</li> <li>A crystalline rodher Mentor gave to her. More than likely a failed experiment of some kind he's putting to use.</li> <li>A deck of tarot cards.</li> <li>Clothes. Most notably a short cloak she used to use as a base for her haloween costumes.</li> <li>Likes to improvise with whatever she could get her hands on.</li> <li>Trying to get her hands on perfected materials, like Lunargent.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Yantras &amp; Tools</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Needles (Path tool): Subtle spells, spells singling out a specific target.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Silver Goblet (Path Tool): Perception and divination magic, 'drinking from the well of knowledge'. Also used for spells that affect the self.</span></li> <li>Tarot Deck (-):</li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Crystal Rod (Dedicated): Spells that command and rule, and spells that directly manipulate the world.</span></li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Details</b></span></span></span></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>General</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Age/Birthday:</b> 19; January 3rd</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Gender:</b> Female</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Height:</b> 5' 3&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Build:</b> Average</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Occupation:</b> Highschool Graduate</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Ethnicity:</b> -</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Nationality:</b> American</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Hair Colour:</b> Brown</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Eye Colour:</b> Gold</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Sexuality:</b> -<br /> <br /> <b><u>Pictures</u></b>:</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">None Yet</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b><u>Background</u></b></span></span><br /> <br /> She's a girl who was born in Chicago and moved to La Grange. Her father raised her and she never knew her mother. Dear old dad always changes the subject or goes silent when the topic inevitably rolls around, and his relatives either don't know or are silent as well. She <i>has</i> confirmed he's her biological dad at least.<br /> <br /> She has a bit of a thing of being a maelstrom of luck. Her luck Nimbus essentially being something that had followed her all through her life, and getting stronger after she Awakened. She got treated as cursed by her classmates in middle school and eventually some of the parents as well. She and her dad moved to La Grange to get away from it all.<br /> <br /> Rene has a bit of an interest in superstitions involving luck and fate, particularly Tarot cards, which I'll probably make as one of her Path Tools somehow. While she does hide the whole 'probably cursed' thing from her friends, she has more or less learned to live with it. After a while of living with strange luck, you learn to minimize the bad sides and exploit the good sides.<br /> <br /> Jack lived a similar life, having been born and raised in La Grange. His dad died a while back and his mother has been trying to raise her son alone for years. He's a bit abrasive and blunt, but tends to cut to the heart of issues to lay it bare. Sometimes this solves things, other times it just makes it more obvious to everyone watching. Once Jack makes a promise he'ss go through hell and high water to keep it.<br /> <br /> Rene's dad and Jack's mom met in La Grange and got engaged. They actually still have two homes since one of them hasn't gotten sold yet, but the two families have started moving in with one another.<br /> <br /> Rene and Jack were cold to each other at first, but eventually Jack reached out since he realizes his problem is more with his mom getting married than with Rene. They promise to try getting closer. That night, Jack gets replaced by the Fetch.<br /> <br /> Jack got cold again and Rene sort of accepts that Jack doesn't actually want anything to do with her, but some part of her knows this isn't the case. During the Deathstorm, things got to ahead in her Mystery Play.<br /> <br /> She's confronted with the fact that she's trying to protect herself with flimsy lies even when she <i>knows</i> something's wrong with Jack. She Awakens and she resolves to find out whats going<br /> <br /> She finds out about the Pentacle Orders and joins the Mystagogues since they have the most information. Her mentor is [Insert Someone Here]<br /> <br /> Jack is captured by the True Fae and has been forced into the role of the 'Hero' of the Fae's story. Each time, he would be clad in armor of resolve and armed with a sword called hope. He would scale up the thousand levels of the Fae's tower, avoiding traps and fighting its minions.<br /> <br /> At the top, he would confront the Fae in the form of a great beast, a nightmarish Manticore invincible to normal arms. They would fight and at the end, Jack would trust the sword through the beast's chest.<br /> <br /> Only to see the blade shatter.<br /> <br /> The monster would then hurl Jack off of the Tower, falling a thousand levels down to the jagged rocks beneath. He would survive, but his armor would break during the fall.<br /> <br /> The servants of the Fae at the bottom would reforge his resolve and hope into a set of armor and weapons and force him up the Tower once more.<br /> <br /> And so the cycle continues.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Daily Life</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Investigating Jack and Researching the Supernal</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Modus Operandi</b></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Less of an MO and more of a fact of her existence. A storm of coincidences and lucky breaks, far too </span>numerous to be natural.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Character links</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>DESTINY:</b> Rene is a locus of fate, often getting tangled up in others problems and stories. Chances are, she's previously met the important people she will encounter and walked away from it with some insight as to their character. Destiny's idea of foreshadowing things to her. This also sometimes manifests as literal foreshadowing, ominous events appearing around her as a portent of things to come.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>FAMILY:</b> </span>Rene's brother, Jack, is currently living out his Durance in Arcadia, battling the shapeshifting True Fae that keeps him hostage. The Tragic Hero to the Fae's Villain. Jack's Fetch has only recently appeared, though both Rene and Jack's mother has begun suspecting something is wrong. They've yet to figure out what however. Moving on, Rene's father, Harold Fraser, has recently married Dr. Sylvia Flores, Jack's Mother, and they all currently live in the Fraser's home. Dr. Flores has opted to not change her name so as to not confuse her patients, and Mr. Fraser agreed to it on the grounds of less paperwork they have to waste their time on. Harold and Slyvia do care deeply about their children, biological or otherwise, but they do have a problem in properly understanding them. A product of their busy schedules. It's honestly a miracle they found time to date and get married as it is.</li> <li><b>LITERATURE</b><b>:</b> Rene quite loves books and so does her luck. She loves reading and learning about new things, and is often found seeking out new books in shops and libraries, having quickly read through her last batch. Her luck often helps her with this, as she often quickly finds just the book with the information she needs, even if she didn't know she would need it yet.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Individual characters (TBD):</b></span></span><ul><li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - <b>LYNX</b>: He brings to mind an older version of her brother, which firmly places him in the category of annoying. She does make an effort to be friendly to him, however. Something of a mix between extending her promise to try to get along with her brother and solidarity for being in the same Order.</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - <b>EURYDICE'S HEIR</b>: Spirits and ghosts are simply another part of Fatewise's occult interests, and she would be glad to take notes from her cabalmate's experiments. Considering her lack of Spirit or Death Sight, she might have trouble interpreting his ramblings at first, but Fatewise is nothing if not meticulous and observant.</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - <b>MORGANNA</b>: Considering her Shadow Name, Rene may find her of interest once she learns more of Fetches and the Fae.</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1096_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1096\" data-vbnamecard=\"1096\">squidheadjax</a> - <b>CALIGNIGOSA</b>: Fatewise doesn't like how sneaky Callie is, even with her being able to spot the Mastigos better than most. It makes her concerned about what else Callie does, unseen by the others.</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Status</b></span></span></span></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Health:</b> 0000000</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Willpower:</b> 6/6</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Mana:</b> 11/11</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Wisdom:</b> 7</span></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Experience Log</b></span></span></span></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Beats:</b> 0/5</span><br /> <b>Arcane Beats:</b> 0/5<br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Experience (Unspent/Total):</b> 0/0</span><br /> <b>Arcane Experience (Unspent/Total):</b> 0/0<br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>Dots Purchased - XP Cost</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">[insert dots purchased]</span></li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 12-29-2020, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T06:16:07-07:00","id":1421149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1420979#post1420979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1: I'll stick with Raven, just to keep it simple. Reading up on her demeanour, it seems right for Lynx.<br /> <br /> 2: With Resources 3, I imagine Lynx has a small but comfortable basement apartment in the suburbs. Private owner, perhaps? That could be a plot point. Or hindrance. Or werewolf. Who knows. Maybe 10-20 minutes away from the university by foot? In the north-west, not too far away from the Bemis Woods, since the place has importance to Lynx, and coincidences are a thing. <br /> <br /> Tell me if you need more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, Raven it is! I think it will be cool to flesh out her character more.<br /> <br /> So with 3 Resources and your background, I feel like Lynx\u2019s parents are helping to pay for his rent for a nice 1-2 bedroom apartment that probably costs in the $900-1,100 range. It could be in a small apartment complex and I could introduce NPCs from there, either the landlord or another tenant.<br /> <br /> In the old background, several of the characters were students or instructors at the University of Chicago and attended classes downtown. Since no one else in this group is a college student (at least from what I\u2019ve seen), we could pick a college closer to the suburbs. <br /> <br /> There actually aren\u2019t any community colleges or full 4-year colleges or universities in La Grange. I actually might suggest Elmhurst College (renamed to Elmhurst University in 2020). It is only a 10-15 minute drive or train ride away from La Grange, just northwest of La Grange and only a few minutes away from the northwest corner of the woods and forest. The college is a private liberal arts college with a Christian affiliation. Coincidentally, the particular affiliation is with a liberal denomination that is pro-LGBT+ and openly affirms same-sex marriage and gay pastors. I think with Lynx\u2019s background and his yearning for a deeper spiritual connection around the time of his Awakening, this might make the college a good fit for him. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - The character sheet is looking great. Only two corrections I see. First, the updated/errata for MtAw 2E says you start with only 3 rotes, not 6 dots of rotes. Please review your rote selection. Also, you get a number of bonuses to the Nimbus tilt equal to half of your Gnosis rounded up, so only one bonus at Gnosis 2. So you could take Wits +1, or Investigation +1 and 8-again, but not both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 10-31-2020, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T07:15:34-07:00","id":1421155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421149#post1421149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - The character sheet is looking great. Only two corrections I see. First, the updated/errata for MtAw 2E says you start with only 3 rotes, not 6 dots of rotes. Please review your rote selection. Also, you get a number of bonuses to the Nimbus tilt equal to half of your Gnosis rounded up, so only one bonus at Gnosis 2. So you could take Wits +1, or Investigation +1 and 8-again, but not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I didn't know about that errata. I guess I'll drop a few of them then.<br /> <br /> Rene actually has Potent Nimbus, which adds +2 to her Gnosis for determining her Nimbus Tilt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T07:23:01-07:00","id":1421158,"title":"","content":"Oh, missed that! My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T00:24:23-07:00","id":1421267,"title":"","content":"So have we all been introduced and running around together already, or are we meeting in-game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T04:35:45-08:00","id":1421279,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - I forgot to say this yesterday, but I saw that your dedicated tool is a crystal staff. Do you think you might want to make that a crystal rod or something instead? Something that is slightly easier to conceal or take with you, since you will be using it a lot. I think a rod still has the same semiotics so it\u2019s just an idea. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421267#post1421267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So have we all been introduced and running around together already, or are we meeting in-game?</div> </div> </div> </div>You all will have met briefly. The Diamond Orders and your mentors collaborated to help you find a cabal due to your auspicious Awakening timing. You were introduced at a Consilium meeting a few days ago, in game time.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s just move up to 2020 and say the Deathstorm occurred on September 8, 2020. You all awakened sometime that week. You were introduced to a full Consilium and each other on Friday, October 2. We can start our game on Saturday, October 3. You could have spent that Friday talking with each other, establishing ideas for your cabal, and initial talking about mutual goals.<br /> <br /> Also, there will be no pandemic going on and there will be a fictional President, if that becomes relevant. I want to avoid politics and admittedly could use an escape from current events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-01-2020, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T09:52:52-08:00","id":1421306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421149#post1421149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, Raven it is! I think it will be cool to flesh out her character more.<br /> <br /> So with 3 Resources and your background, I feel like Lynx\u2019s parents are helping to pay for his rent for a nice 1-2 bedroom apartment that probably costs in the $900-1,100 range. It could be in a small apartment complex and I could introduce NPCs from there, either the landlord or another tenant.<br /> <br /> In the old background, several of the characters were students or instructors at the University of Chicago and attended classes downtown. Since no one else in this group is a college student (at least from what I\u2019ve seen), we could pick a college closer to the suburbs.<br /> <br /> There actually aren\u2019t any community colleges or full 4-year colleges or universities in La Grange. I actually might suggest Elmhurst College (renamed to Elmhurst University in 2020). It is only a 10-15 minute drive or train ride away from La Grange, just northwest of La Grange and only a few minutes away from the northwest corner of the woods and forest. The college is a private liberal arts college with a Christian affiliation. Coincidentally, the particular affiliation is with a liberal denomination that is pro-LGBT+ and openly affirms same-sex marriage and gay pastors. I think with Lynx\u2019s background and his yearning for a deeper spiritual connection around the time of his Awakening, this might make the college a good fit for him. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. It sounds like an interesting direction to go re: spirituality and such. I don't know how much I necessarily want to lean into the Christian part of it, but it does seem like a good fit logistically, and I do want to challenge myself in terms of roleplay. I'm in favour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421149#post1421149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the updated/errata for MtAw 2E says you start with only 3 rotes, not 6 dots of rotes. Please review your rote selection. Also, you get a number of bonuses to the Nimbus tilt equal to half of your Gnosis rounded up, so only one bonus at Gnosis 2. So you could take Wits +1, or Investigation +1 and 8-again, but not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so I'm sure, we get 3 rotes, regardless of dots? So I could theoretically start with three Life 3 rotes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T10:23:02-08:00","id":1421309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421306#post1421306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this. It sounds like an interesting direction to go re: spirituality and such. I don't know how much I necessarily want to lean into the Christian part of it, but it does seem like a good fit logistically, and I do want to challenge myself in terms of roleplay. I'm in favour.</div> </div> </div> </div>We definitely don't have to explore the Christian part much or at all. I just figured of the real colleges/universities within a 20-mile radius, this is probably the closest to what Lynx would be interested in given the backstory you created. If you don't like it, we could also create a fictional university in La Grange or nearby that fits better with what you are interested in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just so I'm sure, we get 3 rotes, regardless of dots? So I could theoretically start with three Life 3 rotes? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you could. That's what the Mage 2E errata says. If you haven't obtained an updated copy of the core book with the errata, you can find them <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9UUZ4UjZJdEhIM2c/view\" target=\"_blank\">linked here.</a><br /> <br /> Quoting the relevant section:<br /> &quot;Instead of being dot-rated as they were in first edition in character creation, given that their Experiences cost after chargen is flat, we have changed &quot;six dots of rotes&quot; in character creation to &quot;three rotes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T10:33:19-08:00","id":1421311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421309#post1421309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We definitely don't have to explore the Christian part much or at all. I just figured of the real colleges/universities within a 20-mile radius, this is probably the closest to what Lynx would be interested in given the backstory you created. If you don't like it, we could also create a fictional university in La Grange or nearby that fits better with what you are interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elmhurst will work out just fine, I think. No need to overcomplicate things when you've already found a good and thoughtful answer. I like it, and am excited to see what it'll end up being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T10:36:44-08:00","id":1421313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421279#post1421279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You all will have met briefly. The Diamond Orders and your mentors collaborated to help you find a cabal due to your auspicious Awakening timing. You were introduced at a Consilium meeting a few days ago, in game time.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s just move up to 2020 and say the Deathstorm occurred on September 8, 2020. You all awakened sometime that week. You were introduced to a full Consilium and each other on Friday, October 2. We can start our game on Saturday, October 3. You could have spent that Friday talking with each other, establishing ideas for your cabal, and initial talking about mutual goals.<br /> <br /> Also, there will be no pandemic going on and there will be a fictional President, if that becomes relevant. I want to avoid politics and admittedly could use an escape from current events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.<br /> <br /> I should probably figure out what Callie thinks of the others...<br /> <br /> Lynx: she probably thinks 'loud and judgy', which is less than fair and will probably change.<br /> <br /> Eurydice's Heir: she's not a fan of being confrontational about things... but she's going to want to learn Death magic (great for covering mundane evidence!), so likely to try and be ingratiating.<br /> <br /> Fatewise: perceptive enough to make Callie a little instinctively anxious. She might also think Rene is leaning into the 'witch' thing a little too dramatically, but that's very pot-and-kettle.<br /> <br /> Morganna: What Callie thinks of her will partly depend on how much of her background she reveals. Respect for her as an ex-con, and also as a thief for actually being successful in a MLM. Callie is probably also an embarassingly easy mark where Morganna is concerned, especially with those Striking Looks (btw, in 2e it's only 1 dot per level, so she'd have level 2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 11-01-2020, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T21:03:35-08:00","id":1421557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418659#post1418659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - Just wanted to say that you\u2019re officially in, in case that wasn\u2019t clear. Looking forward to playing with you!<br /> <br /> I have also posted a recruitment post on the RPG.net forums. It seems like they are way more active. Hoping that draws some more interest.<br /> <br /> If I am somehow able to access RPG.net from work, I might suggest that we migrate there to play the game. I\u2019ll let you know if I suggest that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. Just chiming in that I'm alive and here. Had some family health issues over the last week and the election is doing nothing to make me feel better about the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T21:23:22-08:00","id":1421558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418959#post1418959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously WIP, but wanted to get it out there before sleeping...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> TBD (Trying to come up with one that would sound like an obvious spy codename or something)<br /> <br /> <br /> Fate 3 Time 2 Prime 1, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Samantha Spade (Sam Spade)?<br /> Bond, Jane Bond<br /> Mata Hari<br /> Agent P<br /> Mycroft<br /> Q","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T22:09:44-08:00","id":1421560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> (1) Aspirations/Obsession: Can you clarify what you mean by \u201cbe less scared\u201d? Or perhaps rephrase this a bit? Your other aspirations/Obsession are great.<br /> </div> </div> </div>She wants to do something to feel more in control of the situation. She's not a banisher but the things that go bump in the night are real. She just purchased (semi-legally) a gun and body armor. This is a person that's still freaked out about awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (2) Background: You made a few posts after I asked follow-up questions with information about your background and Hannah pre- and post-Awakening. Please consolidate the extra information into one post, as well as the rest of the requested information listed here. </div> </div> </div>I'll try to put everything into a nicely formatted character sheet in the morning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (3) Photo: Please post a link to a photo or photos that represent how you view your character. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcRLxUUl5EGJOvngQe70mhDKMDts4puf_tAhQg&amp;usqp=CAU\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcSScVG04Y9ifH0hbL5UYGjTr6ssWp5wIz9rGw&amp;usqp=CAU\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (4) Mentor: Please decide on which existing NPC you'd like to be your Order mentor, or give me a general, brief character concept of a new NPC and I will start to flesh them out myself. If you have questions about an NPC posted on the &quot;List of Supporting Characters&quot; section on the IC thread, let me know. </div> </div> </div>I had some ideas for Vivian. Actually I just saw a bit of Season 6 of the old Buffy The Vampire Slayer TV series. The Willow character does a good job of pulling off a high gnosis / low wisdom mage. I wonder if that might be an idea: somebody who is actually nice and has real friends within the concillium and order but has a gnosis of at least 6, a wisdom of 4, is the master of at least one art and fundamentally doesn't see the world the same way regular people do any more. (I'm thinking of one scene where Willow offers to search a dance floor quickly by shunting everyone that doesn't match the age/gender she is looking for into an alternative dimension for a couple of seconds). Let me play with this concept a bit and I'll message you a draft.<br /> <br /> [quote]<br /> (5) Residence: I need a general description of what kind of house/apartment/shelter you live in and where it is generally located.<br /> [quote]<br /> <br /> Two bedroom apartment in a nice but not pircey complex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (6) Character and setting connections: Please come up with at least 3 general links to the setting and/or other characters. Look to Lynx or Caliginosa's character sheet for examples. </div> </div> </div>1. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=923352#post923352\">Lynx</a>, Thyrsus animist/college student. <br /> - Wants to learn Spirit so that she manifest Goetia. Lynx might be able to help.<br /> <br /> 2. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - TBD, Moros or Thyrsus<br /> - If allowable, was one of the cops that investigated the student deaths/disappearances. Wants to talk to him now that he's no longer working for the PD. <br /> <br /> 3. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417994#post1417994\">Morganna</a>, Mastigos soccer mom / con-woman<br /> <br /> 4. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1418997#post1418997\">Fatewise</a>, Acanthus high school grad with supernatural family problems<br /> - Wants to talk to her about the student deaths.<br /> <br /> 5. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1096_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1096\" data-vbnamecard=\"1096\">squidheadjax</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419522#post1419522\">Caligniosa</a>, Obrimos enlightened 'lady' thief<br /> - Professional interest. Has heard rumors. Wonders if she can help in a con.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","user":"DrSteve","date":". 11-03-2020, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T11:55:35-08:00","id":1421658,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1096_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1096\" data-vbnamecard=\"1096\">squidheadjax</a> both start with a Beat for completing their characters in full before yesterday morning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421558#post1421558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Samantha Spade (Sam Spade)?<br /> Bond, Jane Bond<br /> Mata Hari<br /> Agent P<br /> Mycroft<br /> Q</div> </div> </div> </div>Squidheadjax ended up going with the name <b>Caliginosa</b>. I think you were responding to an older message. I have been updating the very first post of the OOC and IC threads as you all have updated or finished your character sheets, so please reference that anytime you need to find the character sheets for the rest of the players. (This is why I'm asking everyone to keep a copy of their current character sheet somewhere in the OOC thread for me to reference.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1421560#post1421560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She wants to do something to feel more in control of the situation. She's not a banisher but the things that go bump in the night are real. She just purchased (semi-legally) a gun and body armor. This is a person that's still freaked out about awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that makes sense. So instead of &quot;be less scared&quot;, let's go with the short-term aspiration <b>&quot;do something to feel more in control of a scary situation.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll try to put everything into a nicely formatted character sheet in the morning. </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I have been linking to your original post with your stats, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1417994#post1417994\">post #1129</a> of this thread from 10/13/20. If you could, please go back and edit that post and consolidate all of your information there, including the photos, summary of her relationship with the others, etc. Let me know if you have any questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had some ideas for Vivian. Actually I just saw a bit of Season 6 of the old Buffy The Vampire Slayer TV series. The Willow character does a good job of pulling off a high gnosis / low wisdom mage. I wonder if that might be an idea: somebody who is actually nice and has real friends within the concillium and order but has a gnosis of at least 6, a wisdom of 4, is the master of at least one art and fundamentally doesn't see the world the same way regular people do any more. (I'm thinking of one scene where Willow offers to search a dance floor quickly by shunting everyone that doesn't match the age/gender she is looking for into an alternative dimension for a couple of seconds). Let me play with this concept a bit and I'll message you a draft. </div> </div> </div>I like the idea, but not the level of power. With only 1 dot in the Mentor merit, which is only available because of the Mystery Cult Initiation merit, the mentor by default would only be a little stronger than you. In practice, the other main NPCs who are serving as mentors will have Gnosis 3-4 and generally be first-degree adepts or have multiple 3-dot Arcana, with about 8-10 Arcana dots total. Their accessibility for benefits and favors will be limited to the rules per the Mentor merit, or for those who didn't put any dots into Mentor, will be limited except when it's appropriate for the scene (and usually requiring a favor in return).<br /> <br /> For NPCs, I would focus on drafting details about how they relate to each other, their history and relationships with others in their Order and the Consilium, and descriptions of how they act towards others. I will generally be taking the lead on roleplaying NPCs during scenes, although I liberally allow players to add NPCs to their posts and to RP for them when it adds to the narrative and doesn't affect mechanics. I will draft the NPC stats myself, which I keep in my ST notes offline. I do like the idea of a lower-Wisdom character who is more brash in style and approach. I imagine she would be effective at achieving her goals, but at times off-putting to Guardians or other higher-Wisdom characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two bedroom apartment in a nice but not pircey complex. </div> </div> </div>With the Resources 2 dots that you get from your Mystery Cult Initiation merit, this makes sense. It won't be as nice as the apartment Lynx will have with Resources 3, and you'll have less spending cash by default (obviously not taking into consideration your in-game use of skills to obtain more money illegally). On a related note, I surprisingly can't find the availability dots of vehicles anywhere in the CofD books I own (including Hurt Locker), which is strange, so I'm just going to say that a mini-van is availability 2 and that isn't an issue for you at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-03-2020, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T12:23:51-08:00","id":1421663,"title":"","content":"Posting an updated to-do list for everyone. As you can see, Second Chances and DArchon5 still need the most work before we can start. Can you two please let me know what a realistic goal might be for when you can complete this, so we can start playing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> (<b>Lynx</b>):<br /> As far as I can tell, your character is completely ready to go! Thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> (<b>Eurydice\u2019s Heir</b>):<br /> (1) Character sheet: I need you to make a post in the OOC thread with your actual game stats. Please use the same post to include all of the additional information we need to know about your character (aspirations/Obsessions, background, photo, etc.).<br /> <br /> (2) Aspirations/Obsession: Your Obsession is probably more appropriate for a short-term aspiration. And honestly, your mentor will probably start as an adept in at least one arcanum, so you could easily pick a mentor who starts with Spirit 4. An Obsession should be like a long-term aspiration that relates specifically to the Supernal realms, a specific known Mystery, or something else related to the Awakened world or magic. Your long-term aspiration might possibly be a better fit as an Obsession, but you might consider something broader like &quot;study goetia of Greek mythological concepts.&quot; Please tweak your aspirations/Obsession accordingly.<br /> <br /> (3) Background: Please flesh out more details about your background. This doesn't need to be lengthy, but it should provide a little more clarification about who Eurydice's Heir is both pre- and post-Awakening.<br /> <br /> (4) Photo: Please post a link to a photo or photos that represent how you view your character.<br /> <br /> (5) Mentor: Please decide on which existing NPC you'd like 