nalize characters. Please try your best to have everything on your character sheet drafted by Monday, even if it's only a rough draft, so I can start to focus on getting the game up and running. I'm itching to play! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We can continue to edit character backgrounds, stats, etc. even once we start posting in the IC thread. I just need enough of a working draft that I have info to go off of as I start to introduce plot hooks, antagonists, and so on. We can retcon things if needed.<br /> <br /> I'm going to work on statting some NPCs, moving a few things around between the introductory posts on the OOC and IC threads, and putting up some gaming conventions/rules that were discussed throughout the OOC and IC threads but need to be compiled in some easy to find location.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - I forgot to ask, would Lynx still have a roommate? If so, would you like to stick with Ewan Byrne? He was the jock who acted really macho but was suspected (at least in the OOC thread) as being closeted gay.<br /> <br /> Let me know if anyone has any questions or concerns, or if you are worried about being able to post 1-2 times in game each week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-06-2020, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T06:10:08-08:00","id":1422420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1422277#post1422277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12046\" data-vbnamecard=\"12046\">Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon</a> - I forgot to ask, would Lynx still have a roommate? If so, would you like to stick with Ewan Byrne? He was the jock who acted really macho but was suspected (at least in the OOC thread) as being closeted gay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd prefer to not have a roommate. Maybe a wall-to-wall neighbour though? Could be Ewan, but I think I'd prefer someone else, in which case, surprise me. I'll leave that up to you though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T06:13:57-08:00","id":1422421,"title":"","content":"Sure, sounds good. I can reuse the character concept somewhere else.<br /> <br /> To be clear...I meant there is more to that NPC that wasn\u2019t explored in the last game. So I can find other ways to use him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-07-2020, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T21:24:02-08:00","id":1422539,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Yeah, I think I'm at the end of my rope, creativity wise. I keep trying to expand on Rene and keep getting distracted by other things. I could probably get through it given time, but I already dragged this out long enough.<br /> <br /> I'll just back out of this. Sorry for wasting everyone's time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T21:57:55-08:00","id":1422542,"title":"","content":"Awww, I'm sorry to hear that. Are you sure you won't reconsider? I'd love to keep you in the group.<br /> <br /> What if we roleplay out more of the Changeling stuff in character? Then we could figure it out as we go along. You could say that you Awakened, and have finally realized that something is very off with Rene's brother. If you're feeling stuck creatively, you can reach out here to me or the other players for ideas. You also could pick the options that would result in the most dramatic play.<br /> <br /> If I were to pick, I would say that the Fetch is still here, but that maybe you realized in hindsight that your brother hasn't been the same for a long time. He could return from captivity at some point during the story when it's dramatically relevant or interesting.<br /> <br /> If you're straining too much to figure out the Changeling crossover stuff, you could drop that explicitly for now and say that your brother was one of the LT High School kids who went missing for weeks at a time. Rather than give in to the Lie and the pressure of La Grange suburban culture, something in your soul pushed back and demanded to know what was happening to change his destiny, and it was a catalyst for your own Awakening. That would give you and Morganna some shared interests with that particular Mystery. We could still add the Changeling crossover later if it's interesting to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T22:02:00-08:00","id":1422543,"title":"","content":"On an unrelated note, I have added some details about game rules and conventions to the introductory posts on the OOC thread here, including info about bookkeeping, combat, rolling dice, and so on. Please let me know if anyone has any other questions/concerns, or anything else you think we should add or discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T22:41:44-08:00","id":1422550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1422542#post1422542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awww, I'm sorry to hear that. Are you sure you won't reconsider? I'd love to keep you in the group.<br /> <br /> What if we roleplay out more of the Changeling stuff in character? Then we could figure it out as we go along. You could say that you Awakened, and have finally realized that something is very off with Rene's brother. If you're feeling stuck creatively, you can reach out here to me or the other players for ideas. You also could pick the options that would result in the most dramatic play.<br /> <br /> If I were to pick, I would say that the Fetch is still here, but that maybe you realized in hindsight that your brother hasn't been the same for a long time. He could return from captivity at some point during the story when it's dramatically relevant or interesting.<br /> <br /> If you're straining too much to figure out the Changeling crossover stuff, you could drop that explicitly for now and say that your brother was one of the LT High School kids who went missing for weeks at a time. Rather than give in to the Lie and the pressure of La Grange suburban culture, something in your soul pushed back and demanded to know what was happening to change his destiny, and it was a catalyst for your own Awakening. That would give you and Morganna some shared interests with that particular Mystery. We could still add the Changeling crossover later if it's interesting to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I'll try this one last push. The changeling crossover part is just a bit too entrancing for me to just drop though.<br /> <br /> Rene's backstory is:<br /> <br /> She's a girl who was born in Chicago and moved to La Grange. Her father raised her and she never knew her mother. Dear old dad always changes the subject or goes silent when the topic inevitably rolls around, and his relatives either don't know or are silent as well. She <i>has</i> confirmed he's her biological dad at least.<br /> <br /> She has a bit of a thing of being a maelstrom of luck. Her luck Nimbus essentially being something that had followed her all through her life, and getting stronger after she Awakened. She got treated as cursed by her classmates in middle school and eventually some of the parents as well. She and her dad moved to La Grange to get away from it all.<br /> <br /> Rene has a bit of an interest in superstitions involving luck and fate, particularly Tarot cards, which I'll probably make as one of her Path Tools somehow. While she does hide the whole 'probably cursed' thing from her friends, she has more or less learned to live with it. After a while of living with strange luck, you learn to minimize the bad sides and exploit the good sides.<br /> <br /> Jack lived a similar life, having been born and raised in La Grange. His dad died a while back and his mother has been trying to raise her son alone for years. He's a bit abrasive and blunt, but tends to cut to the heart of issues to lay it bare. Sometimes this solves things, other times it just makes it more obvious to everyone watching. Once Jack makes a promise he'ss go through hell and high water to keep it.<br /> <br /> Rene's dad and Jack's mom met in La Grange and got engaged. They actually still have two homes since one of them hasn't gotten sold yet, but the two families have started moving in with one another.<br /> <br /> Rene and Jack were cold to each other at first, but eventually Jack reached out since he realizes his problem is more with his mom getting married than with Rene. They promise to try getting closer. That night, Jack gets replaced by the Fetch.<br /> <br /> Jack got cold again and Rene sort of accepts that Jack doesn't actually want anything to do with her, but some part of her knows this isn't the case. During the Deathstorm, things got to ahead in her Mystery Play.<br /> <br /> She's confronted with the fact that she's trying to protect herself with flimsy lies even when she <i>knows</i> something's wrong with Jack. She Awakens and she resolves to find out whats going<br /> <br /> She finds out about the Pentacle Orders and joins the Mystagogues since they have the most information. Her mentor is [Insert Someone Here]<br /> <br /> Jack is captured by the True Fae and has been forced into the role of the 'Hero' of the Fae's story. Each time, he would be clad in armor of resolve and armed with a sword called hope. He would scale up the thousand levels of the Fae's tower, avoiding traps and fighting its minions.<br /> <br /> At the top, he would confront the Fae in the form of a great beast, a nightmarish Manticore invincible to normal arms. They would fight and at the end, Jack would trust the sword through the beast's chest.<br /> <br /> Only to see the blade shatter.<br /> <br /> The monster would then hurl Jack off of the Tower, falling a thousand levels down to the jagged rocks beneath. He would survive, but his armor would break during the fall.<br /> <br /> The servants of the Fae at the bottom would reforge his resolve and hope into a set of armor and weapons and force him up the Tower once more.<br /> <br /> And so the cycle continues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T22:42:28-08:00","id":1422551,"title":"","content":"Looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T09:05:45-08:00","id":1422605,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - That looks great. That is perfectly reasonable as a starting point, we can always flesh it out as we start playing. <br /> <br /> That is assuming you still want to play? Please don\u2019t feel pressured or obligated. If you are worried you won\u2019t have enough interest to keep playing, please let me know now. No hard feelings. I just figured that if you needed help with the creative process, we can help with that. <br /> <br /> From your backstory, and your emphasis in Fate Arcana, I\u2019m guessing you would want another Acanthus as your mentor? Would Fatewise intentionally seek out a mentor who shares her Path so she could learn more about Arcadia?<br /> <br /> Would Rene still live at home? Or would she feel a need to get out of the house while the Fetch is living there? If she would have moved, she would probably have a one-bedroom apartment somewhere in La Grange, maybe near Lynx.<br /> <br /> Still need a photo, if you can find one you like. You can always update it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T21:30:59-08:00","id":1422692,"title":"","content":"Well, this week was more exhausting than I expected, so not quite as far as planned, but I've got stats and a photo at least! While its tempting to take one of the Olympians as a Mentor, I will go with Ovid, since they are also on theme. Tweaked aspirations/obsession. Will keep picking away at background as I have, but it is still point form. Character/setting connections are on the todo list too, but this should be enough to at least get started.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Former high school teacher, mid to late 30s, single. Greek neopagan since teens.<br /> - Was married, built a house together, but things soured when he started getting restless at his job. She didn't want anything when they parted, so he still lives in an empty house made for a family. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Looked for a career change, so planned to go back to the University of Chicago to get a Masters in Classics</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Awakened during the first week, causing him to experience a particularly Orphic Mystery Play of Stygia, where he met various Chthonic entities form the Greco-Roman underworld. Scribed his name in Orpheus\u2019 place to give him another chance to escape the Underworld with Eurydice. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Basically had to drop out of his program because he was MIA for so long, but doesn\u2019t regret it since he gets to experience the Supernatural (and Supernal) directly. Blamed it on a mental break/mid-life crisis to the faculty, who (mostly) bought it. Tutors high school students to keep up appearances. Sometimes tutors freshman it at the University if he needs an excuse to be on campus or stick his nose downtown. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Sees spirits, ghosts, and goetia as different manifestations of the divine, despite most Mages categorizing them as entirely separate and unrelated phenomena. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Joined the Arrows by reasoning that Greek Gods and Heroes both grow through conflict, be it with nature, each other, or themselves. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Lived in La Grange prior to the Deathstorm, but didn\u2019t get super involved with other Mages. Believed the Highstorms were blessings form a Supernal Olympus/Atlantis.<br /> - Is now concerned the consilium has lost the Supernal's favour and that the ghosts of the deceased may yet linger, becoming restless ancestors for the Pentacle.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b>General Links</b></u><br /> <b>Places of Worship: </b>The Heir's general thesis is that all faiths point toward a greater Supernal Truth (in that the Gods actually exist in the Supernal), but even Mages have difficulty perceiving it because it requires viewing multiple Paths at once (he may or may not be right about that). Goetia, spirits, ghosts, shadow names, and nimbuses are all emanations of the greater truth in his view. He's very protective of all religious spaces as a result, even those who look down upon his own faith.<br /> <b>Wild Spaces:</b> These are one of the places the Gods and the Nymphs inhabit and the Heir prefers to relax in them when he needs to clear his head. Probably something he would get along with Lynx about, although they would have different perspectives on why its important.<br /> <b>Homes:</b> These are the other important place that Gods inhabit, albeit the less well-known ones in pop culture. The Heir loathes violating homes and Sanctums, even if it would be the most expedient way to get something done.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Specific Links</b></u><br /> <b>Fatewise: </b>The Heir would be VERY interested in finding out what happened to Jack and trying to fit Changelings/the Fae into his idiosyncratic metaphysics. Also, FATE is a significant belief for him, so taking that on as a Shadow Name is something that would intrigue him. Its possible that he taught or tutored her as Rene.<br /> <b>The Olympians: </b>The Heir puts special weight on Shadow Names tied to his faith, believing that the Mages using them are channeling the Gods from the Supernal. He tends to regard everything the Olympians do as significant, above and beyond their prominence on the Council. That doesn't necessarily mean he defers to their wishes, Heroes quarreling with Gods is a fixture of Hellenic myth, after all, but he pays very close attention to the leads they give and the causes they champion.<br /> <b>The Mythologos:</b> The Heir has been actively pursuing closer ties with this Column, hoping they will become allies (and Allies) in the future. Homer and Dante are the two he is drawn most to.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://thehardtimes.net/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/teacher.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Concept:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A neopagan obsessed with ephemeral beings</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sympathetic Name:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Peter Hunter </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Shadow Name:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eurydice's Heir</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mentor:</span></b>Askia<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Path:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Moros</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Order:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adamantine Arrow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Legacy:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> n/a</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attributes:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 2; Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2; Presence 3,</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manipulation 1, Composure 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skills: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Academics 3 (Hellenic Religion)*, Computers 1, Investigation 2, Medicine 2 (First Aid), Occult 3, Politics 1; Athletics 3 (Archery), Drive 1; Empathy 1, Expression 2, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 1, Socialize 1</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wisdom:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Virtue:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Curious</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vice: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hasty</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">9</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gnosis: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mana/per turn:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10/1</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Arcana: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Death 3, Matter 1, Mind 1, Space 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dedicated Magical Tool:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lead Obol</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Counterspell (Death, Matter, Mind, Space), Eyes of the Dead, Mage Armour (Death), Targeted Summoning (Death)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Praxes:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Know Nature (Mind 1), The Outward and Inward Eye (Space 1) </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rotes: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Odysseus\u2019 Offering (Speak With Dead - Occult), Asclepius\u2019 Intuition (Correspondence - Medicine*), Hephaestus' Insight (Craftsman\u2019s Eye - Investigation*) </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">*Order Rotes</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Adamant Hand (Athletics), Contacts (Students, Teachers)*, Dream 1, High Speech, Interdisciplinary Specialization (Hellenic Religion), Language (Ancient Greek), Professional Training (Teacher; Academics, Expression) 2, Shadow Name 1, Status (Adamantine Arrows) 1 Supernatural Taxonomy </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">*Professional Training</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Long-Term Nimbus: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those around the Heir become more musically inclined and attract the attention of ephemeral entities, particularly ghosts and ancestors. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Immediate: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thunder and lightning crash around the Heir and witness here the joyful shouts of the maenads. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Signature:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The smell of blood and burnt offerings. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nimbus Tilt:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The majesty of the Gods fills witness, granting +1 on Presence rolls. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>STA: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meet a spirit. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>STA:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Descend into the Underworld</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">LTA:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Form a neopagan support group. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ob: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Study goetia of Greek mythological concepts.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 11-23-2020, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T01:17:55-08:00","id":1422708,"title":"","content":"Everything is consolidated into an official character sheet post #1199 on page 80.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T07:07:33-08:00","id":1422737,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here are some initial notes for connections and impressions Lynx has with his new cabalmates:<br /> <br /> <b>Callie (squidheadjax):</b> Lynx is probably fascinated with Callie in many ways, in particular how ... true? she is with herself (on account of her 3 Dots of Shadow Name). However, he is also slightly reserved, since she's a Guardian, and her nimbus reminds him a lot of his depression a couple of years back.<br /> <br /> <b>Eurydice's Heir (Second Chances):</b> Lynx is very engaged in helping the Heir understand the nature of Spirits, and as a Moros, Lynx is likewise looking for guidance in how to understand the Matter arcanum. Lynx also finds him physically appealing (because that beard, woof).<br /> <br /> <b>Fatewise (dArchon5):</b> Lynx and Fatewise both being Mystagogues probably have a lot in common when it comes to the acquisition of knowledge. He is also interested in the Fate arcanum. However, Fatewise also makes Lynx feel a little frustrated due to her superior intelligence, academics and occult abilities, which makes her seem like a better fit for the Mysterium as a whole.<br /> <br /> <b>Morganna (DrSteve):</b> Lynx is engaged with Morganna when it comes to the Spirit arcanum, though he's dubious about the nature of Goetia - reflecting Mind being his inferior as a Thyrsus. He is also a little uneasy with her as an individual, since she can be difficult to read due to her astounding Subterfuge skill.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the absence as of late, life does what life does.<br /> <br /> Re: praxes and rotes, I'll look over them sometime later, today's a bit rough in general. Figured connections were more important to focus on right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":12046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","user":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","date":". 11-09-2020, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T19:21:02-08:00","id":1422861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1422605#post1422605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - That looks great. That is perfectly reasonable as a starting point, we can always flesh it out as we start playing.<br /> <br /> That is assuming you still want to play? Please don\u2019t feel pressured or obligated. If you are worried you won\u2019t have enough interest to keep playing, please let me know now. No hard feelings. I just figured that if you needed help with the creative process, we can help with that.<br /> <br /> From your backstory, and your emphasis in Fate Arcana, I\u2019m guessing you would want another Acanthus as your mentor? Would Fatewise intentionally seek out a mentor who shares her Path so she could learn more about Arcadia?<br /> <br /> Would Rene still live at home? Or would she feel a need to get out of the house while the Fetch is living there? If she would have moved, she would probably have a one-bedroom apartment somewhere in La Grange, maybe near Lynx.<br /> <br /> Still need a photo, if you can find one you like. You can always update it later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do want to play, its just been like hitting my head against a brick wall in terms of getting the paragraphs written. I think I'll just output streams of thought for now, to make it a bit easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fatewise probably has an Acanthus watching her since she got to La Grange. Her maelstrom of fate is sort of hard to miss, even for sleepers. She lights up like a chrismas tree to Fate Sight. That might mean people with the Fate Arcanum already know who Fatewise is, but maybe not since people don't generally walk around with Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Another Acanthus Mystagogue would fit as a mentor. Since she doesn't know about the Mage Orders yet, she was using her magic to guide her to information that could help her out and managed to cross paths with them. They probably have some knowledge of the True Fae, but hasn't told her anything because she hasn't opened up about her problems. I forgot how long ago the Deathstorm was, but since it's recent them focusing on aspects of Magic Society for their mentorship seems like a good bet.<br /> <br /> Rene hasn't had a chance to move out yet, the Fetch is pretty recent. She might be in the process of getting her own place during the campaign though. Speaking of Jack, I'll move the dot of Ally from him to Resources, to represent the money Rene regularly finds lying around. I also thought about giving her Destiny with a Doom of Bad Luck or increasing Potent Nimbus to 2. I think there's also some Nimbus perks of Signs of Sorcery that might fit, but I don't have that book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some stuff about Jack I came up with:<br /> <br /> Jack has resolve and hope in spades and will cimb the tower however many times it takes, but willpower alone cannot overcome the Manticore. He's essentially trying to punch through a brick wall with his bare hands. Yeah, he might accomplish it if he tries hard enough for long enough, but there are way easier ways to do this. He needs to stop trying to face it head on and try finding a weakness or a tool better suited for the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T22:21:30-08:00","id":1422872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1422692#post1422692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this week was more exhausting than I expected, so not quite as far as planned, but I've got stats and a photo at least! While its tempting to take one of the Olympians as a Mentor, I will go with Ovid, since they are also on theme. Tweaked aspirations/obsession. Will keep picking away at background as I have, but it is still point form. Character/setting connections are on the todo list too, but this should be enough to at least get started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally understand! I appreciate you taking the time to try and flesh out the character more. I had a few questions for you.<br /> <br /> First, I can make Ovid work but it would make you unique because everyone else's mentor is from the same Order. Unless Ovid was the one to &quot;discover&quot; your Awakening and was one of the first mages to whom you build a connection post-Awakening, it would probably make more sense to have at least one mage contact within the Arrows. Because you don't have any dots in the Mentor merit and he's a Libertine, this relationship with Ovid would start pretty one-way, probably consisting of you ingratiating yourself to earn his favor and social maneuvering to enhance the relationship over time. If you don't like this, you could have an Order mentor who has a greater initial connection to you and is more accessible for navigating Awakened society, and we can say that he points you in the direction of the Mythologos cabal early on in the game so you can pursue your shared interests.<br /> <br /> Second, you need a second Praxis, since you start with Gnosis 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1422708#post1422708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything is consolidated into an official character sheet post #1199 on page 80.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks! There are a few random formatting issues on your post (formatting tags that don't have missing partners) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but that's just me nitpicking. You also do have several Attainments you could add (Counterspell, Mage Armor, Targeted Summoning, etc.). Otherwise your character sheet looks great!<br /> <br /> I will try to work on drafting Vivian using the ideas you have already shared on the forums here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1422861#post1422861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do want to play, its just been like hitting my head against a brick wall in terms of getting the paragraphs written. I think I'll just output streams of thought for now, to make it a bit easier.<br /> <br /> Fatewise probably has an Acanthus watching her since she got to La Grange. Her maelstrom of fate is sort of hard to miss, even for sleepers. She lights up like a chrismas tree to Fate Sight. That might mean people with the Fate Arcanum already know who Fatewise is, but maybe not since people don't generally walk around with Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Another Acanthus Mystagogue would fit as a mentor. Since she doesn't know about the Mage Orders yet, she was using her magic to guide her to information that could help her out and managed to cross paths with them. They probably have some knowledge of the True Fae, but hasn't told her anything because she hasn't opened up about her problems. I forgot how long ago the Deathstorm was, but since it's recent them focusing on aspects of Magic Society for their mentorship seems like a good bet.<br /> <br /> Rene hasn't had a chance to move out yet, the Fetch is pretty recent. She might be in the process of getting her own place during the campaign though. Speaking of Jack, I'll move the dot of Ally from him to Resources, to represent the money Rene regularly finds lying around. I also thought about giving her Destiny with a Doom of Bad Luck or increasing Potent Nimbus to 2. I think there's also some Nimbus perks of Signs of Sorcery that might fit, but I don't have that book.<br /> <br /> Some stuff about Jack I came up with:<br /> <br /> Jack has resolve and hope in spades and will cimb the tower however many times it takes, but willpower alone cannot overcome the Manticore. He's essentially trying to punch through a brick wall with his bare hands. Yeah, he might accomplish it if he tries hard enough for long enough, but there are way easier ways to do this. He needs to stop trying to face it head on and try finding a weakness or a tool better suited for the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear you want to stick it out. I am really intrigued by all of the flavor stuff regarding the Fae.<br /> <br /> Of the NPC concepts I have created, Cadence is an Acanthus Mystagogue whose Shadow Name I've come up with but haven't really fleshed out her out yet. I would be glad to do that, unless that character sounds uninteresting to you at the surface level, in which case I can create a new NPC concept. Cadence would be the cabalmate of Melody, the Consilium's Herald, so you would have some potential neat opportunities to interact with her if you developed that mentor relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-10-2020, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T06:08:17-08:00","id":1423044,"title":"","content":"FYI, I have the day off today and I have a late work day tomorrow, so if anyone has questions about their character or the game that I can help to address so we can get started, let me know and I'll try to reply quickly.<br /> <br /> Please work on helping to finalize your characters! Itching to play and get the creative juices going again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T12:34:27-08:00","id":1423095,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> (<b>Eurydice\u2019s Heir</b>):<br /> (1) Character sheet: You need a second Praxis because of Gnosis 2. Also, if I did the math right, I think you\u2019re missing an Attribute dot somewhere? Did you add your free 1 dot to Resolve, Stamina, or Resolve from adding the Mage template?<br /> <br /> (2) Mentor: Please see my notes regarding Ovid; he is a Libertine, I\u2019d like you to pick at least one Arrow that you would know and who would serve as a primary mentor or point of contact within your Order. You can work in-game at building a relationship with Ovid or his cabal if interested (and you can pick that as an aspiration now or later, if interested).<br /> <br /> (3) Character and setting connections: Please come up with at least 3 general links to the setting and/or other characters. Look to Lynx or Caliginosa's character sheet for examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> (<b>Fatewise</b>):<br /> (1) Background: Please consolidate the background information you\u2019ve posted recently into the larger post with your character sheet (post #1184 on page 79) and all of the other requested information listed here.<br /> <br /> (2) Photo: Please post a link to a photo or photos that represent how you view your character.<br /> <br /> (3) Mentor: Please let me know if you like the idea of Cadence (an Acanthus Mystagogue, and cabalmate to Melody, the Consilium Herald) sounds like a good potential fit for your Order mentor.<br /> <br /> (4) Character and setting connections: Please come up with at least 3 general links to the setting and/or other characters. Look to Lynx or Caliginosa's character sheet for examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T07:01:10-08:00","id":1424006,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> <br /> <br /> (1) I am starting to write it out, but my sensibilities is making consolidating it hard. here's what I have currently.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If I were to say that my life wasn\u2019t always weird, I would be lying. I mean sure, everything with the magic, and the fairies, and the Deathstorm is new, but I\u2019m honestly not all that surprised that my life escalated to\u2026 all of this.<br /> <br /> But, I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> I was born in Chicago and lived there for most of my life at this point with my dear old dad. He raised me by himself, always juggling being the paternal father and doing enough work to support us. He always struggled with it, trying to be two people at once and having to be in three places at the same time. He dropped the ball a few times, but I try not to blame him for it. He has enough on his plate as it is.<br /> <br /> It always made me wonder where my mom is though, everyone always told how weird it is that my dad\u2019s raising me alone. I\u2019ve brought it up with him a couple of times, but he always either changes the subject or just goes silent and ends the conversation on the spot. Eventually I just, stopped asking.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> know he\u2019s my biological dad though, so there\u2019s that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, ever since I was little I\u2019ve always been a bit of a luck magnet. And by a bit, I mean a lot. Good luck, bad luck, and some weird luck here and there. Basically, if something is notably improbable then it\u2019s pretty much guaranteed to happen to me at some point.<br /> <br /> My mentor said it\u2019s something to do with my Nimbus, but I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s an effect of my Nimbus or if the Nimbus just made it stronger.<br /> <br /> I digress.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (2) I have no idea how to even begin to find a photo of Rene. I mean, if all else fails I'll just look up Rose Lalonde cosplayers, but I'd prefer that stay a last resort.<br /> <br /> (3) Cadence sounds like a good enough fit.<br /> <br /> (4) I'll get to it as I finish up Backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T08:06:48-08:00","id":1424015,"title":"","content":"The photo is mostly fluff. You can always change it later. I just use Google Image searches for most NPCs, and then link the photo here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T11:30:29-08:00","id":1424059,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to this coming together <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T12:54:05-08:00","id":1424076,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - I just realized that I might not have been clear. I don\u2019t need you to rewrite or synthesize all of your writing in a different way. I meant literally copy and paste it all into one post here, in the same post as your photo and character sheet. You had \u201cstream of consciousness\u201d background in multiple posts; I just need one specific post I can reference that you will use for your character sheet throughout our time playing, including tracking XP, aspirations, Obessions, equipment, and so on. Sorry if that was not clear!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T16:45:29-08:00","id":1424112,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Oh, well that's much easier. I guess I'll just put up the more polished version on my own time then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T16:56:13-08:00","id":1424116,"title":"","content":"Yeah! I know you\u2019ve been slowly chipping away at more ideas about your backstory. I\u2019m a believer in letting players tweak character sheets and backstory early on in the campaign if it makes the game more fun for them, and it\u2019s ok if you learn more about Fatewise simply by deciding in the moment how to respond to a conflict or Mystery. I need stats most importantly, then enough of a background to know what is most important and interesting to you so I can start brainstorming ideas for plot hooks. After that, I like fluff like character photos to make the world more vivid and engaging.<br /> <br /> As soon as you and the Heir are both finalized with those basics, I think we are just about ready to go live with the IC posts!! Which means I better get to work double time with brainstorming and writing, haha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T21:37:55-08:00","id":1424174,"title":"","content":"Here's the links I have right now:<ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>DESTINY:</b> Rene is a locus of fate, often getting tangled up in others problems and stories. Chances are, she's previously met the important people she will encounter and walked away from it with some insight as to their character. Destiny's idea of foreshadowing things to her. This also sometimes manifests as literal foreshadowing, ominous events appearing around her as a portent of things to come.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>FAMILY:</b> </span>Rene's brother, Jack, is currently living out his Durance in Arcadia, battling the shapeshifting True Fae that keeps him hostage. The Tragic Hero to the Fae's Villain. Jack's Fetch has only recently appeared, though both Rene and Jack's mother has begun suspecting something is wrong. They've yet to figure out what however. Moving on, Rene's father, Harold Fraser, has recently married Dr. Sylvia Flores, Jack's Mother, and they all currently live in the Fraser's home. Dr. Flores has opted to not change her name so as to not confuse her patients, and Mr. Fraser agreed to it on the grounds of less paperwork they have to waste their time on. Harold and Slyvia do care deeply about their children, biological or otherwise, but they do have a problem in properly understanding them. A product of their busy schedules. It's honestly a miracle they found time to date and get married as it is.</li> <li><b>LITERATURE</b><b>:</b> Rene quite loves books and so does her luck. She loves reading and learning about new things, and is often found seeking out new books in shops and libraries, having quickly read through her last batch. Her luck often helps her with this, as she often quickly finds just the book with the information she needs, even if she didn't know she would need it yet.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T01:10:56-08:00","id":1424199,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> - Those are great. I looked through the character sheet and it looks fantastic. Other than the photo, the only thing I noticed was that the number of dots next to your Shadow Name merit didn\u2019t seem to be listed or displaying, which I think is only 1 for now but I know you can put more into that later. Thanks for your thoughtfulness with the background and your willingness to stick it out!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - And then there was one! I know you\u2019ve been really busy. Do you have time this week to finalize your character sheet? See my questions above for final details I have questions about. Do you have any concerns about your availability or ability to post 1-2 times per week once we get started? Let me know so we can talk about it.<br /> <br /> Everyone else: Does anyone have any other questions or concerns we need to discuss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":8136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","user":"rwknoll","date":". 11-16-2020, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T07:29:05-08:00","id":1424261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1424199#post1424199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar