>Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T03:22:34-08:00","id":1427120,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - I am going to put up my next post hopefully today or tomorrow. If you still want to include part of the scene at breakfast that you had mentioned, or taking Lynx to stop and pick up Lucy\u2019s clothes like you had mentioned, feel free to put that in your post. Let me know if you had questions about what I mentioned earlier regarding limits on Beats and Arcane Beats per scene. <br /> <br /> Everyone else: Let me know if you have any questions before we move on in the scene. I\u2019ll put up info about the dramatic failure for the Heir as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T05:14:47-08:00","id":1427128,"title":"","content":"Still recruiting people here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T05:38:27-08:00","id":1427129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1427128#post1427128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still recruiting people here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn\u2019t officially, but we are just getting underway so I may be open to adding someone if the fit is right. I would have a cap at 6 active players for now. What kind of character did you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T07:54:45-08:00","id":1427141,"title":"","content":"I have two concepts for now:<br /> 1) A healer.<br /> 2) A medium for ghosts.<br /> But If you cannot handle more than six player, I don't wish to stress you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T21:29:23-08:00","id":1427940,"title":"","content":"One success short of exceptional on the spellcasting, damn it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> <br /> Should Fatewise declare what Boons she has, or would she be able to have them take form as the scene progresses?.<br /> <br /> Actually, one more question: Is Rene allowed to use the &quot;grant bonus to Spellcasting roll&quot; +2 Reach option?. While her being a powerful spellcaster is appropriate for the character concept (That's what the Potent Nimbus is supposed to represent), her being able to apply a +5/6 bonus to spellcasting whenever she wants is a bit... well it feels a bit munchkin-y.<br /> <br /> I'd be cool with giving her a lower bound, like limiting her to the free Potency whenever she tries to boost spellcasting or even just pretending that option doesn't exist. But letting her just boost her spellcasting like that is also alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T03:40:57-08:00","id":1427953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1427940#post1427940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One success short of exceptional on the spellcasting, damn it.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> Should Fatewise declare what Boons she has, or would she be able to have them take form as the scene progresses?.<br /> <br /> Actually, one more question: Is Rene allowed to use the &amp;quot;grant bonus to Spellcasting roll&amp;quot; +2 Reach option?. While her being a powerful spellcaster is appropriate for the character concept (That's what the Potent Nimbus is supposed to represent), her being able to apply a +5/6 bonus to spellcasting whenever she wants is a bit... well it feels a bit munchkin-y.<br /> <br /> I'd be cool with giving her a lower bound, like limiting her to the free Potency whenever she tries to boost spellcasting or even just pretending that option doesn't exist. But letting her just boost her spellcasting like that is also alright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to Mage! You can do some crazy powerful shit with starting levels of arcana. A +2 reach effect is definitely expensive and not to be underestimated, especially once you have Gnosis 3 and start generating multiple paradox dice per overreach. So yes, you can absolutely use Fate to enhance your spell casting if you desire. Your reach count is currently off; instant, advanced duration, and advanced potency is only 3 reach. You could drop advanced potency and add the reach effect for spell casting and that would keep you safely at 4 reach.<br /> <br /> I do need you to choose the boon at the time of casting. Please look at the list on p. 134 and edit your post to include that when you have time.<br /> <br /> I am hoping to have some downtime today to put up my next post, which will include results of the perception checks and some other miscellaneous stuff. Let me know if anyone has any other questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T04:03:09-08:00","id":1427955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1427953#post1427953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welcome to Mage! You can do some crazy powerful shit with starting levels of arcana. A +2 reach effect is definitely expensive and not to be underestimated, especially once you have Gnosis 3 and start generating multiple paradox dice per overreach. So yes, you can absolutely use Fate to enhance your spell casting if you desire. Your reach count is currently off; instant, advanced duration, and advanced potency is only 3 reach. You could drop advanced potency and add the reach effect for spell casting and that would keep you safely at 4 reach.<br /> <br /> I do need you to choose the boon at the time of casting. Please look at the list on p. 134 and edit your post to include that when you have time.<br /> <br /> I am hoping to have some downtime today to put up my next post, which will include results of the perception checks and some other miscellaneous stuff. Let me know if anyone has any other questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take the spellcasting bonus instead of Advanced Potency then. Fatewise isn't taking anything to chance.<br /> <br /> As for boons, I actually already decided them, but decided to ask first. I'll edit them in, but they are the Charmed condition, Informed condition, +5 to 3 rolls (2x Occult, 1x Investigation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T06:16:57-08:00","id":1428177,"title":"","content":"Sorry for not posting yet. Had some family stuff come up yesterday. I have it mostly written now and will try to post it soon unless I get interrupted again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T09:22:23-08:00","id":1428183,"title":"","content":"All good! Life happens and family is important!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T23:46:55-08:00","id":1428565,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> For your questions regarding Orokos, there's actually a page where the various dice modifiers are explained: <a href=\"https://orokos.com/roll/?action=dicehelp\" target=\"_blank\">https://orokos.com/roll/?action=dicehelp</a><br /> <br /> For our purposes:<br /> oZ: is open roll Z means that an extra roll is done when the dice result is Z or greater. This is how we add 8- or 9-Again. Basic 10-Again doesn't need this because<br /> hZ: is hit Z means that Z+ results are successes, with an implicit oY where Y is the highest number. For our purposes, that means it automatically gains 10-Again.<br /> roZ: is reroll once Z, remans that the die rerolls once on a Z or lower. Basically the Rote Quality.<br /> <br /> So, in the example given by Orokos7d10o9h7 means Seven dice, hits on 7+, roll again on 9+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T17:12:45-08:00","id":1428685,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I forgot to add a subject line for Informed. Can I just say it represents a lucky break like Charmed?<br /> <br /> If not, then I'll just go with Informed (The Strings of Fate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T05:23:47-08:00","id":1428737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1428685#post1428685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> I forgot to add a subject line for Informed. Can I just say it represents a lucky break like Charmed?<br /> <br /> If not, then I'll just go with Informed (The Strings of Fate).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would pick a subject. Informed (The Strings of Fate) is fine with me. The purpose of this condition is to give you a bonus on a specific skill (non-spellcasting) roll. Informed (The Strings of Fate) could help you on an Occult, Investigation, or other similar roll where knowledge about the workings of Fate might be relevant.<br /> <br /> If you prefer, because you are casting this specifically heading into an interaction with Valentine, you could also take Informed (Valentine). Your exceptional luck would essentially allow you to do or say just the right thing to interact more effectively with him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - I have been playing Mage 2E for a few years now and I seriously have never caught that reference you provided about players choosing their own conditions on an exceptional success! Wow. Yeah, I am fine with players choosing their own conditions, then. My only request as a ST is that you all pick conditions that are related to the dramatic action that created them. I also prefer that players not select special conditions that are normally reserved for specific dramatic moments (e.g., the Triumphant condition that is normally earned by winning a Duel Arcane).<br /> <br /> You can also create a custom condition; if you do, I reserve the right to tweak it if I think it's too &quot;cheesy&quot; or not appropriate for the situation. I can add any new conditions that we make to the OOC thread introductory posts, for easy reference in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> For everyone: I haven't seen much activity this week but I'm wondering if it's because people don't have much more to say or do right now in response to my most recent post? I wanted to offer others the chance to take any other actions they wanted before we move on, but I will try to work on the next ST post over the next day or two to help us move the story along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T09:30:02-08:00","id":1428772,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think the Heir has much to add right now. I'll double-check if there is anything he can respond to from the rest of the Cabal, but I'm ready to move on to the meeting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T19:17:12-08:00","id":1428822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1428565#post1428565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> For your questions regarding Orokos, there's actually a page where the various dice modifiers are explained: <a href=\"https://orokos.com/roll/?action=dicehelp\" target=\"_blank\">https://orokos.com/roll/?action=dicehelp</a><br /> <br /> For our purposes:<br /> oZ: is open roll Z means that an extra roll is done when the dice result is Z or greater. This is how we add 8- or 9-Again. Basic 10-Again doesn't need this because<br /> hZ: is hit Z means that Z+ results are successes, with an implicit oY where Y is the highest number. For our purposes, that means it automatically gains 10-Again.<br /> roZ: is reroll once Z, remans that the die rerolls once on a Z or lower. Basically the Rote Quality.<br /> <br /> So, in the example given by Orokos7d10o9h7 means Seven dice, hits on 7+, roll again on 9+</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, especially for giving an example for 9 again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T23:26:57-08:00","id":1428834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1428737#post1428737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would pick a subject. Informed (The Strings of Fate) is fine with me. The purpose of this condition is to give you a bonus on a specific skill (non-spellcasting) roll. Informed (The Strings of Fate) could help you on an Occult, Investigation, or other similar roll where knowledge about the workings of Fate might be relevant.<br /> <br /> If you prefer, because you are casting this specifically heading into an interaction with Valentine, you could also take Informed (Valentine). Your exceptional luck would essentially allow you to do or say just the right thing to interact more effectively with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I'll think about it for a bit. Will definitely ake a decision once the next post is up.<br /> <br /> Actually, speaking of Valentine, how much does Fatewise know about him, and did she have enough time to do research on the guy?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of actually using that Research Specialty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T05:42:54-08:00","id":1428848,"title":"","content":"Don't really think Lynx has much to contribute at the moment, I'm just waiting for things to move on for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Character Sheet: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1419997#post1419997\" target=\"_blank\">Oscar &quot;Lynx&quot; Dalgren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12046-kvitebj\u00f8rn-kong-valemon","name":"Kvitebj\u00f8rn Kong Valemon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T09:32:06-08:00","id":1429164,"title":"","content":"Working on the next post but I\u2019ve had family visiting this weekend. Sorry for the delay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T11:45:49-08:00","id":1429200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1428834#post1428834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I'll think about it for a bit. Will definitely ake a decision once the next post is up.<br /> <br /> Actually, speaking of Valentine, how much does Fatewise know about him, and did she have enough time to do research on the guy?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of actually using that Research Specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s actually a moot point. The idea of Fate magic is that you don\u2019t need to do research per se, you just conveniently know the right thing to say or do at a given moment to have a desired outcome. The Informed condition normally comes from doing research and preparing something to help you apply it, like reading about werewolves from a Mysterium Athanaeum and then using it to prepare a trap for them. But with Fate, it\u2019s like randomly choosing what you say or do, and it just happens to hit home or have the desired response. You usually don\u2019t even know how it will happen, it just works out that way. <br /> <br /> So you don\u2019t need to research Valentine to actually select him for the Informed condition. The imago of your spell simply allowed you to will the strings of Fate to bend to your way, and it just so happens to work out that you know how to interact with Valentine to have a positive outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T22:09:33-08:00","id":1429295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rwknoll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1429200#post1429200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s actually a moot point. The idea of Fate magic is that you don\u2019t need to do research per se, you just conveniently know the right thing to say or do at a given moment to have a desired outcome. The Informed condition normally comes from doing research and preparing something to help you apply it, like reading about werewolves from a Mysterium Athanaeum and then using it to prepare a trap for them. But with Fate, it\u2019s like randomly choosing what you say or do, and it just happens to hit home or have the desired response. You usually don\u2019t even know how it will happen, it just works out that way.<br /> <br /> So you don\u2019t need to research Valentine to actually select him for the Informed condition. The imago of your spell simply allowed you to will the strings of Fate to bend to your way, and it just so happens to work out that you know how to interact with Valentine to have a positive outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that makes sense. I guess I'll take that Informed Condition about Valentine after all.<br /> <br /> Btw, Rene has an Empathy Specialty to detect lies, would that apply to the Wits + Empathy roll offered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T03:04:58-08:00","id":1429321,"title":"","content":"No, your specialty would not apply here. Same thing with Morganna, her Pierce Deception spell would not detect any active untruths in Valentine\u2019s words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T01:46:36-08:00","id":1429725,"title":"","content":"Planning my Post right now, probably just going to make another Perception roll. Rene is really observant when she's anxious, when bad luck hits her as often as it does it pays to keep an eye out for details. You never know what's going to be important after all.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> Is Fatewise able to spend the last Divination question without speaking out loud? Like, can she ask the question in her head and still get an answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T01:53:11-08:00","id":1429726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1429725#post1429725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Planning my Post right now, probably just going to make another Perception roll. Rene is really observant when she's anxious, when bad luck hits her as often as it does it pays to keep an eye out for details. You never know what's going to be important after all.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Is Fatewise able to spend the last Divination question without speaking out loud? Like, can she ask the question in her head and still get an answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don\u2019t see why not. It\u2019s no different than the result you get from casting it the original time, which doesn\u2019t require you to speak your question aloud either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T12:17:30-08:00","id":1429883,"title":"","content":"Merry Christmas everyone! Take a free Beat in celebration of the holiday. Hope all is well with you and yours. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T22:40:24-08:00","id":1430542,"title":"","content":"Ouch. Just realized that the group is weak when it comes to combat skills and spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T11:48:43-08:00","id":1430597,"title":"","content":"Michelle can punch like the Hulk and do it from invisibility when she gets a couple spells up. And can also fling lightning, though not as a rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T18:21:46-08:00","id":1430635,"title":"","content":"Rene is more of a buffing character than an offense one. She doesn't really plan on fighting her own battles. She'll probably try to counterspell though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T23:52:23-08:00","id":1430651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1430597#post1430597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michelle can punch like the Hulk and do it from invisibility when she gets a couple spells up. And can also fling lightning, though not as a rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, saw that, which is better than Morganna's firearms skills but not enough Str to avoid a -1 penalty (though she does have a combat rote). These characters are more civilians with a smattering of combat skills than folks that are going to go toe to toe with some CoD heavy hitters.<br /> <br /> <br /> What are Michelle's asset skills? They're not on the character sheet. I'm guessing Larceny and Stealth but could also be Larceny and Athletics or Streetwise.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T00:28:22-08:00","id":1430653,"title":"","content":"Hmm, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8136\" data-vbnamecard=\"8136\">rwknoll</a> can Fatewise use her Status (Mysterium), such as it is, to requisition a Grimoire? A one-dot one would suffice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T17:19:10-08:00","id":1430702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1430651#post1430651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, saw that, which is better than Morganna's firearms skills but not enough Str to avoid a -1 penalty (though she does have a combat rote). These characters are more civilians with a smattering of combat skills than folks that are going to go toe to toe with some CoD heavy hitters.<br /> <br /> <br /> What are Michelle's asset skills? They're not on the character sheet. I'm guessing Larceny and Stealth but could also be Larceny and Athletics or Streetwise.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, forgot to mark those on that sheet format. Larceny and Athletics, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T20:37:12-08:00","id":1430720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1430635#post1430635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rene is more of a buffing character than an offense one. She doesn't really plan on fighting her own battles. She'll probably try to counterspell though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lol, your character has fate magic to find whatever research topic she wants, a photographic memory for what she reads, and the equivalent of an M.A. coming out of high school (possibly pushing a Ph.D. in Anthropology with that occult skill). I know that person! (Ok they were older and actually getting a Ph.D.).<br /> <br /> I'm looking at the hurt locker rules right now. Maybe Rene should pick up a can of Pepper Spray. She'd be rolling 1 dice (dex -1 unskilled) but could spend a point of willpower to add 3 dice. Since Pepper Spray and stun guns have flat effects that don't scale with hits, Pepper spray and panic might be an option.<br /> <br /> Edit. Can you change the text color you use for IC. The yellow is really hard to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","user":"DrSteve","date":". 01-02-2021, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T21:03:27-08:00","id":1430721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia?p=1430720#post1430720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit. Can you change the text color you use for IC. The yellow is really hard to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's supposed to be gold, but sure.<br /> <br /> I was hoping bolding it would make it easier to see but apparently not.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#AA6C39\">How About this?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T21:12:42-08:00","id":1430722,"title":"","content":"I find that much better!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T12:46:47-08:00","id":1430780,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25593\" data-vbnamecard=\"25593\">DrSteve</a> - I really like the creativity here. As a Storyteller, I'm less experienced with the Astral realms so I'm a little unsure of how to evaluate how realistic your idea is and the mechanics of how it works. Can you explain further here in the OOC thread what you are proposing in your post regarding the candle and the Oneiros?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to say that no, Morganna can't see the Supernal entity that is visible to the Heir. Honestly I don't understand those mechanics either, Signs of Sorcery clarifies it a little but not much. But for now, I'll say that only the Heir can view it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - Sorry, we're in the same scene still. I haven't advanced it yet because very little has actually happened so far with regards to story advancement. I will indicate scene changes very clearly in my IC posts using this text: <b>* NEW SCENE *</b><br /> <br /> In my experience, many mages tend to be fantastic at combat without even building for it, but primarily when they have advance warning of a threat. That's the beauty of the Mage system: It really gives you an incentive for gaining information and problem-solving creatively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T05:02:07-08:00","id":1431674,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay in posting, everyone. I had a busy week and I have family visiting this weekend. I am working on an